msgctxt "scene:1:0"
msgid "Was für ein unrühmliches Ende..."
msgstr "What an ignominious end..."

msgctxt "scene:1:1"
msgid "Trinken gefährdet dir Gesundheit!"
msgstr "Drinking endangers your health!"

msgctxt "scene:1:2"
msgid "Weitere Details erparen wir Euch..."
msgstr "We'll spare you the further details..."

msgctxt "scene:2:0"
msgid ""
"Eine schmucke Wand-\n"
"lampe."
msgstr ""
"A handsome wall-\n"
"lamp."

msgctxt "scene:2:2"
msgid ""
"Für eine Kajüte ist\n"
"dieses Zimmer ganz\n"
"hübsch eingerichtet.\n"
"In der Luft hängt der\n"
"Duft eines süsslichen\n"
"Parfums."
msgstr ""
"For a ship's cabin\n"
"this room is quite\n"
"nicely furnished.\n"
"The scent of a\n"
"sweetish perfume\n"
"hangs in the air."

msgctxt "scene:2:8"
msgid ""
"Sogar ein Spiegel mit\n"
"geschnitztem Rahmen\n"
"hängt hier herum."
msgstr ""
"Even a mirror with\n"
"a carved frame\n"
"hangs around here."

msgctxt "scene:2:11"
msgid ""
"Die Tür auf den Gang\n"
"scheint ganz stabil\n"
"zu sein, doch etwas\n"
"Farbe könnte die auch\n"
"vertragen."
msgstr ""
"The door to the corridor\n"
"appears quite solid,\n"
"yet a coat of paint\n"
"would do it no harm."

msgctxt "scene:2:16"
msgid ""
"Der Kleiderschrank\n"
"wird wohl kaum stark\n"
"genutzt, wenn die\n"
"ganzen Sachen hier\n"
"herumliegen."
msgstr ""
"The wardrobe is likely\n"
"scarcely put to use,\n"
"if all these things lie\n"
"scattered about."

msgctxt "scene:2:21"
msgid ""
"Ich weiss nicht, ob der\n"
"Bewohner dieser Kajüte\n"
"sich darüber freut, dass\n"
"ich den Krug ausgeleert\n"
"habe."
msgstr ""
"I know not whether the\n"
"occupant of this cabin\n"
"will be pleased that I\n"
"have emptied the mug."

msgctxt "scene:2:26"
msgid ""
"Ein Waschset mit Krug,\n"
"der sogar gefüllt ist.\n"
"Richtig nobel..."
msgstr ""
"A washing set with a jug,\n"
"which is indeed full.\n"
"Truly noble..."

msgctxt "scene:2:29"
msgid ""
"Ein Nachttischchen mit\n"
"Schublade."
msgstr ""
"A small nightstand with\n"
"a drawer."

msgctxt "scene:2:31"
msgid ""
"Ein komfortables und\n"
"weiches Bett. Sicher\n"
"angenehmer wie eine\n"
"rauhe Satteldecke."
msgstr ""
"A comfortable and\n"
"soft bed. Surely\n"
"more pleasant than\n"
"a rough saddle blanket."

msgctxt "scene:2:35"
msgid ""
"Dieser Raum scheint den\n"
"Kleidern nach von einer\n"
"Frau bewohnt zu sein."
msgstr ""
"Judging by the clothes,\n"
"this room appears to be\n"
"inhabited by a woman."

msgctxt "scene:2:38"
msgid ""
"Die beiden Stühle hier\n"
"kann man wohl gerade\n"
"noch als Kleiderablage\n"
"gebrauchen. Die machen\n"
"einen ganz schön\n"
"wackeligen Eindruck."
msgstr ""
"The two chairs here\n"
"may likely just serve\n"
"as a clothes rack. They\n"
"make quite a rickety\n"
"impression."

msgctxt "scene:2:44"
msgid ""
"Um die herunter zu holen,\n"
"müsste man auf das Bett\n"
"steigen, und das ist\n"
"nicht sehr nett."
msgstr ""
"To fetch them down, one\n"
"would have to climb on\n"
"the bed, and that would\n"
"scarcely be proper."

msgctxt "scene:2:48"
msgid ""
"Wie soll ich das Zimmer\n"
"benutzen? Das kann nur\n"
"ein Versehen sein, oder?"
msgstr ""
"How am I to use this room?\n"
"This can only be an oversight,\n"
"can it not?"

msgctxt "scene:2:51"
msgid ""
"Mitnehmen werde ich ihn\n"
"nicht, aber wenn ich mich\n"
"so betrachte, muss ich\n"
"schon sagen, dass ein\n"
"neuer Haarschnitt ange-\n"
"bracht wäre."
msgstr ""
"Take it with me I shall\n"
"not, yet as I look upon\n"
"myself, I must truly say\n"
"that a new haircut would\n"
"be most fitting.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:57"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"ein Schläfchen in einem\n"
"fremden Zimmer angebracht\n"
"wäre - obwohl ich etwas\n"
"Schlaf gebrauchen könnte."
msgstr ""
"I deem it not proper to take\n"
"a nap in a stranger's room-\n"
"though I could well use a bit\n"
"of sleep.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:62"
msgid ""
"Hallo, was ein echter\n"
"Westmann ist, gibt sich\n"
"nicht mit Frauenkleider\n"
"ab..."
msgstr ""
"Hallo, what a true\n"
"westman is, does not\n"
"meddle with women's\n"
"attire..."

msgctxt "scene:2:66"
msgid ""
"Ich schätze, wenn ich\n"
"mich auf den Stuhl\n"
"setze, bricht er zu-\n"
"sammen."
msgstr ""
"I reckon that if I sit\n"
"upon this chair, it shall\n"
"collapse beneath me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:70"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube kaum, dass\n"
"es gut wäre, hier etwas\n"
"kaputtzumachen."
msgstr ""
"I scarcely believe it would\n"
"be wise to break anything\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:2:73"
msgid ""
"Der Spiegel ist komplett,\n"
"oder glaubst du, dass die\n"
"Holzwürmer sich im Spiegel\n"
"sehen wollen?"
msgstr ""
"The mirror is whole,\n"
"or do you believe that the\n"
"woodworms wish to look upon\n"
"themselves in the mirror?"

msgctxt "scene:2:77"
msgid ""
"Das nutzt auch nichts,\n"
"die eine Schranktür\n"
"klemmt zu fest."
msgstr ""
"That is of no avail, for\n"
"the one wardrobe door\n"
"is jammed far too tight."

msgctxt "scene:2:80"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brett kann man\n"
"die altersschwachen Stühle\n"
"auch nicht mehr retten."
msgstr ""
"That board will not help\n"
"to save those decrepit\n"
"chairs."

msgctxt "scene:2:83"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich die Türe\n"
"verrammeln? Dies ist weder\n"
"meine Kajüte, noch will ich\n"
"jemanden vor dem Eintreten\n"
"abhalten."
msgstr ""
"Why should I barricade\n"
"the door? This is neither\n"
"my cabin, nor do I wish to\n"
"keep anyone from entering.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:88"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich die Lampe\n"
"abdecken, dabei riskie-\n"
"re ich doch nur einen\n"
"Zimmerbrand."
msgstr ""
"Whyshould I cover the\n"
"lamp? In doing so, I\n"
"would only risk a fire\n"
"in the room."

msgctxt "scene:2:92"
msgid ""
"Der Hut würde sich auf\n"
"dem Bett sicher gut machen,\n"
"doch wenn ich ihn nicht\n"
"mitnehmen soll, pack ich\n"
"ihn wohl besser zurück in\n"
"den Schrank."
msgstr ""
"The hat would surely look well\n"
"upon the bed, yet if I am not\n"
"to take it with me, I had best\n"
"pack it back into the wardrobe.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:98"
msgid ""
"Das wäre ein Spass, zu\n"
"sehen wie die Dame rea-\n"
"giert, wenn sie den Käfer\n"
"im Kleid entdeckt. Für\n"
"solche Spässe habe ich\n"
"aber keine Zeit."
msgstr ""
"It would be a merry jest to\n"
"see how the lady reacts when\n"
"she discovers the beetle in\n"
"her dress. Yet for such jests,\n"
"I have no time.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:104"
msgid ""
"Ja, sicher gäbe das eine\n"
"lustige Reaktion wenn die\n"
"Dame ins Bett steigt und\n"
"den Käfer findet, doch\n"
"ich könnte es nicht sehen,\n"
"d'rum lass ich es sein."
msgstr ""
"Aye, 'twould surely yield\n"
"a merry reaction when the\n"
"lady steps into bed and\n"
"finds the beetle, yet I could\n"
"not witness it, wherefore I\n"
"shall let it be."

msgctxt "scene:2:110"
msgid ""
"Zuerst bestehst Du darauf,\n"
"dass ich diesen Käfer ein-\n"
"stecke und nun soll ich\n"
"ihn einfach im Zimmer wie-\n"
"der aussetzen...Nein!"
msgstr ""
"First you insist that I pocket\n"
"this beetle, and now I am to\n"
"simply release it in the room\n"
"once more... No!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:115"
msgid ""
"Ich könnte wohl die\n"
"Kleider in den Eimer\n"
"stopfen, aber das\n"
"hilft mir nicht weiter."
msgstr ""
"I might well stuff the\n"
"clothes into the\n"
"bucket, but that\n"
"would avail me nothing."

msgctxt "scene:2:119"
msgid ""
"Das Kleid sieht nicht aus\n"
"als ob es eine Wäsche nötig\n"
"hätte, das lass ich mal."
msgstr ""
"The dress does not look as\n"
"though it stands in need of\n"
"a washing, so I shall leave it be."

msgctxt "scene:2:122"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"die Dame eine Kneipp-\n"
"Kur bestellt hat, und\n"
"somit über ein nasses\n"
"Bett sicher nicht lachen\n"
"kann. Ich lass das."
msgstr ""
"I believe not that the lady\n"
"has ordered a cold water\n"
"cure, and would thus\n"
"scarcely laugh at a wet\n"
"bed. I shall leave it be.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:128"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir nicht vor-\n"
"stellen, dass einem \n"
"Schrank der klemmt,\n"
"Wasser noch gut tut..."
msgstr ""
"I can scarcely imagine that water\n"
"would do a jammed wardrobe\n"
"any good...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:132"
msgid ""
"Ich bin die Hauptfigur\n"
"dieses Abenteuers und\n"
"somit nicht angestellt,\n"
"um die Kulissen zu\n"
"reinigen. Warte auf die\n"
"Putzfrau..."
msgstr ""
"I am the protagonist of\n"
"this adventure, and thus\n"
"not employed to clean the\n"
"scenery. Wait for the\n"
"housemaid...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:138"
msgid ""
"Ich würde gerne das Fass\n"
"nutzen, doch ich bekomme\n"
"den Deckel nicht ab."
msgstr ""
"I would gladly make use of\n"
"the barrel, yet I cannot\n"
"get the lid off."

msgctxt "scene:2:141"
msgid ""
"Die Stuhlbeine sind doch\n"
"gerade in der richtigen\n"
"Länge, und da soll ich\n"
"daran rumschnitzen..?"
msgstr ""
"The chair legs are of\n"
"just the right length, and\n"
"yet I am to whittle away\n"
"at them...?"

msgctxt "scene:2:145"
msgid "Hello, FREDDY K. is calling."
msgstr "Hello, FREDDY K. is calling."

msgctxt "scene:2:146"
msgid ""
"Mit etwas Geschick liesse\n"
"sich der Schrank sicher\n"
"reparieren, doch dabei ris-\n"
"kiere ich, dass die Klinge\n"
"abbricht."
msgstr ""
"With a bit of skill, the\n"
"wardrobe could surely be fixed,\n"
"yet I risk breaking the blade\n"
"in doing so.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:151"
msgid ""
"Huch! Was machen Sie\n"
"denn hier?\n"
"Wer sind Sie?"
msgstr ""
"Why, hello! What are you\n"
"doing here?\n"
"Who are you?"

msgctxt "scene:2:154"
msgid ""
"1. Ich wollte bestimmt\n"
"   nichts stehlen."
msgstr ""
"1. I surely had no intention\n"
"   of stealing anything."

msgctxt "scene:2:156"
msgid "2. Ich bin Old Firehand."
msgstr "2. I am Old Firehand."

msgctxt "scene:2:157"
msgid ""
"3. Was wollen Sie denn\n"
"   hier?"
msgstr ""
"3. What business do you\n"
"   have here, anyway?"

msgctxt "scene:2:159"
msgid ""
"4. Ich wollte mir nur\n"
"   kurz den Hut borgen."
msgstr ""
"4. I only wanted to borrow\n"
"    the hat for a moment."

msgctxt "scene:2:161"
msgid ""
"Und was machen Sie\n"
"dann bitte mit\n"
"meinem Hut?"
msgstr ""
"And what, pray tell,\n"
"are you doing with\n"
"my hat then?"

msgctxt "scene:2:164"
msgid ""
"Old ... wie? Nie\n"
"gehört. Machen Sie,\n"
"dass Sie hier ver-\n"
"schwinden, oder ich\n"
"schreie das ganze\n"
"Schiff zusammen!"
msgstr ""
"Old... who? Never\n"
"heard of you. Get out\n"
"of here, or I shall\n"
"scream and rouse the\n"
"whole ship!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:170"
msgid ""
"Was ich hier will?\n"
"Das hier ist meine\n"
"Kabine! Verschwinden\n"
"Sie auf der Stelle,\n"
"oder ich rufe nach\n"
"dem Kapitän! Und\n"
"kommen Sie mir nicht\n"
"zu nahe!"
msgstr ""
"What I want here?\n"
"This is my cabin!\n"
"Get out this instant,\n"
"or I shall call for\n"
"the captain! And do\n"
"not come any closer\n"
"to me!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:178"
msgid ""
"Meinen Hut borgen?\n"
"Sie können doch nicht\n"
"einfach in meine\n"
"Kabine gehen, und sich\n"
"an meinem Schrank\n"
"zu schaffen machen!"
msgstr ""
"Borrowing my hat?\n"
"You cannot just walk\n"
"into my cabin and go\n"
"meddling with my\n"
"wardrobe like that!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:184"
msgid ""
"1. Ich wollte den Hut\n"
"   wirklich nicht\n"
"   stehlen."
msgstr ""
"1. I truly did not\n"
"   intend\n"
"   to steal the hat."

msgctxt "scene:2:187"
msgid ""
"2. Ich wusste ja nicht,\n"
"   dass das Ihr Hut ist."
msgstr ""
"2. I did not know that\n"
"   this hat was yours."

msgctxt "scene:2:189"
msgid ""
"3. Der Hut ist so schön,\n"
"   dass ich ihn mir\n"
"   mal ansehen wollte."
msgstr ""
"3. The hat is so fine,\n"
"   that I wanted to have\n"
"   a look at it."

msgctxt "scene:2:192"
msgid ""
"Ja, ja, natürlich wollten\n"
"Sie ihn nicht stehlen.\n"
"Sagen Sie mal, für wie\n"
"dumm halten Sie mich\n"
"eigentlich? Also raus\n"
"mit der Sprache, was\n"
"wollten Sie mit dem Hut\n"
"anstellen?"
msgstr ""
"Sure, of course\n"
"you did not intend to\n"
"steal it. Tell me, how\n"
"foolish do you take\n"
"me for anyway? So out\n"
"with it, what were you\n"
"going to do with the\n"
"hat?"

msgctxt "scene:2:200"
msgid ""
"Wessen Hut sollte es\n"
"denn sonst sein, wenn\n"
"Sie ihn aus MEINEM\n"
"Schrank genommen ha-\n"
"ben. Was wollten Sie\n"
"überhaupt mit dem Hut\n"
"anfangen?"
msgstr ""
"Whose hat else should\n"
"it be, if you took it\n"
"from MY wardrobe.\n"
"What were you going\n"
"to do with the hat\n"
"anyway?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:207"
msgid ""
"So, Sie finden meinen\n"
"Hut schön. Freut mich.\n"
"Aber woher wussten Sie,\n"
"dass ich den Hut über-\n"
"haupt besitze. Ich habe\n"
"ihn noch gar nicht ge-\n"
"tragen."
msgstr ""
"So, you think my hat\n"
"is fine. Glad to hear it.\n"
"But how did you know\n"
"that I even owned the\n"
"hat. I have not worn\n"
"it even once.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:214"
msgid ""
"Also hören Sie auf\n"
"mir Märchen zu er-\n"
"zählen, und sagen Sie\n"
"frei heraus, wofür\n"
"Sie den Hut gebrau-\n"
"chen wollten?"
msgstr ""
"So stop telling me\n"
"fairy tales, and speak\n"
"right up-what did you\n"
"want to use the hat\n"
"for?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:220"
msgid ""
"1. Ich trage gerne so\n"
"   grosse Hüte."
msgstr ""
"1. I like to wear such\n"
"   grand hats."

msgctxt "scene:2:222"
msgid ""
"2. Ich brauche den Hut,\n"
"   um damit einen Tramp\n"
"   hinters Licht zu\n"
"   führen."
msgstr ""
"2. I need the hat to\n"
"   fool a tramp with it.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:226"
msgid ""
"3. Ich suchte ein Prä-\n"
"   sent für eine Dame."
msgstr ""
"3. I was looking for a\n"
"   present for a lady."

msgctxt "scene:2:228"
msgid "Wie bitte?"
msgstr "Pardon?"

msgctxt "scene:2:229"
msgid ""
"So, so, das müssen\n"
"Sie mir aber näher\n"
"erklären!"
msgstr ""
"Is that so? Explain\n"
"that to me in\n"
"more detail!"

msgctxt "scene:2:232"
msgid ""
"Und dafür haben Sie\n"
"sich ausgerechnet\n"
"meinen Hut ausge-\n"
"sucht. So etwas\n"
"ist Diebstahl!"
msgstr ""
"And for that you chose\n"
"my hat, of all things.\n"
"That sort of thing is\n"
"outright theft!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:237"
msgid ""
"Und überhaupt, was\n"
"machen Sie eigentlich\n"
"mit meinem Hut?"
msgstr ""
"And anyway, what\n"
"are you actually\n"
"doing with my hat?"

msgctxt "scene:2:240"
msgid ""
"1. Ich brauche den Hut,\n"
"   um ein Verbrechen zu\n"
"   verhindern!"
msgstr ""
"1. I need the hat to\n"
"   prevent a crime!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:243"
msgid ""
"2. Geben Sie mir gefäl-\n"
"   ligst den Hut. Ich\n"
"   bringe ihn ja bald\n"
"   zurück!"
msgstr ""
"2. Hand over the hat at\n"
"   once. I shall bring it\n"
"   back soon enough!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:247"
msgid ""
"Ist ja interessant.\n"
"Erklären Sie das mal\n"
"ein bisschen genauer!"
msgstr ""
"How interesting.\n"
"Explain that in a bit\n"
"more detail!"

msgctxt "scene:2:250"
msgid ""
"Was ist denn das\n"
"für ein Ton?\n"
"Sie Rüpel,\n"
"Sie unflätiger!"
msgstr ""
"What sort of tone is\n"
"that? You ruffian,\n"
"you foul-mouthed\n"
"rascal!"

msgctxt "scene:2:254"
msgid ""
"1. Mit dem Hut kann\n"
"   sich mein Freund\n"
"   tarnen."
msgstr ""
"1. With the hat my\n"
"   friend can disguise\n"
"   himself."

msgctxt "scene:2:257"
msgid ""
"2. Der Tramp darf\n"
"   meinen Partner\n"
"   nicht erkennen,\n"
"   sonst ist unser\n"
"   Plan durchschaut."
msgstr ""
"2. The tramp must\n"
"   not recognize\n"
"   my partner,\n"
"   otherwise our\n"
"   plan will be blown."

msgctxt "scene:2:262"
msgid ""
"Mir scheint, es ist zum\n"
"Wohle aller Fahrgäste,\n"
"wenn diese finsteren\n"
"Gesellen im Zaume ge-\n"
"halten werden.\n"
"Ausserdem, so einfach\n"
"können Sie das Schiff\n"
"ja nicht verlassen."
msgstr ""
"It seems to me, it is\n"
"for the good of all\n"
"passengers, if these\n"
"sinister fellows are\n"
"kept in check. Besides,\n"
"you cannot leave the\n"
"ship so easily.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:270"
msgid ""
"Dann nehmen Sie eben\n"
"den Hut. Aber wehe,\n"
"Sie bringen ihn nicht\n"
"unversehrt zurück."
msgstr ""
"Then take the hat.\n"
"But God help you\n"
"if you don't bring\n"
"it back in one piece."

msgctxt "scene:2:274"
msgid ""
"Danke, Sie haben mir\n"
"sehr geholfen."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, you have\n"
"helped me a great deal."

msgctxt "scene:2:276"
msgid ""
"So etwas habe ich ja\n"
"noch nie erlebt. Das\n"
"muss ich sofort dem\n"
"Kapitän erzählen."
msgstr ""
"I have never experienced\n"
"anything like this! I must\n"
"tell the captain about\n"
"this immediately."

msgctxt "scene:2:280"
msgid ""
"Hilfe, Hilfe! Ich werde\n"
"bestohlen! Zu Hilfe!"
msgstr ""
"Help, help! I am\n"
"being robbed!"

msgctxt "scene:2:282"
msgid ""
"Der Mann da ist in\n"
"meine Kabine einge-\n"
"drungen und wollte\n"
"mich bestehlen."
msgstr ""
"The man there broke\n"
"into my cabin and\n"
"tried to rob me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:286"
msgid ""
"Mr. Firehand?! Das\n"
"hätte ich nun wirk-\n"
"lich nicht von Ihnen\n"
"erwartet. Es tut mir\n"
"leid, aber ich muss\n"
"sie bis zum Ende der\n"
"Fahrt unter Arrest\n"
"stellen."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Firehand?!\n"
"I really would not\n"
"have expected that\n"
"of you. I am sorry,\n"
"but I must place\n"
"you under arrest\n"
"until the end\n"
"of the voyage."

msgctxt "scene:2:294"
msgid ""
"Ich verlange, dass Sie\n"
"den Kerl einsperren."
msgstr ""
"I demand that you\n"
"lock the fellow up."

msgctxt "scene:2:296"
msgid ""
"Habe ich es doch\n"
"gewusst! Der war mir\n"
"immer schon verdäch-\n"
"tig! Aber die Tramps\n"
"schlecht machen!"
msgstr ""
"I knew it! That one\n"
"always seemed\n"
"suspicious to me!\n"
"Yet he runs down the\n"
"tramps!"

msgctxt "scene:2:301"
msgid ""
"Captain! Wollen Sie\n"
"der Sache nicht auf\n"
"den Grund gehen,\n"
"bevor Sie über mich\n"
"urteilen?"
msgstr ""
"Captain! Will you\n"
"not get to the\n"
"bottom of this\n"
"before you judge\n"
"me?"

msgctxt "scene:2:306"
msgid ""
"Sobald wir an unserem\n"
"Ziel angekommen sind,\n"
"können wir die Sache\n"
"dann klären."
msgstr ""
"As soon as we reach\n"
"our destination, we can\n"
"settle the matter then.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:2:310"
msgid ""
"Aber momentan bleibt\n"
"mir nichts anderes\n"
"übrig, als Sie unter\n"
"Arrest zu stellen."
msgstr ""
"But for the moment I\n"
"have no choice but\n"
"to place you under\n"
"arrest."

msgctxt "scene:2:314"
msgid ""
"Wundert mich, dass\n"
"dieser Schrank be-\n"
"nutzt wird, die\n"
"eine Tür ist total\n"
"verklemmt."
msgstr ""
"It surprises me that\n"
"this wardrobe is\n"
"in use, the one\n"
"door is completely\n"
"jammed."

msgctxt "scene:2:319"
msgid ""
"Wundert mich, dass\n"
"dieser Schrank be-\n"
"nutzt wird, die\n"
"eine Tür ist total\n"
"verklemmt."
msgstr ""
"It surprises me that\n"
"this wardrobe is\n"
"in use, the one\n"
"door is completely\n"
"jammed."

msgctxt "scene:2:324"
msgid ""
"Ich mach' die Hutschachtel\n"
"wieder zu."
msgstr ""
"I'll close the hatbox\n"
"back up again."

msgctxt "scene:2:326"
msgid ""
"In der Schublade ist\n"
"nichts mehr drinn'!"
msgstr ""
"There is nothing left\n"
"in the drawer!"

msgctxt "scene:2:328"
msgid ""
"Oha, in der Schublade\n"
"krabbelt ja ein Käfer."
msgstr ""
"Oh, look, a beetle is\n"
"crawling in the drawer!"

msgctxt "scene:2:330"
msgid ""
"Soll ich den wirklich\n"
"mitnehmen?"
msgstr ""
"Should I really\n"
"take it with me?"

msgctxt "scene:2:332"
msgid "Naja, wenn es sein muss..."
msgstr "Well, if it must be..."

msgctxt "scene:3:0"
msgid ""
"Hallo! Ich bin Karl May.\n"
"Nun bin ich zwar schon\n"
"über 80 Jahre tot, aber\n"
"noch immer werden meine\n"
"Abenteuer - Erzählungen\n"
"überall auf der Welt\n"
"gelesen."
msgstr ""
"Hello! I am Karl May.\n"
"Although I died over\n"
"80 years ago, my\n"
"adventures - stories\n"
"are still read all over\n"
"the world.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:3:7"
msgid ""
"Zu meinen Lebzeiten be-\n"
"reiste Old Shatterhand\n"
"den Wilden Westen von\n"
"Nordamerika und Kara\n"
"Ben Nemsi den Orient.\n"
"Die zahlreichen Aben-\n"
"teuer die sie dort er-\n"
"lebten, und die berühm-"
msgstr ""
"During my lifetime, Old\n"
"Shatterhand traveled\n"
"the Wild West of North\n"
"America and Kara Ben \n"
"Nemsi the Orient. The\n"
"numerous adventures\n"
"they experienced there,\n"
"and the famous"

msgctxt "scene:3:15"
msgid ""
"ten und bewundernswer-\n"
"ten Menschen, die sie\n"
"auf den Reisen trafen,\n"
"sind in meinen Erzäh-\n"
"lungen verewigt.\n"
"Eines dieser zahlreichen\n"
"Abenteuer ist 'Der\n"
"Schatz im Silbersee'."
msgstr ""
"and admirable people\n"
"they met on their\n"
"journeys, are\n"
"immortalized in my\n"
"stories. One of\n"
"these many adven-\n"
"tures is 'The Trea-\n"
"sure of Silver Lake'."

msgctxt "scene:3:23"
msgid ""
"Old Firehand, Tante\n"
"Droll, Winnetou und viele\n"
"andere Bekannte, machen\n"
"sich in dieser Erzählung\n"
"auf den Weg, quer durch\n"
"Nordamerika zum sagen-\n"
"umwobenen Silbersee, der\n"
"irgendwo hoch oben in"
msgstr ""
"Old Firehand, Aunt\n"
"Droll, Winnetou, and many\n"
"other acquaintances set\n"
"out in this story,\n"
"crossing North America\n"
"to the legendary\n"
"Silver Lake, said to lie\n"
"hidden and remote"

msgctxt "scene:3:31"
msgid ""
"den Rocky Mountains\n"
"einsam und versteckt\n"
"liegen soll. Doch es\n"
"wird nicht nur eine\n"
"Reise zum Silbersee,\n"
"die unsere Freunde\n"
"unternehmen werden -"
msgstr ""
"somewhere high up in\n"
"the Rocky Mountains.\n"
"Yet it will not be\n"
"merely a journey to\n"
"Silver Lake that our\n"
"friends undertake-\n"
"it will be, rather,"

msgctxt "scene:3:38"
msgid ""
"es wird vielmehr eine\n"
"spannende und gefähr-\n"
"liche Verfolgungsjagd,\n"
"die sie vom Arkansas\n"
"aus, quer durch die\n"
"Prärie und schliess-\n"
"lich in die"
msgstr ""
"a thrilling and perilous\n"
"chase, leading them\n"
"from the Arkansas River,\n"
"across the prairies,\n"
"and finally into the\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:3:45"
msgid ""
"Rocky Mountains führen\n"
"wird.\n"
"Aber was erzähle ich...\n"
"erleben Sie selbst das\n"
"Abenteuer! Viel Glück,\n"
"Old Firehand!"
msgstr ""
"Rocky Mountains.\n"
"But why go on...\n"
"experience the adventure\n"
"for yourself! Good luck,\n"
"Old Firehand!\n"
"­"

