msgstr "LICENSED"

msgctxt "scene:4:9"
msgid "KARL MAY VERLAG"
msgstr "KARL MAY VERLAG"

msgctxt "scene:5:0"
msgid ""
"Freunde! Ihr werdet\n"
"schon gewusst haben,\n"
"warum Ihr den weiten\n"
"Weg hierher auf Euch\n"
"genommen habt. Und\n"
"ich kann Euch sagen:\n"
"Eure Mühen werden\n"
"sich lohnen."
msgstr ""
"Friends! You must have\n"
"already known why you\n"
"took the long journey\n"
"here. And I can tell\n"
"you: Your efforts will\n"
"be well rewarded.\n"
"The treasure awaits\n"
"us all."

msgctxt "scene:5:8"
msgid ""
"Hoffentlich versprichst\n"
"Du uns nicht zuviel,\n"
"Brinkley."
msgstr ""
"I hope you aren't\n"
"promising us too much,\n"
"Brinkley."

msgctxt "scene:5:11"
msgid ""
"Sicher nicht. Ihr\n"
"könnt mir vertrauen!\n"
"Ich versichere Euch,\n"
"dass oben am Silber-\n"
"see genug Schätze\n"
"für jeden von Euch\n"
"liegen."
msgstr ""
"Certainly not.\n"
"You can trust me!\n"
"I assure you that\n"
"up at Silver Lake\n"
"enough treasures\n"
"for each of you\n"
"lie."

msgctxt "scene:5:18"
msgid ""
"Woher willst Du das\n"
"denn wissen, hä? Bei\n"
"den Rafter's wäre es\n"
"beinahe schief ge-\n"
"gangen."
msgstr ""
"How would you know\n"
"that, huh? With the\n"
"Rafter's it almost\n"
"went quite\n"
"wrong."

msgctxt "scene:5:23"
msgid ""
"Diese Karte hier ist\n"
"der Schlüssel zu un-\n"
"serem Erfolg.Auf ihr\n"
"ist der genaue Weg\n"
"zum Schatz beschrie-\n"
"ben, es kann über-\n"
"haupt nichts"
msgstr ""
"This map here is\n"
"the key to our\n"
"success. On it\n"
"the exact path\n"
"to the treasure is\n"
"described, nothing\n"
"at all can"

msgctxt "scene:5:30"
msgid ""
"schiefgehen. Doch be-\n"
"vor wir uns auf den\n"
"Weg in die Berge ma-\n"
"chen können, sollten\n"
"wir Butler's Farm\n"
"einen Besuch abstat-\n"
"ten."
msgstr ""
"go wrong. But be-\n"
"fore we can make\n"
"for the mountains\n"
"we should pay\n"
"Butler's Farm\n"
"a brief visit."

msgctxt "scene:5:37"
msgid ""
"Und was die Rafter's\n"
"anbelangt, so kann man\n"
"doch wohl sagen, dass\n"
"es ein Erfolg war: Wir\n"
"haben das Geld."
msgstr ""
"And as the Rafter's\n"
"are concerned, one\n"
"can well say that\n"
"it was a success: We\n"
"have the money."

msgctxt "scene:5:42"
msgid ""
"Gut, die Rafter's waren\n"
"ein Erfolg, aber warum\n"
"den Butler's einen\n"
"Besuch abstatten?"
msgstr ""
"Fine, the Rafter's were\n"
"a success, but why\n"
"pay the Butler's\n"
"a visit?"

msgctxt "scene:5:46"
msgid ""
"Butler ist ein verdammt\n"
"reicher Mann. Es wäre\n"
"bestimmt nicht Euer\n"
"Schaden, wenn wir ihn\n"
"um sein Geld erleich-\n"
"tern."
msgstr ""
"Butler is a damned\n"
"rich man. It would\n"
"surely not be your\n"
"loss if we eased\n"
"him of his money."

msgctxt "scene:5:52"
msgid ""
"Schliesslich ist es noch\n"
"ein weiter Weg zum Sil-\n"
"bersee. Wir brauchen\n"
"das Geld!"
msgstr ""
"After all, it is still\n"
"a long way to Silver\n"
"Lake. We need\n"
"the money!"

msgctxt "scene:5:56"
msgid ""
"Und Du hast uns hier-\n"
"her bestellt, nur um\n"
"uns das zu sagen?"
msgstr ""
"And you called us\n"
"here just to tell\n"
"us that?"

msgctxt "scene:5:59"
msgid ""
"Nicht nur deshalb,\n"
"ich brauche Eure\n"
"Hilfe. Butler's Farm\n"
"gleicht einer Festung.\n"
"Allein oder zu zweit\n"
"ist es fast"
msgstr ""
"Not only for that,\n"
"I need your\n"
"help. Butler's Farm\n"
"is like a fortress.\n"
"Alone or as a pair\n"
"it is almost"

msgctxt "scene:5:65"
msgid ""
"unmöglich, die Farm\n"
"zu stürmen. Gegen\n"
"uns alle hat Butler\n"
"jedoch keine Chance."
msgstr ""
"impossible to storm\n"
"the farm. Against\n"
"us all, Butler\n"
"has no chance."

msgctxt "scene:5:69"
msgid ""
"Wenn das alles stimmt,\n"
"und für uns genug da-\n"
"bei herausspringt,\n"
"frage ich mich, wo-\n"
"rauf wir noch warten."
msgstr ""
"If all that is true,\n"
"and enough comes\n"
"out of it for us,\n"
"I ask myself what\n"
"we still wait for."

msgctxt "scene:5:74"
msgid ""
"Das sind die Worte\n"
"auf die ich gewartet\n"
"habe. Also, Männer,\n"
"auf zu Butler's Farm!"
msgstr ""
"Those are the words\n"
"I've been waiting\n"
"for. So, men,\n"
"on to Butler's Farm!"

msgctxt "scene:5:78"
msgid "Etwas Später..."
msgstr "A bit later..."

msgctxt "scene:5:79"
msgid ""
"Die Tramps waren hier.\n"
"Sie haben immer noch\n"
"einen Vorsprung."
msgstr ""
"The Tramps were here.\n"
"They still have\n"
"a head start."

msgctxt "scene:5:82"
msgid ""
"Naja, die Gauner haben\n"
"auch Pferde. Wir sind\n"
"nur zu Fuss unterwegs."
msgstr ""
"Well, the crooks have\n"
"horses too. We're\n"
"only going on foot."

msgctxt "scene:5:85"
msgid ""
"Wir müssen uns sehr\n"
"beeilen, um Butler's\n"
"Farm noch rechtzeitig\n"
"zu erreichen. Die\n"
"Tramps werden mit den\n"
"Pferden nicht über"
msgstr ""
"We must hurry a lot\n"
"to reach Butler's\n"
"Farm in time. The\n"
"Tramps will not\n"
"have ridden\n"
"over"

msgctxt "scene:5:91"
msgid ""
"die Berge geritten sein,\n"
"obwohl das eine Abkür-\n"
"zung ist. Vielleicht\n"
"haben wir noch eine\n"
"Chance."
msgstr ""
"the mountains yet,\n"
"although that is a\n"
"shortcut. Maybe\n"
"we still have a\n"
"chance."

msgctxt "scene:6:0"
msgid ""
"Oh,  Mr. Firehand.\n"
"Es ist mir eine Ehre,\n"
"Sie an Bord begrüssen\n"
"zu dürfen!"
msgstr ""
"Oh, Mr. Firehand.\n"
"It is an honor\n"
"to welcome you\n"
"on board!"

msgctxt "scene:6:4"
msgid ""
"Freut mich, Kapitän,\n"
"dass Sie meiner\n"
"Person soviel Bedeu-\n"
"tung beimessen."
msgstr ""
"Flattered, Captain,\n"
"that you put so\n"
"much stock in me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:8"
msgid ""
"Na ja, man trifft\n"
"ja nicht alle Tage\n"
"einen so berühmten\n"
"Westmann wie Sie,\n"
"Mr. Firehand. Ihr\n"
"Ruf eilt Ihnen weit\n"
"voraus. Ihre Anwe-\n"
"senheit wird sich"
msgstr ""
"Well, one doesn't\n"
"meet such a famous\n"
"Westman as you\n"
"every day, Mr.\n"
"Firehand. Your\n"
"reputation precedes\n"
"you by far. Word of\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:16"
msgid ""
"sicher schnell an\n"
"Bord herumsprechen.\n"
"Hoffen wir, dass Ihr\n"
"Name auch das Gesin-\n"
"del beeindruckt."
msgstr ""
"your presence will\n"
"surely spread fast\n"
"across the deck. Let\n"
"us hope your name\n"
"impresses the scoundrels."

msgctxt "scene:6:21"
msgid ""
"Gesindel? Ist das\n"
"ein Problem für Sie?"
msgstr ""
"Scoundrels? Is that\n"
"a problem for you?"

msgctxt "scene:6:23"
msgid ""
"Da fragen Sie noch !\n"
"Haben Sie sie denn\n"
"noch nicht gesehen -\n"
"die drei Tramps, die\n"
"auf meinem Schiff\n"
"herumlungern und die\n"
"Passagiere in Furcht\n"
"versetzen ?"
msgstr ""
"You still have to ask?!\n"
"Have you not seen\n"
"them yet-the three\n"
"tramps loitering on my\n"
"ship and putting the\n"
"passengers in fear?\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:31"
msgid ""
"Nein, nein, den dreien\n"
"bin ich noch nicht\n"
"begegnet. Ich bin ja\n"
"auch gerade erst an\n"
"Bord gekommen."
msgstr ""
"No, no, I have not met\n"
"those three yet. After\n"
"all, I have only just\n"
"come aboard.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:36"
msgid ""
"Würde mich interessie-\n"
"ren, was in der Kiste\n"
"ist, vielleicht gibt\n"
"es für mich etwas zu\n"
"holen."
msgstr ""
"I wonder what is inside\n"
"that crate; perhaps\n"
"there is something in it\n"
"for me to take.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:41"
msgid "Holla ho!"
msgstr "Holler ho!"

msgctxt "scene:6:42"
msgid ""
"Oh, was ist denn\n"
"das? Ich glaube,\n"
"der leiste ich\n"
"mal ein bisschen\n"
"Gesellschaft..."
msgstr ""
"Oh, what is this?\n"
"I think I will\n"
"keep her company\n"
"for a little bit...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:47"
msgid "Ugh!"
msgstr "Ugh!"

msgctxt "scene:6:48"
msgid "Splash!"
msgstr "Splash!"

msgctxt "scene:6:49"
msgid ""
"Oh,oh! Die haben mir\n"
"ganz schön eins über-\n"
"gebraten!"
msgstr ""
"Oh, oh! They really\n"
"gave me quite a\n"
"walloping!"

msgctxt "scene:6:52"
msgid ""
"Ich wurde bestohlen!\n"
"Ich wurde bestohlen!\n"
"Ein Gauner hat mein\n"
"Messer gestohlen!\n"
"Bitte, Mr. Firehand,\n"
"helfen Sie mir!"
msgstr ""
"I've been robbed!\n"
"I've been robbed!\n"
"A rogue stole my\n"
"knife!\n"
"Please, Mr. Firehand,\n"
"help me!"

msgctxt "scene:6:58"
msgid ""
"Bitte finden Sie\n"
"mein Messer! Sonst\n"
"bin ich ein armer\n"
"Mann!"
msgstr ""
"Please find my\n"
"knife! Otherwise\n"
"I am a poor\n"
"man!"

msgctxt "scene:6:62"
msgid ""
"Ich werde sehen, was\n"
"sich machen lässt!\n"
"Beruhigen Sie sich\n"
"inzwischen, und gehen\n"
"Sie zurück auf ihre\n"
"Kabine!"
msgstr ""
"I will see what\n"
"can be done!\n"
"Calm yourself in\n"
"the meantime, and go\n"
"back to your\n"
"cabin!"

msgctxt "scene:6:68"
msgid ""
"Ich sage ihnen dann\n"
"Bescheid, sobald ich\n"
"etwas herausgefunden\n"
"habe."
msgstr ""
"I will let you\n"
"know as soon as I\n"
"have found out\n"
"something."

msgctxt "scene:6:72"
msgid ""
"Mr. Firehand!\n"
"Kommen Sie mal hier\n"
"rüber."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Firehand!\n"
"Come over here\n"
"a moment."

msgctxt "scene:6:75"
msgid ""
"Oh, oh, näher komm ich auf\n"
"keinen Fall an den Panther\n"
"heran, ohne dass er mich,\n"
"oder das Mädchen anfällt."
msgstr ""
"Oh, oh, I can't get\n"
"any closer to the panther\n"
"without it attacking me\n"
"or the girl."

msgctxt "scene:6:79"
msgid ""
"Hier wäre eine gute\n"
"Deckung, aber leider\n"
"kann ich den Panther von\n"
"hier aus nicht erreichen !"
msgstr ""
"Here would be good\n"
"cover, but unfortunately\n"
"I can't reach the panther\n"
"from here!"

msgctxt "scene:6:83"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das Holz auf den\n"
"Panther werfe, zerreisst\n"
"er mich, noch bevor ich\n"
"eine Deckung gefunden\n"
"habe !"
msgstr ""
"If I throw the wood at the\n"
"panther, it will tear me to\n"
"pieces before I can even\n"
"find cover!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:88"
msgid ""
"Ahoi, ist es erlaubt\n"
"an Bord zu kommen,\n"
"Mr. Firehand ?"
msgstr ""
"Ahoy, is it permitted\n"
"to come aboard,\n"
"Mr. Firehand?"

msgctxt "scene:6:91"
msgid ""
"1. Haha, die Tante\n"
"   Droll! Seien Sie\n"
"   mir gegrüsst."
msgstr ""
"1. Haha, Auntie Droll!\n"
"   Greetings to you!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:94"
msgid ""
"2. Ja, ja, an Bord\n"
"   ist wohl noch ein\n"
"   Plätzchen frei."
msgstr ""
"2. Yes, yes, there is\n"
"   surely a little spot\n"
"   left on board."

msgctxt "scene:6:97"
msgid ""
"Was für ein Zufall,\n"
"Sie hier zu treffen,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."
msgstr ""
"What a coincidence,\n"
"meeting you here,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."

msgctxt "scene:6:100"
msgid ""
"Dann bleib ich wohl\n"
"am besten ein Weilchen\n"
"hier."
msgstr ""
"Then I suppose it's best\n"
"if I stay here for a little\n"
"while."

msgctxt "scene:6:103"
msgid ""
"Darf ich fragen, was\n"
"Euch auf diesen\n"
"klapprigen Kahn führt ?"
msgstr ""
"May I ask what\n"
"brings you onto this\n"
"rickety tub?"

msgctxt "scene:6:106"
msgid ""
"1. Der Kahn bringt mich\n"
"   über die erste Etap-\n"
"   pe meiner Reise. Ich\n"
"   muss in die Berge."
msgstr ""
"1. The tub is taking me\n"
"   through the first leg\n"
"   of my journey. I head\n"
"   into the mountains."

msgctxt "scene:6:110"
msgid ""
"2. Ich will rauf zum\n"
"   Silbersee. Die Silber-\n"
"   minen dort oben\n"
"   interessieren mich."
msgstr ""
"2. I want to go up to\n"
"   Silver Lake. The silver\n"
"   mines up there\n"
"   interest me."

msgctxt "scene:6:114"
msgid ""
"Aha, in die Berge.\n"
"Darf ich fragen, was\n"
"Sie dort oben suchen,\n"
"wenn nicht Indianer ?"
msgstr ""
"Aha, into the mountains.\n"
"May I ask what\n"
"you are looking for up\n"
"there, if not Indians?"

msgctxt "scene:6:118"
msgid ""
"Am Silbersee soll es\n"
"ein paar Silberminen\n"
"geben. Für die\n"
"interessiere ich mich."
msgstr ""
"There are said to be\n"
"a few silver mines\n"
"at Silver Lake. I am\n"
"interested in those."

msgctxt "scene:6:122"
msgid ""
"Klingt ja interessant!\n"
"Aber erzählen Sie\n"
"besser nicht zu laut\n"
"darüber - nicht nur\n"
"Wände haben Ohren,\n"
"wenn Sie verstehen\n"
"was ich meine."
msgstr ""
"Sounds interesting!\n"
"But better not talk\n"
"too loudly about it -\n"
"it's not just walls\n"
"that have ears, if you\n"
"understand what\n"
"I mean."

msgctxt "scene:6:129"
msgid ""
"So, so - Silberminen.\n"
"Und glauben Sie, dass\n"
"darin noch etwas zu\n"
"finden ist?"
msgstr ""
"Well, well - silver mines.\n"
"And do you believe that\n"
"there is still something to\n"
"be found in them?"

msgctxt "scene:6:133"
msgid ""
"1. Natürlich, sonst\n"
"   würde ich die Reise\n"
"   kaum machen."
msgstr ""
"1. Of course, otherwise\n"
"   I would hardly make\n"
"   the trip."

msgctxt "scene:6:136"
msgid ""
"2. Nein, aber vielleicht\n"
"   habe ich ja Glück."
msgstr ""
"2. No, but perhaps\n"
"   I'll be lucky."

msgctxt "scene:6:138"
msgid "Ja dann, viel Glück!"
msgstr "Well then, good luck!"

msgctxt "scene:6:139"
msgid ""
"Respekt, Respekt -\n"
"Soviel Optimismus\n"
"wünschte ich mir auch!"
msgstr ""
"Respect, respect -\n"
"I wish I had so\n"
"much optimism too!"

msgctxt "scene:6:142"
msgid ""
"Wie kann ich Ihnen nur\n"
"danken? Wären Sie nicht\n"
"gewesen ... nicht auszu-\n"
"denken, was passiert\n"
"wäre. Meine Tochter\n"
"und ich, stehen für\n"
"immer in Ihrer Schuld."
msgstr ""
"How can I ever thank\n"
"you? If it hadn't been\n"
"for you... unthinkable\n"
"what would have\n"
"happened. My daughter\n"
"and I are forever in\n"
"your debt."

msgctxt "scene:6:149"
msgid ""
"Warum gehen wir drei\n"
"nicht ein Weilchen in\n"
"die Bar? Nach so viel\n"
"Tapferkeit und Glück,\n"
"wird uns ein Drink\n"
"wohl nicht schaden!"
msgstr ""
"Why don't the three of us\n"
"go to the bar for a while?\n"
"After so much bravery\n"
"and luck, a drink surely\n"
"won't do us any harm!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:155"
msgid ""
"He, da! Was soll das?\n"
"Willst Du uns belau-\n"
"schen?"
msgstr ""
"Hey! What is this?\n"
"Listening in on us?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:158"
msgid ""
"1. Ich wollte eigent-\n"
"   lich nur die Aus-\n"
"   sicht geniessen."
msgstr ""
"1. I actually just\n"
"   wanted to enjoy\n"
"   the view."

msgctxt "scene:6:161"
msgid ""
"2. T'schuldigung. Ich\n"
"   wollte nicht\n"
"   stören."
msgstr ""
"2. Sorry. I didn't\n"
"   mean to bother\n"
"   you."

msgctxt "scene:6:164"
msgid ""
"Keinen Schritt\n"
"näher, sonst mache\n"
"ich Dir Beine!"
msgstr ""
"Not another step,\n"
"or I'll make you\n"
"run!"

msgctxt "scene:6:167"
msgid ""
"Dann verzieh' Dich\n"
"lieber, bevor ich\n"
"runter komme!"
msgstr ""
"Then better clear out\n"
"before I come\n"
"down!"

msgctxt "scene:6:170"
msgid ""
"Der war nicht besonders\n"
"freundlich. Und 3 gegen\n"
"einen, ist ein schlechtes\n"
"Verhältnis!"
msgstr ""
"He wasn't particularly\n"
"friendly. And 3 to\n"
"1 is bad odds!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:174"
msgid ""
"Da sollte ich besser\n"
"nicht näher ran, sonst\n"
"sehen die mich."
msgstr ""
"Better not get any\n"
"closer, or they'll\n"
"see me."

msgctxt "scene:6:177"
msgid ""
"Und was schlägst Du\n"
"als nächstes vor?"
msgstr ""
"And what do you\n"
"suggest we do next?"

msgctxt "scene:6:179"
msgid ""
"Ich würde ja zu gerne\n"
"wissen, was es mit\n"
"dem Messer von diesem\n"
"Patterson auf sich hat."
msgstr ""
"I'd love to know\n"
"what's the deal\n"
"with this Patterson's\n"
"knife."

msgctxt "scene:6:183"
msgid ""
"Aber dieser Firehand\n"
"hat doch das Messer\n"
"jetzt. Wie sollen wir\n"
"es dem denn abnehmen.\n"
"Der Mann ist doch ge-\n"
"rissen wie ein Fuchs."
msgstr ""
"But this Firehand\n"
"has the knife now.\n"
"How are we supposed\n"
"to take it from him?\n"
"The man is as sly\n"
"as a fox."

msgctxt "scene:6:189"
msgid ""
"Mach Dir darüber keine\n"
"Sorgen. Bis jetzt habe\n"
"ich noch immer bekom-\n"
"men, was ich haben\n"
"wollte."
msgstr ""
"Don't worry about\n"
"that. Up until now,\n"
"I've always gotten\n"
"what I wanted.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:194"
msgid ""
"Na ja, der Ingenieur\n"
"wird uns wohl keine\n"
"Schwierigkeiten machen."
msgstr ""
"Well, the engineer\n"
"won't give us any\n"
"trouble, I suppose."

msgctxt "scene:6:197"
msgid ""
"Stimmt. Wir werden uns\n"
"später um ihn kümmern.\n"
"Dann sehen wir ja,\n"
"warum er so sehr auf\n"
"sein Messerchen auf-\n"
"passt."
msgstr ""
"True. We'll deal\n"
"with him later.\n"
"Then we'll see why\n"
"he takes such good\n"
"care of his little\n"
"knife."

msgctxt "scene:6:203"
msgid ""
"Und was ist, wenn wir\n"
"das Messer haben. Hier\n"
"auf dem Dampfer wird\n"
"man uns doch sofort\n"
"finden, oder?"
msgstr ""
"And what if we get\n"
"the knife? Here on\n"
"the steamboat, they'll\n"
"find us right away,\n"
"won't they?"

msgctxt "scene:6:208"
msgid ""
"Ich hab da schon einen\n"
"Plan, wie wir uns aus\n"
"dem Staube machen\n"
"können. Du wirst schon\n"
"sehen!"
msgstr ""
"I already have a plan\n"
"for how we can make\n"
"off. You'll see!\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:213"
msgid ""
"Ich hoffe, dass wir\n"
"nachher auch schnell\n"
"vom Schiff runter-\n"
"kommen. Ist es dann\n"
"noch weit bis zu\n"
"den Rafters?"
msgstr ""
"I hope we can get off\n"
"the ship quickly\n"
"afterwards. Is it\n"
"still far to the\n"
"Rafters then?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:219"
msgid ""
"Ach ja, die Rafters!\n"
"Hatte ich schon fast\n"
"vergessen. Na ja, denen\n"
"wollen wir später noch\n"
"einen Besuch abstatten."
msgstr ""
"Oh right, the Rafters!\n"
"I'd almost forgotten.\n"
"Well, we'll pay them\n"
"a visit later on.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:224"
msgid ""
"Ein guter Bekannter\n"
"hat mir erzählt, die\n"
"Rafters hätten einiges\n"
"an Geld bei sich.\n"
"Das wird uns sicher-\n"
"lich nützen, wenn wir\n"
"zum Silbersee hoch\n"
"wollen."
msgstr ""
"A good friend told me\n"
"the Rafters are carrying\n"
"a lot of cash.\n"
"That'll definitely help\n"
"us if we want to head\n"
"up to Silver Lake.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:232"
msgid ""
"Wird das Geld der\n"
"Rafters denn reichen,\n"
"um genügend Männer für\n"
"die Reise zum Silber-\n"
"see zu bezahlen?"
msgstr ""
"Will the Rafters'\n"
"money be enough\n"
"to pay for enough\n"
"men for the trip\n"
"to Silver Lake?"

msgctxt "scene:6:237"
msgid ""
"Wahrscheinlich nicht,\n"
"aber bis zum Silbersee\n"
"ist es ja noch ein\n"
"weiter Weg. Wir werden\n"
"bestimmt noch einige\n"
"Schnippchen schlagen\n"
"können, haha!"
msgstr ""
"Probably not,\n"
"but it's still a\n"
"long way to Silver\n"
"Lake. I'm sure we'll\n"
"be able to pull a few\n"
"more tricks, haha!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:244"
msgid ""
"Erst mal sind ja die\n"
"Rafters d'ran. Hast\n"
"Du schon einen Plan,\n"
"wie wir sie am besten\n"
"überfallen."
msgstr ""
"First off, it's the\n"
"Rafters' turn. Got a\n"
"plan yet for how best\n"
"to ambush them?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:249"
msgid ""
"Mir wurde gesagt,\n"
"dass die Rafters am\n"
"Ufer des Black Bear\n"
"Flusses lagern. Es\n"
"wird leicht sein, sie\n"
"bei Nacht zu über-\n"
"fallen, und sie um ihr\n"
"Geld zu erleichtern."
msgstr ""
"I was told that\n"
"the Rafters are camped\n"
"on the banks of the\n"
"Black Bear River.\n"
"It'll be easy to\n"
"ambush them at night\n"
"and relieve them\n"
"of their money."

msgctxt "scene:6:257"
msgid ""
"Ausserdem werden uns\n"
"noch ein paar Tramps\n"
"zur Hilfe kommen, die\n"
"wir treffen, sobald\n"
"wir vom Schiff runter\n"
"sind."
msgstr ""
"Plus, a few tramps will\n"
"be helping us out,\n"
"whom we'll meet as\n"
"soon as we're off\n"
"the ship.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:263"
msgid ""
"Ah, da sind Sie ja,\n"
"Firehand! Hands up!"
msgstr ""
"Ah, there you are,\n"
"Firehand! Hands up!"

msgctxt "scene:6:265"
msgid ""
"So, Kerl! Jetzt rück'\n"
"ganz schnell das Messer\n"
"raus!"
msgstr ""
"So, fellow! Now hand\n"
"over the knife right\n"
"now!"

msgctxt "scene:6:268"
msgid ""
"1. Well,welches Mes-\n"
"   ser? Ich habe\n"
"   kein Messer!"
msgstr ""
"1. Well, what knife?\n"
"   I don't have\n"
"   a knife!"

msgctxt "scene:6:271"
msgid ""
"2. Ich werde Ihnen das\n"
"   Bowiemesser nicht\n"
"   geben"
msgstr ""
"2. I will not give\n"
"   you the Bowie\n"
"   knife"

msgctxt "scene:6:274"
msgid ""
"3. Was? Ja... hier...\n"
"   bitte schön!"
msgstr ""
"3. What? Yes... here...\n"
"   there you go!"

msgctxt "scene:6:276"
msgid ""
"Ein Westmann willst\n"
"Du sein? Ich würde\n"
"sagen, eher eine\n"
"Memme!"
msgstr ""
"You claim to be a\n"
"westerner? I'd say\n"
"more like a coward!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:280"
msgid "Man muss..."
msgstr "One ought to..."

msgctxt "scene:6:281"
msgid ""
"Mit besten Empfeh-\n"
"lungen von mir..."
msgstr ""
"With best regards\n"
"from me..."

msgctxt "scene:6:283"
msgid ""
"Was? Du willst nicht,\n"
"verdammter Dutchman?\n"
"Mit Dir werde ich\n"
"nicht viel Federlesen\n"
"machen! Ich weiss\n"
"genau, dass Du das\n"
"Messer hast!"
msgstr ""
"What? You won't,\n"
"you damned Dutchman?\n"
"I won't mince words\n"
"with you! I know\n"
"for sure that you\n"
"have the knife!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:290"
msgid ""
"Ja, wir wissen das\n"
"aus zuverlässiger\n"
"Quelle."
msgstr ""
"Yes, we know that\n"
"from a reliable\n"
"source."

msgctxt "scene:6:293"
msgid ""
"Mir scheint, Eure\n"
"Quelle ist nicht so\n"
"zuverlässig, wie Ihr\n"
"glaubt!"
msgstr ""
"It seems to me your\n"
"source isn't as\n"
"reliable as you\n"
"think!"

msgctxt "scene:6:297"
msgid ""
"Willst Du mich nicht\n"
"hören? Ich verstehe\n"
"keinen Spass!"
msgstr ""
"Don't you want to\n"
"listen to me? I don't\n"
"take jokes!"

msgctxt "scene:6:300"
msgid ""
"Wir sollten ihn wohl\n"
"mit UNSEREN Bowie-\n"
"messern etwas kitzeln.\n"
"Vielleicht hilft das!"
msgstr ""
"We should probably\n"
"tickle him with OUR\n"
"Bowie knives.\n"
"Maybe that'll help!"

msgctxt "scene:6:304"
msgid ""
"Ich bezweifle, dass\n"
"Dir dies gelingen\n"
"wird Bursche,\n"
"denn..."
msgstr ""
"I doubt you will\n"
"succeed in that,\n"
"my lad, because...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:308"
msgid ""
"Mit besten Empfeh-\n"
"lungen von mir..."
msgstr ""
"With best regards\n"
"from me..."

msgctxt "scene:6:310"
msgid ""
"Was habt Ihr vor-\n"
"hin mit dem alten\n"
"Geldsack in der\n"
"Bar bequatscht?\n"
"Los, raus mit der\n"
"Sprache!"
msgstr ""
"What were you\n"
"blabbering about\n"
"with that old\n"
"moneybag in the bar\n"
"earlier?\n"
"Come on, spill it!"

msgctxt "scene:6:316"
msgid ""
"1. Ich weiss gar nicht,\n"
"   was Sie meinen!"
msgstr ""
"1. I have no idea\n"
"   what you mean!"

msgctxt "scene:6:318"
msgid ""
"2. Ich kann mir nicht\n"
"   vorstellen, dass\n"
"   Sie das etwas an-\n"
"   geht!"
msgstr ""
"2. I can't imagine\n"
"   that to be any\n"
"   of your business!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:322"
msgid ""
"Ganz schön frech, wenn\n"
"man bedenkt, dass ich\n"
"am Drücker bin."
msgstr ""
"Pretty cheeky, considering\n"
"I'm the one calling\n"
"the shots."

msgctxt "scene:6:325"
msgid ""
"Ich könnt ihn einer\n"
"kleinen Sonderbehand-\n"
"lung unterziehen,\n"
"Cornel!"
msgstr ""
"I could give him\n"
"a little special\n"
"treatment, Cornel!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:329"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir kaum\n"
"vorstellen, dass\n"
"einer wie Du einen\n"
"echten Westmann zu\n"
"irgendetwas über-\n"
"reden könnte."
msgstr ""
"I can hardly imagine\n"
"that someone like you\n"
"could convince a\n"
"real westerner of\n"
"anything.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:335"
msgid ""
"Mal sehen, was der\n"
"Kerl in seinen\n"
"Taschen hat..."
msgstr ""
"Let's see what the\n"
"fellow has in\n"
"his pockets..."

msgctxt "scene:6:338"
msgid ""
"Aus dem ist ja\n"
"sowieso nichts\n"
"herauszuholen!\n"
"Lass uns sehen,\n"
"ob er etwas\n"
"bei sich hat!"
msgstr ""
"There's nothing to\n"
"get out of him\n"
"anyway!\n"
"Let's see if he's\n"
"got anything on him!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:344"
msgid ""
"Ah! Da haben wir ja\n"
"das Messer!"
msgstr ""
"Ah! There we have\n"
"the knife!"

msgctxt "scene:6:346"
msgid ""
"Verdammt, der Kerl hat\n"
"das Messer nicht mehr\n"
"bei sich!"
msgstr ""
"Dammit, the fellow\n"
"doesn't have the\n"
"knife on him anymore!"

msgctxt "scene:6:349"
msgid ""
"Aber das finden wir\n"
"schon noch!"
msgstr ""
"But we'll find it yet!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:351"
msgid ""
"Verdammt, der Kerl hat\n"
"überhaupt nichts von\n"
"Wert bei sich!"
msgstr ""
"Dammit, the fellow\n"
"has nothing of\n"
"value on him!"

msgctxt "scene:6:354"
msgid ""
"Oh, oh - mit dem ist nicht\n"
"zu spassen."
msgstr ""
"Oh, oh - he's not to\n"
"be trifled with."

msgctxt "scene:6:356"
msgid ""
"Mein Gott, das Mädchen steht\n"
"da, und rührt sich nicht. Nicht\n"
"mehr lange, und der Panther\n"
"stürzt sich auf sie !"
msgstr ""
"My God, the girl is standing\n"
"there and not moving. Not\n"
"much longer, and the panther\n"
"will leap at her!"

msgctxt "scene:6:360"
msgid ""
"Die Kiste ist sehr stabil\n"
"gebaut."
msgstr ""
"The chest is built of sturdy\n"
"craftsmanship."

msgctxt "scene:6:362"
msgid ""
"Die Planken sind schon ganz\n"
"blank gescheuert. Wahrschein-\n"
"lich wird hier jeden Tag das\n"
"Deck geschrubbt."
msgstr ""
"The planks are worn bare\n"
"already. In all likelihood,\n"
"the deck is scrubbed here\n"
"every single day."

msgctxt "scene:6:366"
msgid ""
"So wie es aussieht, führt\n"
"die Tür in die Bar."
msgstr ""
"Looks like that door\n"
"leads into the bar."

msgctxt "scene:6:368"
msgid ""
"Die Witterung hat der Farbe\n"
"der Schiffsaufbauten ganz\n"
"schön mitgespielt."
msgstr ""
"The weather has really\n"
"taken a toll on the\n"
"ship's superstructure paint."

msgctxt "scene:6:371"
msgid ""
"Bei dieser Ladung wird sich\n"
"die Fahrt sicher lohnen."
msgstr ""
"With a cargo like this, the trip\n"
"will surely be worth it."

msgctxt "scene:6:373"
msgid ""
"Bei diesen Wolken scheint\n"
"mir, dass schon bald Regen\n"
"angesagt ist."
msgstr ""
"With clouds like these,\n"
"it seems to me that rain\n"
"will be coming soon."

msgctxt "scene:6:376"
msgid ""
"Die Berge verlieren sich\n"
"im Dunst."
msgstr ""
"The mountains fade\n"
"into the mist."

msgctxt "scene:6:378"
msgid ""
"Bei Gelegenheit solltest\n"
"du mal wieder fischen\n"
"gehen."
msgstr ""
"When you get the chance,\n"
"you ought to go fishing\n"
"again."

msgctxt "scene:6:381"
msgid ""
"Die alte Winde ist auch\n"
"schon ganz schön ver-\n"
"rostet."
msgstr ""
"That old winch is pretty\n"
"darn rusty, too.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:6:384"
msgid ""
"Na ja, die Bretter dieses\n"
"alten Kahns scheinen ganz\n"
"schön morsch zu sein."
msgstr ""
"Well, the planks of this\n"
"old tub seem to be\n"
"pretty rotten."

msgctxt "scene:6:387"
msgid ""
"Dem komme ich lieber nicht\n"
"zu nahe !"
msgstr ""
"I'd better not get\n"
"too close to that one!"

msgctxt "scene:6:389"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube kaum, dass der\n"
"Kapitän erbaut ist, wenn ich\n"
"sein Schiff zerlege."
msgstr ""
"I doubt the captain\n"
"would be thrilled if I\n"
"tore his ship apart."

msgctxt "scene:6:392"
msgid ""
"Ich lasse wohl besser die\n"
"Finger von der Ladung."
msgstr ""
"I'd better keep my\n"
"hands off the cargo."

msgctxt "scene:6:394"
msgid ""
"Ich habe jetzt leider\n"
"keine Zeit zum Fischen."
msgstr ""
"Unfortunately, I don't\n"
"have time for fishing."

msgctxt "scene:6:396"
msgid ""
"Das rostige Ding funk-\n"
"tioniert sowieso nicht."
msgstr ""
"That rusty thing doesn't\n"
"work anyway."

msgctxt "scene:6:398"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte wohl zuerst\n"
"das Problem mit dem\n"
"Panther lösen !"
msgstr ""
"I should probably solve\n"
"the panther problem\n"
"first!"

msgctxt "scene:9:0"
msgid ""
"Ich würde ja zu gerne\n"
"wissen, worüber die\n"
"drei sich jetzt unter-\n"
"halten. Der Ingenieur\n"
"sieht nicht so aus,\n"
"als würde er am Hunger-\n"
"tuch nagen."
msgstr ""
"I'd love to know what\n"
"the three of them are\n"
"talking about right now.\n"
"The engineer doesn't look\n"
"like he's starving.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:7"
msgid ""
"Well, wir können uns\n"
"wohl kaum neben sie\n"
"setzen. Ich möchte\n"
"nicht riskieren,\n"
"dass uns einer von\n"
"ihnen erkennt."
msgstr ""
"Well, we can hardly\n"
"pull up a chair next to\n"
"them. I wouldn't want to\n"
"risk any of them\n"
"recognizing us.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:13"
msgid ""
"Na warte erst einmal ab.\n"
"Es wird sich schon\n"
"ein Weg finden, von\n"
"den Herren was zu\n"
"erfahren."
msgstr ""
"Just you wait and see.\n"
"We'll find a way to\n"
"learn something from\n"
"those gentlemen.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:18"
msgid ""
"Na mein Freund,\n"
"was hast Du\n"
"herausgefunden?"
msgstr ""
"Well, my friend,\n"
"what have you\n"
"found out?"

msgctxt "scene:9:21"
msgid ""
"Tut mir leid, Sir.\n"
"Aber der grosse Kerl\n"
"hat mich durchschaut.\n"
"Er hat mir Tinte in\n"
"den Eimer geschüttet."
msgstr ""
"I'm sorry, Sir.\n"
"But the big guy\n"
"saw right through me.\n"
"He poured ink into\n"
"my bucket."

msgctxt "scene:9:26"
msgid ""
"Ja, und? Worüber\n"
"haben sie vorher\n"
"gesprochen? Hä?"
msgstr ""
"Yeah, and? What were\n"
"they talking about\n"
"before that? Huh?"

msgctxt "scene:9:29"
msgid ""
"Ich hab' doch gesagt:\n"
"Der Kerl hat mich\n"
"erwischt, noch bevor\n"
"ich etwas wichtiges\n"
"gehört habe."
msgstr ""
"I told you:\n"
"The guy caught me\n"
"before I could hear\n"
"anything important.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:34"
msgid ""
"Was? So leicht lässt\n"
"Du Dich übertölpeln?\n"
"Hast Du denn sonst\n"
"irgendwas gehört oder\n"
"gesehen?"
msgstr ""
"What? You let yourself\n"
"get fooled that easily?\n"
"Did you hear or see\n"
"anything else at all?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:39"
msgid ""
"Warten Sie ... ja,\n"
"doch, ich habe noch\n"
"durch die Tür gesehen,\n"
"wie der Ingenieur\n"
"sein grosses Bowie-"
msgstr ""
"Wait ... yes,\n"
"come to think of it,\n"
"I did see through the door\n"
"how the engineer had his\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:44"
msgid ""
"messer auf dem Tisch\n"
"liegen hatte. Schon\n"
"komisch, normalerweise\n"
"trägt man so ein Ding\n"
"am Gürtel."
msgstr ""
"big Bowie knife sitting on\n"
"the table. Pretty strange,\n"
"normally you'd wear a thing\n"
"like that on your belt.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:49"
msgid ""
"Das Messer muss ihm\n"
"viel bedeuten, wenn\n"
"er es nicht aus den\n"
"Augen lässt."
msgstr ""
"That knife must mean\n"
"a lot to him if he\n"
"won't let it out of\n"
"his sight."

msgctxt "scene:9:53"
msgid ""
"Na ja, wenigstens\n"
"etwas. Hast Du sonst\n"
"noch etwas über das\n"
"Messer erfahren?"
msgstr ""
"Well, at least that's\n"
"something. Did you learn\n"
"anything else about\n"
"the knife?"

msgctxt "scene:9:57"
msgid ""
"Hm - Ich habe noch\n"
"gesehen, wie der\n"
"Ingenieur dem grossen\n"
"Kerl sein Messer\n"
"gegeben hat. Bestimmt\n"
"soll der d'rauf\n"
"aufpassen."
msgstr ""
"Hm-I did see how the\n"
"engineer gave the knife\n"
"to that big fellow.\n"
"Surely, he shall have\n"
"an eye on it.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:64"
msgid ""
"Der Ingenieur hat\n"
"sein Messer dann\n"
"wieder eingesteckt.\n"
"Mehr weiss ich nicht."
msgstr ""
"The engineer\n"
"pocketed his\n"
"knife again. I do\n"
"not know more."

msgctxt "scene:9:68"
msgid ""
"Ich habe fast jedes\n"
"Wort mitgekriegt. Die\n"
"haben sich aber nur\n"
"über das Wetter und\n"
"über eine Farm unter-\n"
"halten - Butlers Farm."
msgstr ""
"I caught almost every\n"
"word. But they were\n"
"only talking about the\n"
"weather and some farm-\n"
"Butler's Farm.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:74"
msgid "Sonst noch etwas?"
msgstr "Anything else?"

msgctxt "scene:9:75"
msgid ""
"Ach ja, der Ingenieur\n"
"hatte die ganze Zeit\n"
"sein Bowiemesser vor\n"
"sich auf dem Tisch\n"
"liegen. Schien so, als\n"
"ob er immer ein Auge\n"
"d'rauf haben wollte."
msgstr ""
"So the engineer kept\n"
"his knife on the table\n"
"the whole time. Seemed\n"
"like he wanted to keep\n"
"an eye on it.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:82"
msgid ""
"Klingt ja interessant.\n"
"Weisst Du noch etwas\n"
"über das Messer?"
msgstr ""
"Sounds interesting.\n"
"Do you know anything\n"
"else about the knife?"

msgctxt "scene:9:85"
msgid ""
"Der Ingenieur hat\n"
"das Messer dann\n"
"wieder eingesteckt."
msgstr ""
"So the engineer put the\n"
"knife back in his pocket\n"
"afterward."

msgctxt "scene:9:88"
msgid ""
"Sehen Sie mal, wen\n"
"ich hier habe,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."
msgstr ""
"Look who I've got\n"
"here, Mr. Firehand.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:91"
msgid "Well, Cornel Brinkley!"
msgstr "Well, Cornel Brinkley!"

msgctxt "scene:9:92"
msgid ""
"Als ich ihn und seinen\n"
"Kumpanen belauscht habe,\n"
"gab er gerade damit an,\n"
"Mr. Pattersons Messer\n"
"gestohlen zu haben."
msgstr ""
"When I was eavesdropping\n"
"on him and his buddy,\n"
"he was just bragging\n"
"about having stolen\n"
"Mr. Patterson's knife."

msgctxt "scene:9:97"
msgid ""
"Da dachte ich mir:\n"
"Den pack ich! Sein\n"
"Kumpane ist mir aller-\n"
"dings entwischt."
msgstr ""
"So I thought to myself:\n"
"I'll grab him! His\n"
"buddy managed to get\n"
"away from me, though."

msgctxt "scene:9:101"
msgid ""
"1. Geben Sie uns das\n"
"   Messer zurück,\n"
"   Cornel!"
msgstr ""
"1. Give us back the\n"
"   knife, Cornel!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:104"
msgid ""
"2. Durchsuchen Sie\n"
"   ihn, Mr. Droll.\n"
"   Bestimmt trägt er\n"
"   das Messer noch\n"
"   bei sich."
msgstr ""
"2. Search him, Mr. Droll.\n"
"   He's surely still carrying\n"
"   the knife with him.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:109"
msgid ""
"Was soll das Ganze?\n"
"Ich habe kein Messer!\n"
"Einen ehrlichen West-\n"
"mann beleidigt man\n"
"nicht ungestraft!"
msgstr ""
"What's the meaning\n"
"of this? I don't have any\n"
"knife! You don't offend\n"
"an honest Westerner\n"
"without paying for it!"

msgctxt "scene:9:114"
msgid ""
"Pshaw! Ehrlicher\n"
"Westmann!? Dass ich\n"
"nicht lache!"
msgstr ""
"Pshaw! Honest\n"
"Westerner!? Don't\n"
"make me laugh!"

msgctxt "scene:9:117"
msgid ""
"Aber leider hat er\n"
"das Messer wirklich\n"
"nicht! Ich habe ihn\n"
"bereits durchsucht.\n"
"Aber vielleicht ist\n"
"sein Kumpane damit\n"
"entwischt!"
msgstr ""
"But unfortunately\n"
"he really doesn't\n"
"have the knife!\n"
"I've already searched\n"
"him. But maybe his\n"
"buddy got away\n"
"with it!"

msgctxt "scene:9:124"
msgid ""
"Das glaube ich\n"
"weniger, Mr.Droll!\n"
"Der Cornel würde\n"
"keinem seiner\n"
"Begleiter trauen!"
msgstr ""
"I don't think so,\n"
"Mr. Droll!\n"
"The Cornel wouldn't\n"
"trust any of his\n"
"companions!"

msgctxt "scene:9:129"
msgid ""
"Da haben wir wohl\n"
"Pech gehabt!\n"
"Aber trotzdem bring\n"
"ich ihn erst mal zum\n"
"Kapitän. Der soll ihn\n"
"einsperren, bis die\n"
"Sache geklärt ist."
msgstr ""
"We must have run out\n"
"of luck then!\n"
"But I'll still take him\n"
"to the captain first.\n"
"He shall lock him up\n"
"until this matter\n"
"is cleared up."

msgctxt "scene:9:136"
msgid ""
"Wir sinken !\n"
"Wir sinken !"
msgstr ""
"We're sinking!\n"
"We're sinking!"

msgctxt "scene:9:138"
msgid ""
"Im Bunker ist\n"
"ein Leck!"
msgstr ""
"There's a leak\n"
"in the bunker!"

msgctxt "scene:9:140"
msgid ""
"Die Gefahr ist vor-\n"
"erst vorüber Captain,\n"
"aber ich kann nicht\n"
"sagen, wie lange der\n"
"Pflock den Wasser-\n"
"druck aushält."
msgstr ""
"The danger is over for\n"
"now, Captain, but I\n"
"cannot say how long\n"
"the plug will withstand\n"
"the water pressure.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:146"
msgid ""
"Danke, Mr.Firehand,\n"
"vielen Dank, Sie ha-\n"
"ben mein Schiff ge-\n"
"rettet. Mit der pro-\n"
"visorischen Abdichtung,\n"
"komme ich bei halber\n"
"Fahrt sicher bis zum\n"
"nächsten Hafen."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, Mr. Firehand,\n"
"many thanks; you have\n"
"saved my ship. With this\n"
"makeshift seal, I shall\n"
"safely reach the next\n"
"harbor at half speed.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:154"
msgid ""
"Wir müssen aber umge-\n"
"hend die Verfolgung\n"
"der Tramps aufnehmen,\n"
"denn in dem Tumult\n"
"der entstanden ist,"
msgstr ""
"We must, however,\n"
"immediately set out in\n"
"pursuit of the tramps,\n"
"for in the tumult that\n"
"arose,"

msgctxt "scene:9:159"
msgid ""
"als der Heizer in\n"
"Panik herumrannte, sind\n"
"die Tramps samt Cornel\n"
"entkommen."
msgstr ""
"when the stoker ran about\n"
"in panic, the tramps\n"
"escaped together with the\n"
"Cornel."

msgctxt "scene:9:163"
msgid ""
"Ja, denn ich bin mir\n"
"sicher, der Schurke\n"
"hat noch Böses vor.\n"
"Doch bis wir bei der\n"
"nächsten Stadt ange-\n"
"langt sind, ist der\n"
"Cornel bereits über\n"
"alle Berge."
msgstr ""
"Yes, for I am certain the\n"
"scoundrel still intends\n"
"evil. Yet by the time we\n"
"reach the next town, the\n"
"Cornel will already be\n"
"gone.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:171"
msgid ""
"Nein, Mr.Firehand, dass\n"
"müssen Sie nicht, die\n"
"Kerle haben nicht alle\n"
"Kanus mitgenommen.\n"
"Hinten am Schiff habe\n"
"ich noch eines, das ich\n"
"Ihnen gerne zur Verfü-\n"
"gung stelle."
msgstr ""
"No, Mr. Firehand, you\n"
"need not do that; the\n"
"fellows did not take all\n"
"the canoes. At the stern\n"
"of the ship I have one\n"
"more, which I gladly\n"
"place at your disposal.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:179"
msgid ""
"Das ist genau das, was\n"
"wir brauchen um die\n"
"Verfolgung aufnehmen\n"
"zu können."
msgstr ""
"That is precisely what we\n"
"need to be able to set\n"
"out in pursuit.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:183"
msgid ""
"Es wäre mir unangenehm\n"
"mit dem Gedanken zu\n"
"leben, dass der Cornel\n"
"wieder einmal der ge-\n"
"rechten Strafe entgeht."
msgstr ""
"It would be unpleasant to\n"
"live with the thought\n"
"that the Cornel once\n"
"again escapes just\n"
"punishment."

msgctxt "scene:9:188"
msgid ""
"Ja, Mr.Firehand, es\n"
"wäre mir eine Ehre\n"
"und Genugtuung, wenn\n"
"ich Ihnen so helfen\n"
"könnte."
msgstr ""
"Yes, Mr. Firehand, it\n"
"would be an honor and\n"
"satisfaction if I could\n"
"help you in this way.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:193"
msgid ""
"Ich nehme dankend an,\n"
"Captain."
msgstr ""
"I accept with thanks,\n"
"Captain."

msgctxt "scene:9:195"
msgid ""
"Also lassen Sie uns\n"
"keine Zeit mehr ver-\n"
"lieren, Droll. Nehmen\n"
"wir die Verfolgung auf."
msgstr ""
"So let us lose no more\n"
"time, Droll. Let us take\n"
"up the pursuit.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:199"
msgid ""
"Das Schild ist fest-\n"
"geschraubt. Bist wohl\n"
"ein heimlicher Schilder-\n"
"sammler?"
msgstr ""
"The sign is screwed\n"
"tight. Are you a secret\n"
"sign collector then?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:203"
msgid ""
"Das Fenster ist\n"
"verschlossen."
msgstr ""
"The window is locked.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:205"
msgid ""
"Bei den schweren Kisten\n"
"hebe ich mir einen\n"
"Bruch! Lassen wir das\n"
"lieber."
msgstr ""
"With these heavy crates I\n"
"should get a hernia!\n"
"Better leave that be.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:209"
msgid ""
"Dieser Kahn hat schon\n"
"einige Tage hinter\n"
"sich. Die Farbe\n"
"blättert gewaltig ab."
msgstr ""
"This craft has seen\n"
"better days. The paint is\n"
"flaking off terribly.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:213"
msgid ""
"Die Aufbauten im\n"
"Südstaatenstil\n"
"scheinen mir recht\n"
"stabil zu sein."
msgstr ""
"The Southern-style\n"
"superstructure appears\n"
"quite sturdy.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:9:217"
msgid ""
"Hier steht:\n"
"BETRETEN VERBOTEN !"
msgstr ""
"It says: NO\n"
"TRESPASSING !"

msgctxt "scene:9:219"
msgid ""
"Die schwere Eisentür\n"
"ist wohl das einzige,\n"
"was an dem Schiff nicht\n"
"verrotten kann."
msgstr ""
"The heavy iron door\n"
"is probably the only\n"
"thing on the ship\n"
"that cannot rot."

msgctxt "scene:9:223"
msgid ""
"Das Fenster führt\n"
"wohl in den Saloon."
msgstr ""
"The window likely\n"
"leads into the saloon."

msgctxt "scene:9:225"
msgid ""
"Die Fracht ist gut\n"
"vertäut. Da lass ich\n"
"besser die Finger\n"
"davon."
msgstr ""
"The cargo is well\n"
"tied down. I had\n"
"best leave my\n"
"hands off it."

msgctxt "scene:9:229"
msgid ""
"Ich bezweifle, dass\n"
"dies eine positive\n"
"Wirkung hätte."
msgstr ""
"I doubt that this\n"
"would have a\n"
"positive effect."

msgctxt "scene:9:232"
msgid ""
"Der Captain wird mich\n"
"Kielholen lassen, wenn\n"
"ich das Fenster mit\n"
"dem Fass einschmeisse."
msgstr ""
"The captain will have\n"
"me keelhauled if I\n"
"smash the window with\n"
"the barrel."

msgctxt "scene:9:236"
msgid ""
"Das wäre wohl möglich,\n"
"doch ich möchte fremdes\n"
"Eigentum nicht be-\n"
"schädigen."
msgstr ""
"That might well be\n"
"possible, yet I do not\n"
"wish to damage property\n"
"belonging to another."

msgctxt "scene:9:240"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tue, bricht\n"
"die Klinge, oder das Fens-\n"
"ter wird beschädigt."
msgstr ""
"If I do that, the blade\n"
"will break, or the window\n"
"shall be damaged."

msgctxt "scene:9:243"
msgid ""
"Soll ich einschnitzen:\n"
"FIREHAND WAR HIER?"
msgstr ""
"Shall I carve into it:\n"
"FIREHAND WAS HERE?"

msgctxt "scene:10:0"
msgid ""
"Kommen Sie nur her,\n"
"Mr. Firehand. Stellen\n"
"Sie sich zu uns!"
msgstr ""
"Do come closer, Mr.\n"
"Firehand. Stand here\n"
"with us!"

msgctxt "scene:10:3"
msgid ""
"Mr. Droll sagte mir,\n"
"Sie wollen hinauf in\n"
"die Berge. Die Silber-\n"
"minen dort oben wollen\n"
"Sie untersuchen,\n"
"Mr. Firehand?"
msgstr ""
"Mr. Droll told me you\n"
"wish to go up into the\n"
"mountains. You intend\n"
"to inspect the silver\n"
"mines up there, Mr.\n"
"Firehand?"

msgctxt "scene:10:9"
msgid ""
"1. Ja, ich will ab-\n"
"   schätzen, ob sich\n"
"   die Arbeit in den\n"
"   Minen noch lohnt."
msgstr ""
"1. Yes, I want to\n"
"   estimate whether\n"
"   working the mines is\n"
"   still worthwhile."

msgctxt "scene:10:13"
msgid ""
"2. Ja, aber bis dort-\n"
"   hin ist es noch ein\n"
"   langer Weg."
msgstr ""
"2. Yes, but it is\n"
"   still a long way\n"
"   until then."

msgctxt "scene:10:16"
msgid ""
"Meinen Sie denn,\n"
"den Ertrag einer\n"
"alten Mine richtig\n"
"abschätzen zu können?"
msgstr ""
"Do you truly think\n"
"you can properly\n"
"estimate the yield\n"
"of an old mine?"

msgctxt "scene:10:20"
msgid ""
"1. Sonst würde ich\n"
"   bestimmt nicht die\n"
"   lange Reise machen."
msgstr ""
"1. Otherwise I certainly\n"
"   would not undertake the\n"
"   long journey."

msgctxt "scene:10:23"
msgid ""
"2. Ich habe schon viel\n"
"   über Minen gelesen\n"
"   und glaube, den Wert\n"
"   der Silberminen\n"
"   richtig abschätzen\n"
"   zu können."
msgstr ""
"2. I have read a\n"
"   great deal about\n"
"   mines and believe I\n"
"   can correctly\n"
"   assess the value of\n"
"   the silver mines."

msgctxt "scene:10:29"
msgid ""
"Ja, da haben Sie\n"
"natürlich recht.\n"
"Entschuldigen Sie\n"
"meine plumpe Frage."
msgstr ""
"Yes, you are quite\n"
"right, of course.\n"
"Forgive my clumsy\n"
"question."

msgctxt "scene:10:33"
msgid ""
"Nun, da trauen Sie sich\n"
"aber viel zu.\n"
"Sollten Sie einmal Hilfe\n"
"brauchen, stehe ich\n"
"Ihnen gerne zur\n"
"Verfügung. Als Ingenieur\n"
"kenne ich mich mit alten\n"
"Minen gut aus."
msgstr ""
"Well, you certainly have\n"
"great confidence. Should\n"
"you ever require\n"
"assistance, I am gladly\n"
"at your disposal. As an\n"
"engineer, I am well\n"
"acquainted with old\n"
"mines."

msgctxt "scene:10:41"
msgid ""
"Und welchen Weg\n"
"werden Sie einschlagen,\n"
"wenn der Dampfer sein\n"
"Ziel erreicht hat,\n"
"Mr. Firehand?"
msgstr ""
"And which route will\n"
"you take once the\n"
"steamer has reached\n"
"its destination, Mr.\n"
"Firehand?"

msgctxt "scene:10:46"
msgid ""
"1. Der Weg über Land\n"
"   ist noch weit. Ich\n"
"   werde einige\n"
"   Stationen machen."
msgstr ""
"1. The overland\n"
"   route is still far.\n"
"   I shall make a few\n"
"   stops."

msgctxt "scene:10:50"
msgid ""
"2. Ich habe mir noch\n"
"   keine Gedanken über\n"
"   den Weg gemacht."
msgstr ""
"2. I have not yet\n"
"   given any thought to\n"
"   the route."

msgctxt "scene:10:53"
msgid ""
"Und welche Stationen\n"
"sollen das sein?"
msgstr ""
"And which stops\n"
"might those be?"

msgctxt "scene:10:55"
msgid ""
"1. Butlers Farm liegt\n"
"   auf dem Weg."
msgstr ""
"1. Butler's Farm\n"
"   lies along the way."

msgctxt "scene:10:57"
msgid ""
"2. Von Sheridan aus,\n"
"   geht es in die\n"
"   Berge."
msgstr ""
"2. From Sheridan,\n"
"   the route leads\n"
"   into the mountains."

msgctxt "scene:10:60"
msgid ""
"Butlers Farm?! So\n"
"ein Zufall aber auch!\n"
"Dann wollen Sie ja\n"
"zu meinem Schwager,\n"
"und obendrein ist das\n"
"auch mein Ziel."
msgstr ""
"Butler's Farm?! What a\n"
"coincidence! Then you\n"
"intend to go to my\n"
"brother-in-law, and\n"
"moreover that is my\n"
"destination as well."

msgctxt "scene:10:66"
msgid ""
"Ich schlage vor,\n"
"dass wir uns auf\n"
"der Farm treffen.\n"
"Sie werden dort\n"
"jederzeit willkommen\n"
"sein."
msgstr ""
"I propose that\n"
"we meet at the\n"
"farm. You shall\n"
"be welcome\n"
"there at any\n"
"time."

msgctxt "scene:10:72"
msgid ""
"Sheridan. Hab schon\n"
"davon gehört. Dort\n"
"arbeitet der Ingenieur\n"
"Charoy. Er kümmert\n"
"sich um den Bau der\n"
"Eisenbahn. Sie werden\n"
"ihn bestimmt treffen."
msgstr ""
"Sheridan. I have\n"
"heard of it. Engineer\n"
"Charoy works there.\n"
"He oversees the\n"
"railway construction.\n"
"You will surely meet\n"
"him."

msgctxt "scene:10:79"
msgid ""
"So was könnte ich mir\n"
"nicht leisten. Wenn\n"
"ich keine Landkarte\n"
"vor mir habe, komme\n"
"ich sowieso nie ans\n"
"Ziel, haha."
msgstr ""
"I could never afford\n"
"such a thing. Without\n"
"a map before me, I\n"
"should never reach my\n"
"destination anyway,\n"
"haha."

msgctxt "scene:10:85"
msgid ""
"Aber so ein richtiger\n"
"Westmann wie Sie, wird\n"
"damit sicherlich kein\n"
"Problem haben."
msgstr ""
"But a true westerner\n"
"like yourself will\n"
"surely have no trouble\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:10:89"
msgid ""
"He, das ist der Pri-\n"
"vatbereich des Cap-\n"
"tains!"
msgstr ""
"Hey, that is\n"
"the captain's\n"
"private area!"

msgctxt "scene:10:92"
msgid ""
"Es kommt mir schon\n"
"etwas eigenartig vor,\n"
"dass die Fenster ge-\n"
"rade jetzt geputzt\n"
"werden, die sehen\n"
"doch sauber aus."
msgstr ""
"It seems a bit\n"
"peculiar to me\n"
"that the windows\n"
"are being cleaned\n"
"right now; they\n"
"look clean enough."

msgctxt "scene:10:98"
msgid "Was haben Sie vor..."
msgstr "What are you planning..."

msgctxt "scene:10:99"
msgid ""
"Ich werde wohl noch\n"
"meinen wohlverdienten\n"
"Whisky trinken, und\n"
"mich dann etwas nie-\n"
"derlegen."
msgstr ""
"I shall drink my\n"
"well-earned\n"
"whisky and\n"
"lay down for a\n"
"while."

msgctxt "scene:10:104"
msgid ""
"Eigenartige Sitten ha-\n"
"ben die schon an Bord,\n"
"einfach die Fenster zu\n"
"reinigen, wenn sich\n"
"Gäste in der Bar befin-\n"
"den..."
msgstr ""
"Peculiar customs they\n"
"have on board here,\n"
"simply cleaning the\n"
"windows when guests\n"
"happen to be in\n"
"the bar..."

msgctxt "scene:10:110"
msgid ""
"Droll und ich unter-\n"
"halten uns noch ein\n"
"wenig, und dann werde\n"
"ich mich wohl etwas\n"
"in meiner Kajüte hin-\n"
"legen, um auszuruhen."
msgstr ""
"Droll and I shall\n"
"converse a little\n"
"longer, and then I\n"
"shall turn in.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:116"
msgid ""
"Es wäre etwas sehr unhöflich\n"
"die Runde wortlos zu verlassen.\n"
"Die Leute haben mich ja einge-\n"
"laden, und ich kann sie nicht\n"
"vor den Kopf stossen."
msgstr ""
"It would be rather rude to leave\n"
"the company without a word.\n"
"These folks have invited me,\n"
"and I cannot offend them.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:121"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"Droll für eine solche\n"
"Handlung Verständnis\n"
"zeigen würde."
msgstr ""
"I do not think Droll\n"
"would show any\n"
"understanding for\n"
"such an action."

msgctxt "scene:10:125"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mich des Ein-\n"
"druckes nicht erwehren,\n"
"dass Du den Sinn dieses\n"
"Spieles nicht richtig\n"
"erfasst hast."
msgstr ""
"I cannot shake the\n"
"impression that you\n"
"have not quite\n"
"grasped the meaning\n"
"of this game."

msgctxt "scene:10:130"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich den\n"
"Mann schlagen, er hat\n"
"mir ja nichts getan?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I strike\n"
"the man, he has done\n"
"me no harm at all?"

msgctxt "scene:10:133"
msgid ""
"Ich kann Deine Gedanken-\n"
"gänge nicht so recht nach-\n"
"vollziehen. Warum sollte\n"
"ich ihn verletzen oder gar\n"
"töten?"
msgstr ""
"I cannot quite follow\n"
"your train of thought.\n"
"Why should I injure or\n"
"even kill him?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:138"
msgid ""
"He, was glaubst Du\n"
"hier zu tun? Schau,\n"
"dass Du sofort aus\n"
"der Bar verschwindest!"
msgstr ""
"Hey, what do you\n"
"think you are doing\n"
"here? Get out of the\n"
"bar at once!"

msgctxt "scene:10:142"
msgid ""
"Jawohl Chef, ich bin\n"
"schon weg Chef..."
msgstr ""
"Yes boss, I am\n"
"already gone boss..."

msgctxt "scene:10:144"
msgid ""
"Na, das ist ja eine\n"
"schöne Sauerei, das\n"
"ganze Fenster ist\n"
"verschmiert, so ein\n"
"Tölpel!"
msgstr ""
"Well, what a fine\n"
"mess, the whole\n"
"window is smeared,\n"
"what a clod!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:149"
msgid ""
"Und ich muss es\n"
"wieder in Ordnung\n"
"bringen."
msgstr ""
"And I have to put\n"
"it right again.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:152"
msgid ""
"He,Firehand! Kommen Sie\n"
"mal eben her!"
msgstr ""
"Hey, Firehand! Come\n"
"over here a moment!"

msgctxt "scene:10:154"
msgid ""
"Oh, wie's aussieht\n"
"wollte der Kerl uns\n"
"wohl belauschen. Na,\n"
"das ist ihm jetzt ja\n"
"vergangen. Ich möchte\n"
"zu gerne wissen, für\n"
"wen er spionieren\n"
"wollte."
msgstr ""
"Oh, it looks like\n"
"that fellow wanted to\n"
"eavesdrop on us. Well,\n"
"that notion has passed\n"
"for him now. I would\n"
"dearly like to know\n"
"whom he wanted to\n"
"spy for."

msgctxt "scene:10:162"
msgid ""
"Das ist eigentlich\n"
"nicht sehr schwer zu\n"
"erraten - der Captain\n"
"hat mir zu Beginn\n"
"der Fahrt von den\n"
"Tramps, die sich auf\n"
"dem Schiff befinden,\n"
"erzählt."
msgstr ""
"That is actually not\n"
"very hard to guess -\n"
"the captain told me\n"
"at the start of the\n"
"voyage about the\n"
"tramps who are on\n"
"board the ship.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:170"
msgid ""
"Da hat bei unserem\n"
"Fensterputzer wohl\n"
"die Aussicht auf\n"
"schnell verdientes\n"
"Geld den Verstand\n"
"getrübt."
msgstr ""
"The prospect of\n"
"quick money must\n"
"have clouded our\n"
"window washer's\n"
"mind.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:176"
msgid ""
"So ist das eben, Mr.\n"
"Patterson. Vor den\n"
"Ganoven ist man nir-\n"
"gends sicher. Noch\n"
"nicht einmal bei einem\n"
"Glas Whisky, haha."
msgstr ""
"That is how it is, Mr.\n"
"Patterson. One is safe\n"
"from crooks nowhere.\n"
"Not even over a glass\n"
"of whisky, haha.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:182"
msgid ""
"Da haben sie leider\n"
"recht, Mr. Droll. Ähm\n"
"- Mr. Firehand? Sie\n"
"würden mir einen gros-\n"
"sen Gefallen tun,"
msgstr ""
"You are unfortunately\n"
"right, Mr. Droll. Um\n"
"- Mr. Firehand? You\n"
"would do me a great\n"
"favour,"

msgctxt "scene:10:187"
msgid ""
"wenn Sie für den Rest\n"
"der Fahrt mein Bowie-\n"
"messer aufbewahren\n"
"könnten."
msgstr ""
"if you could keep my\n"
"Bowie knife for the\n"
"rest of the voyage.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:191"
msgid ""
"Wieso? Was ist denn\n"
"so Besonderes an dem\n"
"Bowiemesser, dass ich\n"
"darauf aufpassen soll?"
msgstr ""
"Why? What is so\n"
"special about the\n"
"Bowie knife that I\n"
"should watch it?"

msgctxt "scene:10:195"
msgid ""
"Nun, nachdem wir nicht\n"
"mehr belauscht werden,\n"
"kann ich es Ihnen ja\n"
"beruhigt erklären: Im\n"
"Griff des Messers habe\n"
"ich 9.000 Dollar ver-\n"
"steckt."
msgstr ""
"Now that we are no\n"
"longer overheard, I\n"
"can calmly explain\n"
"it: In the handle of\n"
"the knife I have\n"
"hidden 9,000 dollars.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:202"
msgid ""
"Verstehen Sie jetzt,\n"
"warum ich es lieber\n"
"Ihnen anvertraue als\n"
"darauf zu warten, dass\n"
"es mir gestohlen wird?"
msgstr ""
"Do you understand now\n"
"why I prefer to\n"
"entrust it to you\n"
"rather than wait for\n"
"it to be stolen?"

msgctxt "scene:10:207"
msgid ""
"Es ehrt mich, dass Sie\n"
"mir so sehr vertrauen,\n"
"Mr. Patterson."
msgstr ""
"It honours me that\n"
"you trust me so much,\n"
"Mr. Patterson."

msgctxt "scene:10:210"
msgid ""
"Ich habe viel Gutes\n"
"über Sie gehört, und\n"
"jetzt auch erlebt.\n"
"Wie ist es Mr. Fire-\n"
"hand, kann ich Ihnen\n"
"mein Messer geben?"
msgstr ""
"I have heard much\n"
"good about you, and\n"
"now experienced it.\n"
"How about it, Mr.\n"
"Firehand, can I give\n"
"you my knife?"

msgctxt "scene:10:216"
msgid ""
"1. Aber ja, seien sie\n"
"   unbesorgt! Ich werde\n"
"   auf ihr Messer auf-\n"
"   passen."
msgstr ""
"1. Why yes, do not\n"
"   fret! I shall watch\n"
"   over your knife.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:220"
msgid ""
"2. Behalten Sie Ihr\n"
"   Messer, auf dem\n"
"   Schiff kann Ihnen\n"
"   nichts geschehen."
msgstr ""
"2. Keep your knife,\n"
"   nothing can happen\n"
"   to you on the ship.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:224"
msgid ""
"Ich danke Ihnen,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."
msgstr ""
"I thank you,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."

msgctxt "scene:10:226"
msgid ""
"Ja und wir können\n"
"Ihnen auch helfen,\n"
"so lange wir Sie auf\n"
"dem Schiff begleiten.\n"
"Wenn wir uns dann tren-\n"
"nen, können wir Ihr\n"
"Geld sowieso nicht mehr\n"
"beschützen."
msgstr ""
"Yes, and we can help\n"
"you as well, as long\n"
"as we accompany you\n"
"on the ship. When we\n"
"part ways, we cannot\n"
"protect your money\n"
"anyway.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:234"
msgid ""
"Unser Droll hat recht,\n"
"wenn ich das Messer an\n"
"mich nehme, ist es nicht\n"
"besser geschützt."
msgstr ""
"Our Droll is right, if I\n"
"take the knife, it is no\n"
"better protected.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:238"
msgid ""
"Nun gut, wenn Sie\n"
"meinen. Dann hoffe\n"
"ich, dass mich nie-\n"
"mand überfällt."
msgstr ""
"Well, if you say so.\n"
"Then I hope that no\n"
"one attacks me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:242"
msgid "Barkeeper..!"
msgstr "Barkeeper..!"

msgctxt "scene:10:243"
msgid ""
"Die Bar ist bereits\n"
"geschlossen, ich räu-\n"
"me hier eigentlich nur\n"
"noch auf. Sie können\n"
"aber gerne noch hier\n"
"bleiben."
msgstr ""
"The bar is already\n"
"closed, I am really\n"
"just clearing up.\n"
"But you are welcome\n"
"to stay here.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:249"
msgid "Barkeeper...!"
msgstr "Barkeeper...!"

msgctxt "scene:10:250"
msgid ""
"Die Bar ist geschlos-\n"
"sen, ich kann Ihnen\n"
"nichts ausschenken,\n"
"aber Sie können gerne\n"
"in der Bar bleiben."
msgstr ""
"The bar is closed, I\n"
"cannot serve you\n"
"anything, but you may\n"
"stay in the bar.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:255"
msgid ""
"Ein Petrolleuchter hängt in\n"
"der Mitte des Raumes."
msgstr ""
"A kerosene lamp hangs in\n"
"the middle of the room."

msgctxt "scene:10:257"
msgid ""
"Eine schön gearbeitete Trenn-\n"
"wand unterteilt den Raum. Ur-\n"
"sprünglich war wohl ein ab-\n"
"getrennter Speisesaal geplant."
msgstr ""
"A nicely crafted partition\n"
"divides the room. Originally\n"
"a separate dining hall was\n"
"likely planned."

msgctxt "scene:10:261"
msgid ""
"Ein Spiegel entlang der ganzen\n"
"Rückwand der Bar, lässt den Raum\n"
"grösser erscheinen."
msgstr ""
"A mirror along the whole back\n"
"wall of the bar makes the room\n"
"appear larger."

msgctxt "scene:10:264"
msgid ""
"Ein typischer Barman, er scheint\n"
"seinen Beruf zu lieben."
msgstr ""
"A typical bartender, he seems\n"
"to love his profession."

msgctxt "scene:10:266"
msgid ""
"Hier hat der Barkeeper seine\n"
"ganze Auswahl aufgereiht."
msgstr ""
"Here the bartender has lined\n"
"up his entire selection."

msgctxt "scene:10:268"
msgid ""
"Ein Tintenfass mit einem Kassa-\n"
"buch des Barkeepers."
msgstr ""
"An inkwell with a cashbook of\n"
"the bartender."

msgctxt "scene:10:270"
msgid ""
"Eine leere Tasse, hat wohl\n"
"ein Gast hier abgestellt,\n"
"und unser Freund an der Bar\n"
"hat sie noch nicht wegge-\n"
"räumt."
msgstr ""
"An empty cup, likely left\n"
"here by a guest, and our\n"
"friend at the bar has not\n"
"cleared it away yet.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:275"
msgid ""
"Ein grosses Fenster, es macht\n"
"den Raum viel freundlicher."
msgstr ""
"A large window, it makes\n"
"the room much friendlier."

msgctxt "scene:10:277"
msgid ""
"Eine schöne Massivholzbar, da\n"
"macht das trinken Spass."
msgstr ""
"A nice solid wood bar, that\n"
"makes drinking a pleasure."

msgctxt "scene:10:279"
msgid ""
"Eine Holzverkleidung, die\n"
"wohl die Tapete schützen soll."
msgstr ""
"Wood panelling, meant to\n"
"protect the wallpaper."

msgctxt "scene:10:281"
msgid ""
"Die grüne Tapete ist etwas grell,\n"
"doch sonst wirkt der Raum un-\n"
"erwartet nobel."
msgstr ""
"The green wallpaper is a bit\n"
"garish, yet otherwise the room\n"
"seems unexpectedly noble."

msgctxt "scene:10:284"
msgid ""
"Wenn der Captain den Raum auch\n"
"später noch als Speisesaal für\n"
"etwas 'bessere' Gäste nutzen\n"
"will, so sollte er wohl einen\n"
"Teppich auslegen."
msgstr ""
"If the captain wants to use\n"
"the room later as a dining\n"
"hall for 'better' guests, he\n"
"should lay down a carpet.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:10:289"
msgid "Das Fensterkreuz."
msgstr "The window cross."

msgctxt "scene:10:290"
msgid ""
"Die ist mit einer etwas\n"
"schrillen Farbe gestrichen."
msgstr ""
"That is painted in a somewhat\n"
"garish colour."

msgctxt "scene:10:292"
msgid ""
"Der hängt zu hoch, da komme\n"
"ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"It hangs too high, I cannot\n"
"reach it."

msgctxt "scene:10:294"
msgid ""
"Durch das Fenster kann ich\n"
"die Bar nicht verlassen..."
msgstr ""
"Through the window I cannot\n"
"leave the bar..."

msgctxt "scene:10:296"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass mich\n"
"der Barkeeper die Flaschen\n"
"wegnehmen lässt."
msgstr ""
"I do not think the bartender\n"
"will let me take the\n"
"bottles."

msgctxt "scene:10:299"
msgid ""
"Hallo, was wollen Sie\n"
"hier hinten, bitte blei-\n"
"ben Sie vorne, hinter\n"
"die Bar komme nur ich\n"
"und eventuell, aber nur\n"
"bei Ausnahmen, der\n"
"Captain."
msgstr ""
"Hello, what do you want\n"
"back here? Please stay\n"
"out front, behind the\n"
"bar only I go and\n"
"possibly, but only in\n"
"exceptions, the\n"
"captain."

msgctxt "scene:10:306"
msgid ""
"Das Tintenfass ist festgebunden,\n"
"da haben wohl schon andere das\n"
"Tintenfass mitgehen lassen."
msgstr ""
"The inkwell is tied down, others\n"
"must have taken the inkwell\n"
"already."

msgctxt "scene:10:309"
msgid ""
"Der wird sich nicht sehr freuen,\n"
"wenn ich versuche ihn mitzunehmen."
msgstr ""
"He will not be very pleased\n"
"if I try to take him along."

msgctxt "scene:10:311"
msgid ""
"Der Barkeeper würde sich be-\n"
"danken, wenn ich hier Unge-\n"
"ziefer verteile."
msgstr ""
"The bartender would hardly thank\n"
"me if I were to spread vermin\n"
"around here."

msgctxt "scene:10:314"
msgid ""
"Das ist unsere Tante Droll\n"
"wie sie leibt und lebt...\n"
"...und drinkt."
msgstr ""
"That is our Aunt Droll\n"
"in the flesh...\n"
"...and drinking."

msgctxt "scene:12:0"
msgid ""
"Unbefugte haben keinen\n"
"Zutritt!\n"
"Gehen Sie zurück an\n"
"Deck, aber ein\n"
"bisschen plötzlich!"
msgstr ""
"Unauthorized persons have no\n"
"admittance!\n"
"Go back up on\n"
"deck, and make\n"
"it snappy!"

msgctxt "scene:12:5"
msgid ""
"Ist ja gut, ich\n"
"gehe ja schon."
msgstr ""
"Alright, alright,\n"
"I am going already."

msgctxt "scene:12:7"
msgid ""
"Ich schätze, ich sollte erst\n"
"mal die Dogfish vor dem Unter-\n"
"gang bewahren!"
msgstr ""
"I reckon I should first save\n"
"the Dogfish from going down\n"
"to the bottom!"

msgctxt "scene:12:10"
msgid ""
"Schätze, da ist gewaltig\n"
"Druck auf den Dampflei-\n"
"tungen."
msgstr ""
"I reckon there is immense\n"
"pressure in the steam\n"
"pipes."

msgctxt "scene:12:13"
msgid ""
"Ganz schön gross, so\n"
"ein Heizkessel..."
msgstr ""
"Quite sizeable, such\n"
"a boiler..."

msgctxt "scene:12:15"
msgid ""
"Meine Tante Erna würde\n"
"hier gleich die Putzwut\n"
"packen."
msgstr ""
"My Aunt Erna would\n"
"be seized by a frenzy\n"
"of cleaning here."

msgctxt "scene:12:18"
msgid ""
"Das sieht mir einem Ofen\n"
"sehr ähnlich, aber ich\n"
"bin eben kein Heizer."
msgstr ""
"This looks very much like a\n"
"furnace, but then I am\n"
"no stoker."

msgctxt "scene:12:21"
msgid ""
"Die Tür zum Kohlebunker\n"
"ist auch schon schön an-\n"
"gerostet."
msgstr ""
"The door to the coal bunker\n"
"is also rather badly\n"
"rusted."

msgctxt "scene:12:24"
msgid ""
"Das ist die Feuerungs-\n"
"klappe. Ganz schön heiss\n"
"das Ding."
msgstr ""
"That is the fire door.\n"
"A rather hot thing,\n"
"that."

msgctxt "scene:12:27"
msgid ""
"Das Feuer sieht auch\n"
"schön heiss aus!"
msgstr ""
"The fire looks rather\n"
"hot as well!"

msgctxt "scene:12:29"
msgid ""
"Da drinn' ist nichts als\n"
"heisse Asche."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing inside\n"
"but hot ashes."

msgctxt "scene:12:31"
msgid ""
"Ganz schön nass der Boden,\n"
"und es sprudelt weiterhin\n"
"fröhlich vor sich hin."
msgstr ""
"The floor is quite wet,\n"
"and it continues to bubble\n"
"away merrily."

msgctxt "scene:12:34"
msgid ""
"Well, die Kohle ist etwas\n"
"nass geworden, aber das\n"
"Schiff ist gerettet. Der\n"
"Holzpflock wird sicher bis\n"
"zum nächsten Hafen halten."
msgstr ""
"Well, the coal got a bit\n"
"wet, but the ship is saved.\n"
"The wooden plug will surely\n"
"hold until the next port\n"
"of call."

msgctxt "scene:12:39"
msgid ""
"Die Leiter könnte eben-\n"
"falls schon etwas Farbe\n"
"gebrauchen."
msgstr ""
"The ladder could also\n"
"use a bit of paint as\n"
"well."

msgctxt "scene:12:42"
msgid ""
"Mit der Menge Kohlen,\n"
"könnten wir leicht den\n"
"ganzen Arkansas rauf und\n"
"wieder runter reisen."
msgstr ""
"With this amount of coal,\n"
"we could easily travel all the\n"
"way up the Arkansas river\n"
"and down again."

msgctxt "scene:12:46"
msgid ""
"Und wenn die Kohle alle\n"
"ist, wird mit Holz ge-\n"
"heizt."
msgstr ""
"And when the coal is gone,\n"
"we shall stoke the fire\n"
"with wood."

msgctxt "scene:12:49"
msgid ""
"Einige Kohlen liegen\n"
"hier einzeln in der\n"
"Gegend herum. Der Heizer\n"
"hatte wohl keine Zeit\n"
"aufzuräumen..."
msgstr ""
"A few pieces of coal\n"
"lie scattered about\n"
"here. The stoker\n"
"likely had no time\n"
"to tidy up..."

msgctxt "scene:12:54"
msgid ""
"Jede Kohle zählt, darum\n"
"lass ich die liegen."
msgstr ""
"Every lump of coal counts,\n"
"so I shall leave them be."

msgctxt "scene:12:56"
msgid ""
"Ich mag nicht Kohlen\n"
"mit mir herumschleppen."
msgstr ""
"I do not care to haul\n"
"lumps of coal about with me."

msgctxt "scene:12:58"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keinen Kamin,\n"
"darum lasse ich das Holz\n"
"lieber liegen."
msgstr ""
"I have no fireplace,\n"
"so I had better leave the\n"
"wood where it is."

msgctxt "scene:12:61"
msgid ""
"Die Tür klemmt, kommt\n"
"wohl von den rostigen\n"
"Angeln."
msgstr ""
"The door is jammed, likely\n"
"on account of the rusty\n"
"hinges."

msgctxt "scene:12:64"
msgid ""
"Well, da komme ich\n"
"nicht d'ran!"
msgstr ""
"Well, I cannot reach\n"
"that!"

msgctxt "scene:12:66"
msgid ""
"Au! Die Klappe kann ich\n"
"von Hand nicht öffnen,\n"
"die ist zu heiss!"
msgstr ""
"Ouch! I cannot open\n"
"the hatch by hand, it\n"
"is far too hot!"

msgctxt "scene:12:69"
msgid ""
"Es hat lang genug gedauert,\n"
"die Klappe aufzukriegen.\n"
"Ich werde sie also sicher\n"
"nicht wieder zumachen!"
msgstr ""
"It took long enough to get\n"
"the hatch open. I shall\n"
"certainly not close it\n"
"again!"

msgctxt "scene:12:73"
msgid ""
"Die Schaufel passt nicht\n"
"in die Vorrichtung der\n"
"Tür."
msgstr ""
"The shovel does not fit\n"
"into the mechanism of\n"
"the door."

msgctxt "scene:12:76"
msgid ""
"Das würde die Klappe\n"
"auch nicht genügend\n"
"abkühlen!"
msgstr ""
"That would not cool down\n"
"the hatch sufficiently\n"
"either!"

msgctxt "scene:12:79"
msgid ""
"Da liegt etwas d'rinn,\n"
"eingewickelt in einem\n"
"Lappen!"
msgstr ""
"There is something inside,\n"
"wrapped up in a rag!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:82"
msgid ""
"Es ist Pattersons\n"
"Bowie-Messer!!!\n"
"Das muss dieser\n"
"Brinkley hier ver-\n"
"steckt haben. Sicher\n"
"hat er das Schiff\n"
"angebohrt."
msgstr ""
"It is Patterson's\n"
"Bowie knife!!!\n"
"That Brinkley fellow\n"
"must have hidden it\n"
"here. Surely he was\n"
"the one who scuttled\n"
"the ship."

msgctxt "scene:12:89"
msgid ""
"Da liegt irgendwas\n"
"d'rinn!"
msgstr ""
"Something is lying\n"
"in there!"

msgctxt "scene:12:91"
msgid ""
"Aber ich komme nicht\n"
"d'ran! Die Hitze von\n"
"unten ist zu gross!"
msgstr ""
"But I cannot reach it!\n"
"The heat from below is\n"
"too great!"

msgctxt "scene:12:94"
msgid ""
"Da oben im Ofen\n"
"gibt es nichts\n"
"mehr zu holen!"
msgstr ""
"Up there in the furnace,\n"
"there is nothing left\n"
"to be had!"

msgctxt "scene:12:97"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"ich etwas finde, indem\n"
"ich mit einem Haken\n"
"in einem Haufen Kohle\n"
"herumstochere."
msgstr ""
"I do not think I shall find\n"
"anything by poking around\n"
"in a pile of coal with a\n"
"hook.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:102"
msgid ""
"Diese Klappe hat keine\n"
"Vorrichtung um mit einem\n"
"Haken geöffnet zu\n"
"werden."
msgstr ""
"This hatch has no\n"
"fixture to be opened\n"
"with a hook.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:106"
msgid ""
"Der Haken scheint\n"
"mir nicht geeignet, die\n"
"verklemmte Tür zu repa-\n"
"rieren. Der Haken ist\n"
"viel zu schwach..."
msgstr ""
"The hook seems unsuitable\n"
"for repairing the jammed\n"
"door. The hook is far\n"
"too weak...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:111"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich den Haken verwende,\n"
"wird das Loch nur grösser,\n"
"und ich will ja das Loch\n"
"stopfen, nicht das Schiff\n"
"noch schneller versenken."
msgstr ""
"If I use the hook, the hole\n"
"will only grow larger, and I\n"
"wish to plug the hole, not\n"
"sink the ship even faster.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:116"
msgid ""
"Meine Probleme werden auch\n"
"nicht gelöst, indem ich mit\n"
"dem Haken auf die Maschine\n"
"einschlage."
msgstr ""
"My problems will not be\n"
"solved by striking the\n"
"engine with the hook.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:120"
msgid ""
"Eine gute Idee, aber den\n"
"Lappen wird es durch den\n"
"Druck einfach wieder heraus-\n"
"spühlen..."
msgstr ""
"A good idea, but the pressure\n"
"would simply wash the rag\n"
"out again...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:124"
msgid ""
"Deine Reinlichkeit in\n"
"Ehren, aber ich glaube,\n"
"dass dies hier nicht\n"
"viel nützt, und unsere\n"
"Probleme kaum lösen\n"
"wird."
msgstr ""
"All honor to your cleanliness,\n"
"but I doubt this will be of\n"
"much use here, nor will it\n"
"solve our problems.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:130"
msgid ""
"Ich denke nicht daran,\n"
"jetzt Kohlen zu schippen."
msgstr ""
"I have no intention of\n"
"shoveling coal right now."

msgctxt "scene:12:132"
msgid ""
"Die Schaufel ist sicher\n"
"zu schwach, um die Türe zu\n"
"lösen. Alles was ich da-\n"
"mit erreiche, ist die\n"
"Schaufel zu verbiegen."
msgstr ""
"The shovel is surely too weak\n"
"to loosen the door. All I would\n"
"achieve by doing so is bending\n"
"the shovel.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:12:137"
msgid ""
"Dies ist sicher nicht\n"
"das richtige Werkzeug\n"
"für eine solche Arbeit."
msgstr ""
"This is surely not the\n"
"right tool for such\n"
"a task."

msgctxt "scene:12:140"
msgid ""
"Den wollten wir ja der\n"
"Dame zurückgeben."
msgstr ""
"We intended to return\n"
"that to the lady."

msgctxt "scene:14:0"
msgid ""
"Die Tür ist\n"
"abgeschlossen!"
msgstr ""
"The door is\n"
"locked!"

msgctxt "scene:14:2"
msgid ""
"Die Tür ist\n"
"abgeschlossen!"
msgstr ""
"The door is\n"
"locked!"

msgctxt "scene:14:4"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, ich lasse\n"
"ihn lieber schlafen,\n"
"bis ich eine Lösung\n"
"für das Problem gefunden\n"
"habe!"
msgstr ""
"I believe I had better let\n"
"him sleep until I have\n"
"found a solution to the\n"
"problem!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:9"
msgid ""
"Ah, da sind Sie ja\n"
"wieder, Mr. Firehand."
msgstr ""
"Ah, there you are again,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."

msgctxt "scene:14:11"
msgid ""
"Und, haben Sie eine\n"
"Lösung für das Problem\n"
"mit den Tramps?"
msgstr ""
"And have you found a\n"
"solution to the problem\n"
"with the tramps?"

msgctxt "scene:14:14"
msgid ""
"1. Sie müssten\n"
"   einen der Tramps\n"
"   ablenken."
msgstr ""
"1. You would have to\n"
"   distract one of the\n"
"   tramps."

msgctxt "scene:14:17"
msgid ""
"2. Sie müssten sich\n"
"   verkleiden."
msgstr ""
"2. You would have to\n"
"   disguise yourself."

msgctxt "scene:14:19"
msgid ""
"Ich weiss! Das haben\n"
"wir ja schon be-\n"
"sprochen. Und wie?\n"
"Wie soll ich ihn\n"
"ablenken???"
msgstr ""
"I know! We have already\n"
"discussed that. But how?\n"
"How am I supposed to\n"
"distract him???\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:24"
msgid ""
"Sie müssten sich\n"
"verkleiden..."
msgstr ""
"You would have to\n"
"disguise yourself..."

msgctxt "scene:14:26"
msgid ""
"Womit denn? Ich habe\n"
"keine anderen Sachen."
msgstr ""
"With what? I have no\n"
"other clothes."

msgctxt "scene:14:28"
msgid ""
"1. Das weiss ich auch\n"
"   nicht."
msgstr ""
"1. I do not know that\n"
"   either."

msgctxt "scene:14:30"
msgid ""
"2. Setzen Sie doch den\n"
"   Hut auf, den ich\n"
"   besorgt habe."
msgstr ""
"2. Why not put on the\n"
"   hat I procured for\n"
"   you?"

msgctxt "scene:14:33"
msgid ""
"Waaas? Diesen Hut?!\n"
"Da sehe ich ja wie\n"
"eine Frau aus!"
msgstr ""
"Whaat? This hat?! Why,\n"
"I shall look like a\n"
"woman!"

msgctxt "scene:14:36"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich es mir aber\n"
"so überlege, dann\n"
"muss ich schon sagen,\n"
"dass die Idee gar\n"
"nicht so schlecht ist."
msgstr ""
"Yet if I think about\n"
"it, I must truly say\n"
"that the idea is not\n"
"all that bad.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:41"
msgid ""
"Auf den Trick fällt\n"
"dieser finstere\n"
"Geselle bestimmt\n"
"herein.\n"
"Was für ein Spass!"
msgstr ""
"That dark fellow will\n"
"surely fall for the\n"
"trick.\n"
"What fun!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:46"
msgid "Einen Moment..."
msgstr "Just a moment..."

msgctxt "scene:14:47"
msgid ""
"So würde mich sicher\n"
"nicht einmal meine\n"
"Mutter erkennen.\n"
"Also, Mr. Firehand, ans'\n"
"Werk. Zeigen Sie mir,\n"
"wo der Tramp herum-\n"
"lungert."
msgstr ""
"Even my mother would not\n"
"recognise me like this.\n"
"So, Mr. Firehand, to work.\n"
"Show me where the tramp\n"
"is loitering.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:54"
msgid ""
"Wäre doch gelacht, wenn\n"
"ich den nicht um den\n"
"kleinen Finger wickeln\n"
"könnte, hehe."
msgstr ""
"It would be a marvel if\n"
"I could not wrap him\n"
"around my little\n"
"finger, hehe."

msgctxt "scene:14:58"
msgid ""
"Vielleicht finden Sie\n"
"ja noch eine Lösung\n"
"für das Problem mit\n"
"den Tramps.\n"
"Bis später..."
msgstr ""
"Perhaps you will find a\n"
"solution to the problem\n"
"with the tramps.\n"
"Until later...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:63"
msgid ""
"Was gibt es denn,\n"
"Mr. Firehand?"
msgstr ""
"What is it then,\n"
"Mr. Firehand?"

msgctxt "scene:14:65"
msgid ""
"1. Mir scheint, die\n"
"   Tramps führen was\n"
"   im Schilde!"
msgstr ""
"1. It seems to me the\n"
"   tramps are up to\n"
"   no good!"

msgctxt "scene:14:68"
msgid ""
"2. Entschuldigen Sie\n"
"   die Störung."
msgstr ""
"2. Pardon the\n"
"   intrusion."

msgctxt "scene:14:70"
msgid ""
"Wie kommen Sie denn\n"
"darauf? Obwohl, das\n"
"würde mich nicht über-\n"
"raschen."
msgstr ""
"Whatever makes you think\n"
"so? Though it would\n"
"scarcely surprise me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:74"
msgid ""
"1. Ich habe die\n"
"   Tramps beobachtet"
msgstr ""
"1. I have been observing\n"
"   the tramps"

msgctxt "scene:14:76"
msgid ""
"2. Ich habe so ein\n"
"   ungutes Gefühl\n"
"   bei diesem Cornel."
msgstr ""
"2. I have an uneasy\n"
"   feeling about\n"
"   this Cornel."

msgctxt "scene:14:79"
msgid ""
"Hat er sich denn\n"
"irgendwie auffällig\n"
"benommen?"
msgstr ""
"Has he been acting in\n"
"any suspicious way?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:82"
msgid ""
"Ich habe ihn und die\n"
"Tramps bei einem\n"
"Gespräch beobachtet,\n"
"und ihr Verhalten\n"
"erschien mir nicht\n"
"ganz geheuer!"
msgstr ""
"I observed him and the\n"
"tramps in conversation,\n"
"and their behaviour\n"
"seemed to me not\n"
"entirely proper!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:88"
msgid ""
"Was ist denn mit den\n"
"Tramps?"
msgstr ""
"What about the tramps\n"
"then?"

msgctxt "scene:14:90"
msgid ""
"1. Ich weiss auch\n"
"   nicht so recht."
msgstr ""
"1. I am not entirely\n"
"   sure myself."

msgctxt "scene:14:92"
msgid ""
"2. Denken Sie nur\n"
"   an den Vorfall\n"
"   in der Bar!"
msgstr ""
"2. Just think of the\n"
"   incident in the\n"
"   bar!"

msgctxt "scene:14:95"
msgid ""
"Dann kommen Sie\n"
"doch wieder, wenn\n"
"Sie näheres heraus-\n"
"gefunden haben.\n"
"Sie können jederzeit\n"
"auf mich zählen."
msgstr ""
"Then come back when you\n"
"have found out more.\n"
"You can count on me at\n"
"any time.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:101"
msgid ""
"Gut, ich werde schauen,\n"
"was ich herausfinden\n"
"kann."
msgstr ""
"Very well, I shall see\n"
"what I can find out.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:104"
msgid ""
"Und glauben Sie,\n"
"dass der Fenster-\n"
"putzer von den\n"
"Tramps angestiftet\n"
"wurde?"
msgstr ""
"And do you believe that\n"
"the window washer was\n"
"instigated by the\n"
"tramps?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:109"
msgid ""
"1. Ja, davon bin ich\n"
"   überzeugt!"
msgstr ""
"1. Yes, I am convinced\n"
"   of it!"

msgctxt "scene:14:111"
msgid ""
"2. Gerade das will\n"
"   ich ja heraus-\n"
"   finden."
msgstr ""
"2. That is precisely\n"
"   what I want to find\n"
"   out."

msgctxt "scene:14:114"
msgid ""
"Dann müsste man die\n"
"Tramps eben ein\n"
"bisschen im Auge be-\n"
"halten!\n"
"Kann ich Ihnen irgend-\n"
"wie dabei helfen?"
msgstr ""
"Then one ought to keep\n"
"an eye on the tramps!\n"
"Can I help you with that\n"
"in any way?\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:120"
msgid ""
"Dann würde ich Ihnen\n"
"empfehlen, dass Sie\n"
"die Tramps etwas im\n"
"Auge behalten. Ich\n"
"werde Ihnen gerne\n"
"behilflich sein, aber\n"
"zuerst brauche ich\n"
"etwas Schlaf."
msgstr ""
"Then I would advise you\n"
"to keep an eye on the\n"
"tramps. I shall gladly\n"
"be of assistance, but\n"
"first I need some sleep.\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:128"
msgid ""
"Dabei will ich Ihnen\n"
"gerne behilflich\n"
"sein! Aber wie!?"
msgstr ""
"I shall gladly help you\n"
"with that! But how!?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:131"
msgid ""
"Sie könnten den einen\n"
"Tramp ablenken."
msgstr ""
"You could distract one\n"
"of the tramps."

msgctxt "scene:14:133"
msgid ""
"Das wird nicht gehen,\n"
"denn die kennen mich\n"
"und wissen, dass ich\n"
"mit Ihnen zusammen-\n"
"arbeite."
msgstr ""
"That will not do, for\n"
"they know me and know\n"
"that I work together\n"
"with you.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:138"
msgid ""
"Haben Sie für dieses\n"
"Problem eine Lösung?"
msgstr ""
"Do you have a solution\n"
"for this problem?"

msgctxt "scene:14:140"
msgid ""
"Das stimmt, ich werde\n"
"mir etwas einfallen\n"
"lassen müssen."
msgstr ""
"That is true, I shall\n"
"have to think of\n"
"something."

msgctxt "scene:14:143"
msgid ""
"Gut, inzwischen\n"
"werde ich etwas\n"
"Schlaf nachholen,\n"
"aber Sie können\n"
"jederzeit auf mich\n"
"zählen!"
msgstr ""
"Good, in the meantime I\n"
"shall catch up on some\n"
"sleep, but you can count\n"
"on me at any time!\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:149"
msgid ""
"Macht nichts!\n"
"Bis später..."
msgstr ""
"No matter!\n"
"Until later..."

msgctxt "scene:14:151"
msgid "Grrrrr!"
msgstr "Grrrrr!"

msgctxt "scene:14:152"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, dem\n"
"komme ich lieber\n"
"nicht zu nahe!"
msgstr ""
"I think I had better\n"
"not get too close to\n"
"that one!"

msgctxt "scene:14:155"
msgid "Matsch!"
msgstr "Splat!"

msgctxt "scene:14:156"
msgid ""
"Die Treppe zum Hauptdeck,\n"
"ganz schön steil."
msgstr ""
"The stairs to the main deck,\n"
"quite steep."

msgctxt "scene:14:158"
msgid ""
"Ein stabiles Geländer,\n"
"zum Schutz der Passa-\n"
"giere."
msgstr ""
"A sturdy railing for the\n"
"protection of the\n"
"passengers."

msgctxt "scene:14:161"
msgid ""
"Dieser Hund wird entweder\n"
"dem Captain, oder aber dem\n"
"Patterson gehören. Eines\n"
"ist aber sicher, zu spassen\n"
"ist mit dem nicht..."
msgstr ""
"This dog must belong either\n"
"to the captain or to\n"
"Patterson. One thing is\n"
"certain: he is not to be\n"
"trifled with..."

msgctxt "scene:14:166"
msgid ""
"Der Boden ist schon regel-\n"
"recht abgelaufen. Der hat\n"
"wohl schon manchen Passagier\n"
"gesehen."
msgstr ""
"The floor is quite worn.\n"
"It must have seen many\n"
"a passenger already.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:170"
msgid ""
"Naja, dem Seil würde ich\n"
"auch nicht gerade die\n"
"höchste Sicherheitsstufe\n"
"nachsagen."
msgstr ""
"Well, I would not call\n"
"this rope the highest\n"
"level of safety.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:14:174"
msgid ""
"Da kann man nur sagen:\n"
"VORSICHT STUFE..."
msgstr ""
"One can only say:\n"
"MIND THE STEP..."

msgctxt "scene:14:176"
msgid ""
"Ein fast wolkenloser Tag.\n"
"Man könnte ein solches\n"
"Wetter auch denen in\n"
"Old Germany wünschen..."
msgstr ""
"An almost cloudless day.\n"
"One could wish such weather\n"
"for those back in Old\n"
"Germany..."

msgctxt "scene:14:180"
msgid ""
"An den Aufbauten kann man\n"
"schon beinahe all die\n"
"Abenteuer auf dem Arkansas\n"
"ablesen. Das Schiff hat\n"
"sicher schon viel erlebt."
msgstr ""
"On the superstructures one\n"
"can read almost all the\n"
"adventures on the Arkansas.\n"
"The ship has surely seen a\n"
"great deal."

msgctxt "scene:14:185"
msgid ""
"Dies ist der Bildrand mein\n"
"lieber Abenteurer, und die\n"
"Welt des Karl May endet hier."
msgstr ""
"This is the image edge, my\n"
"dear adventurer, and the\n"
"world of Karl May ends here."

msgctxt "scene:14:188"
msgid ""
"Die Wand zu den Kabinen,\n"
"so wie die aussieht, kann\n"
"man erwarten, dass die\n"
"Kabinen ruhig sind."
msgstr ""
"The wall to the cabins,\n"
"from the look of it, one\n"
"may expect that the\n"
"cabins are quiet."

msgctxt "scene:14:192"
msgid ""
"Das müsste die Kabine von\n"
"Mr. Patterson sein."
msgstr ""
"That ought to be the cabin\n"
"of Mr. Patterson."

msgctxt "scene:14:194"
msgid ""
"Das wird die Kabine unserer\n"
"Tante Droll sein. Drollig ist\n"
"er wirklich, ich hätte nie\n"
"gedacht, dass er in einer Kabine\n"
"schlafen würde als einge-\n"
"fleischter Westmann."
msgstr ""
"That will be the cabin of\n"
"our Aunt Droll. Droll he\n"
"truly is, I never would\n"
"have thought he would sleep\n"
"in a cabin as a confirmed\n"
"westman."

msgctxt "scene:14:200"
msgid ""
"Ah, das ist die Kajüte dieser\n"
"verschrobenen Lehrerin."
msgstr ""
"Ah, that is the cabin of\n"
"this eccentric teacher."

msgctxt "scene:14:202"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Geländer weiss ich\n"
"nichts anzufangen, zudem\n"
"wird der Captain nicht gerade\n"
"erbaut sein, wenn sein Schiff\n"
"beschädigt wird."
msgstr ""
"I know not what to do with\n"
"the railing; besides, the\n"
"captain will hardly be\n"
"pleased if his ship is\n"
"damaged."

msgctxt "scene:14:207"
msgid ""
"Das Seil darf ich nicht ent-\n"
"fernen, das wäre zu gefährlich,\n"
"es könnte jemand runterstürzen."
msgstr ""
"I must not remove the rope,\n"
"that would be too dangerous,\n"
"someone might fall down."

msgctxt "scene:14:210"
msgid ""
"Das wäre aber nicht fein,\n"
"wenn ich an die Wand\n"
"klopfen würde und die Leute\n"
"beim Schlafen störe..."
msgstr ""
"It would not be polite,\n"
"were I to knock on\n"
"the wall and disturb\n"
"people sleeping..."

msgctxt "scene:14:214"
msgid ""
"Das kann nicht ernst ge-\n"
"meint sein, der würde mich\n"
"glatt zerfleischen..."
msgstr ""
"That cannot be meant in\n"
"earnest, he would tear me\n"
"to pieces outright..."

msgctxt "scene:14:217"
msgid ""
"Das wäre ein Spass, aber ich\n"
"sehe keinen tieferen Sinn\n"
"darin, und möchte den Hund\n"
"nicht unnötig ärgern."
msgstr ""
"That would be sport, but I\n"
"see no deeper sense in\n"
"it, and do not wish to\n"
"annoy the dog needlessly."

msgctxt "scene:14:221"
msgid ""
"Ich kann doch nicht einfach\n"
"einen Hund niederstechen!"
msgstr ""
"I cannot simply stab a\n"
"dog to death!"

msgctxt "scene:14:223"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, das ich\n"
"mit dem Brett eine Chance\n"
"gegen den Hund hätte!"
msgstr ""
"I do not think that with\n"
"the board I stand a chance\n"
"against the dog!"

msgctxt "scene:14:226"
msgid ""
"Wir nähern uns dem Gipfel\n"
"des Absurden. Ich werde\n"
"NICHT mit der Wand reden!"
msgstr ""
"We approach the peak of the\n"
"absurd. I shall NOT\n"
"talk to the wall!"

msgctxt "scene:14:229"
msgid ""
"Jetzt wird es aber etwas\n"
"lächerlich, warum soll ich\n"
"mit dem Boden sprechen!?"
msgstr ""
"Now it becomes somewhat\n"
"ridiculous; why should I\n"
"speak to the floor!?"

msgctxt "scene:14:232"
msgid ""
"1. Na, mein liebes\n"
"   Hundchen, lässt du\n"
"   mich vorbei?!"
msgstr ""
"1. Well, my dear\n"
"   doggie, will you\n"
"   let me pass?!"

msgctxt "scene:14:235"
msgid ""
"2. Braver Hund, ich tu\n"
"   dir ja nichts..."
msgstr ""
"2. Good dog, I am not\n"
"   going to hurt you..."

msgctxt "scene:14:237"
msgid ""
"3. Hau ab, du blöde Töle\n"
"   oder es setzt was!"
msgstr ""
"3. Get lost, you cur,\n"
"   or you'll get it!"

msgctxt "scene:14:239"
msgid "GRRRRR!"
msgstr "GRRRRR!"

msgctxt "scene:14:240"
msgid ""
"Oh mir scheint er mag\n"
"mich nicht sonderlich."
msgstr ""
"Oh, it seems he does\n"
"not care for me much."

msgctxt "scene:14:242"
msgid "GRRRR!"
msgstr "GRRRR!"

msgctxt "scene:14:243"
msgid ""
"Dass ich ihm nichts tue\n"
"scheint für ihn ausser\n"
"Frage zu stehen, aber\n"
"bei ihm bin ich mir\n"
"nicht so sicher."
msgstr ""
"That I will do him no\n"
"harm seems out of the\n"
"question for him, but\n"
"as for him, I am not\n"
"so sure."

msgctxt "scene:14:248"
msgid "GRRROOOARR!"
msgstr "GRRROOOARR!"

msgctxt "scene:14:249"
msgid ""
"Die autoritäre Tour\n"
"scheint nicht sonderlich\n"
"zu wirken.\n"
"Einen eingeschüchterten\n"
"Eindruck macht er mir\n"
"jedenfalls nicht."
msgstr ""
"The authoritative line\n"
"does not seem to work\n"
"very well.\n"
"At any rate, he does\n"
"not seem intimidated\n"
"to me at all."

msgctxt "scene:17:0"
msgid ""
"Nun, Mr.Firehand,das\n"
"war ein schönes Stück,\n"
"dass wir heute noch zu-\n"
"rückgelegt haben."
msgstr ""
"Well, Mr. Firehand, that\n"
"was a fine distance that\n"
"we have covered today\n"
"nonetheless."

msgctxt "scene:17:4"
msgid ""
"Das kann man wohl sa-\n"
"gen...Es wäre mir aber\n"
"im Augenblick wohler,\n"
"wenn ich wüsste wo die\n"
"Tramps lagern..."
msgstr ""
"One may well say so...\n"
"Yet I should feel easier\n"
"for the moment if I knew\n"
"where the tramps are\n"
"camped..."

msgctxt "scene:17:9"
msgid ""
"Pst! Mr. Firehand!\n"
"Kommen Sie schnell her!"
msgstr ""
"Hist! Mr. Firehand!\n"
"Come over here quickly!"

msgctxt "scene:17:11"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, wir haben\n"
"die Galgenvögel ent-\n"
"deckt!"
msgstr ""
"I believe we have\n"
"spotted the gallows-\n"
"birds!"

msgctxt "scene:17:14"
msgid ""
"Dort hinten glaube ich\n"
"das Flackern eines\n"
"Lagerfeuers gesehen\n"
"zu haben. Ich werde\n"
"das einmal näher\n"
"untersuchen."
msgstr ""
"Over there I believe I\n"
"have seen the flicker\n"
"of a campfire. I shall\n"
"investigate that a\n"
"little closer\n"
"myself."

msgctxt "scene:17:20"
msgid ""
"Pshaw! Auch das noch!\n"
"Das Boot ist weg!!!\n"
"Ohne Kanu muss ich\n"
"fürs Erste auf dieser\n"
"Seite des Flusses\n"
"bleiben. Ich habe\n"
"keine andere Wahl."
msgstr ""
"Pshaw! That on top of it!\n"
"The boat is gone!!!\n"
"Without a canoe I must\n"
"for the present remain\n"
"on this side of the\n"
"river. I have no\n"
"other choice."

msgctxt "scene:17:27"
msgid ""
"Zum Glück lagern\n"
"die Tramps auf\n"
"dieser Seite des\n"
"Ufers, sonst könnte\n"
"ich ihnen von hier\n"
"zuwinken."
msgstr ""
"Fortunately the tramps\n"
"are camped on this\n"
"side of the bank,\n"
"otherwise I could only\n"
"wave to them from\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:17:33"
msgid ""
"Doch sich darüber\n"
"Gedanken zu machen\n"
"ist müssig, jetzt\n"
"sind zuerst andere\n"
"Probleme zu lösen."
msgstr ""
"Yet to ponder that\n"
"is idle; right now\n"
"other problems must\n"
"first be solved\n"
"at hand."

msgctxt "scene:17:38"
msgid ""
"Puh, das war knapp!\n"
"Doch ich habe was\n"
"ich wollte. Der alte\n"
"Trick klappt noch\n"
"immer."
msgstr ""
"Phew, that was close!\n"
"Yet I have what I\n"
"wanted. The old trick\n"
"still works every\n"
"time."

msgctxt "scene:17:43"
msgid ""
"Mr. Firehand, das Boot\n"
"konnte ich nirgendwo\n"
"finden, es muss wohl\n"
"abgetrieben sein."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Firehand, the boat\n"
"I could find nowhere;\n"
"it must surely have\n"
"drifted away."

msgctxt "scene:17:47"
msgid ""
"Ja, das wollte ich\n"
"vorhin schon sagen,\n"
"aber Sie sind so\n"
"schnell verschwunden.\n"
"Doch ich hab mir be-\n"
"reits etwas einfallen\n"
"lassen, wie wir den\n"
"Fluss überqueren kön-\n"
"nen."
msgstr ""
"Yes, I wanted to say\n"
"that earlier, but you\n"
"disappeared so\n"
"quickly. Yet I have\n"
"already thought of\n"
"something so that we\n"
"can cross the river\n"
"together.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:56"
msgid ""
"Dann haben Sie die\n"
"Stämme losgeschnitten\n"
"und auf die Felsen\n"
"treiben lassen?"
msgstr ""
"So you cut the logs\n"
"free and let them\n"
"drift onto the\n"
"rocks?"

msgctxt "scene:17:60"
msgid ""
"Ja sicher, aber nun\n"
"müssen wir uns be-\n"
"eilen, bevor das Was-\n"
"ser zu hoch steigt."
msgstr ""
"To be sure, but now\n"
"we must hurry before\n"
"the water rises\n"
"too high."

msgctxt "scene:17:64"
msgid ""
"Mehr wie die Steine\n"
"die ich bereits habe,\n"
"kann ich nicht ge-\n"
"brauchen. Ich habe\n"
"kein Haus mit Vor-\n"
"platz, und brauche so-\n"
"mit auch nicht so\n"
"viel Kies..."
msgstr ""
"I cannot use more\n"
"stones than I already\n"
"have. I have no house\n"
"with a front yard,\n"
"and thus do not need\n"
"so much gravel...\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:72"
msgid ""
"Der Trick mit den Kiesel-\n"
"steinen hat geklappt, ich\n"
"brauche keine weiteren\n"
"Kieselsteine mehr."
msgstr ""
"The trick with the pebbles\n"
"worked; I do not need any\n"
"more pebbles at\n"
"present."

msgctxt "scene:17:76"
msgid ""
"Ich habe das bereits,\n"
"mehr will ich jetzt\n"
"nicht ernten. Ich bin\n"
"ja kein Gärtner."
msgstr ""
"I have that already;\n"
"I want to harvest no\n"
"more now. I am no\n"
"gardener, after all."

msgctxt "scene:17:80"
msgid ""
"Durch die untergehende\n"
"Sonne wirkt der Himmel\n"
"beinahe unnatürlich."
msgstr ""
"Due to the setting sun,\n"
"the sky seems almost\n"
"unnatural."

msgctxt "scene:17:83"
msgid ""
"Eine Hügelkette zieht\n"
"zieht sich über den\n"
"gesamten Horizont."
msgstr ""
"A range of hills\n"
"stretches across the\n"
"entire horizon."

msgctxt "scene:17:86"
msgid ""
"Der Wald säumt den\n"
"Fluss."
msgstr ""
"The forest skirts\n"
"the river."

msgctxt "scene:17:88"
msgid ""
"Ruhig, beinahe gemäch-\n"
"lich zieht der Fluss\n"
"dahin."
msgstr ""
"Calmly, almost\n"
"leisurely, the river\n"
"flows along."

msgctxt "scene:17:91"
msgid ""
"Ein knorriger Baum,\n"
"der schon Jahre auf\n"
"diesem mageren Boden\n"
"dahinfristet."
msgstr ""
"A gnarled tree that\n"
"has eked out an\n"
"existence on this\n"
"meagre soil for years."

msgctxt "scene:17:95"
msgid ""
"Aus dem Fluss ragen\n"
"einige grosse Felsen.\n"
"An diesen Steinen wird\n"
"sich oft Treibgut ver-\n"
"fangen."
msgstr ""
"Some large rocks project\n"
"from the river. Driftwood\n"
"will often get caught\n"
"on these stones.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:100"
msgid ""
"Trockenes Gestrüpp\n"
"säumt beide Seiten\n"
"des Weges."
msgstr ""
"Dry scrub lines\n"
"both sides of\n"
"the path."

msgctxt "scene:17:103"
msgid ""
"Trockenes Schilf steht\n"
"hier am Flussufer."
msgstr ""
"Dry reeds stand here\n"
"on the riverbank."

msgctxt "scene:17:105"
msgid ""
"Ein sandiger Boden,\n"
"sicher angeschwemmt\n"
"vom Fluss."
msgstr ""
"A sandy soil,\n"
"surely washed up by\n"
"the river."

msgctxt "scene:17:108"
msgid ""
"Einige Kiselsteine liegen\n"
"zusammen auf einem Haufen."
msgstr ""
"A few pebbles lie\n"
"together in a heap."

msgctxt "scene:17:110"
msgid ""
"Der Baum hat den\n"
"kargen Boden wohl\n"
"nicht so recht über-\n"
"standen..."
msgstr ""
"The tree probably\n"
"did not quite survive\n"
"the barren soil...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:114"
msgid ""
"Ein dichtes Dickicht\n"
"und Buschwerk steht\n"
"hier wie eine undurch-\n"
"dringliche Mauer."
msgstr ""
"Dense thicket and\n"
"bushes stand here\n"
"like an impenetrable\n"
"wall."

msgctxt "scene:17:118"
msgid "Ein grosser Granitfelsen."
msgstr "A large granite rock."

msgctxt "scene:17:119"
msgid ""
"Ein etwas stacheliger\n"
"Strauch."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat prickly\n"
"shrub."

msgctxt "scene:17:121"
msgid ""
"Ich bin nicht durstig,\n"
"und gebaded habe ich\n"
"gerade erst im Früh-\n"
"jahr."
msgstr ""
"I am not thirsty,\n"
"and I bathed only\n"
"recently in the\n"
"spring."

msgctxt "scene:17:125"
msgid ""
"Auf den Steinen den\n"
"Fluss zu überqueren\n"
"ist unmöglich, sie\n"
"liegen zu weit aus-\n"
"einander."
msgstr ""
"Crossing the river\n"
"upon the stones is\n"
"impossible, they lie\n"
"too far apart from\n"
"each other."

msgctxt "scene:17:130"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit einer\n"
"Hand voll Dreck an-\n"
"fangen."
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with\n"
"a handful of dirt\n"
"or soil."

msgctxt "scene:17:133"
msgid ""
"Ich bin Westman und\n"
"nicht Gärtner."
msgstr ""
"I am a westman,\n"
"not a gardener."

msgctxt "scene:17:135"
msgid ""
"Der wäre bestimmt ein\n"
"gutes Brennmaterial,\n"
"doch für ein Lagerfeuer,\n"
"ist es nicht die richtige\n"
"Zeit."
msgstr ""
"That would surely make\n"
"good firewood, yet\n"
"for a campfire it is\n"
"not the right time\n"
"at present."

msgctxt "scene:17:140"
msgid ""
"Well, danke für das\n"
"Kompliment, aber der\n"
"ist selbst für mich\n"
"zu schwer."
msgstr ""
"Well, thanks for the\n"
"compliment, but that\n"
"is too heavy even for\n"
"me."

msgctxt "scene:17:144"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir nicht vor-\n"
"stellen, wozu ich das Ge-\n"
"strüpp brauchen könnte."
msgstr ""
"I cannot imagine what\n"
"I could possibly use\n"
"the scrub for."

msgctxt "scene:17:147"
msgid ""
"Ich finde der Baum\n"
"passt gut in diese\n"
"Gegend, ich lass ihn\n"
"stehen."
msgstr ""
"I think the tree fits\n"
"well into this area,\n"
"I shall leave it\n"
"standing."

msgctxt "scene:17:151"
msgid ""
"Ich habe schon davon gehört,\n"
"dass man mit seinen Pflanzen\n"
"reden soll, aber ich weiss\n"
"nicht...ist das hier ange-\n"
"bracht..?"
msgstr ""
"I have heard that one ought\n"
"to talk to one's plants,\n"
"yet I know not... is that\n"
"appropriate here..?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:156"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mit den Aesten\n"
"des Strauches nichts\n"
"anfangen, und ich glaube\n"
"kaum, dass die Blätter\n"
"einen guten Tee ergeben."
msgstr ""
"I can do nothing with the\n"
"branches of the shrub, and\n"
"I scarcely think the\n"
"leaves make good tea.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:161"
msgid ""
"Ich habe schon davon gehört,\n"
"dass man mit seinen Pflanzen\n"
"reden soll, aber ich weiss\n"
"nicht...ist das hier ange-\n"
"bracht..?"
msgstr ""
"I have heard that one ought\n"
"to talk to one's plants,\n"
"yet I know not... is that\n"
"appropriate here..?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:17:166"
msgid ""
"Ich habe schon davon gehört,\n"
"dass man mit seinen Pflanzen\n"
"reden soll, aber bei dem\n"
"nützt selbst das Reden nicht\n"
"mehr viel?"
msgstr ""
"I have heard that one ought\n"
"to talk to one's plants,\n"
"yet with this one even\n"
"talking will no longer do\n"
"much good?"

msgctxt "scene:17:171"
msgid ""
"Da soll es einen geben der\n"
"mit Steinen redet, aber ich\n"
"glaube der lebt jetzt nur\n"
"noch in einem Raum und trägt\n"
"eine Zwangsjacke....."
msgstr ""
"There is said to be someone\n"
"who talks to stones, but I\n"
"believe he now lives in a\n"
"single room and wears a\n"
"straitjacket....."

msgctxt "scene:18:0"
msgid "Irgendwo am Arkansas.."
msgstr "Somewhere on the Arkansas.."

msgctxt "scene:18:1"
msgid ""
"Männer, wir haben\n"
"unser Ziel fast er-\n"
"reicht! Etwas weiter\n"
"flussaufwärts lagern\n"
"die Rafters. Morgen,\n"
"noch vor Sonnenauf-\n"
"gang, werden wir die\n"
"Burschen besuchen."
msgstr ""
"Men, we have almost\n"
"reached our goal!\n"
"A little further\n"
"upstream the rafters\n"
"are camped. Tomorrow,\n"
"before sunrise, we\n"
"shall pay those\n"
"fellows a visit."

msgctxt "scene:18:9"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich richtig infor-\n"
"miert bin, wird dabei\n"
"für jeden von euch ein\n"
"nettes Sümmchen\n"
"herausspringen."
msgstr ""
"If I am informed\n"
"aright, a tidy sum\n"
"will be in it for\n"
"every one of you.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:14"
msgid ""
"Und was ist mit diesem\n"
"Old Firehand und der\n"
"verrückten Tante Droll?"
msgstr ""
"And what about this\n"
"Old Firehand and mad\n"
"Aunt Droll?"

msgctxt "scene:18:17"
msgid ""
"Macht euch über die\n"
"beiden keine Sorgen!\n"
"Bis die unser Lager\n"
"finden, sind wir schon\n"
"längst über alle Berge."
msgstr ""
"Do not worry about\n"
"the pair! By the time\n"
"they find our camp, we\n"
"shall be long gone\n"
"over the hills."

msgctxt "scene:18:22"
msgid ""
"Und sollten sie uns\n"
"doch in die Quere kom-\n"
"men, werden wir mit den\n"
"zwei Anfängern doch\n"
"wohl spielend fertig,\n"
"oder?"
msgstr ""
"And should they cross\n"
"our path after all, we\n"
"shall surely handle\n"
"those two beginners\n"
"with ease, shall we\n"
"not?"

msgctxt "scene:18:28"
msgid ""
"Ich habe aber schon die\n"
"tollsten Geschichten\n"
"über die Tante Droll\n"
"und Old Firehand\n"
"gehört. Mit denen ist\n"
"nicht zu spassen!"
msgstr ""
"Yet I have heard the\n"
"wildest tales about\n"
"Aunt Droll and Old\n"
"Firehand. They are\n"
"not to be trifled\n"
"with!"

msgctxt "scene:18:34"
msgid ""
"Jetzt zerbrecht euch\n"
"nicht meinen Kopf,\n"
"ihr Memmen! Passt lieber\n"
"auf, dass ihr mir den\n"
"Plan mit den Rafters\n"
"nicht versaut!"
msgstr ""
"Now do not worry your\n"
"heads, you cowards!\n"
"Mind rather that you\n"
"do not ruin my plan\n"
"with the rafters!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:40"
msgid ""
"...ist doch eine ideale\n"
"Nacht für unsere Vor-\n"
"bereitungen zum..."
msgstr ""
"...is an ideal\n"
"opportunity for...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:43"
msgid ""
"Seht mal her, was ich\n"
"hier gefunden habe..."
msgstr ""
"Look here at what I\n"
"have found..."

msgctxt "scene:18:45"
msgid ""
"Na, wen haben wir denn\n"
"da? Die berühmte Tante\n"
"Droll!? Nun hat sich\n"
"das Blatt wohl gewen-\n"
"det, was?"
msgstr ""
"Well, whom do we have\n"
"here? The famous Aunt\n"
"Droll!? Now the tables\n"
"have turned, eh?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:50"
msgid ""
"So trifft man Schurken\n"
"an Orten, wo man sie\n"
"am wenigsten erwartet\n"
"hätte."
msgstr ""
"So one meets villains\n"
"in places where one\n"
"least expected them.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:54"
msgid ""
"Wo ist denn dein\n"
"Freund, dieser\n"
"Firehand!? Der muss\n"
"ja auch irgendwo in\n"
"der Gegend herum-\n"
"lungern."
msgstr ""
"Where is your friend,\n"
"that Firehand!? He\n"
"must be loitering\n"
"somewhere about in\n"
"the area.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:60"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keine Ahnung\n"
"wo der sein könnte, wir\n"
"haben uns nach eurer\n"
"Flucht getrennt..."
msgstr ""
"I have no idea where\n"
"he might be, we parted\n"
"ways after your\n"
"escape..."

msgctxt "scene:18:64"
msgid ""
"Das stimmt Cornel, ich\n"
"habe nur ihn beim lau-\n"
"schen erwischt."
msgstr ""
"That is true Cornel, I\n"
"caught only him\n"
"eavesdropping."

msgctxt "scene:18:67"
msgid ""
"Da hat dir wohl dein\n"
"Freund Firehand die\n"
"Freundschaft gekündigt,\n"
"nahdem ich dir ent-\n"
"kommen bin."
msgstr ""
"Then your friend Firehand\n"
"must have broken off your\n"
"friendship after I\n"
"escaped from you.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:72"
msgid ""
"Los! Fesselt den Kerl\n"
"und dann werden wir\n"
"uns etwas Schlaf gön-\n"
"nen.\n"
"Um den werde ich mich\n"
"morgen selbst kümmern."
msgstr ""
"Come! Bind the fellow\n"
"and then we shall get\n"
"some sleep.\n"
"I shall deal with him\n"
"myself tomorrow.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:78"
msgid "He! Wer schiesst da?"
msgstr "Hey! Who is firing there?"

msgctxt "scene:18:79"
msgid ""
"Wir werden Ange-\n"
"griffen. Das sind\n"
"sicher die Rafters!"
msgstr ""
"We are under attack.\n"
"Those are surely the\n"
"rafters!"

msgctxt "scene:18:82"
msgid ""
"Lasst uns zu deren\n"
"Lager gehen. Der\n"
"Überfall wird nicht\n"
"erst morgen durch-\n"
"geführt. Das erledi-\n"
"gen wir gleich!"
msgstr ""
"Let us go to their\n"
"camp. The raid will\n"
"not be carried out\n"
"tomorrow. We shall do\n"
"it right now!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:88"
msgid ""
"Was ist denn hier los?\n"
"Wir haben Schüsse ge-\n"
"hört!"
msgstr ""
"What is going on here?\n"
"We heard gunshots!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:91"
msgid ""
"Hier lagerte eine\n"
"Gruppe von Tramps,\n"
"die diesem Herrn\n"
"hier nichts gutes\n"
"wollten. Ich habe\n"
"sie vertrieben."
msgstr ""
"A group of tramps\n"
"was camped here, and\n"
"meant no good to this\n"
"gentleman. I drove\n"
"them off.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:97"
msgid ""
"Wenn das nicht der\n"
"berühmte Mr. Fire-\n"
"hand ist. Seien Sie\n"
"uns gegrüsst, wir\n"
"sind Rafter und la-\n"
"gern etwas Flussauf-\n"
"wärts."
msgstr ""
"If that is not the\n"
"famous Mr. Firehand.\n"
"Greetings to you, we\n"
"are rafters and camped\n"
"a little upstream.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:104"
msgid ""
"Freut mich, Sie zu\n"
"sehen, Gentlemans.\n"
"In der Tat, ich bin\n"
"Old Firehand und\n"
"diesen ehrenwerten\n"
"Herrn nennt man die\n"
"Tante Droll."
msgstr ""
"Pleased to see you,\n"
"gentlemen. Indeed, I am\n"
"Old Firehand, and this\n"
"honourable gentleman is\n"
"called Aunt Droll.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:111"
msgid ""
"Sie haben sie ver-\n"
"trieben? Womit denn?\n"
"Ein Mann kann doch\n"
"höchstens mit zwei\n"
"Gewehren schiessen\n"
"und das klang mir\n"
"nach einer ganzen\n"
"Kavalerieschwadron."
msgstr ""
"You drove them off?\n"
"With what? A man can\n"
"at most shoot with two\n"
"rifles, and that sounded\n"
"to me like an entire\n"
"cavalry squadron.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:119"
msgid ""
"Ich habe die Gauner\n"
"getäuscht. Die Ge-\n"
"wehrschüsse waren\n"
"nichts weiter als\n"
"harmlose Knall-\n"
"frösche. Doch die\n"
"Tramps sind auf den\n"
"Trick hereingefal-\n"
"len."
msgstr ""
"I tricked the rogues.\n"
"The rifle shots were\n"
"nothing more than\n"
"harmless firecrackers.\n"
"Yet the tramps fell for\n"
"the trick.\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:128"
msgid ""
"Und mich hat der\n"
"Trick vor dem siche-\n"
"ren Tod gerettet."
msgstr ""
"And the trick saved me\n"
"from certain death.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:131"
msgid ""
"Aber wenn Sie die\n"
"Schurken nur ver-\n"
"trieben haben, dann\n"
"ist ja unser Lager\n"
"in Gefahr. Wir müssen\n"
"schnell die Verfol-\n"
"gung aufnehmen."
msgstr ""
"But if you only drove\n"
"the villains off, then\n"
"our camp is in danger.\n"
"We must quickly set off\n"
"in pursuit.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:138"
msgid ""
"Ich werde das Boot klar\n"
"machen, um die Verfol-\n"
"gung aufzunehmen..."
msgstr ""
"I shall make the boat\n"
"ready to take up the\n"
"pursuit..."

msgctxt "scene:18:141"
msgid "Halt! Wer da?"
msgstr "Halt! Who goes there?"

msgctxt "scene:18:142"
msgid ""
"Alarm!...Hands up oder\n"
"ich schiesse!"
msgstr ""
"Alarm!... Hands up or\n"
"I shoot!"

msgctxt "scene:18:144"
msgid ""
"Ah, sieh einer an, da\n"
"ist ja Old Firehand.\n"
"Na dir werden wir die\n"
"Flügel etwas stutzen."
msgstr ""
"Ah, look at that, there\n"
"is Old Firehand.\n"
"Well, we shall clip your\n"
"wings a bit."

msgctxt "scene:18:148"
msgid ""
"Der Baum bildet ein\n"
"richtiges Blätterdach\n"
"über dem Lagerplatz.\n"
"Die Tramps haben sich\n"
"diesen Platz gut aus-\n"
"gesucht."
msgstr ""
"The tree forms a real\n"
"canopy of leaves over\n"
"the campsite. The tramps\n"
"chose this spot well.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:154"
msgid ""
"An dieser Stelle ist\n"
"der Fluss ruhig und\n"
"ohne Stromschnellen."
msgstr ""
"At this point the\n"
"river is calm and without\n"
"rapids."

msgctxt "scene:18:157"
msgid ""
"Der Baum bietet eine\n"
"Deckung zum Lagerfeuer\n"
"hin."
msgstr ""
"The tree offers cover\n"
"towards the campfire.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:160"
msgid ""
"Ein grosses Lagerfeuer,\n"
"die Tramps müssen sich\n"
"sehr sicher sein..."
msgstr ""
"A large campfire,\n"
"the tramps must feel\n"
"very secure..."

msgctxt "scene:18:163"
msgid ""
"Hier liegt überall\n"
"Schwemmgut vom Fluss.\n"
"Ein grosser Ast..."
msgstr ""
"Flotsam from the river\n"
"lies everywhere here.\n"
"A large branch..."

msgctxt "scene:18:166"
msgid ""
"Das niedere Gestrüpp\n"
"entlang des Ufers zeugt\n"
"davon, dass der Fluss\n"
"öfters über seine Ufer\n"
"tritt."
msgstr ""
"The low scrub along\n"
"the bank shows that\n"
"the river often\n"
"overflows its banks.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:171"
msgid ""
"Ah, einige Büsche von der\n"
"Art, die bei der kleinsten\n"
"Berührung rascheln, so\n"
"hat man von der Seite des\n"
"Lagers eine natürliche Wache."
msgstr ""
"Ah, some bushes of the\n"
"kind that rustle at the\n"
"slightest touch, thus\n"
"providing a natural guard\n"
"for the camp."

msgctxt "scene:18:176"
msgid ""
"Felsen und grosse Steine\n"
"liegen hier überall herum.\n"
"Zum Teil sind sie schon\n"
"richtig vermoost..."
msgstr ""
"Rocks and large stones\n"
"lie all around here.\n"
"Some are already quite\n"
"overgrown with moss..."

msgctxt "scene:18:180"
msgid ""
"Der Baum bildet mit\n"
"seinen Blättern ein\n"
"Dach über dem Lager.\n"
"Er wird den Morgentau\n"
"etwas abhalten."
msgstr ""
"The tree forms a roof\n"
"over the camp with its\n"
"leaves. It will keep\n"
"off the morning dew a\n"
"little."

msgctxt "scene:18:185"
msgid "Ich bin nicht durstig."
msgstr "I am not thirsty."

msgctxt "scene:18:186"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mit einem\n"
"Baum nicht sehr viel\n"
"anfangen. Abgesehen\n"
"davon, würde er mich\n"
"sicher etwas behin-\n"
"dern."
msgstr ""
"I cannot do much with a\n"
"tree. Apart from that,\n"
"it would surely hinder\n"
"me somewhat.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:192"
msgid ""
"Da könnte ich mir in\n"
"doppelter Hinsicht die\n"
"Finger verbrennen,\n"
"wenn ich jetzt ans\n"
"Feuer will."
msgstr ""
"I could burn my fingers\n"
"in two ways if I were\n"
"to go to the fire\n"
"now.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:197"
msgid ""
"An den komme ich\n"
"jetzt nicht heran."
msgstr ""
"I cannot reach that\n"
"one right now."

msgctxt "scene:18:199"
msgid ""
"Das Gestrüpp ist,\n"
"ausser zum ver-\n"
"brennen, zu nichts\n"
"zu gebrauchen."
msgstr ""
"The scrub is of no use,\n"
"except for burning.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:203"
msgid ""
"Das Gestrüpp ist,\n"
"ausser zum ver-\n"
"brennen, zu nichts\n"
"zu gebrauchen."
msgstr ""
"The scrub is of no use,\n"
"except for burning.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:207"
msgid "Die sind mir zu schwer"
msgstr "They are too heavy for me."

msgctxt "scene:18:208"
msgid ""
"Der bestbekannte Schurke,\n"
"unser Cornel."
msgstr ""
"The well-known rogue,\n"
"our Cornel."

msgctxt "scene:18:210"
msgid "Raschel!"
msgstr "Rustle!"

msgctxt "scene:18:211"
msgid "Was war denn das?"
msgstr "What was that?"

msgctxt "scene:18:212"
msgid ""
"Hat wieder einer\n"
"feuchtes Holz ins\n"
"Feuer getan."
msgstr ""
"Someone put damp wood\n"
"into the fire again.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:215"
msgid ""
"Dieser Tramp scheint\n"
"seine Aufgabe nicht allzu\n"
"ernst zu nehmen."
msgstr ""
"This tramp seems not to\n"
"take his task too\n"
"seriously."

msgctxt "scene:18:218"
msgid ""
"Das ist einer der drei\n"
"Gesellen des Cornel."
msgstr ""
"That is one of Cornel's\n"
"three companions."

msgctxt "scene:18:220"
msgid ""
"Der Tramp schläft so\n"
"fest, den kann wahr-\n"
"scheinlich nur ein\n"
"Kanonenschuss wecken."
msgstr ""
"The tramp sleeps so soundly\n"
"that likely only a cannon\n"
"shot could awaken him.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:18:224"
msgid ""
"Ich stehe zu weit weg,\n"
"um sicher zu sein, dass\n"
"ich das Feuer treffe.\n"
"Und das Risiko, gesehen\n"
"zu werden, ist sehr gross."
msgstr ""
"I am standing too far away\n"
"to be sure I hit the fire.\n"
"And the risk of being seen\n"
"is very great.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:19:0"
msgid ""
"Man sieht beinahe den\n"
"Wald vor lauter Bäumen\n"
"nicht mehr."
msgstr ""
"One can scarcely see the\n"
"wood for the trees.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:19:3"
msgid ""
"Das Buschwerk säumt\n"
"den Pfad wie eine\n"
"dichte und undurch-\n"
"dringliche Wand."
msgstr ""
"The bushes line the path\n"
"like a dense and\n"
"impenetrable wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:19:7"
msgid ""
"Steinige Wege, ja eigent-\n"
"lich nur Trampelpfade,\n"
"führen in alle Richtungen."
msgstr ""
"Stony paths, indeed only\n"
"beaten tracks, lead in all\n"
"directions."

msgctxt "scene:19:10"
msgid ""
"So oft scheint der Weg\n"
"nicht begangen zu werden,\n"
"überall auf dem Pfad\n"
"wachsen Grasbüschel."
msgstr ""
"The path seems not to be\n"
"trodden often; tufts of\n"
"grass grow everywhere\n"
"upon the trail."

msgctxt "scene:19:14"
msgid ""
"Ein Stein, die Gegend\n"
"scheint nicht gerade\n"
"geeignet für den Acker-\n"
"bau."
msgstr ""
"A stone, the area seems\n"
"scarcely suited for\n"
"agriculture.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:19:18"
msgid ""
"Ich bin ein Westman,\n"
"und kein Rafter. Ich\n"
"kann mit einem Baum\n"
"nichts anfangen."
msgstr ""
"I am a westman, not a\n"
"rafter. I can do nothing\n"
"with a tree.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:19:22"
msgid ""
"Das Gestrüpp kann kaum\n"
"von Nutzen sein."
msgstr ""
"The scrub can scarcely\n"
"be of use."

msgctxt "scene:19:24"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit einem\n"
"Weg anfangen?"
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with\n"
"a path?"

msgctxt "scene:19:26"
msgid ""
"Ein Gärtner wäre mit\n"
"deinen Aufträgen ent-\n"
"zückt."
msgstr ""
"A gardener would be\n"
"delighted with your\n"
"orders."

msgctxt "scene:19:29"
msgid ""
"Ich kann damit nichts\n"
"anfangen, ausser bei\n"
"dir ist die Sammel-\n"
"leidenschaft ausge-\n"
"brochen, doch das\n"
"möchte ich vermeiden."
msgstr ""
"I can do nothing with it,\n"
"unless a passion for\n"
"collecting has broken out\n"
"in you, but I wish to\n"
"avoid that.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:0"
msgid "Grrrr..."
msgstr "Grrrr..."

msgctxt "scene:20:1"
msgid ""
"Das kenn ich doch\n"
"irgendwoher..."
msgstr ""
"I know that from\n"
"somewhere..."

msgctxt "scene:20:3"
msgid ""
"So, den wäre ich endlich\n"
"los..."
msgstr ""
"There, I am finally rid\n"
"of that one..."

msgctxt "scene:20:5"
msgid ""
"Von hier kann ich\n"
"die Mütze nicht\n"
"richtig werfen, um\n"
"den Hund abzulenken!"
msgstr ""
"From here I cannot throw\n"
"the cap properly to\n"
"distract the dog!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:9"
msgid ""
"Ein düsterer und undurch-\n"
"dringlicher Wald. Gut,\n"
"dass es hier Pfade gibt!"
msgstr ""
"A gloomy and impenetrable\n"
"forest. Good that there\n"
"are paths here!"

msgctxt "scene:20:12"
msgid ""
"Ein knorriger, abgestor-\n"
"bener Baum."
msgstr ""
"A gnarled, dead\n"
"tree."

msgctxt "scene:20:14"
msgid ""
"Ein Seil, dient als Wäsche-\n"
"leine."
msgstr ""
"A rope, serving as a\n"
"clothesline."

msgctxt "scene:20:16"
msgid ""
"Heute scheint grosser\n"
"Waschtag zu sein."
msgstr ""
"Today seems to be a big\n"
"washday."

msgctxt "scene:20:18"
msgid ""
"Naja, englischer Rasen\n"
"ist dies nicht gerade."
msgstr ""
"Well, this is hardly an\n"
"English lawn."

msgctxt "scene:20:20"
msgid ""
"Ja, mangels Baum, muss\n"
"ein Stock diese Seite\n"
"der Wäscheleine halten."
msgstr ""
"For lack of a tree, a\n"
"stick must hold this side\n"
"of the clothesline."

msgctxt "scene:20:23"
msgid ""
"Der steinige Trampelpfad\n"
"ist sicherlich mühsam von\n"
"den Rafters in den Wald\n"
"gehauen worden."
msgstr ""
"The stony trail was\n"
"surely laboriously cut into\n"
"the forest by the\n"
"rafters."

msgctxt "scene:20:27"
msgid ""
"Eine sauber gezimmerte\n"
"Blockhütte, die die\n"
"Rafters hier hingestellt\n"
"haben. Sieht mir sehr\n"
"stabil aus."
msgstr ""
"A neatly built log cabin\n"
"that the rafters put up\n"
"here. Looks very sturdy to\n"
"me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:32"
msgid ""
"Der ganze Pfad wird von\n"
"undurchdringlichem Gebüsch\n"
"gesäumt."
msgstr ""
"The entire path is lined\n"
"by impenetrable\n"
"bushes."

msgctxt "scene:20:35"
msgid ""
"Eine massive Holztüre\n"
"soll wohl vor ungebete-\n"
"nen Gästen schützen."
msgstr ""
"A solid wooden door is\n"
"meant to protect against\n"
"uninvited guests."

msgctxt "scene:20:38"
msgid ""
"Das Fenster ist durch\n"
"einen massiven Bretter-\n"
"verschlag geschützt."
msgstr ""
"The window is protected\n"
"by a solid wooden\n"
"boarding."

msgctxt "scene:20:41"
msgid ""
"Eine eigenartige Konstruk-\n"
"tion diese Hundehütte..."
msgstr ""
"A peculiar construction,\n"
"this doghouse..."

msgctxt "scene:20:43"
msgid ""
"Eine Hundehütte die direkt\n"
"an das Haus angebaut ist."
msgstr ""
"A doghouse built directly\n"
"onto the house."

msgctxt "scene:20:45"
msgid ""
"In den Wald kann man nicht\n"
"vor lauter Gestrüpp und ich\n"
"brauche auch nichts von dem\n"
"soweit ich das sehen kann."
msgstr ""
"One cannot enter the forest\n"
"for the scrub, and I need\n"
"nothing from it, as far as\n"
"I can see."

msgctxt "scene:20:49"
msgid ""
"Bis zum Winter ist lange\n"
"Zeit, also werde ich noch\n"
"etwas damit warten, Kamin-\n"
"holz zu machen."
msgstr ""
"It is a long time until\n"
"winter, so I shall wait\n"
"a while before making\n"
"firewood."

msgctxt "scene:20:53"
msgid ""
"Ich werde das Wäscheseil\n"
"nicht nehmen. Es ist zum\n"
"Einen durch die Feuchtig-\n"
"keit schon ganz morsch\n"
"und dann glaube ich nicht,\n"
"dass die Rafters Freude\n"
"daran haben, wenn die\n"
"Trockenvorrichtung kaputt\n"
"gemacht wird."
msgstr ""
"I shall not take the\n"
"clothesline. For one,\n"
"it is quite rotten from\n"
"the moisture, and then\n"
"I do not think the\n"
"rafters would be pleased\n"
"if their drying rig\n"
"were destroyed.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:62"
msgid ""
"Fussball kennen wir noch\n"
"nicht, und nach Gold zu\n"
"graben, bringt hier eben-\n"
"falls nichts."
msgstr ""
"Football is unknown to\n"
"us as yet, and digging\n"
"for gold here yields\n"
"nothing either."

msgctxt "scene:20:66"
msgid ""
"Den Stock lass ich stehen,\n"
"es ist mir zu mühsam den\n"
"auszugraben. Wenn wir wirk-\n"
"lich einen brauchen, dann\n"
"suchen wir uns einen\n"
"anderen."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the stick,\n"
"it is too troublesome to\n"
"dig up. If we really\n"
"need one, we shall\n"
"look for another.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:72"
msgid ""
"Die Blockhütte kann ich\n"
"nicht verwenden und ich\n"
"glaube nicht, dass ich\n"
"sie irgendwie beschädigen\n"
"soll, oder!?"
msgstr ""
"I cannot use the log\n"
"cabin, and I do not\n"
"think I should damage\n"
"it in any way, should I!?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:77"
msgid ""
"Dieses Gestrüpp ist zu\n"
"nichts nütze."
msgstr ""
"This scrub is of no\n"
"use whatsoever."

msgctxt "scene:20:79"
msgid ""
"Oho, die Tür ist fest\n"
"verschlossen, da gibt\n"
"es keine Aussicht auf\n"
"Einlass."
msgstr ""
"Oho, the door is tightly\n"
"locked; there is no\n"
"prospect of gaining\n"
"entry."

msgctxt "scene:20:83"
msgid ""
"Well, durch das Fenster\n"
"komme ich nicht in das\n"
"Haus, das ist fest mit\n"
"schweren Brettern ver-\n"
"rammelt."
msgstr ""
"Well, through the window\n"
"I cannot enter the house;\n"
"it is barricaded with\n"
"heavy boards.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:88"
msgid ""
"Oh nein, dem Fenster\n"
"komme ich nicht zu\n"
"nahe, so lange der\n"
"Hund da ist."
msgstr ""
"Oh no, I shall not go\n"
"near the window as long\n"
"as the dog is there.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:20:92"
msgid ""
"Der Hundehütte werde ich\n"
"nicht zu nahe kommen, denn\n"
"der Hund sieht mir nicht\n"
"aus, als ob er spassen würde."
msgstr ""
"I shall not get too close to\n"
"the doghouse, for the dog\n"
"does not look to me as if he\n"
"were joking."

msgctxt "scene:20:96"
msgid ""
"Well, der Hund ist weg,\n"
"aber was soll ich mit\n"
"einer Hundehütte?"
msgstr ""
"Well, the dog is gone, but\n"
"what am I to do with a\n"
"doghouse?"

msgctxt "scene:21:0"
msgid ""
"Pshaw, das war ganz schön\n"
"eng da unten... Aber die\n"
"Idee mit dem Geheimgang\n"
"ist gut."
msgstr ""
"Pshaw, that was quite\n"
"tight down there... But\n"
"the idea with the secret\n"
"passage is good."

msgctxt "scene:21:4"
msgid ""
"Ach, das Schloss am\n"
"Koffer ist kaputt!"
msgstr ""
"Ah, the lock on the\n"
"trunk is broken!"

msgctxt "scene:21:6"
msgid ""
"Oh, ich glaube ich habe\n"
"etwas gefunden... Ein\n"
"Schürhaken."
msgstr ""
"Oh, I believe I have\n"
"found something...\n"
"A poker."

msgctxt "scene:21:9"
msgid ""
"Ausser Asche sehe ich\n"
"da nichts mehr, und die\n"
"nützt mir nichts!"
msgstr ""
"Except for ashes I see\n"
"nothing more, and that\n"
"is of no use to me!"

msgctxt "scene:21:12"
msgid "Was soll ich mit der Asche?"
msgstr "What am I to do with the ashes?"

msgctxt "scene:21:13"
msgid ""
"Die Asche nutzt mir wirk-\n"
"lich nichts."
msgstr ""
"The ashes really do me\n"
"no good."

msgctxt "scene:21:15"
msgid ""
"Ein gemauerter Kamin.\n"
"Da liegt noch die Asche\n"
"d'rin."
msgstr ""
"A brick fireplace. The\n"
"ashes are still lying\n"
"inside."

msgctxt "scene:21:18"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, da liegt\n"
"noch irgendetwas d'rin!"
msgstr ""
"I believe something is\n"
"still lying in there!"

msgctxt "scene:21:20"
msgid ""
"Da sind nur noch Asche\n"
"und Kohlereste d'rin."
msgstr ""
"Only ashes and charcoal\n"
"remains are left inside."

msgctxt "scene:21:22"
msgid ""
"Die Asche ist viel zu\n"
"heiss, um darin herum\n"
"zu wühlen."
msgstr ""
"The ashes are far too\n"
"hot to rummage about\n"
"inside."

msgctxt "scene:21:25"
msgid ""
"Eine Luke mit einem Seil.\n"
"Die führt in eine Dach-\n"
"kammer."
msgstr ""
"A hatch with a rope.\n"
"It leads into an attic\n"
"chamber."

msgctxt "scene:21:28"
msgid ""
"Mit den zur Verfügung\n"
"stehenden Mitteln, wurde\n"
"der Raum recht gemüt-\n"
"lich eingerichtet.\n"
"Dabei fällt mir auf,\n"
"dass die Hütte gar keine\n"
"Tür hat."
msgstr ""
"With the available means,\n"
"the room was furnished\n"
"quite cosily. At that, it\n"
"strikes me that the cabin\n"
"has no door at all.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:35"
msgid ""
"Die ist nur eine Atrappe\n"
"von aussen, um ungebetene\n"
"Gäste abzuhalten. Eine\n"
"gute Idee."
msgstr ""
"It is merely a dummy from\n"
"the outside to keep away\n"
"uninvited guests. A good\n"
"idea."

msgctxt "scene:21:39"
msgid ""
"Ein Vogelkäfig, sein\n"
"Insasse ist wohl ent-\n"
"fleucht."
msgstr ""
"A birdcage; its inmate\n"
"has likely escaped.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:42"
msgid ""
"Weit können die Besitzer\n"
"nicht sein, denn die\n"
"Lampe haben sie brennen\n"
"lassen."
msgstr ""
"The owners cannot be far,\n"
"for they left the lamp\n"
"burning.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:46"
msgid ""
"Ein Whiskyglas steht\n"
"auf dem Tisch."
msgstr ""
"A whisky glass stands\n"
"upon the table."

msgctxt "scene:21:48"
msgid ""
"Ein, aus grob gehauenen\n"
"Brettern, gezimmerter\n"
"Tisch."
msgstr ""
"A table crafted from\n"
"roughly hewn boards.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:51"
msgid "Ein schweres Eichenfass."
msgstr "A heavy oak barrel."

msgctxt "scene:21:52"
msgid ""
"Der Deckel zum Einstieg\n"
"in den Geheimgang."
msgstr ""
"The hatch for entering\n"
"the secret passage."

msgctxt "scene:21:54"
msgid ""
"Eine grosse Seekiste.\n"
"Sie ist fest ver-\n"
"schlossen."
msgstr ""
"A large sea chest.\n"
"It is firmly locked.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:57"
msgid ""
"Eine Whiskeyflasche.\n"
"Da ist auch noch etwas\n"
"d'rin."
msgstr ""
"A whisky bottle. There\n"
"is still something inside\n"
"it."

msgctxt "scene:21:60"
msgid ""
"Eine Flasche, doch die\n"
"ist leider leer."
msgstr ""
"A bottle, but it is\n"
"unfortunately empty."

msgctxt "scene:21:62"
msgid ""
"Ein Bett, oder eher\n"
"nur eine Pritsche."
msgstr ""
"A bed, or rather\n"
"merely a cot."

msgctxt "scene:21:64"
msgid ""
"Ein schäbiger Koffer.\n"
"Muss ein reisefreudiger\n"
"Mensch sein."
msgstr ""
"A shabby suitcase. Must\n"
"be a person fond of\n"
"travel."

msgctxt "scene:21:67"
msgid ""
"Die Fensterscheiben\n"
"müssten wieder einmal\n"
"gereinigt werden."
msgstr ""
"The windowpanes ought\n"
"to be cleaned once\n"
"again."

msgctxt "scene:21:70"
msgid ""
"Dies ist der Einstieg\n"
"zum Geheimgang nach\n"
"draussen."
msgstr ""
"This is the entrance to\n"
"the secret passage\n"
"leading outside."

msgctxt "scene:21:73"
msgid ""
"An die Luke komm ich\n"
"so nicht heran."
msgstr ""
"I cannot reach the hatch\n"
"in this manner."

msgctxt "scene:21:75"
msgid ""
"Der Käfig hängt zu hoch\n"
"um ihn herunter nehmen\n"
"zu können."
msgstr ""
"The cage hangs too high\n"
"to be taken down.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:78"
msgid ""
"Sie brennt ja, aber nehmen\n"
"darf ich die nicht. Hier\n"
"in der Wildnis ist so eine\n"
"Oellampe zu wertvoll."
msgstr ""
"It is burning, but I may\n"
"not take it. Here in the\n"
"wilderness an oil lamp is\n"
"too valuable."

msgctxt "scene:21:82"
msgid ""
"Ich trinke meinen Whiskey\n"
"immer aus der Flasche."
msgstr ""
"I always drink my whisky\n"
"straight from the bottle."

msgctxt "scene:21:84"
msgid ""
"Der Tisch ist viel zu\n"
"schwer für mich."
msgstr ""
"The table is far too\n"
"heavy for me."

msgctxt "scene:21:86"
msgid ""
"Der Trinkwasservorrat,\n"
"aber mir steht jetzt\n"
"nicht der Sinn nach\n"
"Wasser."
msgstr ""
"The drinking water supply,\n"
"yet my mind is not set upon\n"
"water right now.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:90"
msgid ""
"Der Deckel zum Einstieg\n"
"in den Geheimgang ist\n"
"verklemmt. Das Holz hat\n"
"wohl noch etwas gear-\n"
"beitet."
msgstr ""
"The cover for the entry\n"
"to the secret passage is\n"
"jammed. The wood has\n"
"likely worked a bit.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:95"
msgid ""
"Die Kiste ist fest\n"
"verschlossen, und ohne\n"
"Werkzeug oder besser\n"
"die Schlüssel, ist die\n"
"nicht aufzukriegen."
msgstr ""
"The chest is firmly locked,\n"
"and without tools, or\n"
"better yet the key, it\n"
"cannot be opened.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:100"
msgid ""
"Ich kann jetzt nicht\n"
"schlafen, es steht zu\n"
"viel auf dem Spiel."
msgstr ""
"I cannot sleep now, there\n"
"is far too much at stake.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:103"
msgid ""
"Ich lass die Fenster\n"
"besser verschlossen,\n"
"dann sieht man mich\n"
"von draussen nicht."
msgstr ""
"I had better keep the\n"
"windows closed, so I am\n"
"not seen from outside.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:107"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit einer\n"
"leeren Flasche, die\n"
"lass ich besser stehen."
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with an\n"
"empty bottle? I had\n"
"better leave it be."

msgctxt "scene:21:110"
msgid ""
"Na, der Käfig passt\n"
"aber nicht in den\n"
"Koffer."
msgstr ""
"Well, the cage does\n"
"not fit into the\n"
"trunk."

msgctxt "scene:21:113"
msgid ""
"Was für eine Kombina-\n"
"tion, Koffer und Luke -\n"
"funktioniert nur nicht,\n"
"sehr tragisch..."
msgstr ""
"What a combination,\n"
"trunk and hatch -\n"
"only it does not work,\n"
"very tragic..."

msgctxt "scene:21:117"
msgid ""
"So tragisch ist das\n"
"Problem aber auch\n"
"nicht, dass ich mich\n"
"gerade mit dem Gürtel\n"
"an der Luke aufhän-\n"
"gen muss."
msgstr ""
"The problem is not so\n"
"tragic, however, that\n"
"I must hang myself\n"
"from the hatch with\n"
"my belt.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:21:123"
msgid ""
"Der Haken an dem der\n"
"Käfig hängt, ist zu\n"
"schwach um sich daran\n"
"aufzuhängen..."
msgstr ""
"The hook from which\n"
"the cage hangs is too\n"
"weak to hang oneself\n"
"from..."

msgctxt "scene:21:127"
msgid ""
"Auf den Koffer kann\n"
"ich so nicht d'rauf-\n"
"steigen, da fallen\n"
"alle Kleider raus.\n"
"Das Schloss am Koffer\n"
"ist ja defekt."
msgstr ""
"I cannot step upon\n"
"the trunk like that,\n"
"for all the clothes\n"
"would fall out.\n"
"The lock on the trunk\n"
"is broken, after all."

msgctxt "scene:21:133"
msgid ""
"Wie soll ich auf einen\n"
"offenen Koffer steigen.\n"
"Da sich das Schloss\n"
"nicht schliessen lässt,\n"
"würden nur die Kleider\n"
"herausfallen."
msgstr ""
"How am I to step upon\n"
"an open trunk. Since\n"
"the lock cannot be\n"
"closed, the clothes\n"
"would merely fall\n"
"out."

msgctxt "scene:21:139"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tue, schiesst\n"
"sicher eine Stichflamme aus\n"
"dem Kamin und verpasst mir\n"
"die Rasur des Lebens."
msgstr ""
"If I do that, a jet of\n"
"flame will shoot from\n"
"the chimney and give me\n"
"the shave of a lifetime."

msgctxt "scene:22:0"
msgid ""
"In dieser Komode ist\n"
"ausser Staub und to-\n"
"ten Käfern nichts zu\n"
"finden."
msgstr ""
"In this chest of drawers\n"
"nothing is to be found\n"
"except dust and dead\n"
"beetles."

msgctxt "scene:22:4"
msgid ""
"Oh, eine Schachtel. Das\n"
"Packpapier ist bereits\n"
"aufgerissen, das zerknüll' \n"
"ich einfach...Hoppla,\n"
"jetzt ist es mir auch noch\n"
"runtergefallen und unter\n"
"den Schrank gerollt. Ach,\n"
"dort stört es niemanden."
msgstr ""
"Oh, a box. The wrapping\n"
"paper is torn open\n"
"already, I shall just\n"
"crumple it up... Oops,\n"
"now I have dropped it as\n"
"well and it rolled under\n"
"the wardrobe. Ah, it\n"
"bothers no one there."

msgctxt "scene:22:12"
msgid "Im Schrank herrscht Leere!"
msgstr "Emptiness reigns in the wardrobe!"

msgctxt "scene:22:13"
msgid ""
"Der Bewohner dieser Hütte\n"
"ist ein etwas eigener Ge-\n"
"selle. Hier liegt ein an-\n"
"geschimmeltes Brot d'rin.\n"
"Ich nehme es trotzdem, man\n"
"kann ja nie wissen wozu es\n"
"gut ist..."
msgstr ""
"The occupant of this cabin\n"
"is a peculiar fellow. A\n"
"mouldy loaf of bread is\n"
"in here. I shall take it\n"
"nevertheless, one never\n"
"knows what it might be\n"
"good for..."

msgctxt "scene:22:20"
msgid ""
"In der Tasche ist nichts\n"
"mehr weiter d'rinn."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing more in\n"
"the bag."

msgctxt "scene:22:22"
msgid ""
"Under dem Schrank liegt\n"
"das zerknüllte Packpapier\n"
"der Schachtel."
msgstr ""
"Under the wardrobe lies\n"
"the crumpled wrapping\n"
"paper of the box."

msgctxt "scene:22:25"
msgid ""
"So komme ich an das Pa-\n"
"pier nicht heran, es liegt\n"
"zu weit hinten."
msgstr ""
"I cannot reach the\n"
"paper like this; it lies\n"
"too far behind."

msgctxt "scene:22:28"
msgid ""
"Das Messer ist zu kurz,\n"
"um an das Papier heran-\n"
"zukommen."
msgstr ""
"The knife is too short\n"
"to reach the paper.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:31"
msgid ""
"Der Axtstiel ist zu dick,\n"
"um unter den Schrank zu\n"
"kommen."
msgstr ""
"The axe handle is too\n"
"thick to get under the\n"
"wardrobe."

msgctxt "scene:22:34"
msgid ""
"Massive Stützbalken\n"
"tragen das Dach."
msgstr ""
"Massive support beams\n"
"carry the roof."

msgctxt "scene:22:36"
msgid ""
"Ein alter, zweitüriger\n"
"Schrank, der wohl aus\n"
"dem Schlafzimmer stammte."
msgstr ""
"An old two-door wardrobe\n"
"that likely came from the\n"
"bedroom."

msgctxt "scene:22:39"
msgid ""
"Ein Schrank, der dem auf\n"
"dem Schiff sehr stark\n"
"gleicht."
msgstr ""
"A wardrobe that closely\n"
"resembles the one on the\n"
"ship."

msgctxt "scene:22:42"
msgid ""
"Eine Treppe, die wohl\n"
"noch nicht zum Ein-\n"
"satz gekommen ist."
msgstr ""
"A staircase that has\n"
"likely not been put to\n"
"use as yet."

msgctxt "scene:22:45"
msgid ""
"Zwei leere Flaschen\n"
"liegen da herum."
msgstr ""
"Two empty bottles lie\n"
"about there."

msgctxt "scene:22:47"
msgid ""
"Ein alter Wasserkrug,\n"
"der bereits ein Loch\n"
"hat."
msgstr ""
"An old water jug that\n"
"has a hole in it\n"
"already."

msgctxt "scene:22:50"
msgid ""
"Eine schon fast abge-\n"
"brannte Kerze."
msgstr ""
"A candle that is almost\n"
"burnt down."

msgctxt "scene:22:52"
msgid ""
"Ein Bärenfell, das\n"
"wohl schon etwas\n"
"feucht geworden ist,\n"
"denn es modert bereits."
msgstr ""
"A bearskin that has\n"
"likely grown damp,\n"
"for it is rotting\n"
"already."

msgctxt "scene:22:56"
msgid ""
"Ein Seekoffer, wie er\n"
"unten im Raum steht."
msgstr ""
"A sea trunk like the\n"
"one down in the room."

msgctxt "scene:22:58"
msgid ""
"Die Luke, runter in\n"
"den anderen Raum."
msgstr ""
"The hatch down into\n"
"the other room."

msgctxt "scene:22:60"
msgid ""
"Ein kleines Schränkchen\n"
"mit zwei Schubladen."
msgstr ""
"A small cabinet with\n"
"two drawers."

msgctxt "scene:22:62"
msgid ""
"Ein Fass, die muss er\n"
"früher wohl zum Sammeln\n"
"von Trinkwasser ver-\n"
"wendet haben."
msgstr ""
"A barrel he must have\n"
"used in former times for\n"
"collecting drinking\n"
"water."

msgctxt "scene:22:66"
msgid ""
"Eine Stofftasche,wie\n"
"sie von Ärzten und\n"
"Handelsreisenden oft\n"
"benutzt werden."
msgstr ""
"A cloth bag such as is\n"
"oft used by doctors and\n"
"commercial travellers.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:70"
msgid ""
"Ein Haufen nutzloses\n"
"Zeug liegt hier herum.\n"
"Nur lauter Gerümpel,\n"
"scheint ein leiden-\n"
"schaftlicher Sammler\n"
"zu sein."
msgstr ""
"A heap of useless stuff\n"
"lies about here. Merely\n"
"clutter; he seems to be\n"
"a passionate collector.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:76"
msgid ""
"Den Balken kann ich\n"
"nicht mitnehmen, da\n"
"würde ja das Dach\n"
"einstürzen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot take the beam,\n"
"for the roof would\n"
"collapse then.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:80"
msgid ""
"Die Holztreppe könnte\n"
"bei einem Hausbau\n"
"sicher nützlich sein,\n"
"aber nur zum herum-\n"
"schleppen ist sie\n"
"einfach zu schwer."
msgstr ""
"The wooden stairs could\n"
"surely be useful when\n"
"building a house, but\n"
"merely to lug around\n"
"they are simply too\n"
"heavy."

msgctxt "scene:22:86"
msgid ""
"Leider ist die Flasche\n"
"bereits leer, sonst\n"
"hätte ich mir einen\n"
"Schluck genehmigt."
msgstr ""
"Regrettably the bottle\n"
"is empty already, else\n"
"I would have taken a\n"
"swig."

msgctxt "scene:22:90"
msgid ""
"Nein, der hat ja schon\n"
"ein Loch, den lasse ich\n"
"stehen."
msgstr ""
"No, it has a hole in it\n"
"already, I shall leave\n"
"it be."

msgctxt "scene:22:93"
msgid ""
"Die ist beinahe schon\n"
"runtergebrannt, dafür\n"
"lohnt es sich nicht,\n"
"über das ganze Gerüm-\n"
"pel zu klettern."
msgstr ""
"It is almost burnt down,\n"
"it is not worth climbing\n"
"over all the junk for\n"
"that.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:98"
msgid ""
"Den vermoderten Fetzen\n"
"lass ich liegen, der\n"
"kann mir nicht von\n"
"Nutzen sein."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the rotten\n"
"rag; it can be of no use\n"
"to me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:102"
msgid ""
"Der Koffer ist mit einem\n"
"grossen Schloss fest ver-\n"
"schlossen. Ich möchte ihn\n"
"nicht aufbrechen."
msgstr ""
"The trunk is firmly\n"
"locked with a large lock.\n"
"I do not wish to break\n"
"it open."

msgctxt "scene:22:106"
msgid ""
"Das Fass ist schwer,\n"
"und Wasservorräte\n"
"muss ich nicht mit-\n"
"nehmen, nachdem der\n"
"Fluss gerade nur ein\n"
"paar Schritte ent-\n"
"fernt ist."
msgstr ""
"The barrel is heavy, and\n"
"I need not carry water\n"
"supplies, since the\n"
"river is but a few steps\n"
"away.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:22:113"
msgid ""
"All das alte Zeug ist\n"
"nutzlos und braucht nur\n"
"viel Platz..."
msgstr ""
"All that old stuff is\n"
"useless and only takes\n"
"up much room..."

msgctxt "scene:23:0"
msgid ""
"HALT!\n"
"Stehenbleiben, oder ich\n"
"schiesse!"
msgstr ""
"HALT!\n"
"Stand still, or I\n"
"shoot!"

msgctxt "scene:23:3"
msgid ""
"Aha, wolltest dich\n"
"wohl an meinem \n"
"Wagen zu schaffen\n"
"machen?"
msgstr ""
"Aha, wanted to meddle\n"
"with my wagon, did\n"
"you?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:7"
msgid ""
"Wo denken sie hin,\n"
"guter Mann. Ich bin\n"
"zufällig auf ihren\n"
"Lagerplatz gestossen."
msgstr ""
"Whatever are you\n"
"thinking, good man. I\n"
"happen to have stumbled\n"
"upon your campsite."

msgctxt "scene:23:11"
msgid ""
"Und was treibst du\n"
"dich dann so heim-\n"
"lich hier herum?"
msgstr ""
"And what are you doing\n"
"prowling about here so\n"
"secretly then?"

msgctxt "scene:23:14"
msgid ""
"Ah, Sie schon wieder!\n"
"Haben Sie sich die Ant-\n"
"wort überlegt?"
msgstr ""
"Ah, you again! Have\n"
"you thought over your\n"
"answer?"

msgctxt "scene:23:17"
msgid ""
"1. Ich bin ganz\n"
"   zufällig hier."
msgstr ""
"1. I am here purely\n"
"   by chance."

msgctxt "scene:23:19"
msgid ""
"2. Ich habe sie\n"
"   gesucht."
msgstr ""
"2. I was looking for\n"
"   you."

msgctxt "scene:23:21"
msgid ""
"3. Gangster haben\n"
"   meinen Freund\n"
"   gefangen."
msgstr ""
"3. Gangsters have\n"
"   captured my\n"
"   friend."

msgctxt "scene:23:24"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:25"
msgid ""
"Zufällig?! Raus' mit\n"
"der Sprache, was\n"
"wollen sie hier?"
msgstr ""
"By chance?! Out with\n"
"it, what do you want\n"
"here?"

msgctxt "scene:23:28"
msgid ""
"Mich gesucht? Ich\n"
"kenne sie ja gar\n"
"nicht, Freundchen!\n"
"Also, warum sollten\n"
"sie mich hier im\n"
"Wald suchen, hä?"
msgstr ""
"Looking for me? I do\n"
"not know you at all,\n"
"my friend! So why\n"
"should you look for me\n"
"here in the forest,\n"
"eh?"

msgctxt "scene:23:34"
msgid ""
"Und die Geschichte\n"
"soll ich dir glau-\n"
"ben? Pah! Denk dir\n"
"schnell was Besse-\n"
"res aus!"
msgstr ""
"And I am to believe\n"
"that story? Pah! Think\n"
"of something better\n"
"quick!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:39"
msgid ""
"Sieh nur zu, dass\n"
"du hier verschwin-\n"
"dest!"
msgstr ""
"Just see that you\n"
"get away from\n"
"here!"

msgctxt "scene:23:42"
msgid ""
"1. Mein Name ist\n"
"   Old Firehand."
msgstr ""
"1. My name is\n"
"   Old Firehand."

msgctxt "scene:23:44"
msgid ""
"2. Ich habe mich im\n"
"   Wald verirrt."
msgstr ""
"2. I have lost my way\n"
"   in the forest."

msgctxt "scene:23:46"
msgid ""
"3. Zielen sie nicht\n"
"   dauernd mit dem\n"
"   Gewehr auf mich!"
msgstr ""
"3. Do not keep pointing\n"
"   that rifle at\n"
"   me!"

msgctxt "scene:23:49"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:50"
msgid ""
"Old Firehand? Na und?\n"
"Noch nie den Namen\n"
"gehört."
msgstr ""
"Old Firehand? So what?\n"
"Never heard the name\n"
"before."

msgctxt "scene:23:53"
msgid ""
"Nun - das kann man\n"
"schon glauben. Die-\n"
"ser Wald kann zu-\n"
"weilen sehr tückisch\n"
"werden."
msgstr ""
"Well - that one can\n"
"easily believe. This\n"
"forest can at times\n"
"become very treacherous\n"
"indeed."

msgctxt "scene:23:58"
msgid ""
"1. Wenn man sich hier\n"
"   auskennt, kann\n"
"   nichts schiefgehen."
msgstr ""
"1. If one knows one's\n"
"   way around here, nothing\n"
"   can go wrong."

msgctxt "scene:23:61"
msgid ""
"2. Sie haben sich doch\n"
"   bestimmt verirrt."
msgstr ""
"2. You must surely have\n"
"   lost your way."

msgctxt "scene:23:63"
msgid ""
"3. Sind sie absichtlich\n"
"   mit ihrem Planwagen\n"
"   hier?"
msgstr ""
"3. Are you here on\n"
"   purpose with your\n"
"   covered wagon?"

msgctxt "scene:23:66"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:67"
msgid ""
"Ja, ja - dafür gibt\n"
"es ja Landkarten."
msgstr ""
"Yes, yes - that is what\n"
"maps are for."

msgctxt "scene:23:69"
msgid ""
"Das geht sie\n"
"gar nichts an!"
msgstr ""
"That is none of\n"
"your business!"

msgctxt "scene:23:71"
msgid ""
"Lassen sie das, Mister!\n"
"Oder ich brenn' ihnen\n"
" 'ne Kugel auf den Pelz!"
msgstr ""
"Stop that, Mister! Or I\n"
"shall put a bullet\n"
"through your hide!"

msgctxt "scene:23:74"
msgid ""
"Mit diesem Gewehr\n"
"treffe ich jeden\n"
"Halunken, auch wenn\n"
"ich nicht auf ihn\n"
"direkt ziele!"
msgstr ""
"With this rifle I hit\n"
"every scoundrel, even\n"
"if I do not aim\n"
"directly at him!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:79"
msgid ""
"1. Ist das Gewehr\n"
"   ein Bärentöter?"
msgstr ""
"1. Is that rifle a\n"
"   Bear Killer?"

msgctxt "scene:23:81"
msgid ""
"2. Ist das Gewehr\n"
"   eine Winchester?"
msgstr ""
"2. Is that rifle a\n"
"   Winchester?"

msgctxt "scene:23:83"
msgid ""
"3. Das Gewehr sieht\n"
"   stark nach einem\n"
"   Henry-Stutzen aus."
msgstr ""
"3. That rifle looks very\n"
"   much like a Henry\n"
"   carbine."

msgctxt "scene:23:86"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:87"
msgid ""
"Quatsch! Sie wollen\n"
"ein Westmann sein,\n"
"und wissen noch nicht\n"
"einmal, was das hier\n"
"für ein Gewehr ist?!"
msgstr ""
"Nonsense! You claim to\n"
"be a westman, and do\n"
"not even know what kind\n"
"of rifle this is?!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:92"
msgid ""
"Nein, nein - keine\n"
"Winchester. Und sie\n"
"wollen ein Westmann\n"
"sein?"
msgstr ""
"No, no - no Winchester.\n"
"And you claim to be a\n"
"westman?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:96"
msgid ""
"Na sowas?! Dass sie\n"
"das erkannt haben!\n"
"Das ist tatsächlich\n"
"ein Henry-Stutzen."
msgstr ""
"Well now?! That you\n"
"recognised that! It is\n"
"indeed a Henry\n"
"carbine."

msgctxt "scene:23:100"
msgid ""
"Es gibt ja wirklich\n"
"nicht sehr viele von\n"
"diesen Stücken. Sie\n"
"müssen ein richtiger\n"
"Westmann sein. Seien\n"
"sie mir willkommen!"
msgstr ""
"There are really not\n"
"very many of these\n"
"pieces. You must be a\n"
"true westman. Be\n"
"welcome to my camp!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:106"
msgid ""
"1. Ich bin berühmt\n"
"   im ganzen Westen."
msgstr ""
"1. I am famous throughout\n"
"   the whole West."

msgctxt "scene:23:108"
msgid ""
"2. Ich bin ein ehren-\n"
"   wehrter Mensch!"
msgstr ""
"2. I am an honourable\n"
"   man!"

msgctxt "scene:23:110"
msgid ""
"3. Was machen sie\n"
"   hier im Wald?"
msgstr ""
"3. What are you doing\n"
"   here in the forest?"

msgctxt "scene:23:112"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:113"
msgid ""
"Fragt sich nur, in\n"
"welcher Hinsicht be-\n"
"rühmt. Ich habe schon\n"
"von Old Firehand ge-\n"
"hört, doch wer garan-\n"
"tiert mir, dass du\n"
"die Wahrheit sagst?"
msgstr ""
"The only question is in\n"
"what respect famous. I\n"
"have heard of Old\n"
"Firehand, yet who\n"
"guarantees that you tell\n"
"the truth?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:120"
msgid ""
"Tsja, wenn ich nur\n"
"einen fragen könnte.\n"
"Sie können mir ja\n"
"viel erzählen. Ich\n"
"habe schon meine\n"
"Erfahrungen gemacht,\n"
"und bin deshalb\n"
"vorsichtig."
msgstr ""
"Well, if only I could\n"
"ask someone. You can\n"
"tell me anything. I\n"
"have had my share of\n"
"experiences, and am\n"
"therefore cautious.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:128"
msgid ""
"Das werde ich Ihnen\n"
"auch noch gerade\n"
"erzählen."
msgstr ""
"I am hardly going to\n"
"tell you that as\n"
"well."

msgctxt "scene:23:131"
msgid ""
"1. Kennen Sie\n"
"   einen Mr. Droll?"
msgstr ""
"1. Do you know a\n"
"   Mr. Droll?"

msgctxt "scene:23:133"
msgid ""
"2. Kennen Sie einen\n"
"   Mr. Patterson?"
msgstr ""
"2. Do you know a\n"
"   Mr. Patterson?"

msgctxt "scene:23:135"
msgid ""
"3. Kennen Sie einen\n"
"   gewissen Cornel?"
msgstr ""
"3. Do you know a\n"
"   certain Cornel?"

msgctxt "scene:23:137"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:138"
msgid ""
"Droll? Droll? Ja! Ich\n"
"habe den Namen schon\n"
"einmal gehört. Können\n"
"sie mir mehr zu diesem\n"
"Mann sagen?"
msgstr ""
"Droll? Droll? Yes! I\n"
"have heard the name\n"
"before. Can you tell\n"
"me more about this\n"
"man?"

msgctxt "scene:23:143"
msgid ""
"Patterson? Nein,\n"
"nie gehört?"
msgstr ""
"Patterson? No,\n"
"never heard of him?"

msgctxt "scene:23:145"
msgid ""
"Der Cornel? Einmal\n"
"erzählte mir jemand,\n"
"dass der Cornel ein\n"
"gefährlicher Bandit\n"
"sei. Stimmt das?"
msgstr ""
"Cornel? Someone once\n"
"told me that Cornel\n"
"was a dangerous\n"
"bandit. Is that\n"
"true?"

msgctxt "scene:23:150"
msgid ""
"1. Der Cornel ist\n"
"   ein Verbrecher."
msgstr ""
"1. Cornel is a\n"
"   criminal."

msgctxt "scene:23:152"
msgid ""
"2. Der Cornel ist\n"
"   kein Verbrecher."
msgstr ""
"2. Cornel is no\n"
"   criminal."

msgctxt "scene:23:154"
msgid ""
"3. Der Cornel hat\n"
"   meinen Kompagnon\n"
"   gefangengenommen."
msgstr ""
"3. Cornel has taken\n"
"   my partner\n"
"   prisoner."

msgctxt "scene:23:157"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:158"
msgid ""
"So, so - ein Verbrecher.\n"
"Was hat er denn schon\n"
"Böses getan?"
msgstr ""
"So, so - a criminal.\n"
"What evil has he\n"
"done then?"

msgctxt "scene:23:161"
msgid ""
"Komisch! Man erzählt\n"
"sich aber die tollsten\n"
"Geschichten über ihn."
msgstr ""
"Strange! Yet people tell\n"
"the wildest stories\n"
"about him."

msgctxt "scene:23:164"
msgid ""
"Welchen Kompangnon\n"
"denn?"
msgstr ""
"Which partner\n"
"then?"

msgctxt "scene:23:166"
msgid ""
"1. Er hat meinen Kom-\n"
"   pangnon gefangen."
msgstr ""
"1. He captured my\n"
"   partner."

msgctxt "scene:23:168"
msgid ""
"2. Nichts, er ist gar\n"
"   nicht so gefährlich,\n"
"   wie man sagt."
msgstr ""
"2. Nothing, he is not\n"
"   as dangerous as\n"
"   people say."

msgctxt "scene:23:171"
msgid ""
"3. Er droht, meinen\n"
"   Freund zu töten."
msgstr ""
"3. He threatens to\n"
"   kill my friend."

msgctxt "scene:23:173"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:174"
msgid "Welchen Kompagnon?"
msgstr "Which partner?"

msgctxt "scene:23:175"
msgid ""
"Na, warum sollen wir\n"
"uns dann das Maul über\n"
"ihn zerreissen."
msgstr ""
"Well, why should we\n"
"run our mouths about\n"
"him then."

msgctxt "scene:23:178"
msgid ""
"Welchen Freund\n"
"meinen sie?"
msgstr ""
"Which friend do you\n"
"mean?"

msgctxt "scene:23:180"
msgid ""
"1. Man nennt ihn\n"
"   auch den 'Onkel'!"
msgstr ""
"1. People also call\n"
"   him 'Uncle'!"

msgctxt "scene:23:182"
msgid ""
"2. Droll trägt den\n"
"   Beinamen 'Tante'?"
msgstr ""
"2. Droll bears the\n"
"   sobriquet 'Aunt'?"

msgctxt "scene:23:184"
msgid ""
"3. Mr. Droll spricht\n"
"   wie eine Frau."
msgstr ""
"3. Mr. Droll speaks\n"
"   like a woman."

msgctxt "scene:23:186"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:187"
msgid ""
"Onkel Droll? Nein,\n"
"nein, da muss ich mich\n"
"geirrt haben. Ich\n"
"habe den Namen wohl\n"
"verwechselt."
msgstr ""
"Uncle Droll? No,\n"
"no, I must have been\n"
"mistaken. I must\n"
"have confused the\n"
"name."

msgctxt "scene:23:192"
msgid ""
"Tante Droll? Genau!\n"
"Das ist der Name. Wenn\n"
"Sie ihn kennen, können\n"
"sie mir ja auch noch\n"
"mehr von ihm erzählen."
msgstr ""
"Aunt Droll? Exactly!\n"
"That is the name. If\n"
"you know him, you can\n"
"tell me even more\n"
"about him."

msgctxt "scene:23:197"
msgid ""
"Der Mann soll wie eine\n"
"Frau sprechen? Davon\n"
"habe ich noch nichts\n"
"gehört!"
msgstr ""
"The man is said to speak\n"
"like a woman? Of that\n"
"I have heard nothing\n"
"yet!"

msgctxt "scene:23:201"
msgid ""
"1. Die Tante trägt\n"
"   nie Hosen."
msgstr ""
"1. The Aunt never\n"
"   wears trousers."

msgctxt "scene:23:203"
msgid ""
"2. Droll ist ein\n"
"   Verbrecher."
msgstr ""
"2. Droll is a\n"
"   criminal."

msgctxt "scene:23:205"
msgid ""
"3. Man nennt Ihn Tante,\n"
"   weil seine Hose ei-\n"
"   nem Rock gleicht."
msgstr ""
"3. They call him Aunt,\n"
"   because his pants\n"
"   resemble a skirt."

msgctxt "scene:23:208"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:209"
msgid ""
"Nun, da muss ich mich\n"
"getäuscht haben. In dem\n"
"Zusammenhang sagt mir\n"
"der Name doch nichts."
msgstr ""
"Well, I must have been\n"
"deceived. In that\n"
"context the name tells\n"
"me nothing after all."

msgctxt "scene:23:213"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, wir sprechen\n"
"nicht von dem gleichen\n"
"Mr.Droll."
msgstr ""
"I believe we are not\n"
"speaking of the same\n"
"Mr. Droll."

msgctxt "scene:23:216"
msgid ""
"Genau! Der Lederrock!\n"
"Und sie kennen die\n"
"Tante Droll?"
msgstr ""
"Exactly! The leather\n"
"skirt! And you know\n"
"Aunt Droll?"

msgctxt "scene:23:219"
msgid ""
"1. Nein, ich bin ihr\n"
"   nie begegnet."
msgstr ""
"1. No, I have never\n"
"   met her."

msgctxt "scene:23:221"
msgid ""
"2. Zusammen mit Droll\n"
"   jage ich den Cornel,\n"
"   einen Verbrecher."
msgstr ""
"2. Together with Droll\n"
"   I hunt Cornel,\n"
"   a criminal."

msgctxt "scene:23:224"
msgid ""
"3. Ich bin mit Droll\n"
"   zur Schule gegangen."
msgstr ""
"3. I went to school\n"
"   with Droll."

msgctxt "scene:23:226"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:227"
msgid ""
"Und warum erzählen sie\n"
"mir dann die ganzen\n"
"Geschichten, hä?"
msgstr ""
"And why do you tell\n"
"me all those stories\n"
"then, eh?"

msgctxt "scene:23:230"
msgid ""
"So, so, den Cornel.\n"
"Und warum sind sie\n"
"dann allein hier im\n"
"Wald."
msgstr ""
"So, so, Cornel.\n"
"And why are you then\n"
"alone here in the\n"
"forest."

msgctxt "scene:23:234"
msgid ""
"Das ist ja schon lange\n"
"her. Vielleicht treffen\n"
"sie die Tante noch ein-\n"
"mal wieder."
msgstr ""
"That was a long time\n"
"ago. Perhaps you will\n"
"meet the Aunt once\n"
"again."

msgctxt "scene:23:238"
msgid ""
"1. Der Cornel hat die\n"
"   Tante und droht\n"
"   Sie umzubringen."
msgstr ""
"1. Cornel holds Aunt\n"
"   and threatens to\n"
"   kill her."

msgctxt "scene:23:241"
msgid "2. Droll ist gegangen."
msgstr "2. Droll has left."

msgctxt "scene:23:242"
msgid ""
"3. Ich treffe Droll\n"
"   später."
msgstr ""
"3. I am meeting Droll\n"
"   later."

msgctxt "scene:23:244"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:245"
msgid ""
"Ja, aber dann helfen\n"
"sie der Tante doch!"
msgstr ""
"Yes, but then go and\n"
"help Aunt!"

msgctxt "scene:23:247"
msgid ""
"Und das soll ich\n"
"ihnen glauben.\n"
"Passen sie bloss\n"
"auf, dass ich nicht\n"
"ungemütlich werde."
msgstr ""
"And I am to believe\n"
"that from you.\n"
"Just watch out that I\n"
"do not get nasty\n"
"with you."

msgctxt "scene:23:252"
msgid ""
"Sie treffen ihn also\n"
"später. Passen sie\n"
"auf, dass ich sie mit\n"
"meinem Gewehr nicht\n"
"zum Tanzen bringe."
msgstr ""
"So you meet him later.\n"
"Watch out that I do\n"
"not make you dance\n"
"with my rifle.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:257"
msgid ""
"1. Ist das Gewehr\n"
"   ein Bärentöter?"
msgstr ""
"1. Is that rifle a\n"
"   Bear Killer?"

msgctxt "scene:23:259"
msgid ""
"2. Ist das Gewehr\n"
"   eine Winchester?"
msgstr ""
"2. Is that rifle a\n"
"   Winchester?"

msgctxt "scene:23:261"
msgid ""
"3. Das Gewehr sieht\n"
"   stark nach einem\n"
"   Henry-Stutzen aus."
msgstr ""
"3. That rifle looks very\n"
"   much like a Henry\n"
"   carbine."

msgctxt "scene:23:264"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:265"
msgid ""
"Quatsch! Sie wollen\n"
"ein Westmann sein,\n"
"und wissen noch nicht\n"
"einmal, was das hier\n"
"für ein Gewehr ist?!"
msgstr ""
"Nonsense! You claim to\n"
"be a westman, and do\n"
"not even know what kind\n"
"of rifle this is?!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:270"
msgid ""
"Nein, nein - keine\n"
"Winchester. Und sie\n"
"wollen ein Westmann\n"
"sein?"
msgstr ""
"No, no - no Winchester.\n"
"And you claim to be a\n"
"westman?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:274"
msgid ""
"Na sowas?! Dass sie\n"
"das erkannt haben!\n"
"Das ist tatsächlich\n"
"ein Henry-Stutzen."
msgstr ""
"Well now?! That you\n"
"recognised that! It is\n"
"indeed a Henry\n"
"carbine."

msgctxt "scene:23:278"
msgid ""
"Es gibt ja wirklich\n"
"nicht sehr viele von\n"
"diesen Stücken. Sie\n"
"müssen ein richtiger\n"
"Westmann sein. Seien\n"
"sie mir willkommen!"
msgstr ""
"There are really not\n"
"very many of these\n"
"pieces. You must be a\n"
"true westman. Be\n"
"welcome to my camp!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:284"
msgid ""
"1. Ach, Droll kommt\n"
"   ganz gut zurecht."
msgstr ""
"1. Ah, Droll manages\n"
"   quite well."

msgctxt "scene:23:286"
msgid ""
"2. Ich pfeif' auf\n"
"   Droll."
msgstr ""
"2. I do not care a\n"
"   fig for Droll."

msgctxt "scene:23:288"
msgid ""
"3. Ich möchte ihm ja\n"
"   helfen! Aber sie\n"
"   bedrohen mich ja."
msgstr ""
"3. I would gladly help\n"
"   him! But you are\n"
"   threatening me."

msgctxt "scene:23:291"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:23:292"
msgid ""
"So ein guter Freund\n"
"sind sie aber nicht!"
msgstr ""
"You are not such a\n"
"good friend, then!"

msgctxt "scene:23:294"
msgid ""
"Sie wollen ein West-\n"
"man sein? Aber von\n"
"Ehre halten sie nicht\n"
"viel..."
msgstr ""
"You claim to be a west-\n"
"man? Yet you do not\n"
"think much of honour...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:298"
msgid ""
"Was? Ach ja, stimmt.\n"
"Ich muss sagen, sie\n"
"haben mich überzeugt.\n"
"Ich werde sie nicht\n"
"weiter bedrohen, sie\n"
"sind, wie mir scheint,\n"
"ein rechtschaffener\n"
"Mensch."
msgstr ""
"What? Ah yes, true.\n"
"I must say, you have\n"
"convinced me. I shall\n"
"threaten you no more;\n"
"you are, as it seems\n"
"to me, an upright\n"
"man.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:306"
msgid ""
"Eine undurchdringliche\n"
"Wildnis dieser Wald.\n"
"Ich bin sicher, die Pfade\n"
"waren ursprünglich Tram-\n"
"pelpfade der Hirsche."
msgstr ""
"An impenetrable\n"
"wilderness, this forest.\n"
"I am sure the paths were\n"
"originally deer trails.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:311"
msgid "BRANSHKY FEUERWERKSKÖRPER"
msgstr "BRANSHKY FIREWORKS"

msgctxt "scene:23:312"
msgid ""
"Ein etwas wackeliges\n"
"Gefährt, dieser Plan-\n"
"wagen."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat rickety\n"
"vehicle, this covered\n"
"wagon."

msgctxt "scene:23:315"
msgid ""
"Eine schöne und ruhige\n"
"Waldlichtung. Zum Lagern\n"
"ideal, da man vom Fluss\n"
"her nichts sieht."
msgstr ""
"A lovely and quiet forest\n"
"clearing. Ideal for a camp,\n"
"as nothing is seen from\n"
"the river."

msgctxt "scene:23:319"
msgid ""
"Das Lagerfeuer ist etwas\n"
"gross geraten. Der muss\n"
"sich sehr sicher fühlen."
msgstr ""
"The campfire turned out\n"
"a bit large. He must feel\n"
"very secure."

msgctxt "scene:23:322"
msgid ""
"Ein Zelt aus dem\n"
"gleichen Stoff wie\n"
"das Verdeck des\n"
"Planwagens."
msgstr ""
"A tent made of the\n"
"same canvas as the\n"
"cover of the\n"
"wagon."

msgctxt "scene:23:326"
msgid ""
"Auf dem Feuer liegt\n"
"genug Holz, ich muss\n"
"nicht noch mehr sam-\n"
"meln."
msgstr ""
"Enough wood lies upon\n"
"the fire; I need not\n"
"gather any more.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:330"
msgid ""
"Ich kann doch nicht ein-\n"
"fach die Schrift heraus-\n"
"schneiden."
msgstr ""
"I cannot simply cut\n"
"out the lettering,\n"
"after all."

msgctxt "scene:23:333"
msgid ""
"Ohne Pferd ist der Wagen\n"
"nicht zu bewegen, zudem\n"
"gehört der nicht mir."
msgstr ""
"Without a horse the\n"
"wagon cannot be moved;\n"
"besides, it is not mine."

msgctxt "scene:23:336"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"ich die Erde dieser\n"
"Waldlichtung mitnehmen\n"
"soll, oder!?"
msgstr ""
"I do not think that I\n"
"should take the soil of\n"
"this forest clearing with\n"
"me, should I!?"

msgctxt "scene:23:340"
msgid ""
"Ich habe nichts, um das\n"
"Feuer zu transportieren."
msgstr ""
"I have nothing in which\n"
"to transport the fire."

msgctxt "scene:23:342"
msgid ""
"Was gibt es denn?\n"
"Ich habe eigentlich\n"
"nichts Neues zu be-\n"
"richten und warte\n"
"nur auf jemanden,\n"
"der mir eine Karte\n"
"bringt."
msgstr ""
"What is it then?\n"
"I actually have nothing\n"
"new to report and am\n"
"merely waiting for someone\n"
"who will bring me a\n"
"map.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:349"
msgid ""
"Vielen dank noch-\n"
"mals für die Karte,\n"
"Mr.Firehand!"
msgstr ""
"Thank you once again\n"
"for the map,\n"
"Mr. Firehand!"

msgctxt "scene:23:352"
msgid ""
"1. Wie sind Sie in\n"
"   den Wald gelangt?"
msgstr ""
"1. How did you get\n"
"   into the forest?"

msgctxt "scene:23:354"
msgid ""
"2. Wozu brauchen Sie\n"
"   den Planwagen?"
msgstr ""
"2. What do you need\n"
"   the covered wagon for?"

msgctxt "scene:23:356"
msgid ""
"3. Können sie mir\n"
"   helfen?"
msgstr ""
"3. Can you help\n"
"   me?"

msgctxt "scene:23:358"
msgid ""
"4. Schon gut, auf\n"
"   Wiedersehen"
msgstr ""
"4. Very well, goodbye\n"
"   then"

msgctxt "scene:23:360"
msgid ""
"Na ja, warum eigent-\n"
"lich nicht? Ich habe\n"
"mich im Wald verirrt.\n"
"Bei meiner letzten\n"
"Station verkaufte\n"
"mir so ein alter Kauz\n"
"eine Landkarte von\n"
"dieser Gegend. Er be-"
msgstr ""
"Well, why not indeed?\n"
"I have lost my way\n"
"in the forest. At my\n"
"last stop, an old\n"
"fellow sold me a map\n"
"of this area. He\n"
"claimed\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:368"
msgid ""
"hauptete, dass wäre\n"
"die neueste und ge-\n"
"naueste Karte, die\n"
"man überhaupt für Geld\n"
"bekommen könnte.\n"
"Dummerweise glaubte\n"
"ich seinen Verspre-\n"
"chungen, und kaufte ihm"
msgstr ""
"that it was the newest\n"
"and most accurate map\n"
"that one could get for\n"
"money anywhere.\n"
"Foolishly I believed his\n"
"promises, and bought\n"
"the map from him\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:376"
msgid ""
"für viel Geld die Karte\n"
"ab. Das Ding sah auch\n"
"wirklich gut aus, fast\n"
"jeder Busch war darauf\n"
"verzeichnet, noch dazu\n"
"Entfernungen und selbst\n"
"kleinste Pfade."
msgstr ""
"for a lot of money. The\n"
"thing looked truly good,\n"
"almost every bush was\n"
"marked upon it, along\n"
"with distances and even\n"
"the smallest of paths.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:383"
msgid ""
"Aber trotzdem war die\n"
"Karte falsch - sie\n"
"stimmte einfach nicht.\n"
"Und deshalb bin ich\n"
"jetzt hier im Wald.\n"
"Wenn ich nur eine\n"
"richtige Landkarte"
msgstr ""
"Yet nevertheless the\n"
"map was false - it\n"
"simply was not right.\n"
"And that is why I am\n"
"now here in the forest.\n"
"If only I had a\n"
"proper map,"

msgctxt "scene:23:390"
msgid ""
"hätte, könnte ich mei-\n"
"nen Weg bald fort-\n"
"setzen. Aber so sitze\n"
"ich wohl erst mal hier\n"
"fest. Können sie mir\n"
"nicht helfen?"
msgstr ""
"I could soon continue\n"
"on my way. But as it is,\n"
"I suppose I am stuck\n"
"here for now. Can you\n"
"not help me?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:396"
msgid ""
"1. Nein, ich kann ihnen\n"
"   nicht helfen. Ich\n"
"   kenne mich hier\n"
"   selbst nicht aus."
msgstr ""
"1. No, I cannot help\n"
"   you. I do not know\n"
"   my way around here\n"
"   myself."

msgctxt "scene:23:400"
msgid ""
"2. Wie kann ich ihnen\n"
"   denn helfen?"
msgstr ""
"2. How can I help\n"
"   you then?"

msgctxt "scene:23:402"
msgid ""
"Schade! Naja, da kann\n"
"man wohl nichts machen.\n"
"Dann muss ich mich\n"
"selbst durchschlagen."
msgstr ""
"Pity! Well, nothing\n"
"can be done about that.\n"
"Then I must fend for\n"
"myself."

msgctxt "scene:23:406"
msgid ""
"Nun, sie könnten mir\n"
"vielleicht eine Land-\n"
"karte besorgen."
msgstr ""
"Well, you could perhaps\n"
"procure a map\n"
"for me."

msgctxt "scene:23:409"
msgid ""
"1. Nun, ich kann\n"
"   es ja versuchen."
msgstr ""
"1. Well, I can\n"
"   try."

msgctxt "scene:23:411"
msgid ""
"2. Wo soll ich denn\n"
"   hier eine Landkarte\n"
"   finden? Nein, nein,\n"
"   da fange ich erst\n"
"   gar nicht zu su-\n"
"   chen an."
msgstr ""
"2. Where should I find\n"
"   a map here? No, no,\n"
"   I shall not even start\n"
"   looking for one.\n"
"   ­\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:23:417"
msgid ""
"Würden sie das wirk-\n"
"lich machen? Vielen\n"
"Dank! Wenn sie mir\n"
"wirklich helfen,\n"
"schenke ich ihnen\n"
"soviele Knallfrösche,\n"
"wie sie wollen -\n"
"versprochen!"
msgstr ""
"Would you really do\n"
"that? Thank you very\n"
"much! If you truly help\n"
"me, I shall give you as\n"
"many firecrackers as\n"
"you want -\n"
"promised!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:425"
msgid ""
"Vielleicht hätten sie\n"
"ja irgendwo eine bei\n"
"sich. Na, dann eben\n"
"nicht."
msgstr ""
"Perhaps you might have\n"
"one on you somewhere.\n"
"Well, then never mind.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:429"
msgid ""
"Mein Planwagen? Ja -\n"
"das ist mein ganzer\n"
"Stolz. Sie müssen\n"
"wissen, ich handle\n"
"mit Feuerwerkskör-\n"
"per. In jeder Stadt\n"
"und jedem Dorf reis-\n"
"sen die Leute mir"
msgstr ""
"My covered wagon? Yes -\n"
"that is my pride and\n"
"joy. You must know, I\n"
"trade in fireworks.\n"
"In every town and\n"
"every village, people\n"
"snatch my firecrackers\n"
"from my"

msgctxt "scene:23:437"
msgid ""
"meine Knallfrösche\n"
"aus den Händen. Bei\n"
"Feiern und solchen\n"
"Gelegenheiten wird\n"
"so was gerne benutzt.\n"
"Natürlich verkaufe\n"
"ich nur beste Ware.\n"
"Meine Knallfrösche"
msgstr ""
"hands. At celebrations\n"
"and such occasions, such\n"
"things are gladly used.\n"
"Of course I sell only\n"
"the best goods. My\n"
"firecrackers are so\n"
"loud that one might\n"
"think someone"

msgctxt "scene:23:445"
msgid ""
"sind so laut, dass\n"
"man denken kann,\n"
"jemand schiesse mit\n"
"Kanonen."
msgstr ""
"were firing with\n"
"cannons.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:449"
msgid ""
"1. Sind die Dinger\n"
"   wirklich so laut?"
msgstr ""
"1. Are those things\n"
"   really that loud?"

msgctxt "scene:23:451"
msgid ""
"2. Kann ich ein paar\n"
"   von den Knall-\n"
"   fröschen haben?"
msgstr ""
"2. Can I have a few of\n"
"   those firecrackers\n"
"   for myself?"

msgctxt "scene:23:454"
msgid ""
"3. Nein, das glaube\n"
"   ich nicht."
msgstr ""
"3. No, I do not believe\n"
"   that."

msgctxt "scene:23:456"
msgid "4. Bis später."
msgstr "4. Until later."

msgctxt "scene:23:457"
msgid ""
"Ja, und wie! Ich habe\n"
"die lautesten Knall-\n"
"frösche überhaupt.\n"
"Damit erschreckt man\n"
"jeden - glauben sie\n"
"mir! Sie werden ihren\n"
"Spass haben."
msgstr ""
"Yes, and how! I have\n"
"the loudest firecrackers\n"
"anywhere. You can scare\n"
"anyone with them -\n"
"believe me! You will\n"
"have your fun.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:464"
msgid ""
"Nun, meine Knallfrösche\n"
"sind schon sehr teuer -\n"
"und es dauert wohl noch\n"
"lange, bis ich wieder\n"
"welche verkaufen kann,\n"
"- hm - also umsonst\n"
"kann ich ihnen keine\n"
"geben."
msgstr ""
"Well, my firecrackers\n"
"are very expensive -\n"
"and it will likely be\n"
"long before I can sell\n"
"any again, - hm - so I\n"
"cannot give you any for\n"
"nothing.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:472"
msgid ""
"Sie müssten schon etwas\n"
"für mich tun."
msgstr ""
"You would have to do\n"
"something for me."

msgctxt "scene:23:474"
msgid "Und was?"
msgstr "And what?"

msgctxt "scene:23:475"
msgid ""
"Sie könnten mir helfen,\n"
"wieder aus dem Wald zu\n"
"finden. Ich habe nur\n"
"eine gefälschte Land-\n"
"karte, nach der kann\n"
"ich mich nur verirren."
msgstr ""
"You could help me find\n"
"my way out of the forest\n"
"again. I only have a\n"
"fake map, according to\n"
"which I can only get\n"
"lost."

msgctxt "scene:23:481"
msgid ""
"Vielleicht könnten sie\n"
"mir ja eine bessere\n"
"Karte besorgen - hm?"
msgstr ""
"Perhaps you could\n"
"procure a better\n"
"map for me - hm?"

msgctxt "scene:23:484"
msgid ""
"Das meinen sie! Passen\n"
"sie mal auf!"
msgstr ""
"You don't say! Just\n"
"watch this!"

msgctxt "scene:23:486"
msgid ""
"So, nun können sie sich\n"
"selbst überzeugen, wie\n"
"laut die Knaller sind,\n"
"haha."
msgstr ""
"So, now you can convince\n"
"yourself how loud the\n"
"crackers are,\n"
"haha."

msgctxt "scene:23:490"
msgid ""
"Na, konnte sie\n"
"das überzeugen?"
msgstr ""
"Well, could that\n"
"convince you?"

msgctxt "scene:23:492"
msgid "O.K."
msgstr "O.K."

msgctxt "scene:23:493"
msgid ""
"1. Ein Knallfrosch\n"
"   wie jeder andere."
msgstr ""
"1. A firecracker like\n"
"   any other."

msgctxt "scene:23:495"
msgid ""
"2. Das soll mich\n"
"   überzeugen?"
msgstr ""
"2. Is that supposed to\n"
"   convince me?"

msgctxt "scene:23:497"
msgid ""
"3. Das schreckt sogar\n"
"   einen Grizzley aus\n"
"   dem Winterschlaf."
msgstr ""
"3. That would scare even\n"
"   a grizzly out of\n"
"   hibernation."

msgctxt "scene:23:500"
msgid "4. Lassen wir das!"
msgstr "4. Let us leave it at that!"

msgctxt "scene:23:501"
msgid ""
"Wenn sie meinen. Ich\n"
"bin davon überzeugt,\n"
"dass man damit selbst\n"
"dem abgebrühtesten\n"
"Westmann einen gehöri-\n"
"gen Schrecken einjagen\n"
"kann."
msgstr ""
"If you think so. I am\n"
"convinced that with these\n"
"you can give even the\n"
"most hardened westman\n"
"a proper fright.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:508"
msgid ""
"Meine Knallfrösche\n"
"klingen ja fast schon\n"
"so, wie mein Henry-\n"
"Stutzen."
msgstr ""
"My firecrackers sound\n"
"almost like my Henry\n"
"carbine.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:512"
msgid ""
"Wenn sie meinen. Ich\n"
"bin davon überzeugt,\n"
"dass man damit selbst\n"
"dem abgebrühtesten\n"
"Westmann einen gehöri-\n"
"gen Schrecken einjagen\n"
"kann."
msgstr ""
"If you think so. I am\n"
"convinced that with these\n"
"you can give even the\n"
"most hardened westman\n"
"a proper fright.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:519"
msgid ""
"Meine Knallfrösche\n"
"klingen ja fast schon\n"
"so, wie mein Henry-\n"
"Stutzen."
msgstr ""
"My firecrackers sound\n"
"almost like my Henry\n"
"carbine.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:523"
msgid ""
"Sag ich doch! Meine\n"
"Knallfrösche sind\n"
"erste Wahl. Mein Henry-\n"
"Stutzen macht den glei-\n"
"chen Krach."
msgstr ""
"Just as I say! My\n"
"firecrackers are first\n"
"choice. My Henry\n"
"carbine makes the same\n"
"noise."

msgctxt "scene:23:528"
msgid ""
"Helfen? Wobei soll\n"
"ich ihnen denn\n"
"helfen? ich bin\n"
"kein Westman wie sie."
msgstr ""
"Help? What should I\n"
"help you with? I am\n"
"no westman like you.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:532"
msgid ""
"1. Haben Sie ein\n"
"   Kanu?"
msgstr ""
"1. Do you have a\n"
"   canoe?"

msgctxt "scene:23:534"
msgid ""
"2. Mein Freund Droll\n"
"   ist in der Gewalt\n"
"   von Verbrechern."
msgstr ""
"2. My friend Droll\n"
"   is in the power\n"
"   of criminals."

msgctxt "scene:23:537"
msgid "3. Entschuldigen Sie."
msgstr "3. Excuse me."

msgctxt "scene:23:538"
msgid ""
"Nein, da kann ich\n"
"ihnen nicht helfen.\n"
"Ich selber habe keine\n"
"Kanus. Bauen sie sich\n"
"doch ein Neues."
msgstr ""
"No, I cannot help\n"
"you there. I have no\n"
"canoes myself. Why\n"
"do you not build\n"
"yourself a new one?"

msgctxt "scene:23:543"
msgid ""
"Ich würde ihnen ja\n"
"gerne helfen, aber\n"
"ich kann meinen Lager-\n"
"platz nicht verlassen.\n"
"Wenn meine Ware ge-\n"
"stohlen wird, bin ich\n"
"ruiniert. Das müssen\n"
"sie verstehen."
msgstr ""
"I would gladly help\n"
"you, but I cannot\n"
"leave my camp. If my\n"
"goods are stolen, I\n"
"am ruined. That you\n"
"must surely understand.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:551"
msgid ""
"Aber sie stören mich\n"
"doch nicht. Im Gegen-\n"
"teil."
msgstr ""
"But you are not\n"
"disturbing me at all.\n"
"Quite the contrary."

msgctxt "scene:23:554"
msgid ""
"Ich habe hier nur\n"
"ein Stück Brot und\n"
"einen Gürtel, den\n"
"ich zum Tausch an-\n"
"bieten kann. Ich\n"
"hatte noch ein schö-\n"
"nes Messer, doch"
msgstr ""
"I have here only a\n"
"piece of bread and a\n"
"belt that I can offer\n"
"in trade. I had another\n"
"fine knife, yet I lost\n"
"it somewhere on the\n"
"forest path,"

msgctxt "scene:23:561"
msgid ""
"das habe ich irgendwo\n"
"am Waldweg verloren,\n"
"und bis jetzt nicht\n"
"wieder gefunden."
msgstr ""
"and have not found it\n"
"again to this day.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:565"
msgid ""
"1. Ich nehme das\n"
"   Brot."
msgstr ""
"1. I shall take the\n"
"   bread."

msgctxt "scene:23:567"
msgid ""
"2. Danke für den\n"
"   Gürtel!"
msgstr ""
"2. Thank you for the\n"
"   belt!"

msgctxt "scene:23:569"
msgid ""
"3. Ich brauche\n"
"   nichts."
msgstr ""
"3. I need nothing.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:571"
msgid ""
"Ah, Mr. Firehand, wol-\n"
"len Sie doch lieber den\n"
"Gürtel. Das kommt mir\n"
"gelegen, dann muss ich\n"
"mir kein neues Brot\n"
"backen."
msgstr ""
"Ah, Mr. Firehand, would\n"
"you rather have the\n"
"belt? That suits me well,\n"
"then I need not bake\n"
"myself fresh bread.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:577"
msgid ""
"Danke Mr. Firehand,\n"
"sie helfen mir sehr.\n"
"Nehmen Sie sich aus\n"
"dem Wagen so viele\n"
"Knallfrösche wie Sie\n"
"brauchen."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, Mr. Firehand,\n"
"you help me greatly. Take\n"
"from the wagon as many\n"
"firecrackers as you\n"
"require.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:583"
msgid ""
"Wieso soll ich dem\n"
"die Karte geben?\n"
"Ich kann die viel-\n"
"leicht selber brau-\n"
"chen."
msgstr ""
"Why should I give him\n"
"the map? I might well\n"
"need it myself.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:588"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"Branshky verreisen will."
msgstr ""
"I do not think Branshky\n"
"wishes to travel."

msgctxt "scene:23:590"
msgid ""
"Branshky sieht mir nicht\n"
"aus als ob er friert."
msgstr ""
"Branshky does not look to\n"
"me as if he were cold."

msgctxt "scene:23:592"
msgid ""
"Das Kuvert ist bereits\n"
"beschriftet und ich glaube\n"
"nicht, dass Branshky Brief-\n"
"umschläge sammelt."
msgstr ""
"The envelope is addressed\n"
"already, and I doubt that\n"
"Branshky collects envelopes.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:596"
msgid ""
"Branshky interessiert\n"
"dieser Brief sicher\n"
"nicht."
msgstr ""
"Branshky is surely not\n"
"interested in this letter.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:599"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich mir das Lager-\n"
"feuer so betrachte, dann\n"
"glaube ich nicht, dass\n"
"er einen Schürhaken\n"
"braucht."
msgstr ""
"Looking at the campfire\n"
"like that, I do not think\n"
"he needs a poker.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:604"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich ihm das Papier\n"
"gebe, schmeisst er es\n"
"sicher nur ins Feuer.\n"
"Wozu habe ich mich dann\n"
"so geplagt um es hevorzu-\n"
"holen..?"
msgstr ""
"If I give him the paper,\n"
"he will only throw it in\n"
"the fire. Why did I bother\n"
"so much to fetch it out,\n"
"then..?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:610"
msgid ""
"Danke Mr.Firehand, aber\n"
"ich bevorzuge etwas\n"
"frischeres Brot."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, Mr. Firehand,\n"
"but I prefer somewhat\n"
"fresher bread."

msgctxt "scene:23:613"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir vorstellen,\n"
"dass ich den noch einmal\n"
"brauchen kann."
msgstr ""
"I can imagine that I\n"
"might need it once again.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:616"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir nicht vor-\n"
"stellen, was er mit einer\n"
"leeren Schachtel anfangen\n"
"soll."
msgstr ""
"I cannot imagine what\n"
"he would do with an\n"
"empty box.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:620"
msgid ""
"Danke, aber ich brauche\n"
"so etwas nicht."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, but I do\n"
"not need such a thing."

msgctxt "scene:23:622"
msgid ""
"Mein Lieber Frund, ich\n"
"habe genug Knallfrö-\n"
"sche, behalten Sie\n"
"sich die paar die Sie\n"
"haben."
msgstr ""
"My dear friend, I have\n"
"enough firecrackers;\n"
"keep the few that you\n"
"have.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:23:627"
msgid ""
"Ich habe doch selbst\n"
"genug davon, behalten\n"
"Sie sich diese."
msgstr ""
"I have enough of those\n"
"myself; keep them for\n"
"yourself."

msgctxt "scene:23:630"
msgid ""
"Ich habe ja bereits\n"
"gesehen, dass die\n"
"Knallfrösche funk-\n"
"tionieren, und unser\n"
"Freund hier weiss\n"
"das noch besser."
msgstr ""
"I have seen already that\n"
"the firecrackers work,\n"
"and our friend here\n"
"knows that even better.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:0"
msgid ""
"Ha! Ha! Das war ein\n"
"leichtes Spiel. Ich\n"
"danke Euch für die\n"
"finanzielle Unter-\n"
"stützung und freue\n"
"mich schon bald auf\n"
"ein Wiedersehen..."
msgstr ""
"Ha! Ha! That was an easy\n"
"game. I thank you for the\n"
"financial support and look\n"
"forward to seeing you\n"
"again soon...\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:7"
msgid ""
"Dieser Schurke, für\n"
"diese und all seine\n"
"anderen Taten wird\n"
"er büssen. Ich nehme\n"
"die Verfolgung auf,\n"
"leben Sie wohl Mr.\n"
"Firehand."
msgstr ""
"That villain shall pay for\n"
"this and all his other\n"
"deeds. I take up the\n"
"pursuit; farewell, Mr.\n"
"Firehand.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:14"
msgid ""
"Leben Sie wohl, und\n"
"viel Glück!"
msgstr ""
"Farewell, and good\n"
"luck!"

msgctxt "scene:24:16"
msgid ""
"Eine richtig unheilver-\n"
"kündende Stimmung hat\n"
"der Himmel."
msgstr ""
"A truly ill-boding\n"
"mood hangs over the\n"
"sky."

msgctxt "scene:24:19"
msgid ""
"In der Ferne kann man\n"
"Ausläufer eines Gebirges\n"
"erkennen."
msgstr ""
"In the distance, foothills\n"
"of a mountain range can\n"
"be seen."

msgctxt "scene:24:22"
msgid ""
"Das gegenüberliegende\n"
"Flussufer ist komplett\n"
"bewaldet."
msgstr ""
"The opposite riverbank\n"
"is completely wooded.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:25"
msgid ""
"An dieser Stelle ist\n"
"der Fluss etwas rauher."
msgstr ""
"At this point the river\n"
"is somewhat rougher."

msgctxt "scene:24:27"
msgid ""
"Ein verkrüppelter Baum.\n"
"Er scheint unter dem\n"
"Feuer der brennenden\n"
"Hütte nicht sonderlich\n"
"gelitten zu haben."
msgstr ""
"A stunted tree. It seems\n"
"not to have suffered much\n"
"under the fire of the\n"
"burning cabin.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:32"
msgid "Oh da ist ein Zettel."
msgstr "Oh, there is a note."

msgctxt "scene:24:33"
msgid ""
"Eine Nachricht vom Cornel:\n"
"Besten Dank, Firehand. Ich\n"
"konnnte mir so die Kase\n"
"etwass aufbesern... Bis zum\n"
"nächsten Trefen..."
msgstr ""
"A message from Cornel:\n"
"Many thanks, Firehand. I\n"
"was able to line my purse a\n"
"bit... Until the next\n"
"meeting..."

msgctxt "scene:24:38"
msgid ""
"Der Cornel ist ganz\n"
"schön unverschämt, aber\n"
"wir werden ihn schon\n"
"noch zu fassen krie-\n"
"gen."
msgstr ""
"Cornel is quite insolent,\n"
"but we shall catch him yet.\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:43"
msgid ""
"Mit der Rechtschreibung\n"
"hat er aber Mühe. Wenn\n"
"es mit seinem Glück nur\n"
"auch so wäre..."
msgstr ""
"He struggles with spelling,\n"
"though. If only it were the\n"
"same with his luck...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:47"
msgid ""
"Ein knorriger Baum, der\n"
"ist sicher schon viele\n"
"Jahre alt."
msgstr ""
"A gnarled tree, surely many\n"
"years old.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:50"
msgid ""
"Wie überall am Ufer, liegen\n"
"auch hier Steine und\n"
"kleinere Felsen."
msgstr ""
"As everywhere along the bank,\n"
"stones and smaller rocks lie\n"
"here as well."

msgctxt "scene:24:53"
msgid ""
"Ein etwas wackeliger Holz-\n"
"steg, der durch die Feuch-\n"
"tigkeit des Flusses morsch\n"
"geworden ist."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat shaky wooden jetty,\n"
"which has rotted from the\n"
"humidity of the river.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:57"
msgid ""
"Ein ausgetretener Pfad.\n"
"Offensichtlich wird er\n"
"regelmässig benutzt."
msgstr ""
"A well-trodden path. It\n"
"is obviously used\n"
"regularly."

msgctxt "scene:24:60"
msgid ""
"Nur noch ein Haufen Asche,\n"
"diese Blockhütte. Da wird\n"
"kaum noch etwas zu retten\n"
"sein."
msgstr ""
"Only a heap of ashes, this\n"
"log cabin. There is hardly\n"
"anything left to save.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:64"
msgid ""
"Die Hütte der Rafters ist\n"
"komplett abgebrannt. Da\n"
"sind nur noch Dinge, die\n"
"nicht brennen, zu retten."
msgstr ""
"The rafters' cabin is burnt\n"
"down completely. Only things\n"
"that do not burn can be\n"
"saved now."

msgctxt "scene:24:68"
msgid ""
"Oh, da scheint etwas in der\n"
"Asche zu liegen... Eine Axt-\n"
"klinge. Die werde ich mit-\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"Oh, something seems to lie in\n"
"the ashes... An axe blade.\n"
"I shall take it with me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:72"
msgid ""
"Alles nur noch ein Haufen\n"
"Asche. Ein weiteres Ver-\n"
"brechen des Cornels..."
msgstr ""
"All just a heap of ashes now.\n"
"Another crime of Cornel's...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:75"
msgid ""
"Das diente wohl um die\n"
"Pferde festzubinden."
msgstr ""
"That served to tie up the\n"
"horses."

msgctxt "scene:24:77"
msgid ""
"Gras wächst schon überall\n"
"wo das Gestrüpp entfernt\n"
"wurde."
msgstr ""
"Grass grows everywhere where\n"
"the scrub was cleared.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:80"
msgid ""
"Wo das Buschwerk nicht\n"
"geschnitten wurde, ist\n"
"ist es undurchdringlich\n"
"wie eine Wand."
msgstr ""
"Where the bushes were not\n"
"cut, it is impenetrable\n"
"like a wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:84"
msgid ""
"Das kann doch nicht\n"
"ernst gemeint sein.\n"
"Was soll ich mit dem\n"
"Himmel anfangen, ich\n"
"bin kein Medizinmann."
msgstr ""
"That cannot be meant in\n"
"earnest, surely.\n"
"What am I to do with\n"
"the sky? I am no\n"
"medicine man."

msgctxt "scene:24:89"
msgid ""
"Nicht doch, die sind\n"
"mir schon etwas zu\n"
"schwer mein Freund."
msgstr ""
"Nay, those are a bit too\n"
"heavy for me, my\n"
"friend."

msgctxt "scene:24:92"
msgid ""
"Das liegt zu weit ent-\n"
"fernt und um dorthin\n"
"zu gelangen, müsste ich\n"
"durchs Wasser, was mir\n"
"bestenfalls nasse Füsse\n"
"einbringen würde."
msgstr ""
"That lies too far away,\n"
"and to get there I\n"
"would have to wade through\n"
"the water, which would\n"
"at best give me wet\n"
"feet."

msgctxt "scene:24:98"
msgid "Ich habe keinen Durst."
msgstr "I am not thirsty."

msgctxt "scene:24:99"
msgid ""
"Nein, Nein, ich bin\n"
"nicht gekommen um den\n"
"Rafters die Arbeit\n"
"abzunehmen."
msgstr ""
"No, no, I have not come\n"
"to take the work off\n"
"the rafters' hands.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:103"
msgid ""
"Die Steine würden\n"
"mich nur behindern"
msgstr ""
"The stones would only\n"
"hinder me."

msgctxt "scene:24:105"
msgid ""
"Well, von Hand ist da\n"
"ist da nichts zu\n"
"machen..."
msgstr ""
"Well, by hand nothing\n"
"can be done about\n"
"that..."

msgctxt "scene:24:108"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich denn mit\n"
"einem Pfad in der\n"
"Tasche."
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with a\n"
"path in my pocket?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:111"
msgid ""
"Well, da ist wohl nichts\n"
"mehr zu machen. Die Hütte\n"
"ist bis auf den letzten\n"
"Stamm abgebrannt."
msgstr ""
"Well, nothing can be done\n"
"there anymore. The cabin\n"
"is burnt down to the\n"
"last log."

msgctxt "scene:24:115"
msgid ""
"Ich habe kein Pferd,\n"
"um es daran festzubinden."
msgstr ""
"I have no horse to tie\n"
"to it."

msgctxt "scene:24:117"
msgid ""
"Von grossem Nutzen kann\n"
"mir ein Büschel Gras\n"
"nicht sein."
msgstr ""
"A tuft of grass cannot\n"
"be of great use to\n"
"me."

msgctxt "scene:24:120"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keine Zeit,\n"
"mich als Gärtner zu\n"
"betätigen."
msgstr ""
"I have no time to act as\n"
"a gardener.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:123"
msgid ""
"Ich zerlege ja nicht\n"
"den ganzen Steg, mein\n"
"Freund!"
msgstr ""
"I am hardly going to take\n"
"apart the whole jetty, my\n"
"friend!"

msgctxt "scene:24:126"
msgid ""
"Ich komme nicht rüber\n"
"auf die Stämme. Sprin-\n"
"gen ist zu gefährlich."
msgstr ""
"I cannot get over to the\n"
"logs. Jumping is too\n"
"dangerous."

msgctxt "scene:24:129"
msgid ""
"Die Stämme sind jetzt\n"
"nur noch am Steg be-\n"
"festigt..."
msgstr ""
"The logs are now only\n"
"fastened to the\n"
"jetty..."

msgctxt "scene:24:132"
msgid ""
"Ich muss die Befesti-\n"
"gung im Wasser zuerst\n"
"lösen, sonst driften\n"
"die Stämme weg vom\n"
"Ufer, und ich komme\n"
"ohne Boot nicht mehr\n"
"zum Seil."
msgstr ""
"I must first undo the\n"
"fastening in the water,\n"
"else the logs will drift\n"
"away from the bank, and\n"
"I cannot reach the rope\n"
"without a boat anymore.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:139"
msgid ""
"Einige Stämme sind im\n"
"Fluss und am Steg fest-\n"
"gebunden."
msgstr ""
"Some logs are tied in the\n"
"river and to the\n"
"jetty."

msgctxt "scene:24:142"
msgid ""
"Das Seil ist viel zu\n"
"stark gespannt, um es\n"
"mit dem rostigen Mes-\n"
"ser durchschneiden zu\n"
"können."
msgstr ""
"The rope is stretched far\n"
"too taut to be cut\n"
"with the rusty\n"
"knife.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:24:147"
msgid ""
"Mit diesem stumpfen\n"
"Messer kann ich das\n"
"Seil zu den Stämmen\n"
"nicht durchschneiden."
msgstr ""
"With this blunt knife I\n"
"cannot cut the rope\n"
"to the logs.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:26:0"
msgid ""
"Oh, da liegt ja ein\n"
"angerostetes Messer.\n"
"Das kann ich sicher\n"
"irgendwo gebrauchen,\n"
"ich nehme es mit."
msgstr ""
"Oh, a rusty knife is\n"
"lying there. I can\n"
"surely use it somewhere,\n"
"so I shall take it with\n"
"me."

msgctxt "scene:26:5"
msgid ""
"Ich wüsste nicht, was\n"
"ich von dort noch\n"
"nehmen könnte."
msgstr ""
"I know not what else I\n"
"could take from there.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:26:8"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit\n"
"einem Busch an-\n"
"fangen?"
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with\n"
"a bush?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:26:11"
msgid ""
"Da liegt etwas unter\n"
"dem Busch, halb im\n"
"Dreck vergraben."
msgstr ""
"Something lies under the\n"
"bush, half buried in the\n"
"dirt."

msgctxt "scene:26:14"
msgid ""
"Da ist nichts mehr, ausser\n"
"Aesten und Erde."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing more, save\n"
"for branches and dirt."

msgctxt "scene:26:16"
msgid ""
"An dem Busch sind einige\n"
"Aeste abgeschnitten wor-\n"
"den..."
msgstr ""
"Some branches have been\n"
"cut off from the bush...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:26:19"
msgid ""
"Der gesamte Weg wird\n"
"von undurchdring-\n"
"lichem Gebüsch ge-\n"
"säumt."
msgstr ""
"The entire path is lined\n"
"by impenetrable\n"
"bushes.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:26:23"
msgid ""
"Ein holpriger Pfad,\n"
"doch ungewöhnlich\n"
"breit, scheint mir."
msgstr ""
"A bumpy path, yet\n"
"unusually wide, it\n"
"seems to me."

msgctxt "scene:26:26"
msgid ""
"Da liegen überall auf\n"
"dem Weg Steine herum."
msgstr ""
"Stones lie about everywhere\n"
"upon the path."

msgctxt "scene:26:28"
msgid ""
"Ein Baum mitten im\n"
"Wald..."
msgstr ""
"A tree in the middle of\n"
"the forest..."

msgctxt "scene:26:30"
msgid ""
"Weit sieht man durch\n"
"dieses Dickicht im\n"
"Wald gar nicht hindurch."
msgstr ""
"One cannot see far through\n"
"this thicket in the\n"
"forest."

msgctxt "scene:26:33"
msgid ""
"Das Gestrüpp könnte man\n"
"eventuell für ein Lager-\n"
"feuer gut gebrauchen,\n"
"doch ich habe nicht vor,\n"
"ein Lagerfeuer zu ent-\n"
"fachen."
msgstr ""
"The scrub might well be\n"
"used for a campfire,\n"
"yet I do not intend\n"
"to kindle a\n"
"campfire.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:26:39"
msgid ""
"Wenn man Wege so ein-\n"
"fach mitnehmen könnte..."
msgstr ""
"If only one could simply\n"
"take paths with oneself..."

msgctxt "scene:26:41"
msgid ""
"Nein, die Steine sind\n"
"nur überflüssiger Bal-\n"
"last für mich."
msgstr ""
"No, the stones are\n"
"merely superfluous\n"
"ballast for me."

msgctxt "scene:26:44"
msgid ""
"Ein Baum wäre wohl\n"
"schön, doch Du über-\n"
"schätzt mich etwas."
msgstr ""
"A tree would be nice,\n"
"yet you overestimate me\n"
"a little."

msgctxt "scene:26:47"
msgid ""
"Mit dem ganzen Wald\n"
"würde ich mich wohl\n"
"etwas übernehmen..."
msgstr ""
"I would likely overreach\n"
"myself with the whole\n"
"forest..."

msgctxt "scene:28:0"
msgid ""
"Wir haben es tatsäch-\n"
"lich geschafft. Wahr-\n"
"scheinlich bereitet\n"
"der Cornel den Angriff\n"
"erst sorgfältig vor -\n"
"das gibt uns etwas\n"
"Zeit."
msgstr ""
"We actually made it.\n"
"Probably the Cornel\n"
"is preparing the\n"
"attack with care\n"
"first - that gives\n"
"us a little\n"
"time."

msgctxt "scene:28:7"
msgid "Es ist verschlossen."
msgstr "It is locked."

msgctxt "scene:28:8"
msgid "Hallo, ist da jemand?"
msgstr "Hello, anyone there?"

msgctxt "scene:28:9"
msgid ""
"Leuten zu helfen ist\n"
"schwieriger als ich\n"
"dachte."
msgstr ""
"Helping people is\n"
"harder than I\n"
"thought."

msgctxt "scene:28:12"
msgid ""
"Am besten versuchen\n"
"Sie's nochmal!"
msgstr ""
"You had best try again!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:28:14"
msgid ""
"Gut, ich hoffe, dass\n"
"unser Freund diesesmal\n"
"für unsere Argumente\n"
"zugänglicher ist."
msgstr ""
"Good, I hope that our\n"
"friend is more receptive\n"
"to our arguments this\n"
"time."

msgctxt "scene:28:18"
msgid ""
"Was wollen Sie denn\n"
"jetzt schon wieder ?"
msgstr ""
"What do you want again\n"
"now?"

msgctxt "scene:28:20"
msgid "Kann ich ihnen helfen?"
msgstr "Can I help you?"

msgctxt "scene:28:21"
msgid ""
"1. Bitte öffnen Sie\n"
"   das Tor und lassen\n"
"   Sie uns hinein."
msgstr ""
"1. Please open the gate\n"
"   and let us in.\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:28:24"
msgid ""
"2. Wir wollten nicht\n"
"   stören, auf Wieder-\n"
"   sehen."
msgstr ""
"2. We did not wish to\n"
"   disturb, goodbye.\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:28:27"
msgid ""
"3. Jeder Zeit kann die\n"
"   Farm angegriffen\n"
"   werden, öffnen Sie!"
msgstr ""
"3. The farm may be\n"
"   attacked at any time,\n"
"   open up!"

msgctxt "scene:28:30"
msgid ""
"Aber wer sind Sie denn?\n"
"Ich kenne Sie nicht?"
msgstr ""
"But who are you then?\n"
"I do not know you?"

msgctxt "scene:28:32"
msgid ""
"1. Unsere Namen sind\n"
"   unwichtig. Lassen\n"
"   Sie uns hinein!"
msgstr ""
"1. Our names are of no\n"
"   consequence. Let us in!\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:28:35"
msgid ""
"2. Ich bin Old Fire-\n"
"   hand und dies ist\n"
"   Tante Droll."
msgstr ""
"2. I am Old Firehand,\n"
"   and this is Aunt\n"
"   Droll."

msgctxt "scene:28:38"
msgid ""
"3. Schon gut, auf\n"
"   Wiedersehen."
msgstr ""
"3. Very well, goodbye\n"
"   then."

msgctxt "scene:28:40"
msgid ""
"Ich habe Anweisun-\n"
"gen, keine Fremden\n"
"hereinzulassen."
msgstr ""
"I have orders not to\n"
"let any strangers in.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:28:43"
msgid "Ich kenne Sie nicht!"
msgstr "I do not know you!"

msgctxt "scene:28:44"
msgid ""
"1. Wir sind hier ver-\n"
"   abredet. Glauben\n"
"   Sie mir doch!"
msgstr ""
"1. We have an appointment\n"
"   here. Pray believe me!\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:28:47"
msgid ""
"2. Was soll das\n"
"   heissen?"
msgstr ""
"2. What is that supposed\n"
"   to mean?"

msgctxt "scene:28:49"
msgid ""
"3. Mr. Butler erwartet\n"
"   uns, fragen Sie ihn."
msgstr ""
"3. Mr. Butler awaits us,\n"
"   ask him."

msgctxt "scene:28:51"
msgid "4. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "4. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:28:52"
msgid ""
"Mit wem sind Sie hier\n"
"verabredet? Mir hat\n"
"niemand etwas gesagt."
msgstr ""
"With whom do you have an\n"
"appointment here? No one\n"
"said anything to me."

msgctxt "scene:28:55"
msgid ""
"1. Wir haben eine\n"
"   Verabredung mit\n"
"   Mr. Butler."
msgstr ""
"1. We have an\n"
"   appointment with\n"
"   Mr. Butler."

msgctxt "scene:28:58"
msgid ""
"2. Mr. Patterson\n"
"   erwartet uns."
msgstr ""
"2. Mr. Patterson\n"
"   expects us."

msgctxt "scene:28:60"
msgid ""
"3. Mrs. Butler er-\n"
"   wartet uns."
msgstr ""
"3. Mrs. Butler\n"
"   expects us."

msgctxt "scene:28:62"
msgid "4. Unwichtig, Bye!"
msgstr "4. Unimportant, bye!"

msgctxt "scene:28:63"
msgid ""
"Das kann nicht sein.\n"
"Mr. Butler ist nicht\n"
"zuhause!"
msgstr ""
"That cannot be.\n"
"Mr. Butler is not\n"
"at home!"

msgctxt "scene:28:66"
msgid ""
"1. Mrs. Butler war-\n"
"   tet auf uns."
msgstr ""
"1. Mrs. Butler is\n"
"   waiting for us."

msgctxt "scene:28:68"
msgid ""
"2. Mr. Patterson er-\n"
"   wartet uns."
msgstr ""
"2. Mr. Patterson\n"
"   expects us."

msgctxt "scene:28:70"
msgid ""
"Am besten besprechen\n"
"Sie das mit Mrs. Butler\n"
"persönlich. Einen\n"
"Moment bitte."
msgstr ""
"You had best discuss\n"
"that with Mrs. Butler\n"
"in person. One\n"
"moment please."

msgctxt "scene:28:74"
msgid ""
"Mr. Patterson ist mit\n"
"Mr. Butler ausser Haus.\n"
"Tut mir leid."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Patterson is out\n"
"with Mr. Butler.\n"
"I am sorry."

msgctxt "scene:28:77"
msgid ""
"Mr. Patterson hat Sie\n"
"eingeladen? Davon\n"
"weiss ich nichts."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Patterson invited\n"
"you? I know nothing\n"
"about that."

msgctxt "scene:28:80"
msgid ""
"Mrs. Butler? Hm - Am\n"
"besten, Sie sprechen\n"
"selbst mit ihr. Einen\n"
"Moment bitte."
msgstr ""
"Mrs. Butler? Hm - you\n"
"had best speak with\n"
"her yourself. One\n"
"moment please."

msgctxt "scene:28:84"
msgid ""
"Sollte ich Sie kennen?\n"
"Entschuldigen Sie, aber\n"
"das muss ich mir nicht\n"
"anhören."
msgstr ""
"Should I know you?\n"
"Pardon me, but I do\n"
"not have to listen\n"
"to this."

msgctxt "scene:28:88"
msgid ""
"Mr. Butler kann ich\n"
"nicht fragen. Mr.\n"
"Butler ist nicht auf\n"
"der Farm."
msgstr ""
"I cannot ask\n"
"Mr. Butler. Mr.\n"
"Butler is not at\n"
"the farm."

msgctxt "scene:28:92"
msgid "Good bye."
msgstr "Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:28:93"
msgid ""
"Ein Angriff? Es ist ja\n"
"alles ruhig hier."
msgstr ""
"An attack? Everything\n"
"is quiet here."

msgctxt "scene:28:95"
msgid ""
"1. Doch, doch!\n"
"   Tramps wollen\n"
"   die Farm plündern."
msgstr ""
"1. Yes, indeed!\n"
"   Tramps want to\n"
"   plunder the farm."

msgctxt "scene:28:98"
msgid ""
"2. Sie werden schon\n"
"   sehen."
msgstr ""
"2. You shall see\n"
"   for yourself."

msgctxt "scene:28:100"
msgid "3. Auf Wiedersehen."
msgstr "3. Goodbye."

msgctxt "scene:28:101"
msgid "Glaub' ich nicht."
msgstr "I do not think so."

msgctxt "scene:28:102"
msgid "Oder auch nicht."
msgstr "Or perhaps not."

msgctxt "scene:28:103"
msgid ""
"Nun, meine Herren, Sie\n"
"wollten mich sprechen?"
msgstr ""
"Well, gentlemen, you\n"
"wished to speak to me?"

msgctxt "scene:28:105"
msgid "Guten Tag, Mrs.Butler."
msgstr "Good day, Mrs. Butler."

msgctxt "scene:28:106"
msgid ""
"Guten Tag Mister. Wie\n"
"kann ich Ihnen helfen?"
msgstr ""
"Good day, Mister. How\n"
"can I help you?"

msgctxt "scene:28:108"
msgid ""
"1. Wir möchten Ihren\n"
"   Mann sprechen."
msgstr ""
"1. We wish to speak\n"
"   to your husband."

msgctxt "scene:28:110"
msgid ""
"2. Mr. Patterson er-\n"
"   wartet uns bestimmt."
msgstr ""
"2. Mr. Patterson surely\n"
"   expects us."

msgctxt "scene:28:112"
msgid ""
"3. Wir müssen dringend\n"
"   mit  ihnen sprechen."
msgstr ""
"3. We must urgently\n"
"   speak with you."

msgctxt "scene:28:114"
msgid ""
"Ich muss Sie enttäu-\n"
"schen. Mein Mann ist\n"
"nicht zuhause."
msgstr ""
"I must disappoint\n"
"you. My husband is\n"
"not at home."

msgctxt "scene:28:117"
msgid ""
"Mr. Patterson ist mit\n"
"meinem Mann ausser\n"
"Haus. Tut mir leid."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Patterson is out\n"
"with my husband.\n"
"I am sorry."

msgctxt "scene:28:120"
msgid "Worum geht es denn?"
msgstr "What is it concerning?"

msgctxt "scene:28:121"
msgid ""
"1. Sie sind in\n"
"   grosser Gefahr!"
msgstr ""
"1. You are in\n"
"   great danger!"

msgctxt "scene:28:123"
msgid ""
"2. Tramps wollen\n"
"   die Farm über-\n"
"   fallen."
msgstr ""
"2. Tramps intend\n"
"   to raid the\n"
"   farm."

msgctxt "scene:28:126"
msgid ""
"Wieso sollte ich gerade\n"
"Ihnen vertrauen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I trust\n"
"you of all people?"

msgctxt "scene:28:128"
msgid ""
"Woher weiss ich, dass\n"
"SIE uns nicht überfal-\n"
"len wollen?"
msgstr ""
"How do I know that\n"
"YOU do not intend to\n"
"raid us?"

msgctxt "scene:28:131"
msgid ""
"1. Wir sind ehrliche\n"
"   Leute."
msgstr ""
"1. We are honest\n"
"   folk."

msgctxt "scene:28:133"
msgid ""
"2. Lassen Sie uns hi-\n"
"   nein. Wir verlieren\n"
"   nur Zeit."
msgstr ""
"2. Let us inside.\n"
"   We are only\n"
"   losing time."

msgctxt "scene:28:136"
msgid ""
"3. Mr. Patterson kennt\n"
"   uns, er könnte Sie\n"
"   überzeugen."
msgstr ""
"3. Mr. Patterson knows\n"
"   us; he could\n"
"   convince you."

msgctxt "scene:28:139"
msgid ""
"Nennen Sie mir doch\n"
"bitte erst einmal\n"
"ihre Namen."
msgstr ""
"Please tell me your\n"
"names first of all.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:28:142"
msgid ""
"Mr. Patterson ist leider\n"
"nicht in der Nähe. Viel-\n"
"leicht sagen mir Ihre\n"
"Namen ja etwas."
msgstr ""
"Mr. Patterson is not\n"
"nearby, unfortunately.\n"
"Perhaps your names tell\n"
"me something."

msgctxt "scene:28:146"
msgid "Wer sind Sie eigentlich?"
msgstr "Who are you, actually?"

msgctxt "scene:28:147"
msgid ""
"Verzeihen Sie bitte\n"
"mein Benehmen, ich bin\n"
"Firehand und meinen\n"
"Begleiter nennt man\n"
"Tante Droll."
msgstr ""
"Please pardon my\n"
"manners, I am\n"
"Firehand and my\n"
"companion is called\n"
"Aunt Droll."

msgctxt "scene:28:152"
msgid ""
"Firehand?! Ja, Sie wer-\n"
"den bereits von Ihren\n"
"Freunden, den Rafters,\n"
"erwartet. Seien Sie mir\n"
"gegrüsst und treten Sie\n"
"ein."
msgstr ""
"Firehand?! Yes, you are\n"
"expected already by your\n"
"friends, the rafters.\n"
"Greetings to you and pray\n"
"step inside.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:0"
msgid ""
"Ah, Firehand, Du schon\n"
"wieder, mir scheint,\n"
"dass sich unsere Wege\n"
"immer wieder kreuzen."
msgstr ""
"Ah, Firehand, you again;\n"
"it seems to me that our\n"
"paths cross again and\n"
"again."

msgctxt "scene:29:4"
msgid ""
"Ja, Cornel, ich werde\n"
"Dir so lange nach-\n"
"stellen, bis Du Deine\n"
"gerechte Strafe\n"
"erlangst."
msgstr ""
"Yes, Cornel, I shall\n"
"pursue you until you\n"
"receive your just\n"
"punishment.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:9"
msgid ""
"Ha,Ha,..! Mir scheint\n"
"Du hast noch nicht\n"
"genug, trotz der zwei\n"
"Niederlagen, die Du\n"
"schon hattest..."
msgstr ""
"Ha, ha,..! It seems you\n"
"have not had enough,\n"
"despite the two defeats\n"
"you have had...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:14"
msgid ""
"Jetzt werden wir ihm\n"
"seine letzte Lektion\n"
"erteilen, und die Sache\n"
"endgültig erledigen."
msgstr ""
"Now we shall teach him\n"
"his final lesson and settle\n"
"the matter once and for all.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:18"
msgid ""
"Ja, der wird sich\n"
"wundern."
msgstr ""
"Yes, he will be\n"
"surprised."

msgctxt "scene:29:20"
msgid ""
"Du siehst Firehand,\n"
"meine Leute sind fest\n"
"entschlossen, und ich\n"
"werde auch nicht gehen,\n"
"bevor wir unsere Kasse\n"
"aufgebessert haben."
msgstr ""
"You see Firehand, my\n"
"men are determined, and\n"
"I shall not leave before\n"
"we have replenished\n"
"our treasury.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:26"
msgid ""
"Wir haben nicht vor,\n"
"Dir das geringste zu\n"
"geben. Mach, dass Du\n"
"wegkommst."
msgstr ""
"We do not intend to\n"
"give you the least bit.\n"
"See that you get away\n"
"from here."

msgctxt "scene:29:30"
msgid ""
"Ich gebe Euch noch\n"
"eine letzte Chance\n"
"aufzugeben. Wenn Ihr\n"
"Euch ergebt, dann\n"
"geschieht Euch nichts."
msgstr ""
"I give you one last\n"
"chance to surrender.\n"
"If you surrender, then\n"
"nothing will happen\n"
"to you."

msgctxt "scene:29:35"
msgid ""
"Deine Versprechungen\n"
"sind nichts wert,\n"
"Cornel. Wir werden uns\n"
"zu wehren wissen."
msgstr ""
"Your promises are worth\n"
"nothing, Cornel. We\n"
"shall know how to\n"
"defend ourselves."

msgctxt "scene:29:39"
msgid ""
"Was reden wir da noch\n"
"lange herum, lasst uns\n"
"die Farm stürmen.."
msgstr ""
"Why talk around it any\n"
"longer, let us storm\n"
"the farm.."

msgctxt "scene:29:42"
msgid "Kawumm!"
msgstr "Kaboom!"

msgctxt "scene:29:43"
msgid ""
"Was war denn das? Ich\n"
"habe geglaubt die sind\n"
"nicht bewaffnet, und\n"
"nun schiessen die mit\n"
"Kanonen auf uns."
msgstr ""
"What was that? I\n"
"thought they were not\n"
"armed, and now they\n"
"are shooting at us with\n"
"cannons."

msgctxt "scene:29:48"
msgid ""
"Na, Ihr Schurken, soll\n"
"ich Euch noch eine\n"
"Kostprobe liefern oder\n"
"seid Ihr nun überzeugt,\n"
"dass es hier für Euch\n"
"nichts zu holen gibt?"
msgstr ""
"Well, you rogues, shall\n"
"I give you another taste\n"
"or are you convinced now\n"
"that there is nothing to\n"
"be had for you here?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:54"
msgid ""
"Damnet, hat uns dieser\n"
"Firehand wieder einen\n"
"Strich durch die Rech-\n"
"nung gemacht..."
msgstr ""
"Dammit, Firehand has\n"
"foiled our plans once\n"
"again...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:58"
msgid ""
"Also Männer, lasst uns\n"
"von hier verschwinden,\n"
"die haben uns ausge-\n"
"bootet, doch wir\n"
"werden uns am Silbersee\n"
"schadlos halten."
msgstr ""
"So men, let us get away\n"
"from here, they have\n"
"outwitted us, but we\n"
"shall compensate\n"
"ourselves at Silver\n"
"Lake."

msgctxt "scene:29:64"
msgid ""
"Wir gehen Firehand,\n"
"doch wir werden uns\n"
"wiedersehen, und\n"
"dann wird sich das\n"
"Blatt wenden."
msgstr ""
"We leave, Firehand,\n"
"yet we shall meet\n"
"again, and then the\n"
"tables will turn.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:29:69"
msgid ""
"Ich kann es kaum\n"
"erwarten Dich wieder\n"
"zu treffen, ich\n"
"werde dann dafür\n"
"sorgen, dass Du nie\n"
"mehr Schaden\n"
"anrichten wirst."
msgstr ""
"I can scarcely wait to\n"
"meet you again; I shall\n"
"then see to it that you\n"
"cause no further harm\n"
"ever again.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:0"
msgid ""
"Ah, Mr.Firehand! Kann\n"
"ich ihnen noch irgend-\n"
"wie behilflich sein ?"
msgstr ""
"Ah, Mr. Firehand! Can I\n"
"be of any further\n"
"assistance to you?"

msgctxt "scene:30:3"
msgid ""
"Nein, Ich glaube, ich\n"
"habe bereits alle\n"
"Probleme gelöst."
msgstr ""
"No, I believe I have\n"
"already solved all the\n"
"problems."

msgctxt "scene:30:6"
msgid ""
"Dann wird der Cornel\n"
"wohl böse Überraschung\n"
"erleben..."
msgstr ""
"Then Cornel will likely\n"
"experience a nasty\n"
"surprise..."

msgctxt "scene:30:9"
msgid ""
"Mrs. Butler, die Lage\n"
"ist sehr ernst. Wir\n"
"müssen damit rechnen,\n"
"dass in wenigen Stun-\n"
"den Tramps ihre Farm\n"
"angreifen werden."
msgstr ""
"Mrs. Butler, the state\n"
"of affairs is very grave.\n"
"We must expect tramps\n"
"to attack your farm in\n"
"a few hours.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:15"
msgid ""
"Aber warum? Was ver-\n"
"sprechen die sich\n"
"davon?"
msgstr ""
"But why? What do they\n"
"hope to gain from\n"
"it?"

msgctxt "scene:30:18"
msgid ""
"Was werden die wohl\n"
"von Ihnen wollen? Ihr\n"
"Geld natürlich, gute\n"
"Frau! Wer so eine gros-\n"
"se Farm weit ab von\n"
"jeder Stadt besitzt,"
msgstr ""
"What would they want from\n"
"you? Your money, of course,\n"
"good lady! Whoever owns\n"
"such a large farm far off\n"
"from any town,\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:24"
msgid ""
"der lässt sein Geld\n"
"bestimmt nicht auf der\n"
"Bank - und das wissen\n"
"diese Gauner."
msgstr ""
"surely does not leave\n"
"their money in the bank -\n"
"and those rogues know it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:28"
msgid ""
"Können Sie bitte Ihren\n"
"Mann holen, Mrs.Butler?\n"
"Es ist sicherlich wich-\n"
"tig,dass auch er weiss,\n"
"worum es hier geht."
msgstr ""
"Could you fetch your\n"
"husband, Mrs. Butler? It\n"
"is surely important that\n"
"he knows what this is\n"
"about as well."

msgctxt "scene:30:33"
msgid ""
"Mein Mann ist leider\n"
"nicht zuhause."
msgstr ""
"My husband is not at\n"
"home, unfortunately."

msgctxt "scene:30:35"
msgid ""
"Wann erwarten Sie\n"
"eigentlich Ihren Mann\n"
"zurück, Mrs. Butler?"
msgstr ""
"When do you actually\n"
"expect your husband\n"
"back, Mrs. Butler?"

msgctxt "scene:30:38"
msgid ""
"Er ist zusammen mit\n"
"meinem Bruder und\n"
"dessen Tochter in\n"
"Fort Dodge, um dort\n"
"nach neuen Kleidern\n"
"für sie zu schauen."
msgstr ""
"He is in Fort Dodge\n"
"together with my brother\n"
"and his daughter to look\n"
"for new clothes for her\n"
"there.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:44"
msgid ""
"Sie werden wohl entwe-\n"
"der heute oder morgen\n"
"von dort zurück sein."
msgstr ""
"They should be back from\n"
"there either today or\n"
"tomorrow."

msgctxt "scene:30:47"
msgid ""
"Ich erwarte die drei\n"
"entweder noch heute\n"
"oder morgen zurück."
msgstr ""
"I expect the three back\n"
"either today or tomorrow.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:50"
msgid ""
"Heavens! Dann laufen\n"
"sie den Tramps ja\n"
"direkt in die Arme!"
msgstr ""
"Heavens! Then they are\n"
"walking straight into the\n"
"tramps' arms!"

msgctxt "scene:30:53"
msgid ""
"Was? Das darf nicht\n"
"sein! Wir müssen sie\n"
"warnen oder sonst\n"
"etwas für sie tun!"
msgstr ""
"What? That must not\n"
"be! We must warn them\n"
"or do something else\n"
"for them!"

msgctxt "scene:30:57"
msgid ""
"Ich fürchte, dafür\n"
"ist es schon zu spät.\n"
"Die Tramps lauern\n"
"sicherlich irgendwo\n"
"dort draussen. Es wäre\n"
"zu gefährlich, einen\n"
"Boten nach Fort Dodge\n"
"zu schicken."
msgstr ""
"I fear it is already\n"
"too late for that.\n"
"The tramps are surely\n"
"lurking somewhere\n"
"out there. It would be\n"
"too dangerous to send\n"
"a messenger to Fort\n"
"Dodge."

msgctxt "scene:30:65"
msgid ""
"Aber was können wir\n"
"sonst unternehmen?"
msgstr ""
"But what else can we\n"
"undertake?"

msgctxt "scene:30:67"
msgid ""
"1. Am besten warten\n"
"   wir ab. Die Tramps\n"
"   werden kaum über\n"
"   die hohen Mauern\n"
"   kommen."
msgstr ""
"1. We had best wait. The\n"
"   tramps will hardly get\n"
"   over the high walls.\n"
"   ­\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:30:72"
msgid ""
"2. Wir müssen uns auf\n"
"   den Angriff vor-\n"
"   bereiten."
msgstr ""
"2. We must prepare for\n"
"   the attack.\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:30:75"
msgid ""
"Ob abwarten das Beste\n"
"ist was wir machen kön-\n"
"nen? Ich glaube nicht!\n"
"Die Mauern sind auf kei-\n"
"nen Fall hoch genug."
msgstr ""
"Whether waiting is the\n"
"best thing we can do? I\n"
"think not! The walls are\n"
"by no means high enough.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:80"
msgid ""
"Und wie soll das\n"
"funktionieren?"
msgstr ""
"And how is that to work?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:82"
msgid ""
"1. Wir müssen die Mau-\n"
"   ern mit bewaffneten\n"
"   Männern besetzen."
msgstr ""
"1. We must man the walls\n"
"   with armed men.\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:30:85"
msgid ""
"2. Wir müssen Schwach-\n"
"   stellen bei den\n"
"   Mauern finden."
msgstr ""
"2. We must find weak\n"
"   points in the walls.\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:30:88"
msgid ""
"3. Das Klügste wäre,\n"
"   wenn wir Verstär-\n"
"   kung holen."
msgstr ""
"3. The wisest thing would\n"
"   be to fetch\n"
"   reinforcements."

msgctxt "scene:30:91"
msgid ""
"Das können wir schon\n"
"übernehmen. Aber wie\n"
"sieht es mit Waffen\n"
"aus, Mrs. Butler?"
msgstr ""
"We can take care of that.\n"
"But how about weapons,\n"
"Mrs. Butler?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:95"
msgid ""
"Waffen? Ich wüsste\n"
"nicht, dass wir so\n"
"etwas im Hause ha-\n"
"ben. Die einzigen\n"
"Gewehre haben mein\n"
"Mann und mein Bruder\n"
"mit nach Fort Dodge\n"
"genommen."
msgstr ""
"Weapons? I know of none\n"
"in the house. The only\n"
"rifles were taken to\n"
"Fort Dodge by my husband\n"
"and my brother.\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:103"
msgid ""
"Das grösste Problem ist\n"
"bestimmt das Haupttor,\n"
"durch das Sie eben he-\n"
"reingekommen sind. Die\n"
"Torflügel sitzen sehr\n"
"locker in den Angeln."
msgstr ""
"The greatest problem is\n"
"surely the main gate through\n"
"which you just entered. The\n"
"gate leaves sit very loose\n"
"in their hinges.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:109"
msgid ""
"Wir wollten das schon\n"
"lange in Ordnung brin-\n"
"gen, doch mein Mann ist\n"
"noch nicht dazu gekom-\n"
"men."
msgstr ""
"We have wanted to fix\n"
"that for a long time, but\n"
"my husband has not gotten\n"
"around to it yet.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:114"
msgid ""
"1. Die Torflügel werden\n"
"   schon halten."
msgstr ""
"1. The gate leaves will\n"
"   hold."

msgctxt "scene:30:116"
msgid ""
"2. Wir müssen das\n"
"   Tor befestigen."
msgstr ""
"2. We must secure the\n"
"   gate."

msgctxt "scene:30:118"
msgid ""
"Heavens! Das ist aber\n"
"eine sehr optimistische\n"
"Einstellung. Das Tor\n"
"muss auf jeden Fall ver-\n"
"barrikadiert werden! Sie\n"
"könnten doch diese Auf-\n"
"gabe übernehmen, Mr.\n"
"Firehand."
msgstr ""
"Heavens! That is a very\n"
"optimistic attitude. The\n"
"gate must be barricaded in\n"
"any case! You could take\n"
"on this task, Mr.\n"
"Firehand.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:126"
msgid ""
"Stimmt! Das Tor muss\n"
"dem Angriff auf jeden\n"
"Fall standhalten. Wir\n"
"müssen es verbarrika-\n"
"dieren! Vielleicht\n"
"könnten sie diese\n"
"Aufgabe übernehmen,\n"
"Mr. Firehand."
msgstr ""
"True! The gate must\n"
"withstand the attack in\n"
"any case. We must\n"
"barricade it! Perhaps\n"
"you could take on this\n"
"task, Mr. Firehand.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:134"
msgid ""
"Nein, das ist zu ge-\n"
"fährlich. Zum einen\n"
"ist die Chance sehr\n"
"gering, dass der Bote\n"
"überhaupt bis nach\n"
"Fort Dodge kommt, und\n"
"zum anderen wäre der"
msgstr ""
"No, that is too dangerous.\n"
"For one, the chance is very\n"
"slight that the messenger\n"
"gets to Fort Dodge at all,\n"
"and for another, Cornel\n"
"would in such a case be\n"
"informed about us."

msgctxt "scene:30:141"
msgid ""
"Cornel in einem sol-\n"
"chen Fall über uns\n"
"informiert. Wenn wir\n"
"uns ruhig verhalten, und\n"
"hier auf den Angriff\n"
"vorbereiten, werden\n"
"die Tramps bestimmt\n"
"überrascht sein,"
msgstr ""
"If we stay quiet and\n"
"prepare for the attack\n"
"here, the tramps will\n"
"surely be surprised\n"
"when bullets fly about\n"
"their ears.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:149"
msgid ""
"wenn ihnen die Ku-\n"
"geln um die Ohren\n"
"fliegen. Aber wo be-\n"
"kommen wir genügend\n"
"Gewehre her?"
msgstr ""
"But where do we get\n"
"enough rifles from?\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:154"
msgid ""
"1. Irgendwo werden\n"
"   wir wohl schon Ge-\n"
"   wehre auftreiben."
msgstr ""
"1. Somewhere we shall\n"
"   surely dig up rifles.\n"
"   ­"

msgctxt "scene:30:157"
msgid ""
"2. Haben Sie denn keine\n"
"   Gewehre dabei,\n"
"   Mr. Blenter?"
msgstr ""
"2. Do you have no rifles\n"
"   with you, Mr.\n"
"   Blenter?"

msgctxt "scene:30:160"
msgid ""
"Die elenden Tramps\n"
"haben uns alles ge-\n"
"stohlen. Wir können\n"
"nur mit Steinen wer-\n"
"fen."
msgstr ""
"Those wretched tramps\n"
"stole everything from us.\n"
"We can only throw stones.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:165"
msgid ""
"Dann sollten wir uns\n"
"unbedingt hier einmal\n"
"umschauen, ob wir nicht\n"
"doch Gewehre oder ähnli-\n"
"ches finden."
msgstr ""
"Then we should by all\n"
"means look around here to\n"
"see if we might not find\n"
"rifles or the like after\n"
"all."

msgctxt "scene:30:170"
msgid ""
"Naja, es wird sich schon\n"
"irgendwo etwas finden.\n"
"Wie sieht es eigentlich\n"
"mit den Befestigungen\n"
"der Farm aus, Mrs.\n"
"Butler?"
msgstr ""
"Well, something will\n"
"surely be found somewhere.\n"
"How are the farm's\n"
"fortifications looking\n"
"actually, Mrs.\n"
"Butler?"

msgctxt "scene:30:176"
msgid ""
"Gut, ich werde mich um-\n"
"sehen und schauen, was\n"
"ich tun kann, um den\n"
"Tramps eine tolle Über-\n"
"raschung zu bereiten."
msgstr ""
"Good, I shall look around\n"
"and see what I can do\n"
"to prepare a fine\n"
"surprise for the\n"
"tramps."

msgctxt "scene:30:181"
msgid ""
"Gut, ich werde mich\n"
"ebenfalls etwas um die\n"
"Vorbereitungen küm-\n"
"mern. Der Cornel wird\n"
"diesesmal ein böses\n"
"Erwachen haben."
msgstr ""
"Good, I shall likewise\n"
"take care of some of\n"
"the preparations.\n"
"Cornel shall have a rude\n"
"awakening this\n"
"time."

msgctxt "scene:30:187"
msgid "Kurze Zeit später..."
msgstr "A short time later..."

msgctxt "scene:30:188"
msgid ""
"Durch dieses Tor wird kein\n"
"ungebetener Gast kommen. Da\n"
"werden sich die Tramps ganz\n"
"schön die Zähne ausbeissen."
msgstr ""
"Through this gate no\n"
"uninvited guest shall pass.\n"
"The tramps will surely\n"
"break their teeth on this."

msgctxt "scene:30:192"
msgid ""
"Die Tramps sind bereits\n"
"vor der Mauer Mr.\n"
"Firehand. Es sieht so\n"
"aus, als ob der Anfüh-\n"
"rer gerne mit jemandem\n"
"hier in der Farm spre-\n"
"chen möchte."
msgstr ""
"The tramps are already in\n"
"front of the wall, Mr.\n"
"Firehand. It looks as though\n"
"the leader would like to\n"
"speak with someone here at\n"
"the farm.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:199"
msgid ""
"Gut, ich werde auf die\n"
"Mauer gehen und mich\n"
"mal mit dem Schurken\n"
"unterhalten."
msgstr ""
"Good, I shall go up on\n"
"the wall and have a talk\n"
"with the villain.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:203"
msgid ""
"Droll, gehen Sie zur\n"
"Kanone auf dem Dach,\n"
"während ich mit dem\n"
"Cornel verhandle.\n"
"Wenn es notwendig ist,\n"
"dann feuern Sie einen"
msgstr ""
"Droll, go to the cannon\n"
"upon the roof while I\n"
"negotiate with Cornel.\n"
"If necessary, fire a\n"
"warning shot,\n"
"that will"

msgctxt "scene:30:209"
msgid ""
"Warnschuss ab, das\n"
"wird meine Argumente\n"
"gegenüber dem Schurken\n"
"noch unterstreichen."
msgstr ""
"underscore my arguments\n"
"against the rogue\n"
"even further.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:213"
msgid ""
"Gut, ich werde denen\n"
"so einheizen, dass\n"
"ihnen Hören und Sehen\n"
"vergeht. Der Schurke\n"
"wird sich wundern...\n"
"Kommen Sie mit, mein\n"
"Freund."
msgstr ""
"Good, I shall make it so\n"
"hot for them that they won't\n"
"know whether they're coming or\n"
"going. The villain will be\n"
"surprised...\n"
"Come along, my\n"
"friend."

msgctxt "scene:30:220"
msgid ""
"Den haben wir vorerst\n"
"verjagt, doch wir\n"
"können nicht einfach\n"
"davon ausgehen, dass\n"
"er nicht zurückkommt."
msgstr ""
"We have driven him off\n"
"for now, yet we cannot\n"
"simply assume that he\n"
"will not return.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:225"
msgid ""
"Glauben Sie wirklich,\n"
"dass der Cornel\n"
"zurückkommt?"
msgstr ""
"Do you truly believe\n"
"that Cornel will\n"
"return?"

msgctxt "scene:30:228"
msgid ""
"Völlig ausschliessen\n"
"kann man das nicht...\n"
"Ich schlage vor,\n"
"Tante Droll bleibt\n"
"zu Ihrem Schutze hier,\n"
"und ich nehme die\n"
"Verfolgung auf."
msgstr ""
"That cannot be ruled out\n"
"entirely...\n"
"I suggest Aunt Droll\n"
"remains here for your\n"
"protection, while I\n"
"take up the pursuit.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:235"
msgid ""
"Wenn der Weg zum\n"
"Silbersee in die Berge\n"
"führt, habe ich gute\n"
"Chancen auf meinen\n"
"Freund Winnetou zu"
msgstr ""
"If the path to Silver\n"
"Lake leads into the\n"
"mountains, I stand good\n"
"chances of meeting my\n"
"friend Winnetou,"

msgctxt "scene:30:240"
msgid ""
"stossen, der wird mir\n"
"sicher behilflich sein\n"
"den Verbrechern das\n"
"Handwerk zu legen."
msgstr ""
"who will surely be of\n"
"assistance in putting an\n"
"end to the criminals'\n"
"trades."

msgctxt "scene:30:244"
msgid ""
"Das ist eine gute Idee,\n"
"wenn die Schurken noch\n"
"einmal auftauchen,werden\n"
"wir denen gewaltig ein-\n"
"heizen."
msgstr ""
"That is a good idea;\n"
"if the rogues show up once\n"
"more, we shall make it\n"
"terribly hot for them.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:249"
msgid ""
"Eine Hügellandschaft unter\n"
"strahlend blauem Himmel."
msgstr ""
"A hilly landscape beneath\n"
"a radiant blue sky."

msgctxt "scene:30:251"
msgid ""
"Ein knorriger Baum,\n"
"der wohl schon vor\n"
"dem Bau der Farm an\n"
"diesem Platz stand."
msgstr ""
"A gnarled tree that\n"
"stood in this spot long\n"
"before the farm was\n"
"built."

msgctxt "scene:30:255"
msgid ""
"Die Mauer macht einen\n"
"stabilen Eindruck, auch\n"
"wenn die abgeschlagenen\n"
"Stellen ins Auge stechen."
msgstr ""
"The wall makes a sturdy\n"
"impression, even if the\n"
"chipped spots catch the\n"
"eye."

msgctxt "scene:30:259"
msgid ""
"Die Treppe ist absolut\n"
"baufällig, und kann nicht\n"
"begangen werden."
msgstr ""
"The staircase is totally\n"
"dilapidated and cannot\n"
"be walked upon."

msgctxt "scene:30:262"
msgid ""
"Das Tor hängt gerade\n"
"noch so in den Angeln."
msgstr ""
"The gate is barely hanging\n"
"on its hinges."

msgctxt "scene:30:264"
msgid ""
"Der Heuwagen ist eine\n"
"ideale Barrikade, und\n"
"verstärkt das Tor."
msgstr ""
"The hay wagon is an ideal\n"
"barricade and reinforces\n"
"the gate."

msgctxt "scene:30:267"
msgid ""
"Holzscheite, ein Hackbock\n"
"und eine Axt liegen hier\n"
"durcheinander."
msgstr ""
"Logs of wood, a chopping\n"
"block, and an axe lie scattered\n"
"here in disarray."

msgctxt "scene:30:270"
msgid ""
"Ein fein säuberlich ge-\n"
"kehrter Vorplatz, sicher\n"
"ist das auf die Anwesen-\n"
"heit von Mrs. Butler zu-\n"
"rückzuführen."
msgstr ""
"A neatly swept yard;\n"
"surely this is attributable\n"
"to the presence of Mrs.\n"
"Butler.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:275"
msgid ""
"Eine Wasserpumpe! Gut,\n"
"so können uns die Tramps\n"
"sicher nicht wegen Was-\n"
"sermangels zum Aufgeben\n"
"zwingen."
msgstr ""
"A water pump! Good, so the\n"
"tramps surely cannot force\n"
"us to surrender for lack\n"
"of water.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:280"
msgid ""
"Ein Fass, um das Regenwas-\n"
"ser aufzufangen, mit einer\n"
"Zuleitung in die daneben-\n"
"stehende Badewanne."
msgstr ""
"A barrel to catch rain-\n"
"water, with a supply line\n"
"into the bathtub standing\n"
"next to it."

msgctxt "scene:30:284"
msgid ""
"Die Holztüre könnte auch\n"
"wieder einmal einen An-\n"
"strich gebrauchen."
msgstr ""
"The wooden door could do\n"
"with a coat of paint once\n"
"again."

msgctxt "scene:30:287"
msgid ""
"Das Farmerhaus ist recht\n"
"beachtlich in der Grösse."
msgstr ""
"The farmhouse is quite\n"
"considerable in size."

msgctxt "scene:30:289"
msgid ""
"Aha, für Treppenersatz\n"
"wurde bereits gesorgt.\n"
"Über die Leiter lässt\n"
"sich der Gang auf der\n"
"Mauer ebenfalls bequem\n"
"erreichen."
msgstr ""
"Aha, a replacement for\n"
"the stairs was provided.\n"
"Via the ladder, the walk\n"
"upon the wall can likewise\n"
"be reached comfortably.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:295"
msgid "Ich habe keinen Durst."
msgstr "I am not thirsty."

msgctxt "scene:30:296"
msgid ""
"Da gibt es nichts zum\n"
"Anzünden."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing there\n"
"to kindle."

msgctxt "scene:30:298"
msgid ""
"Wäsche soll ich nun auch\n"
"noch waschen?"
msgstr ""
"Now I am supposed to wash\n"
"laundry as well?"

msgctxt "scene:30:300"
msgid ""
"Jetzt soll ich wohl die\n"
"Pumpe wegsprengen."
msgstr ""
"Now I suppose I am to blow\n"
"up the pump."

msgctxt "scene:30:302"
msgid ""
"In der Schüssel ist ja\n"
"bereits Teig."
msgstr ""
"In the bowl there is dough\n"
"already."

msgctxt "scene:30:304"
msgid ""
"Die Schüssel fasst nicht\n"
"genug Wasser und kann auch\n"
"nicht aufgehängt werden."
msgstr ""
"The bowl holds not enough\n"
"water and cannot be hung\n"
"up either."

msgctxt "scene:30:307"
msgid ""
"Daran kann ich nichts\n"
"aufschliessen."
msgstr ""
"I can unlock nothing with\n"
"that."

msgctxt "scene:30:309"
msgid ""
"Ich mag nicht sinnlos\n"
"nach Wasser graben,\n"
"wenn ich doch nur zu\n"
"pumpen brauche."
msgstr ""
"I do not care to dig for\n"
"water pointlessly, when\n"
"I need only pump.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:313"
msgid ""
"Ja, jetzt noch ein\n"
"zweites Rad, und wir\n"
"haben einen Feuer-\n"
"wehrwagen..."
msgstr ""
"Yes, now one more wheel\n"
"and we shall have a fire\n"
"engine...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:317"
msgid ""
"Verwechselst Du die Pumpe\n"
"nicht mit einer Weinfla-\n"
"sche?!"
msgstr ""
"Are you not confusing the\n"
"pump with a wine bottle?!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:320"
msgid ""
"Warum nach Wasser graben,\n"
"wenn ich doch nur zu pumpen\n"
"brauche."
msgstr ""
"Why dig for water when I\n"
"need only pump?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:323"
msgid ""
"Da ist edelster Schnaps\n"
"in der Flasche, ich werde\n"
"den doch nicht mit Wasser\n"
"verdünnen."
msgstr ""
"In the bottle is finest\n"
"liquor; I shall hardly\n"
"dilute that with water.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:327"
msgid ""
"In der Flasche befindet\n"
"sich bereits Schnaps, wir\n"
"wollen den edlen Saft\n"
"doch nicht pantschen."
msgstr ""
"Inside the bottle there\n"
"is liquor already; we would\n"
"hardly adulterate that\n"
"noble juice."

msgctxt "scene:30:331"
msgid "Der Eimer ist bereits voll."
msgstr "The bucket is full already."

msgctxt "scene:30:332"
msgid ""
"Die Tasse ist ja bis\n"
"zum Rand voll mit Oel."
msgstr ""
"The cup is full to the\n"
"brim with oil."

msgctxt "scene:30:334"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich die Wolle\n"
"mit Wasser tränken?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I soak the\n"
"wool with water?"

msgctxt "scene:30:336"
msgid ""
"Die Wolle ist bereits mit\n"
"Alkohol getränkt, warum soll\n"
"ich sie wieder waschen?"
msgstr ""
"The wool is soaked with\n"
"alcohol already; why should\n"
"I wash it again?"

msgctxt "scene:30:339"
msgid ""
"Zum Befestigen des Tores\n"
"eignet sich das Seil nicht."
msgstr ""
"The rope is not suitable for\n"
"fastening the gate."

msgctxt "scene:30:341"
msgid ""
"Das Seil ist nicht gerade das,\n"
"was die Tramps am Eindringen\n"
"hindern wird."
msgstr ""
"The rope is hardly what will\n"
"prevent the tramps from\n"
"breaking in."

msgctxt "scene:30:344"
msgid ""
"Ich brauche etwas grösseres\n"
"um das Tor zu befestigen, ein\n"
"Seil hilft da wenig."
msgstr ""
"I need something larger to\n"
"secure the gate; a rope\n"
"helps little there."

msgctxt "scene:30:347"
msgid ""
"Der Pfahl ist nicht genug,\n"
"um das Tor gegen einen An-\n"
"griff zu befestigen."
msgstr ""
"The stake is not enough to\n"
"secure the gate against an\n"
"attack."

msgctxt "scene:30:350"
msgid ""
"Selbst wenn wir alles Brennholz\n"
"vor das Tor schaffen, dadurch\n"
"wird es immer noch zu wenig ge-\n"
"stützt."
msgstr ""
"Even if we bring all the firewood\n"
"in front of the gate, that\n"
"would still not strengthen\n"
"the gate."

msgctxt "scene:30:354"
msgid ""
"Die Mauer kann ich nicht\n"
"benutzen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot use the wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:356"
msgid ""
"Die Treppe zu benutzen,\n"
"wäre lebensgefährlich."
msgstr ""
"Using the stairs would be\n"
"hazardously dangerous."

msgctxt "scene:30:358"
msgid ""
"Wir sollten das Tor\n"
"nicht mehr öffnen, denn\n"
"die Tramps warten sicher\n"
"auf so eine Gelegenheit."
msgstr ""
"We should no longer open\n"
"the gate, for that would\n"
"render the barricade\n"
"useless."

msgctxt "scene:30:362"
msgid ""
"Ich bin froh, das Ding\n"
"endlich an seiner Stelle\n"
"zu haben und will es\n"
"nicht mehr wegziehen."
msgstr ""
"I am glad to finally have\n"
"the thing in its place.\n"
"I shall not move it again.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:366"
msgid ""
"An die Axt kommt man\n"
"nicht heran, ohne vor-\n"
"her den ganzen Hau-\n"
"fen Holz zu beseiti-\n"
"gen. Das hat der\n"
"Knecht nicht gerade \n"
"intelligent angestellt."
msgstr ""
"One cannot reach the axe\n"
"without moving the heavy\n"
"wagon away first; besides,\n"
"the axe is not needed\n"
"for securing the gate\n"
"any longer.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:373"
msgid ""
"Auch ist das Holz noch\n"
"zu frisch, um als Feuer-\n"
"holz gebraucht zu wer-\n"
"den."
msgstr ""
"Also, the wood is still\n"
"too green to be used for\n"
"strengthening the gate.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:30:377"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube Mrs. Butler\n"
"wäre nicht sehr erbaut,\n"
"wenn ich in ihrem Hof\n"
"ein Loch buddle."
msgstr ""
"I believe Mrs. Butler\n"
"would not be very pleased\n"
"if I dug a hole in her\n"
"yard."

msgctxt "scene:30:381"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte schon einen\n"
"Behälter haben, um das\n"
"Wasser aufzufangen."
msgstr ""
"I should really have a\n"
"container to catch the\n"
"water."

msgctxt "scene:30:384"
msgid ""
"Das Fass gehört zur Bade-\n"
"einrichtung, und das letzte\n"
"was ich jetzt tun möchte\n"
"ist, gemütlich ein Bad\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"The barrel belongs to the\n"
"bath setup, and the last\n"
"thing I wish to do now\n"
"is to take a comfortable\n"
"bath."

msgctxt "scene:30:389"
msgid ""
"Was immer Deine Idee ist,\n"
"lass sie uns vergessen."
msgstr ""
"Whatever your idea is,\n"
"let us forget it."

msgctxt "scene:31:0"
msgid ""
"Der Spachtel wurde mit einge-\n"
"mauert, und sitzt zu fest um\n"
"ihn herausziehen zu können."
msgstr ""
"The spatula was bricked\n"
"in and sits too fast to be\n"
"pulled out easily."

msgctxt "scene:31:3"
msgid ""
"Die Wand ist nass genug,\n"
"um den Spachtel heraus\n"
"zu brechen."
msgstr ""
"The wall is wet enough\n"
"to break out the\n"
"spatula."

msgctxt "scene:31:6"
msgid "Ein strahlender Himmel."
msgstr "A radiant sky."

msgctxt "scene:31:7"
msgid ""
"Der Baum wirft auf den\n"
"Hof einen schönen Schat-\n"
"ten, doch verdeckt er\n"
"auch ganz schön die Sicht."
msgstr ""
"The tree casts a lovely\n"
"shade upon the yard, yet\n"
"it obstructs the view\n"
"quite a bit."

msgctxt "scene:31:11"
msgid ""
"Hinter den Büschen kann\n"
"sich das Tramp-Gesindel\n"
"leicht heranschleichen."
msgstr ""
"Behind the bushes the\n"
"tramp riffraff can easily\n"
"sneak up."

msgctxt "scene:31:14"
msgid ""
"Eine schöne und fruchtbare\n"
"Hügellandschaft."
msgstr ""
"A lovely and fertile\n"
"hilly landscape."

msgctxt "scene:31:16"
msgid ""
"Die Angreifer werden hin-\n"
"ter den Felsen gute Deckung\n"
"finden."
msgstr ""
"The attackers will find\n"
"good cover behind the\n"
"rocks."

msgctxt "scene:31:19"
msgid ""
"Der kleine Fluss windet\n"
"sich gemächlich durch die\n"
"Hügellandschaft."
msgstr ""
"The little river winds\n"
"leisurely through the\n"
"hilly landscape."

msgctxt "scene:31:22"
msgid ""
"Das Wasser hat den Mörtel\n"
"um den Spachtel aufgeweicht."
msgstr ""
"The water has softened the\n"
"mortar around the spatula."

msgctxt "scene:31:24"
msgid ""
"Ein Spachtel steckt in\n"
"der Mauer. Muss wohl\n"
"bei den letzten Ausbes-\n"
"serungsarbeiten verges-\n"
"sen worden sein."
msgstr ""
"A spatula is stuck in\n"
"the wall. Must have been\n"
"forgotten during the last\n"
"repair work.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:29"
msgid ""
"Der Mauervorsprung wurde\n"
"breit genug angelegt, um\n"
"gut an jede Stelle der\n"
"Mauer zu gelangen und\n"
"auch noch Deckung nehmen\n"
"zu können."
msgstr ""
"The wall ledge was made\n"
"wide enough to reach every\n"
"spot on the wall well and\n"
"to be able to take cover\n"
"as well.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:35"
msgid ""
"Von hier sieht man, wie sehr\n"
"die Treppe zerfallen ist."
msgstr ""
"From here one sees how\n"
"very decayed the stairs are."

msgctxt "scene:31:37"
msgid ""
"Eine Leiter, um auf den\n"
"Mauervorsprung gelangen\n"
"zu können."
msgstr ""
"A ladder to reach the\n"
"wall ledge.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:40"
msgid ""
"Die Mauer sieht teilweise\n"
"etwas reparaturbedürftig\n"
"aus, doch den Tramps wird\n"
"sie sicher standhalten."
msgstr ""
"The wall looks in parts\n"
"somewhat in need of repair,\n"
"yet it will surely hold up\n"
"against the tramps."

msgctxt "scene:31:44"
msgid ""
"Den Himmel kann ich nicht\n"
"herunterholen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot fetch down the\n"
"sky."

msgctxt "scene:31:46"
msgid ""
"Ich bin überzeugt, wenn\n"
"Mrs. Butler wollte,dass\n"
"dieser Baum kleinge-\n"
"hackt werden sollte, hätte\n"
"sie dem Knecht bereits den\n"
"Auftrag dazu gegeben."
msgstr ""
"I am convinced that if\n"
"Mrs. Butler wanted this\n"
"tree chopped up, her\n"
"husband would have given the\n"
"farmhand the order long ago.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:52"
msgid ""
"Die Büsche da draussen\n"
"können wir jetzt auch\n"
"nicht mehr entfernen."
msgstr ""
"The bushes out there\n"
"we cannot remove now\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:31:55"
msgid ""
"Die Hügel sind zu gross,\n"
"um sie wegzuschufeln..."
msgstr ""
"The hills are too large\n"
"to shovel away..."

msgctxt "scene:31:57"
msgid ""
"Die Felsen können wir\n"
"nicht mehr entfernen,\n"
"zudem wären sie viel\n"
"zu schwer."
msgstr ""
"The rocks we cannot\n"
"remove anymore,\n"
"besides they would be\n"
"far too heavy."

msgctxt "scene:31:61"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir Wasser\n"
"aus der Pumpe holen."
msgstr ""
"I can fetch water\n"
"from the pump."

msgctxt "scene:31:63"
msgid ""
"Um darauf gehen zu kön-\n"
"nen, brauche ich den\n"
"Mauervorsprung nicht\n"
"gleich einzustecken."
msgstr ""
"In order to walk upon it,\n"
"I need not pocket the\n"
"wall ledge right away.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:67"
msgid ""
"Davon ist abzuraten, so\n"
"wie die Treppe aussieht\n"
"breche ich mir gleich das\n"
"Genick wenn ich da hinun-\n"
"tergehe."
msgstr ""
"That is ill-advised; from\n"
"the look of the stairs, I\n"
"would break my neck right\n"
"away if I went down there.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:72"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das Oel auf die\n"
"Mauer schütte, erreiche\n"
"ich nichts, ausser dass\n"
"es ein fürchterliches\n"
"Geschmiere gäbe..."
msgstr ""
"If I pour the oil onto\n"
"the wall, I achieve\n"
"nothing, save that there\n"
"would be a terrible mess.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:77"
msgid ""
"Der Schnaps ist wirklich\n"
"zu wertvoll, so weit ab\n"
"von der nächsten Bar, um\n"
"ihn dafür zu verschwenden."
msgstr ""
"The liquor is truly too\n"
"precious, so far off from\n"
"the next bar, to waste\n"
"it on that."

msgctxt "scene:31:81"
msgid ""
"Der Schnaps ist wirklich\n"
"zu wertvoll, so weit ab\n"
"von der nächsten Bar, um\n"
"ihn dafür zu verschwenden."
msgstr ""
"The liquor is truly too\n"
"precious, so far off from\n"
"the next bar, to waste\n"
"it on that."

msgctxt "scene:31:85"
msgid ""
"Ich kann doch nicht die\n"
"ganze Mauer zerschlagen,\n"
"um den Spachtel zu be-\n"
"kommen. Es könnte auch\n"
"sein, dass ich ihn be-\n"
"schädige."
msgstr ""
"I cannot smash the whole\n"
"wall to get the spatula.\n"
"It might also be that I\n"
"damage it in the process.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:91"
msgid ""
"Die Spitze ohne Stil, kann\n"
"ich nicht für so etwas ver-\n"
"wenden."
msgstr ""
"The pick without a handle\n"
"cannot be used for such a\n"
"purpose."

msgctxt "scene:31:94"
msgid ""
"Die Schaufel ist vorne\n"
"ganz stumpf, dafür kann\n"
"ich sie nicht verwenden."
msgstr ""
"The shovel is quite blunt\n"
"in front; for this I\n"
"cannot use it."

msgctxt "scene:31:97"
msgid ""
"So kann ich den Spachtel\n"
"nicht lösen, da beschädi-\n"
"ge ich die Wand nur un-\n"
"nötig."
msgstr ""
"I cannot loosen the\n"
"spatula that way, I would\n"
"only damage the wall\n"
"needlessly."

msgctxt "scene:31:101"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Korkenzieher werde\n"
"ich wenig ausrichten können,\n"
"das ist wirklich nicht das\n"
"geeignete Werkzeug."
msgstr ""
"With the corkscrew I shall\n"
"accomplish little, that is\n"
"truly not the right tool.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:105"
msgid ""
"Mit Küchengeräten sollte\n"
"man keine Maurerarbeiten\n"
"machen."
msgstr ""
"With kitchen utensils one\n"
"should do no masonry\n"
"work."

msgctxt "scene:31:108"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich Munition hätte,\n"
"dann könnte ich den Spachtel\n"
"aus der Mauer schiessen."
msgstr ""
"If I had ammunition, I\n"
"could shoot the spatula\n"
"out of the wall."

msgctxt "scene:31:111"
msgid ""
"Die Mauer sieht an manchen\n"
"Stellen zwar etwas schwächer\n"
"aus, doch ich bezweifle, dass\n"
"ich den Spachtel aus der\n"
"Mauer blasen kann."
msgstr ""
"The wall looks somewhat\n"
"weaker in places, yet I\n"
"doubt that I can blow the\n"
"spatula out of the wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:31:116"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich mit den Holzscheiten\n"
"auf den Spachtel schlage, geht\n"
"der sicher kaputt."
msgstr ""
"If I strike the spatula\n"
"with the logs, it will\n"
"surely break."

msgctxt "scene:32:0"
msgid ""
"Mehr, als das, was ich schon\n"
"genommen habe, brauche ich\n"
"nicht."
msgstr ""
"More than what I have\n"
"taken already, I do not\n"
"need."

msgctxt "scene:32:3"
msgid "Die Tür ist jetzt auf."
msgstr "The door is open now."

msgctxt "scene:32:4"
msgid "Die hab ich schon aufgeschlossen."
msgstr "I have unlocked it already."

msgctxt "scene:32:5"
msgid "Die Tür ist verschlossen."
msgstr "The door is locked."

msgctxt "scene:32:6"
msgid "Arrrrrghhh..."
msgstr "Arrrrrghhh..."

msgctxt "scene:32:7"
msgid ""
"So, jetzt stell ich den\n"
"Wagen vor's Tor."
msgstr ""
"So, now I shall place the\n"
"wagon in front of the gate."

msgctxt "scene:32:9"
msgid ""
"Von Vorne gesehen wirkt\n"
"das Haus eigentlich gar\n"
"nicht so gross, doch jetzt\n"
"sieht man erst wie gross\n"
"es eigentlich ist."
msgstr ""
"Seen from the front, the\n"
"house does not appear\n"
"all that large. But that\n"
"can be deceiving, my\n"
"friend."

msgctxt "scene:32:14"
msgid ""
"Eine Tür, die in den\n"
"Anbau führt."
msgstr ""
"A door leading into\n"
"the extension."

msgctxt "scene:32:16"
msgid ""
"Ein etwas wackliger\n"
"Heuwagen steht da, der\n"
"offensichtlich schon\n"
"eine Weile nicht mehr\n"
"gebraucht wurde."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat wobbly\n"
"hay wagon stands there,\n"
"which obviously has not\n"
"been used for quite\n"
"some time."

msgctxt "scene:32:21"
msgid ""
"Der Wagen wird mit\n"
"einem Pfahl gestützt."
msgstr ""
"The wagon is propped up\n"
"with a stake."

msgctxt "scene:32:23"
msgid ""
"Geschnittenes Holz, das\n"
"ist sicher zum Heizen\n"
"bereit gemacht."
msgstr ""
"Cut wood, which is\n"
"surely intended for\n"
"heating."

msgctxt "scene:32:26"
msgid ""
"Durch das viele Begehen,\n"
"ist der Boden schon ganz\n"
"festgetreten."
msgstr ""
"From much walking upon\n"
"it, the ground is quite\n"
"trodden firm."

msgctxt "scene:32:29"
msgid ""
"Sämtliche Fenster sind ver-\n"
"glast, was erstaunlich ist,\n"
"so weit von der nächsten\n"
"Stadt entfernt."
msgstr ""
"All windows are glazed,\n"
"which is astonishing so\n"
"far off from any\n"
"civilisation."

msgctxt "scene:32:33"
msgid ""
"Von hier sieht man den Baum\n"
"aus dem Vorhof ebenfalls."
msgstr ""
"From here one sees the tree\n"
"from the front yard as well."

msgctxt "scene:32:35"
msgid ""
"Eine Mauer aus gebranntem\n"
"Ziegel, die bereits mit\n"
"Unkraut bewachsen ist."
msgstr ""
"A wall of burnt brick,\n"
"covered over with moss\n"
"already."

msgctxt "scene:32:38"
msgid ""
"Dieses Unkraut blüht in\n"
"einem hübschen Blau."
msgstr ""
"These weeds bloom in\n"
"a pretty blue."

msgctxt "scene:32:40"
msgid ""
"Hier kann man die Pferde\n"
"anbinden."
msgstr ""
"Here one can tie up the\n"
"horses."

msgctxt "scene:32:42"
msgid ""
"Die ganze Farm ist von einer\n"
"hohen Mauer umgeben, dass er-\n"
"leichtert die Verteidigung\n"
"gegen die Tramps."
msgstr ""
"The entire farm is surrounded by a\n"
"high wall, which makes defense\n"
"against the tramps much\n"
"easier."

msgctxt "scene:32:46"
msgid ""
"Ein schöner, blauer Himmel,\n"
"nur vereinzelte Wolken sind\n"
"zu sehen."
msgstr ""
"A beautiful, blue sky;\n"
"only scattered clouds are to\n"
"be seen."

msgctxt "scene:32:49"
msgid ""
"Durch das Fenster sollte\n"
"man nur einsteigen, wenn\n"
"keine andere Möglichkeit\n"
"vorhanden ist."
msgstr ""
"One should only climb through\n"
"the window if no other\n"
"possibility presents\n"
"itself."

msgctxt "scene:32:53"
msgid ""
"Ein Rad fehlt an dem Wagen,\n"
"den kann man nicht wegbe-\n"
"wegen, ohne ihn zu reparieren."
msgstr ""
"A wheel is missing from the wagon;\n"
"it cannot be moved without\n"
"repairing it first."

msgctxt "scene:32:56"
msgid ""
"Die Ziegelsteine sitzen\n"
"fest, und ich könnte damit\n"
"auch nichts anfangen."
msgstr ""
"The bricks are set firm, and\n"
"I could not do anything with\n"
"them anyway."

msgctxt "scene:32:59"
msgid ""
"Die Blumen sind zwar hübsch,\n"
"doch ich habe keine Zeit Blu-\n"
"men zu pflücken."
msgstr ""
"The flowers are pretty,\n"
"yet I have no time to pick\n"
"flowers."

msgctxt "scene:32:62"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das zerlege, dann\n"
"kann man die Pferde nicht\n"
"mehr anbinden."
msgstr ""
"If I dismantle that, then\n"
"one can no longer tie up\n"
"the horses."

msgctxt "scene:32:65"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keine Lust, über die\n"
"Mauer zu klettern."
msgstr ""
"I have no desire to climb\n"
"over the wall."

msgctxt "scene:32:67"
msgid ""
"Das Holz mit dem Brotmesser\n"
"zu zerkleinern würde Jahre\n"
"dauern - oder soll ich einen\n"
"Spruch hineinschnitzen?"
msgstr ""
"Chopping up the wood with a bread\n"
"knife would take years - or\n"
"am I supposed to carve a\n"
"motto into it?"

msgctxt "scene:32:71"
msgid ""
"Das ist eine Spitzhacke, mit\n"
"der kann man kein Holz hacken."
msgstr ""
"That is a pickaxe; one\n"
"cannot chop wood with it."

msgctxt "scene:32:73"
msgid ""
"Hier draussen sollte ich das\n"
"Holz nicht anzünden, das könnte\n"
"fatale Folgen haben."
msgstr ""
"I ought not to light the wood\n"
"out here; that could have\n"
"fatal consequences."

msgctxt "scene:32:76"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich die Tür\n"
"nicht öffnen."
msgstr ""
"With that, the door\n"
"cannot be opened."

msgctxt "scene:32:78"
msgid ""
"Die Tür lässt sich nicht auf-\n"
"schneiden wie ein Laib Brot."
msgstr ""
"The door cannot be cut open\n"
"like a loaf of bread."

msgctxt "scene:32:80"
msgid ""
"Es ist keine Lösung, die Tür\n"
"kaputt zu machen."
msgstr ""
"It is no solution to break\n"
"the door."

msgctxt "scene:32:82"
msgid ""
"Aufbrechen werde ich die Tür\n"
"nicht, da gibt es eine bessere\n"
"Lösung."
msgstr ""
"I shall not break open the\n"
"door; there is a better\n"
"solution."

msgctxt "scene:32:85"
msgid ""
"Gute Idee, doch hier hilft\n"
"nur ein Schlüssel."
msgstr ""
"Good idea, yet here only\n"
"a key will help."

msgctxt "scene:32:87"
msgid ""
"Ja, mit etwas Munition könnte ich\n"
"die Tür wegschiessen, doch das\n"
"wäre wiederum Sachbeschädigung."
msgstr ""
"Aye, with ammunition I could shoot\n"
"the door away, yet that would be\n"
"damage to property again."

msgctxt "scene:32:90"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Pfahl könnte ich die\n"
"Tür sicher eintreten, doch\n"
"Mrs. Butler wäre darüber nicht\n"
"sehr erbaut."
msgstr ""
"With the post I could surely kick\n"
"the door in, yet Mrs. Butler\n"
"would not be very pleased\n"
"about that."

msgctxt "scene:32:94"
msgid ""
"Ich darf die Tür nicht\n"
"beschädigen."
msgstr ""
"I must not damage the\n"
"door."

msgctxt "scene:32:96"
msgid ""
"Sicher könnte ich die Tür weg-\n"
"sprengen, doch ich frage mich,\n"
"ob anschliessend noch etwas\n"
"hinter der Tür zu finden ist..."
msgstr ""
"To be sure, I could blow the door\n"
"away, yet I wonder if anything\n"
"remains to be found behind\n"
"it afterwards..."

msgctxt "scene:32:100"
msgid ""
"Der Spachtel wird abbrechen,\n"
"wenn ich ihn benutze."
msgstr ""
"The spatula will snap if\n"
"I use it."

msgctxt "scene:32:102"
msgid ""
"Die Tür anzünden und zuschauen\n"
"wie die Farm niederbrennt! Der\n"
"Cornel würde mich anschliessend\n"
"sicher beteiligen..."
msgstr ""
"Set fire to the door and watch the\n"
"farm burn down! The Cornel would\n"
"surely give me a cut of the\n"
"spoils afterwards..."

msgctxt "scene:33:0"
msgid "10 Minuten später..."
msgstr "10 minutes later..."

msgctxt "scene:33:1"
msgid ""
"Puh, das war ganz\n"
"schön anstrengend!"
msgstr ""
"Phew, that was quite\n"
"strenuous!"

msgctxt "scene:33:3"
msgid ""
"Aber die Mühe hat\n"
"sich gelohnt, da\n"
"ist ein Geheimgang!"
msgstr ""
"Yet the effort was\n"
"well worth it, there\n"
"is a secret passage!"

msgctxt "scene:33:6"
msgid ""
"So, ich schätze den\n"
"Pfahl habe ich jetzt\n"
"genug gelockert."
msgstr ""
"There, I reckon I\n"
"have loosened the\n"
"post enough now."

msgctxt "scene:33:9"
msgid ""
"Es wird mir im Traum\n"
"nicht einfallen, den\n"
"Mist zurückzuschaufeln!"
msgstr ""
"It would not occur to\n"
"me in my dreams to shovel\n"
"the dung back!"

msgctxt "scene:33:12"
msgid ""
"Oh, da gehts ganz schön\n"
"tief runter, da habe ich\n"
"kein passendes Seil um\n"
"hinunter zu klettern!"
msgstr ""
"Oh, it goes down quite\n"
"deep there; I have no\n"
"suitable rope with which\n"
"to climb down!"

msgctxt "scene:33:16"
msgid ""
"Ein alter Eimer steht da\n"
"an der Mauer, muss wohl\n"
"vom Knecht vergessen wor-\n"
"den sein."
msgstr ""
"An old bucket stands there\n"
"by the wall; must have been\n"
"forgotten by the farm\n"
"hand."

msgctxt "scene:33:20"
msgid ""
"Gut, dass die Mauer so\n"
"hoch gebaut wurde, dass\n"
"erleichtert es mir, die\n"
"ungebetenen Gäste draus-\n"
"sen zu halten."
msgstr ""
"A good thing the wall was built\n"
"so high; that makes it easier\n"
"for me to keep uninvited\n"
"guests outside.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:33:25"
msgid ""
"Der Pfahl steht nicht\n"
"so schön gerade wie all\n"
"die anderen."
msgstr ""
"The stake does not stand\n"
"as nicely straight as all\n"
"the others."

msgctxt "scene:33:28"
msgid ""
"Phu, ein Haufen Pferdemist,\n"
"und der stinkt..."
msgstr ""
"Phew, a pile of horse dung,\n"
"and it stinks..."

msgctxt "scene:33:30"
msgid ""
"Eine Art Holzgeländer um zu\n"
"vermeiden, dass der Mist nach\n"
"vorne rutscht."
msgstr ""
"A kind of wooden railing to\n"
"prevent the dung from sliding\n"
"forward."

msgctxt "scene:33:33"
msgid ""
"Der ganze Boden ist richtig\n"
"festgetreten, aber da und\n"
"dort wachsen bereits Büschel\n"
"von saftig grünem Gras."
msgstr ""
"The entire ground is firmly\n"
"trodden down, yet here and\n"
"there grow tufts of lush\n"
"green grass."

msgctxt "scene:33:37"
msgid ""
"Zwei Stockwerke hoch dieses\n"
"Haus - es fordert sicher sehr\n"
"viel Arbeit von Mrs. Butler."
msgstr ""
"Two stories high, this house -\n"
"it surely requires much work\n"
"from Mrs. Butler."

msgctxt "scene:33:40"
msgid ""
"Es wuchert überall Unkraut,\n"
"doch es sieht noch hübsch\n"
"aus."
msgstr ""
"Weeds grow everywhere,\n"
"yet it still looks\n"
"pretty."

msgctxt "scene:33:43"
msgid ""
"Eine Backsteinmauer, die\n"
"Ziegel sind aber besonders\n"
"flach."
msgstr ""
"A brick wall, yet the\n"
"bricks are particularly\n"
"flat."

msgctxt "scene:33:46"
msgid ""
"Es scheint, dass die Pfähle\n"
"ein Ueberrest einer ehemali-\n"
"gen Pferdekoppel sind."
msgstr ""
"It appears that the posts\n"
"are the remnant of a former\n"
"horse paddock."

msgctxt "scene:33:49"
msgid "Ein fast wolkenloser Himmel."
msgstr "An almost cloudless sky."

msgctxt "scene:33:50"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich über die\n"
"Mauer klettern, ich kann\n"
"doch das Tor benutzen."
msgstr ""
"Why should I climb over the\n"
"wall when I can simply use\n"
"the gate?"

msgctxt "scene:33:53"
msgid ""
"Der Pfahl sitzt zu fest im\n"
"Boden, als dass ich ihn mit\n"
"blosser Hand herausziehen\n"
"könnte."
msgstr ""
"The post is set too firm in the\n"
"ground for me to pull it out\n"
"with my bare hands.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:33:57"
msgid ""
"Das war sicher ein schlechter\n"
"Scherz, warum sollte ich in\n"
"einem Haufen Pferdemist herum-\n"
"wühlen."
msgstr ""
"That was surely a poor jest;\n"
"why should I rummage about\n"
"in a pile of horse dung?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:33:61"
msgid ""
"Das Geländer ist ja voller\n"
"Pferdemist, ich werde mich\n"
"hüten es anzugreifen."
msgstr ""
"The railing is full of horse\n"
"dung; I shall take good care\n"
"not to touch it."

msgctxt "scene:33:64"
msgid ""
"Ich bin ja kein Gärtner, mein\n"
"Freund. Wir sollten uns auf\n"
"unsere Aufgabe konzentrieren."
msgstr ""
"I am no gardener, my friend.\n"
"We ought to concentrate on\n"
"our task."

msgctxt "scene:33:67"
msgid ""
"Ich kann nicht einfach eine\n"
"Mauer abtragen, dazu wären\n"
"die Ziegel sowieso viel zu\n"
"brüchig um etwas bauen zu\n"
"können."
msgstr ""
"I cannot simply tear down a\n"
"wall; the bricks would be far\n"
"too brittle to build anything\n"
"with anyway.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:33:72"
msgid ""
"Die Pfähle sitzen fest im Boden,\n"
"um die heraus zu holen bräuchten\n"
"wir sicher Sprengstoff. Doch ich\n"
"glaube, dass dies dem Haus auch\n"
"nicht sehr zuträglich wäre."
msgstr ""
"The posts are firmly in the ground;\n"
"to pull them out we would surely\n"
"need explosives. Yet I believe that\n"
"would not be beneficial to the\n"
"house either."

msgctxt "scene:33:77"
msgid ""
"Damit werde ich den Pfahl nie\n"
"aus dem festgetretenen Boden\n"
"herausbekommen."
msgstr ""
"With that I shall never get the\n"
"post out of the hard-trodden\n"
"ground."

msgctxt "scene:33:80"
msgid ""
"Eine gute Idee, mit dem Wasser\n"
"den Boden um den Pfahl aufzu-\n"
"weichen, doch das klappt nicht,\n"
"sonst würden die Pfähle nach\n"
"jedem Regen umkippen."
msgstr ""
"A fine idea, to soften the ground\n"
"around the post with water, yet\n"
"that will not work, or the posts\n"
"would topple after every rain.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:33:85"
msgid ""
"Das könnte klappen, der hin-\n"
"terste scheint am lockersten\n"
"in der Erde zu stecken."
msgstr ""
"That might work; the rearmost\n"
"post seems to be set most\n"
"loosely in the earth."

msgctxt "scene:33:88"
msgid ""
"Ohne Stil habe ich zu wenig\n"
"Wucht."
msgstr ""
"Without a handle I have too\n"
"little leverage."

msgctxt "scene:33:90"
msgid ""
"Das ist kein Korken, es lässt\n"
"sich nicht so einfach raus-\n"
"ziehen."
msgstr ""
"That is no cork; it\n"
"cannot be pulled out so\n"
"easily."

msgctxt "scene:33:93"
msgid ""
"Der Boden ist zu hart, um mit\n"
"der defekten Schaufel etwas\n"
"auszurichten."
msgstr ""
"The ground is too hard to\n"
"accomplish anything with the\n"
"broken shovel."

msgctxt "scene:33:96"
msgid ""
"Ohne Stil kann man die Schaufel-\n"
"spitze nicht richtig halten."
msgstr ""
"Without a handle one cannot hold\n"
"the shovel blade properly."

msgctxt "scene:33:98"
msgid ""
"Mit Schwarzpulver könnte man\n"
"den Pfahl sicher raussprengen,\n"
"doch das würde grossen Schaden\n"
"anrichten."
msgstr ""
"With gunpowder one could\n"
"surely blast the post out, yet\n"
"that would cause great\n"
"damage."

msgctxt "scene:33:102"
msgid ""
"Mit dem kleinen Spachtel ist\n"
"da nichts zu machen."
msgstr ""
"With the small spatula nothing\n"
"can be done there."

msgctxt "scene:33:104"
msgid ""
"Den Pfahl anzünden?!..Aber\n"
"nicht doch..! Das hilft auch\n"
"nicht weiter."
msgstr ""
"Set fire to the post?!.. Surely\n"
"not..! That does not help us\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:33:107"
msgid ""
"Ich könnte den Zettel an dem\n"
"Pfahl befestigen, doch das\n"
"würde auch nicht weiter helfen."
msgstr ""
"I could attach the note to the\n"
"post, yet that would not help\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:33:110"
msgid "Der Mist stinkt mir zu stark."
msgstr "The dung stinks too strongly for me."

msgctxt "scene:33:111"
msgid "Der Beutel ist bereits voll."
msgstr "The pouch is already full."

msgctxt "scene:33:112"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich den stinkenden\n"
"Mist mit mir herumschleppen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I haul the foul-smelling\n"
"dung about with me?"

msgctxt "scene:33:114"
msgid "Da ist bereits Wasser im Eimer."
msgstr "There is already water in the bucket."

msgctxt "scene:33:115"
msgid ""
"Das wäre mit Kanonen auf\n"
"Spatzen schiessen."
msgstr ""
"That would be taking a sledgehammer\n"
"to crack a nut."

msgctxt "scene:33:117"
msgid ""
"Nur mit der Schaufelspitze zu\n"
"graben, würde bedeuten, dass\n"
"ich sicher mit den Händen in\n"
"den Pferdemist gerate, und das\n"
"möchte ich vermeiden."
msgstr ""
"To dig with only the shovel\n"
"blade would mean getting my\n"
"hands into the horse dung\n"
"for certain, and that I\n"
"wish to avoid."

msgctxt "scene:33:122"
msgid ""
"Mit einem Küchengerät im Mist\n"
"herumwühlen ist nicht mein Stil."
msgstr ""
"Rummaging about in dung with a\n"
"kitchen utensil is not my style."

msgctxt "scene:33:124"
msgid ""
"Den Mist mit Scharzpulver weg-\n"
"zusprengen, würde eine schöne\n"
"Schweinerei geben."
msgstr ""
"Blowing the dung away with\n"
"black powder would make\n"
"a fine mess."

msgctxt "scene:33:127"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Spachtel im Misthaufen\n"
"herumzustochern, bringt sicher\n"
"nicht sehr viel."
msgstr ""
"Poking around in the dung heap with\n"
"a spatula will surely not accomplish\n"
"very much."

msgctxt "scene:33:130"
msgid ""
"Mit einer Tasse kann man ins\n"
"Volle schöpfen, aber bitte\n"
"nicht in einem Misthaufen."
msgstr ""
"With a cup one can scoop to one's\n"
"heart's content, yet please not in\n"
"a dung heap."

msgctxt "scene:34:0"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich die Winde\n"
"wieder hochkurbeln? Es hilft\n"
"mir nicht weiter, meine\n"
"Probleme zu lösen!"
msgstr ""
"Why should I wind up the\n"
"winch again? It does not help\n"
"me any further to solve my\n"
"problems!"

msgctxt "scene:34:4"
msgid ""
"Das alte Ding ist verrostet\n"
"und klemmt, kein Wunder,\n"
"wenn es dauernd der Witte-\n"
"rung ausgesetzt ist."
msgstr ""
"The old thing is rusted and\n"
"stuck; no wonder, if it is\n"
"constantly exposed to the\n"
"weather."

msgctxt "scene:34:8"
msgid ""
"Entlang des Ufers stehen nur\n"
"vereinzelte Büsche, das macht\n"
"einen unbemerkten Angriff für\n"
"die Tramps unmöglich."
msgstr ""
"Along the bank stand only\n"
"scattered bushes; that makes\n"
"an unnoticed attack impossible\n"
"for the tramps."

msgctxt "scene:34:12"
msgid ""
"Das Ufer fällt zum Fluss hin\n"
"flach ab. Etwas Treibgut liegt\n"
"herum."
msgstr ""
"The bank slopes gently down\n"
"to the river. Some flotsam\n"
"lies about."

msgctxt "scene:34:15"
msgid ""
"Massive Stahlkugeln für die\n"
"Kanone, das Dach muss da ganz\n"
"schön was' aushalten."
msgstr ""
"Massive steel balls for the\n"
"cannon; the roof must withstand\n"
"quite a lot there."

msgctxt "scene:34:18"
msgid ""
"Ein gemauerter Rauchabzug, der\n"
"wohl für die Küche und das Wohn-\n"
"zimmer gleichermassen dient."
msgstr ""
"A brick chimney flue that likely\n"
"serves for the kitchen and living\n"
"room alike."

msgctxt "scene:34:21"
msgid ""
"Die Kanone ist jetzt\n"
"Feuerbereit."
msgstr ""
"The cannon is now\n"
"ready to fire."

msgctxt "scene:34:23"
msgid ""
"Die Kanone ist zwar ein älte-\n"
"res Modell, doch wenn die los-\n"
"feuert, dann kracht es sicher-\n"
"lich in beeindruckender Weise."
msgstr ""
"The cannon is indeed an older\n"
"model, yet when it fires off,\n"
"it surely bangs in an\n"
"impressive manner."

msgctxt "scene:34:27"
msgid ""
"Ein Holzdach, das rot ange-\n"
"strichen wurde."
msgstr ""
"A wooden roof that has been\n"
"painted red."

msgctxt "scene:34:29"
msgid ""
"Eine Winde, an der ein Seil\n"
"ins Haus führt."
msgstr ""
"A winch with a rope that\n"
"leads into the house."

msgctxt "scene:34:31"
msgid ""
"Die Luke, um auf das Dach\n"
"zu gelangen."
msgstr ""
"The hatch to get onto\n"
"the roof."

msgctxt "scene:34:33"
msgid "Die Fenster des Hauses."
msgstr "The windows of the house."

msgctxt "scene:34:34"
msgid ""
"Obwohl das Haus einen etwas\n"
"eigenen Stil hat, muss der\n"
"Erbauer sich dabei etwas ge-\n"
"dacht haben."
msgstr ""
"Although the house has a somewhat\n"
"peculiar style, the builder must\n"
"have had something in mind with\n"
"it."

msgctxt "scene:34:38"
msgid "Die stehen zu weit weg."
msgstr "Those stand too far away."

msgctxt "scene:34:39"
msgid ""
"Ich werde mich nicht am\n"
"Ufer sonnen..."
msgstr ""
"I am not going to sunbathe\n"
"on the bank..."

msgctxt "scene:34:41"
msgid ""
"Durch den Kamin in ein Haus\n"
"zu gelangen, ist sicher weit-\n"
"aus unbequemer, als durch die\n"
"dafür vorgesehene Luke..."
msgstr ""
"Getting into a house through the\n"
"chimney is surely far more un-\n"
"comfortable than through the\n"
"hatch intended for it..."

msgctxt "scene:34:45"
msgid ""
"Um das zu tun, brauche ich\n"
"noch einige Bestandteile."
msgstr ""
"To do that, I still need\n"
"a few components."

msgctxt "scene:34:47"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich aus dem Dach Bretter\n"
"herausnehmen würde, könnte mir\n"
"das sicherlich Aerger mit Mrs.\n"
"Butler einbringen."
msgstr ""
"If I were to take boards out of\n"
"the roof, that could surely bring\n"
"me trouble with Mrs.\n"
"Butler."

msgctxt "scene:34:51"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich riskieren, dass\n"
"ich mir das Genick breche,wenn\n"
"ich statt durch das Fenster,\n"
"auch durch die Luke ins Haus\n"
"gelangen kann."
msgstr ""
"Why should I risk breaking my\n"
"neck when, instead of through\n"
"the window, I can also get into\n"
"the house through the\n"
"hatch."

msgctxt "scene:34:56"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brotmesser kann ich die\n"
"verrostete Winde nicht wieder\n"
"in Gang setzen."
msgstr ""
"With the bread knife I cannot\n"
"set the rusted winch back into\n"
"motion."

msgctxt "scene:34:59"
msgid ""
"Wasser hilft bei einer ver-\n"
"klemmten und verrosteten\n"
"Winde sicher nicht."
msgstr ""
"Water surely won't help with\n"
"a jammed and rusted\n"
"winch."

msgctxt "scene:34:62"
msgid ""
"Nicht immer ist rohe Gewalt die\n"
"beste Lösung."
msgstr ""
"Brute force is not always the\n"
"best solution."

msgctxt "scene:34:64"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Korkenzieher ist hier\n"
"nichts zu machen."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing to be done\n"
"here with the corkscrew."

msgctxt "scene:34:66"
msgid ""
"Mit roher Gewalt geht in der\n"
"Regel mehr kaputt..."
msgstr ""
"Brute force usually breaks\n"
"more things..."

msgctxt "scene:34:68"
msgid ""
"Die Winde sollte man vorsichtig\n"
"lösen, und nicht einfach mit Ge-\n"
"walt losbrechen."
msgstr ""
"The winch should be released\n"
"carefully, and not simply broken\n"
"off with force."

msgctxt "scene:34:71"
msgid ""
"Die Kanone durchzublasen, ist\n"
"vielleicht eine gute Idee, man\n"
"weiss ja nie ob sich da Spinnen\n"
"eingenistet haben...He,he."
msgstr ""
"Blowing through the cannon is\n"
"maybe a good idea, you never\n"
"know if spiders have nested\n"
"in there... He, he."

msgctxt "scene:34:75"
msgid ""
"Das ist kein Ofenrohr, das\n"
"ist eine echte Kanone."
msgstr ""
"That is no stovepipe, that\n"
"is a real cannon."

msgctxt "scene:34:77"
msgid "Soll ich eine Scheibe abschneiden?"
msgstr "Should I cut off a slice?"

msgctxt "scene:34:78"
msgid ""
"Auch wenn ich in die Kanone\n"
"Wasser schütte, wird daraus\n"
"lange keine Gulaschkanone..."
msgstr ""
"Even if I pour water into the\n"
"cannon, that won't turn it into\n"
"a field kitchen..."

msgctxt "scene:34:81"
msgid ""
"Die Kanone muss ich erst\n"
"mit Alkohol reinigen, nach-\n"
"dem ich sie benutzt habe."
msgstr ""
"I must first clean the cannon\n"
"with alcohol after I have\n"
"used it."

msgctxt "scene:34:84"
msgid ""
"Ich muss die Kanone jetzt\n"
"nicht reinigen."
msgstr ""
"I do not need to clean\n"
"the cannon right now."

msgctxt "scene:34:86"
msgid ""
"Mit der Kerze könnte ich die\n"
"Kanone zünden, wäre sie ge-\n"
"laden und mit einer Lunte\n"
"fertig versehen."
msgstr ""
"With the candle I could ignite\n"
"the cannon, if it were loaded\n"
"and fully equipped with\n"
"a fuse."

msgctxt "scene:34:90"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die Kerze hier\n"
"hinstelle, wird Sie\n"
"sofort vom Wind gelöscht."
msgstr ""
"If I place the candle here,\n"
"it will be blown out by the\n"
"wind immediately."

msgctxt "scene:34:93"
msgid ""
"So explodiert Salpeter nicht,\n"
"und kann nicht als Munition\n"
"verwendet werden."
msgstr ""
"Saltpeter does not explode\n"
"like this, and cannot be used\n"
"as ammunition."

msgctxt "scene:34:96"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich die Kanone\n"
"bestenfalls gelblich färben."
msgstr ""
"With this I can at best dye\n"
"the cannon yellowish."

msgctxt "scene:34:98"
msgid ""
"Das ist zu dick um als Lunte\n"
"verwendet zu werden."
msgstr ""
"That is too thick to be\n"
"used as a fuse."

msgctxt "scene:34:100"
msgid ""
"Das brennt nicht gut genug, und\n"
"wäre für eine Lunte zu dick."
msgstr ""
"That does not burn well enough,\n"
"and would be too thick for a fuse."

msgctxt "scene:34:102"
msgid ""
"Als Lunte denkbar ungeeignet,\n"
"das Seil ist zu dick."
msgstr ""
"Completely unsuitable as a fuse,\n"
"the rope is too thick."

msgctxt "scene:34:104"
msgid "Die Kanone friert nicht."
msgstr "The cannon does not freeze."

msgctxt "scene:34:105"
msgid ""
"Damit könnte man die Kanone\n"
"zünden, hätte man alles, um\n"
"sie zu laden."
msgstr ""
"With this one could ignite the\n"
"cannon, if one had everything\n"
"needed to load it."

msgctxt "scene:34:108"
msgid ""
"An der Kanone gibt es\n"
"nichts zu schmieren."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing on the\n"
"cannon to lubricate."

msgctxt "scene:34:110"
msgid ""
"Das wäre eine gute Lunte,\n"
"doch brennt die Wolle so\n"
"nicht sehr gut."
msgstr ""
"That would be a good fuse,\n"
"yet wool does not burn\n"
"very well like this."

msgctxt "scene:34:113"
msgid ""
"Den Zettel, zusammengerollt,\n"
"könnte man als Lunte verwenden.\n"
"Das bedeutet aber, dass wir nur\n"
"einen Schuss abfeuern können."
msgstr ""
"The note, rolled up, could be\n"
"used as a fuse. But that means\n"
"that we can only fire a single\n"
"shot."

msgctxt "scene:34:117"
msgid ""
"Sicher, die werde ich ver-\n"
"wenden, um die Kanone zu\n"
"laden, doch ich werde sie\n"
"nicht mit mir herumschlep-\n"
"pen."
msgstr ""
"Sure, I will use those to\n"
"load the cannon, but I am\n"
"not going to drag them\n"
"around with me where-\n"
"ever I go."

msgctxt "scene:34:122"
msgid ""
"Die Kanone ist bereits\n"
"geladen!"
msgstr ""
"The cannon is already\n"
"loaded!"

msgctxt "scene:34:124"
msgid ""
"Ein Windlicht, das ich\n"
"dort hingestellt habe,\n"
"um die Kanone zünden zu\n"
"können."
msgstr ""
"A lantern that I have\n"
"placed there in order\n"
"to be able to ignite\n"
"the cannon."

msgctxt "scene:34:128"
msgid ""
"Das lasse ich besser da\n"
"stehen, der Cornel kann\n"
"jeden Moment eintreffen!"
msgstr ""
"I had better leave that\n"
"there, the Cornel can\n"
"arrive at any moment!"

msgctxt "scene:35:0"
msgid ""
"Mir fehlt ein Stück Papier,\n"
"um das Feuer zu entfachen."
msgstr ""
"I am missing a piece of paper\n"
"to kindle the fire."

msgctxt "scene:35:2"
msgid ""
"Ich habe nichts, um dem\n"
"Feuer Sauerstoff zuzufüh-\n"
"ren."
msgstr ""
"I have nothing to supply\n"
"the fire with oxy-\n"
"gen."

msgctxt "scene:35:5"
msgid "Etwas später..."
msgstr "A little later..."

msgctxt "scene:35:6"
msgid ""
"Im Kamin ist nichts,\n"
"was ich anzünden\n"
"möchte."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing in the\n"
"fireplace that I would\n"
"care to light."

msgctxt "scene:35:9"
msgid ""
"Ich möchte aus dem Kamin\n"
"nichts herausnehmen,\n"
"und darin hochzuklettern,\n"
"solltest Du das wünschen,\n"
"ist wenig sinnvoll."
msgstr ""
"I do not wish to take anything\n"
"out of the fireplace, and climbing\n"
"up inside it, should you desire\n"
"that, makes little sense.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:14"
msgid ""
"Ich habe nur ein Streich-\n"
"holz, und das brauche ich\n"
"vielleicht noch für eine\n"
"andere Gelegenheit."
msgstr ""
"I have but one match, and I\n"
"may yet need it for another\n"
"occasion.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:18"
msgid ""
"Der Kamin ist leer, die\n"
"Wand ist geschwärzt, doch\n"
"abgesehen davon, ist darin\n"
"nichts zu finden."
msgstr ""
"The fireplace is empty, the\n"
"wall is blackened, yet apart\n"
"from that, nothing is to be\n"
"found inside."

msgctxt "scene:35:22"
msgid ""
"Da liegt Papier in der\n"
"Feuerstelle."
msgstr ""
"There is paper lying in\n"
"the hearth."

msgctxt "scene:35:24"
msgid ""
"Da liegt Brennholz in der\n"
"Feuerstelle."
msgstr ""
"There is firewood lying in\n"
"the hearth."

msgctxt "scene:35:26"
msgid ""
"Da liegt Brennholz und\n"
"Papier in der Feuer-\n"
"stelle."
msgstr ""
"There is firewood and paper\n"
"lying in the hearth.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:29"
msgid ""
"Asche und Holzkohle\n"
"liegt im Kamin."
msgstr ""
"Ashes and charcoal lie in\n"
"the fireplace."

msgctxt "scene:35:31"
msgid ""
"Der Raum ist recht spar-\n"
"tanisch eingerichtet."
msgstr ""
"The room is furnished quite\n"
"spartanly."

msgctxt "scene:35:33"
msgid ""
"Da hängt ein Spiegel\n"
"an der Wand."
msgstr ""
"A mirror hangs there upon\n"
"the wall."

msgctxt "scene:35:35"
msgid ""
"Ein Brett ist an der Wand\n"
"befestigt, und darauf ste-\n"
"hen verschiedene Flaschen."
msgstr ""
"A shelf is attached to the wall,\n"
"and upon it stand various\n"
"bottles."

msgctxt "scene:35:38"
msgid "Eine Holzbank."
msgstr "A wooden bench."

msgctxt "scene:35:39"
msgid ""
"Ein recht grosser Tisch\n"
"mit zwei Stühlen, da fehlen\n"
"sicher noch Stühle..."
msgstr ""
"A rather large table with two\n"
"chairs; surely chairs are missing\n"
"here..."

msgctxt "scene:35:42"
msgid ""
"Von welchem Tier kann das\n"
"Fell nur stammen?"
msgstr ""
"From what beast might that pelt\n"
"possibly come?"

msgctxt "scene:35:44"
msgid ""
"Zwei alte Musketen. Das\n"
"sind ja noch Vorderlader."
msgstr ""
"Two old muskets. Why, those\n"
"are still muzzle-loaders."

msgctxt "scene:35:46"
msgid ""
"Ein massiv gemauerter\n"
"Kamin, er passt gut in\n"
"dieses Zimmer, und ist\n"
"im Winter sicherlich\n"
"auch notwendig."
msgstr ""
"A fireplace of solid masonry;\n"
"it suits this room well, and\n"
"in winter is surely quite\n"
"necessary as well.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:51"
msgid "Eine schlichte Holztüre."
msgstr "A plain wooden door."

msgctxt "scene:35:52"
msgid ""
"Diese Treppe ist im Gegen-\n"
"satz zur übrigen Einrich-\n"
"tung recht pompös gebaut."
msgstr ""
"This staircase, in contrast to\n"
"the rest of the furnishings, is\n"
"built quite grandly."

msgctxt "scene:35:55"
msgid ""
"Ein Landschaftsbild, sieht\n"
"aus wie die Ölmalereien\n"
"englischer Grafschaften."
msgstr ""
"A landscape painting; looks like\n"
"the oil paintings of English\n"
"shires."

msgctxt "scene:35:58"
msgid ""
"Da steht allerhand Ge-\n"
"rümpel herum..."
msgstr ""
"All manner of junk is standing\n"
"about there..."

msgctxt "scene:35:60"
msgid "So eitel bin ich nicht."
msgstr "I am not that vain."

msgctxt "scene:35:61"
msgid ""
"Die Flaschen lass ich mal\n"
"da oben stehen..."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the bottles standing\n"
"up there..."

msgctxt "scene:35:63"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich die Sitzbank\n"
"mitnehmen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I take the bench\n"
"with me?"

msgctxt "scene:35:65"
msgid ""
"Es hat noch nicht zum Essen\n"
"geläutet."
msgstr ""
"The bell for dinner has not\n"
"rung yet."

msgctxt "scene:35:67"
msgid ""
"Das Fell ist schon abge-\n"
"treten und schmutzig, ich\n"
"kann mir nicht vorstellen,\n"
"dass das Fell mir etwas\n"
"nützen kann."
msgstr ""
"The pelt is already trampled and\n"
"dirty; I cannot imagine that\n"
"the pelt could be of any\n"
"use to me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:72"
msgid ""
"Was sollte ich mit einem\n"
"Ölgemälde anfangen."
msgstr ""
"What should I do with an\n"
"oil painting."

msgctxt "scene:35:74"
msgid ""
"Die Sachen lass ich stehen\n"
"wo sie sind."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave those things\n"
"where they are."

msgctxt "scene:35:76"
msgid ""
"Der brennt sicher, doch der\n"
"ist noch gut erhalten, und\n"
"könnte noch dienlich sein."
msgstr ""
"That surely burns, yet it is still\n"
"well preserved and might still prove\n"
"useful."

msgctxt "scene:35:79"
msgid "Da ist noch etwas im Beutel."
msgstr "There is still something in the pouch."

msgctxt "scene:35:80"
msgid ""
"Lebensmittel soll man nie\n"
"verschwenden."
msgstr ""
"Food should never be\n"
"wasted."

msgctxt "scene:35:82"
msgid "Es wäre schade um das Brot."
msgstr "It would be a pity for the bread."

msgctxt "scene:35:83"
msgid ""
"Bücher darf man nicht verbrennen,\n"
"sie sind hier in der Wildnis sehr\n"
"wertvoll, denn es ist eine der we-\n"
"nigen Freizeitbeschäftigungen, ein\n"
"interessantes Buch zu lesen."
msgstr ""
"Books must not be burned; they are\n"
"very valuable here in the wilderness,\n"
"for reading an interesting book is one\n"
"of the few pastimes.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:88"
msgid ""
"Der eigentliche Besitzer wäre\n"
"sicher traurig, wenn der Drache\n"
"verbrannt wird."
msgstr ""
"The actual owner would surely be\n"
"sad if the kite were burned.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:91"
msgid ""
"Der eigentliche Besitzer wäre\n"
"sicher traurig, wenn der Drache\n"
"verbrannt wird."
msgstr ""
"The actual owner would surely be\n"
"sad if the kite were burned.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:94"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich da Wasser reinschütte,\n"
"dann wird da in nächster Zeit\n"
"kein Feuer zum Brennen kommen."
msgstr ""
"If I pour water in there, then no\n"
"fire will burn there in the near\n"
"future."

msgctxt "scene:35:97"
msgid ""
"Alkohol würde sicher helfen\n"
"ein Feuer zu entfachen, doch\n"
"da gibt es Methoden, bei denen\n"
"man nicht den wertvollen Schnaps\n"
"opfern muss."
msgstr ""
"Alcohol would surely help to kindle a\n"
"fire, yet there are methods where\n"
"one need not sacrifice the precious\n"
"liquor.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:102"
msgid ""
"Alkohol würde sicher helfen\n"
"ein Feuer zu entfachen, doch\n"
"da gibt es Methoden, bei denen\n"
"man nicht den wertvollen Schnaps\n"
"opfern muss."
msgstr ""
"Alcohol would surely help to kindle a\n"
"fire, yet there are methods where\n"
"one need not sacrifice the precious\n"
"liquor.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:107"
msgid ""
"Das wäre nicht schlecht, nur\n"
"schade, dass ich keine Zeit\n"
"habe - gebratene Kartoffeln\n"
"esse ich sehr gerne."
msgstr ""
"That would not be bad, only a\n"
"pity that I have no time - I like\n"
"roasted potatoes very much.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:111"
msgid ""
"Warum die Kerzen in den Kamin\n"
"werfen, die könnten sicher noch\n"
"sehr dienlich sein."
msgstr ""
"Why throw the candles into the fireplace;\n"
"they could surely still be very\n"
"useful."

msgctxt "scene:35:114"
msgid ""
"Der Pfahl würde sicher gut\n"
"brennen, doch er ist leider\n"
"etwas zu gross für den Kamin."
msgstr ""
"The post would surely burn well, yet\n"
"it is unfortunately somewhat too\n"
"large for the fireplace."

msgctxt "scene:35:117"
msgid ""
"Das Rad ist aus schönem, trocke-\n"
"nem Holz, das brennt sicher gut,\n"
"aber es ist zu gross für den Kamin."
msgstr ""
"The wheel is made of fine, dry wood;\n"
"that surely burns well, but it is\n"
"too large for the fireplace."

msgctxt "scene:35:120"
msgid ""
"Die Lampe ist aus sehr trockenem\n"
"Holz, doch ist sie zu gross, und\n"
"passt nicht in den Kamin."
msgstr ""
"The lamp is made of very dry wood,\n"
"yet it is too large, and does not fit\n"
"into the fireplace."

msgctxt "scene:35:123"
msgid ""
"Die brennen zwar, doch es muss\n"
"da etwas anderes geben,um das\n"
"Feuer anzufachen."
msgstr ""
"Those do burn, yet there must be\n"
"something else to kindle the\n"
"fire."

msgctxt "scene:35:126"
msgid ""
"Nicht doch, wir können doch\n"
"nicht das Kinderspielzeug\n"
"verheizen..."
msgstr ""
"Surely not, we cannot burn the\n"
"children's toy...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:129"
msgid ""
"Das Öl würde sicher nur stark\n"
"rauchen und sonst nichts,\n"
"und das hilft auch nicht das\n"
"Problem zu lösen."
msgstr ""
"The oil would surely only smoke heavily\n"
"and nothing else, and that does not\n"
"help to solve the problem either.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:35:133"
msgid ""
"Die Würfel dürfen wir nicht ein-\n"
"fach verbrennen."
msgstr ""
"We must not simply burn the\n"
"dice."

msgctxt "scene:35:135"
msgid ""
"Der Topflappen könnte unter\n"
"Umständen noch recht nützlich\n"
"sein."
msgstr ""
"The potholder might under certain\n"
"circumstances still be quite\n"
"useful."

msgctxt "scene:35:138"
msgid ""
"Die Lampe war wohl früher\n"
"mal ein Rad."
msgstr ""
"The lamp was likely a wheel at\n"
"one time."

msgctxt "scene:35:140"
msgid ""
"Mrs. Rafter wird wohl nicht\n"
"sehr glücklich darüber sein,\n"
"dass ich ihre Lampe demoliert\n"
"habe."
msgstr ""
"Mrs. Rafter will likely not be very\n"
"happy about my having demolished\n"
"her lamp.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:36:0"
msgid ""
"Mehr Kartoffeln kann\n"
"ich nicht tragen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot carry any more\n"
"potatoes."

msgctxt "scene:36:2"
msgid ""
"Ich lass die Kiste\n"
"stehen wo sie ist."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the crate\n"
"standing where it is."

msgctxt "scene:36:4"
msgid ""
"Ich räum' die restlichen\n"
"Kartoffeln auch noch\n"
"rüber."
msgstr ""
"I'll clear the remaining\n"
"potatoes over as\n"
"well."

msgctxt "scene:36:7"
msgid "10 Minuten später..."
msgstr "10 minutes later..."

msgctxt "scene:36:8"
msgid ""
"Oh, da ist ja ein Geheim-\n"
"fach hinter der Kiste."
msgstr ""
"Oh, there is a secret\n"
"compartment behind the crate."

msgctxt "scene:36:10"
msgid ""
"Das Fach lässt sich von\n"
"Hand nicht öffnen."
msgstr ""
"The compartment cannot be\n"
"opened by hand."

msgctxt "scene:36:12"
msgid "Das Fach ist komplett leer."
msgstr "The compartment is completely empty."

msgctxt "scene:36:13"
msgid ""
"Das sieht aus wie ein\n"
"Geheimfach."
msgstr ""
"That looks like a secret\n"
"compartment."

msgctxt "scene:36:15"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja etwas in dem\n"
"Geheimfach. Mir scheint\n"
"Mr. Butler traut dem\n"
"Gehilfen nicht, wenn es\n"
"um seinen Whisky geht."
msgstr ""
"Why, there is something in the\n"
"secret compartment. It seems\n"
"Mr. Butler does not trust the\n"
"farm hand when it comes to\n"
"his whisky."

msgctxt "scene:36:20"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja nichts mehr im\n"
"Geheimfach... doch, da\n"
"liegt ja noch etwas..."
msgstr ""
"Why, there is nothing left in\n"
"the secret compartment... yet\n"
"there is still something..."

msgctxt "scene:36:23"
msgid "Das Fach ist leer."
msgstr "The compartment is empty."

msgctxt "scene:36:24"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich den Korken-\n"
"zieher ins Fach legen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I put the corkscrew\n"
"into the compartment?"

msgctxt "scene:36:26"
msgid ""
"Das Öl schwimmt oben auf,\n"
"doch ich komme immer noch\n"
"nicht daran."
msgstr ""
"The oil floats on top, yet\n"
"I still cannot reach\n"
"it."

msgctxt "scene:36:29"
msgid ""
"Das Wasser wird das Öl\n"
"weiter nach oben bringen."
msgstr ""
"The water will bring the oil\n"
"further up."

msgctxt "scene:36:31"
msgid ""
"Nein, mehr Wasser braucht\n"
"es nicht."
msgstr ""
"No, it needs no more\n"
"water."

msgctxt "scene:36:33"
msgid ""
"An das Öl komme ich nicht,\n"
"es ist zu tief unten."
msgstr ""
"I cannot reach the oil; it\n"
"is too far down."

msgctxt "scene:36:35"
msgid ""
"Ich komme noch immer nicht\n"
"an das Öl."
msgstr ""
"I still cannot reach the\n"
"oil."

msgctxt "scene:36:37"
msgid ""
"Jetzt kann ich die Tasse\n"
"füllen."
msgstr ""
"Now I can fill the\n"
"cup."

msgctxt "scene:36:39"
msgid ""
"Ein leeres Holzfass, ohne\n"
"Deckel."
msgstr ""
"An empty wooden barrel, without\n"
"a lid."

msgctxt "scene:36:41"
msgid ""
"In dem Fass sind Kartof-\n"
"feln aus der Kiste."
msgstr ""
"In the barrel are potatoes\n"
"from the crate."

msgctxt "scene:36:43"
msgid ""
"Die Decke ist hier nicht\n"
"einfach nur aus Holz -\n"
"dadurch ist der Keller\n"
"sehr gut als Voratsraum\n"
"geeignet."
msgstr ""
"The ceiling here is not simply\n"
"made of wood - thus making the\n"
"cellar very well suited as a\n"
"storage room.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:36:48"
msgid ""
"Die Wände haben schon\n"
"einige Risse."
msgstr ""
"The walls already have a\n"
"few cracks."

msgctxt "scene:36:50"
msgid ""
"Hier haben sich bereits\n"
"die Spinnen eingenistet."
msgstr ""
"Spiders have already nested\n"
"in here."

msgctxt "scene:36:52"
msgid ""
"Schleifspuren von Holzspänen\n"
"auf dem Boden, eigenartig."
msgstr ""
"Drag marks of wood shavings on\n"
"the floor, peculiar."

msgctxt "scene:36:54"
msgid ""
"Auch der Boden ist aus\n"
"Steinen und Mörtel."
msgstr ""
"The floor, too, is made of\n"
"stone and mortar."

msgctxt "scene:36:56"
msgid ""
"Ein Holzfass mit gärendem\n"
"Inhalt, fest verschlossen.\n"
"Da quillt etwas aus den\n"
"Ritzen, und das sieht gar\n"
"nicht sehr appetitlich aus."
msgstr ""
"A wooden barrel with fermenting\n"
"contents, tightly sealed. Something\n"
"seeps from the cracks, and that\n"
"looks not very appetizing at all.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:36:61"
msgid ""
"Eine Schaufel mit\n"
"abgebrochener Spitze."
msgstr ""
"A shovel with a broken\n"
"point."

msgctxt "scene:36:63"
msgid ""
"Die Treppe ist etwas\n"
"beschädigt."
msgstr ""
"The stairs are somewhat\n"
"damaged."

msgctxt "scene:36:65"
msgid "Eine Holztür."
msgstr "A wooden door."

msgctxt "scene:36:66"
msgid ""
"Es scheint Licht aus\n"
"der Küche in den Keller."
msgstr ""
"Light seems to shine from\n"
"the kitchen into the cellar."

msgctxt "scene:36:68"
msgid ""
"Ein Eichenfass, am Boden\n"
"des Fasses befindet sich\n"
"noch etwas Oel."
msgstr ""
"An oak barrel; at the bottom\n"
"of the barrel there is still\n"
"a bit of oil."

msgctxt "scene:36:71"
msgid ""
"Das Fass ist halb voll\n"
"Wasser und obenauf\n"
"schwimmt etwas Öl."
msgstr ""
"The barrel is half full of\n"
"water and on top floats a\n"
"bit of oil."

msgctxt "scene:36:74"
msgid ""
"Das Fass ist zu zwei\n"
"Drittel mit Wasser\n"
"gefüllt und obenauf\n"
"schwimmt etwas Öl."
msgstr ""
"The barrel is two thirds full\n"
"of water and on top floats\n"
"a bit of oil.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:36:78"
msgid "Das Fass ist mir zu schwer."
msgstr "The barrel is too heavy for me."

msgctxt "scene:36:79"
msgid ""
"Bin ich hier die Putzfrau,\n"
"oder was?!?"
msgstr ""
"Am I the housemaid here, or\n"
"what?!?"

msgctxt "scene:36:81"
msgid ""
"Ich greife das Fass nicht\n"
"nicht an, wer weiss was\n"
"da drinnen ist."
msgstr ""
"I shall not touch the barrel, who\n"
"knows what is inside there.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:36:84"
msgid ""
"Mit blossen Händen kann ich\n"
"das Öl nicht herausschöpfen."
msgstr ""
"With bare hands I cannot scoop\n"
"out the oil."

msgctxt "scene:36:86"
msgid ""
"Eine Kartoffelkiste zum\n"
"Einlagern von Kartoffeln."
msgstr ""
"A potato crate for storing\n"
"potatoes."

msgctxt "scene:36:88"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brotmesser kann ich\n"
"das Fach nicht aufmachen, da\n"
"wird nur die Klinge brechen."
msgstr ""
"With the bread knife I cannot open\n"
"the compartment; that will only\n"
"break the blade."

msgctxt "scene:36:91"
msgid ""
"Der Spachtel passt nicht in\n"
"die Öffnung in der Mitte des\n"
"Fachs."
msgstr ""
"The spatula does not fit into\n"
"the opening in the middle of\n"
"the compartment."

msgctxt "scene:36:94"
msgid ""
"Die Mauer darf ich nicht be-\n"
"schädigen."
msgstr ""
"I must not damage the\n"
"wall."

msgctxt "scene:36:96"
msgid ""
"Damit beschädige ich nur die\n"
"Mauer."
msgstr ""
"With that I shall only damage\n"
"the wall."

msgctxt "scene:36:98"
msgid ""
"Der Schluessel passt nicht in\n"
"die Öffnung des Fachs."
msgstr ""
"The key does not fit into the\n"
"opening of the compartment."

msgctxt "scene:36:100"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, Du verwechselst das\n"
"mit einem Luftballon."
msgstr ""
"I believe you are confusing that\n"
"with a balloon."

msgctxt "scene:36:102"
msgid ""
"Was soll das, ich bin nicht\n"
"hier um die Einrichtungen\n"
"zu beschädigen."
msgstr ""
"What is the meaning of this; I am\n"
"not here to damage the furnishings.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:37:0"
msgid "Autsch!"
msgstr "Ouch!"

msgctxt "scene:37:1"
msgid ""
"Da ist ein Brot im Ofen,\n"
"das nehme ich gleich mit!"
msgstr ""
"There is bread in the oven, I'll\n"
"take that along at once!"

msgctxt "scene:37:3"
msgid "Der Ofen ist jetzt leer."
msgstr "The oven is empty now."

msgctxt "scene:37:4"
msgid "Das ist der Bilderrahmen."
msgstr "That is the picture frame."

msgctxt "scene:37:5"
msgid ""
"Aus Holzplanken, stabil\n"
"gebaut."
msgstr ""
"Made of wooden planks, sturdily\n"
"built."

msgctxt "scene:37:7"
msgid "Ein Hängeschrank aus Holz."
msgstr "A hanging wooden cabinet."

msgctxt "scene:37:8"
msgid "Weiss gekalkte Wände."
msgstr "White-limed walls."

msgctxt "scene:37:9"
msgid ""
"Zwei Gusspfannen hängen\n"
"da an der Wand."
msgstr ""
"Two cast-iron pans hang\n"
"there on the wall."

msgctxt "scene:37:11"
msgid "Die Tür führt ins Wohnzimmer."
msgstr "The door leads into the living room."

msgctxt "scene:37:12"
msgid "Eine Schüssel mit Teig."
msgstr "A bowl with dough."

msgctxt "scene:37:13"
msgid "Da liegt Teig auf dem Tisch."
msgstr "There is dough on the table."

msgctxt "scene:37:14"
msgid "Eine schlichte Holztür."
msgstr "A plain wooden door."

msgctxt "scene:37:15"
msgid ""
"Ein Gussofen mit Backrohr,\n"
"ein neues Modell. Damit\n"
"hat Mrs. Butler sicher viel\n"
"Freude."
msgstr ""
"A cast-iron stove with oven,\n"
"a new model. Mrs. Butler\n"
"surely takes great pleasure\n"
"in it."

msgctxt "scene:37:19"
msgid "Ein einfacher Holztisch."
msgstr "A simple wooden table."

msgctxt "scene:37:20"
msgid ""
"Ein grüner, abgetretener\n"
"Wollteppich."
msgstr ""
"A green, worn woolen\n"
"carpet."

msgctxt "scene:37:22"
msgid "Eine leere Glasflasche."
msgstr "An empty glass bottle."

msgctxt "scene:37:23"
msgid "Eine grüne Tonvase."
msgstr "A green clay vase."

msgctxt "scene:37:24"
msgid ""
"Ein Brett dient\n"
"hier an der Wand\n"
"als Ablage."
msgstr ""
"A shelf serves\n"
"as a ledge here\n"
"on the wall."

msgctxt "scene:37:27"
msgid ""
"Den Bildrahmen des Spieles\n"
"kann ich nicht nehmen, mein\n"
"lieber Freund."
msgstr ""
"I cannot take the picture frame\n"
"of the game, my dear\n"
"friend."

msgctxt "scene:37:30"
msgid ""
"Die Pfannen lass ich besser\n"
"an der Wand hängen, sonst\n"
"könnte ich mit Mrs. Butler\n"
"Schwierigkeiten bekommen,\n"
"denn es würde Ihr mit\n"
"Sicherheit sofort auffal-\n"
"len, wenn die fehlen."
msgstr ""
"I had better leave the pans\n"
"hanging on the wall, or I might\n"
"get into trouble with Mrs. Butler,\n"
"for she would surely notice\n"
"immediately if they were\n"
"missing.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:37:37"
msgid ""
"Den rohen Teig lass ich\n"
"liegen, ich bin kein ge-\n"
"schickter Bäcker."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the raw dough\n"
"be; I am no skillful\n"
"baker."

msgctxt "scene:37:40"
msgid ""
"Den Tisch kann ich nicht\n"
"wegrücken, ich sehe auch\n"
"keine Notwendigkeit darin."
msgstr ""
"I cannot move the table,\n"
"nor do I see any need to\n"
"do so."

msgctxt "scene:37:43"
msgid ""
"Unter dem Teppich liegt\n"
"bestimmt Nichts, oder soll\n"
"ich den Schmutz darunter-\n"
"kehren..?"
msgstr ""
"Surely there is nothing under the\n"
"carpet, or am I supposed to sweep\n"
"the dirt under it..?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:37:47"
msgid ""
"Ich brauche die leere\n"
"Flasche nicht."
msgstr ""
"I do not need the empty\n"
"bottle."

msgctxt "scene:37:49"
msgid ""
"Die Vase ist zwar hübsch,\n"
"doch ich brauche sie be-\n"
"stimmt nicht."
msgstr ""
"The vase is pretty indeed,\n"
"yet I surely do not need\n"
"it."

msgctxt "scene:37:52"
msgid ""
"Ich kann doch nicht ein-\n"
"fach die Küche zerlegen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot simply dismantle\n"
"the kitchen."

msgctxt "scene:37:54"
msgid ""
"Der Ofen ist ja brennend\n"
"heiss, der braucht nicht\n"
"noch mehr Brennmaterial."
msgstr ""
"Why, the stove is burning\n"
"hot; it needs no more fuel\n"
"for burning."

msgctxt "scene:37:57"
msgid ""
"Die werden wir da nicht ein-\n"
"heizen."
msgstr ""
"We shall not heat those in\n"
"there."

msgctxt "scene:37:59"
msgid ""
"Eine rauhe Methode den Ofen\n"
"auszumachen - es würde auch\n"
"eine Ueberschwemmung hinter-\n"
"lassen, über die Mrs. Butler\n"
"sicher nicht glücklich wäre."
msgstr ""
"A rough method to put out the\n"
"stove - it would also leave a\n"
"flood behind, which Mrs. Butler\n"
"would surely not be happy\n"
"about."

msgctxt "scene:37:64"
msgid ""
"Damit den Ofen zu öffnen, ist\n"
"wie Zähne ziehen mit einem\n"
"Raddampfer...Unmöglich!"
msgstr ""
"Opening the stove with that is\n"
"like pulling teeth with a\n"
"steamboat... Impossible!"

msgctxt "scene:37:67"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich den Ofen nicht\n"
"aufmachen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot open the stove\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:37:69"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich etwas Zeit hätte, würde\n"
"ich mir die schon braten."
msgstr ""
"If I had some time, I would\n"
"surely roast them for myself."

msgctxt "scene:37:71"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich den Ofen nicht\n"
"aufmachen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot open the stove\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:37:73"
msgid ""
"Der Pfahl ist zu gross um ihn\n"
"in den Ofen zu stecken."
msgstr ""
"The post is too large to put\n"
"it into the stove."

msgctxt "scene:37:75"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich den Ofen nicht\n"
"öffnen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot open the stove\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:37:77"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich der Ofen nicht\n"
"öffnen."
msgstr ""
"The stove cannot be opened\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:37:79"
msgid ""
"Die Socken sind zu klein,um\n"
"mit der Hand hineinzufahren\n"
"und diese so zu schützen."
msgstr ""
"The socks are too small to\n"
"slip one's hand inside and\n"
"thus protect it."

msgctxt "scene:37:82"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich das Ofentürchen\n"
"nicht öffnen."
msgstr ""
"The stove door cannot be\n"
"opened with that."

msgctxt "scene:37:84"
msgid ""
"Das würde sicher einen guten Ton\n"
"geben, wenn ich mit dem Spachtel\n"
"einen heissen Rhytmus darauf\n"
"schlagen würde, doch dazu fehlt\n"
"mir die Zeit..."
msgstr ""
"That would surely make a good sound\n"
"if I were to beat a hot rhythm on\n"
"it with the spatula, yet for that I\n"
"lack the time...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:37:89"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich das Ofentürchen\n"
"nicht öffnen, was für ein Einfall."
msgstr ""
"The stove door cannot be opened\n"
"with that; what an idea."

msgctxt "scene:38:0"
msgid ""
"Der Bildrahmen ausserhalb\n"
"des Spieles."
msgstr ""
"The picture frame outside\n"
"the game."

msgctxt "scene:38:2"
msgid ""
"Ein brauner Teddybär, aus\n"
"weichem Fell."
msgstr ""
"A brown teddy bear, made of\n"
"soft fur."

msgctxt "scene:38:4"
msgid ""
"Ein Bild, mit mit einem Rei-\n"
"ter,der durch die Wüste reitet."
msgstr ""
"A picture with a rider\n"
"riding through the desert."

msgctxt "scene:38:6"
msgid "Eine weiss getünchte Wand."
msgstr "A whitewashed wall."

msgctxt "scene:38:7"
msgid ""
"Eine Holztür, in einen\n"
"weiteren Raum."
msgstr ""
"A wooden door, into another\n"
"room."

msgctxt "scene:38:9"
msgid ""
"Eine Holzkiste, wie sie oft\n"
"für Seereisen verwendet\n"
"wird."
msgstr ""
"A wooden chest, such as is\n"
"often used for sea\n"
"voyages."

msgctxt "scene:38:12"
msgid "Spielklötze aus Holz."
msgstr "Wooden building blocks."

msgctxt "scene:38:13"
msgid "Ein grünes Holzpferd."
msgstr "A green wooden horse."

msgctxt "scene:38:14"
msgid ""
"Zwei Holzeier, ein Blaues\n"
"und ein Rotes."
msgstr ""
"Two wooden eggs, a blue\n"
"and a red one."

msgctxt "scene:38:16"
msgid ""
"Der Boden aus Holzplanken\n"
"ist schon ganz bleichge-\n"
"scheuert."
msgstr ""
"The floor of wooden planks\n"
"is already scrubbed completely\n"
"bleached."

msgctxt "scene:38:19"
msgid ""
"Eine Schublade, die unten\n"
"in den Schrank eingebaut\n"
"wurde."
msgstr ""
"A drawer built into the\n"
"bottom of the wardrobe.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:38:22"
msgid ""
"Ein Holzstuhl, wie sie unten\n"
"im Wohnzimmer herumstehen."
msgstr ""
"A wooden chair, such as stand\n"
"about downstairs in the living room."

msgctxt "scene:38:24"
msgid ""
"Ein etwas ausgebleichter\n"
"Schlafzimmerschrank."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat faded bedroom\n"
"wardrobe."

msgctxt "scene:38:26"
msgid ""
"Ein Bett, aber die Decke\n"
"und das Kissen fehlen."
msgstr ""
"A bed, yet the blanket and\n"
"pillow are missing."

msgctxt "scene:38:28"
msgid "Eine braune Stoffschlange."
msgstr "A brown cloth snake."

msgctxt "scene:38:29"
msgid ""
"Mein Freund, ich bin ein\n"
"Teil des Spieles, und kann\n"
"nicht den Rahmen ausserhalb\n"
"des Bildes nehmen..."
msgstr ""
"My friend, I am part of\n"
"the game, and cannot take the\n"
"frame outside of the picture...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:38:33"
msgid ""
"Den Teddy lass ich sitzen,\n"
"er wird mir nicht viel\n"
"nutzen."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the teddy sitting,\n"
"he will not be of much\n"
"use to me."

msgctxt "scene:38:36"
msgid "Ich sammel keine Bilder."
msgstr "I do not collect pictures."

msgctxt "scene:38:37"
msgid ""
"Mit Bauklötzen habe ich\n"
"schon lange nicht mehr\n"
"gespielt, doch dazu ist\n"
"jetzt keine Zeit."
msgstr ""
"I have not played with building\n"
"blocks for a long time, yet\n"
"there is no time for that\n"
"now."

msgctxt "scene:38:41"
msgid ""
"Ich bevorzuge richtige\n"
"Pferde."
msgstr ""
"I prefer real\n"
"horses."

msgctxt "scene:38:43"
msgid ""
"Die lassen sich so schlecht\n"
"in der Pfanne braten..."
msgstr ""
"Those are so difficult to\n"
"roast in a pan..."

msgctxt "scene:38:45"
msgid ""
"Oh, da liegt ja ein\n"
"Drachen oben auf dem\n"
"Schrank!"
msgstr ""
"Oh, why there is a\n"
"kite lying atop the\n"
"wardrobe!"

msgctxt "scene:38:48"
msgid ""
"Den nehm ich mit,\n"
"vieleicht kann ich\n"
"den irgendwo ge-\n"
"brauchen!"
msgstr ""
"I'll take it along,\n"
"perhaps I can\n"
"use it somewhere!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:38:52"
msgid ""
"Da oben ist nichts\n"
"mehr ausser Staub."
msgstr ""
"Up there is nothing\n"
"more except dust."

msgctxt "scene:38:54"
msgid "Zum Schlafen ist keine Zeit."
msgstr "There is no time for sleeping."

msgctxt "scene:38:55"
msgid ""
"Als Seil ist das absolut\n"
"ungeeignet, und zum Spielen\n"
"habe ich jetzt keine Zeit."
msgstr ""
"As a rope that is completely\n"
"unsuitable, and for playing\n"
"I have no time now."

msgctxt "scene:38:58"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich die Tür\n"
"nicht öffnen."
msgstr ""
"The door cannot be opened\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:38:60"
msgid ""
"Ich kann doch die Tür nicht\n"
"einfach mit der Hacke aufbrechen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot simply force the door\n"
"open with the pickaxe."

msgctxt "scene:38:62"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich die Tür nicht\n"
"öffnen."
msgstr ""
"The door cannot be opened with\n"
"that."

msgctxt "scene:38:64"
msgid ""
"Damit mache ich nur das Türschloss\n"
"kaputt, aber die Tür kriege ich \n"
"nicht auf."
msgstr ""
"With that I shall only break the\n"
"door lock, but I won't get the\n"
"door open."

msgctxt "scene:38:67"
msgid ""
"Damit würde ich die Tür sicher\n"
"aufbekommen, doch ich kann nicht\n"
"einfach Türen einschlagen."
msgstr ""
"With that I would surely get the\n"
"door open, yet I cannot simply\n"
"smash doors in."

msgctxt "scene:38:70"
msgid ""
"Damit liesse sich die Tür sicher\n"
"aufbrechen, doch das kann ich in\n"
"einem fremden Haus bei Freunden\n"
"nicht machen."
msgstr ""
"The door could surely be forced\n"
"open with that, yet I cannot do\n"
"that in a strange house belonging\n"
"to friends."

msgctxt "scene:38:74"
msgid ""
"Damit lässt sich die Tür nicht\n"
"öffnen."
msgstr ""
"The door cannot be opened with\n"
"that."

msgctxt "scene:38:76"
msgid "Dieser Schlüssel passt nicht."
msgstr "This key does not fit."

msgctxt "scene:38:77"
msgid ""
"Damit öffne ich jede Tür,\n"
"nur wird von dem Teil des\n"
"Hauses nicht mehr viel\n"
"übrig sein. Lassen wir\n"
"das also!"
msgstr ""
"With that I'll open any door,\n"
"only there won't be much left\n"
"of that part of the house.\n"
"So let us leave it alone!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:38:82"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich die Tür nicht auf-\n"
"schliessen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot unlock the door\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:38:84"
msgid "Die Tür ist verschlossen."
msgstr "The door is locked."

msgctxt "scene:38:85"
msgid ""
"Also, schauen wir mal durch's\n"
"Schlüsselloch, obwohl ich das\n"
"normalerweise nicht tue...\n"
"Ein Schlafzimmer, recht einfach\n"
"eingerichtet, mit einem grossen\n"
"Bett in der Mitte des Zimmers,\n"
"und einem Schrank, an der gegen-\n"
"überliegenden Wand."
msgstr ""
"Well, let us look through the\n"
"keyhole, although I usually\n"
"do not do that...\n"
"A bedroom, furnished quite simply,\n"
"with a large bed in the middle\n"
"of the room, and a wardrobe\n"
"on the opposite wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:38:93"
msgid ""
"Das ist sicher das Schlafzimmer\n"
"von Mr. und Mrs. Butler."
msgstr ""
"That is surely the bedroom\n"
"of Mr. and Mrs. Butler."

msgctxt "scene:38:95"
msgid "Die Tür ist verschlossen."
msgstr "The door is locked."

msgctxt "scene:39:0"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich da\n"
"am Fels rumschaben?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I scrape away\n"
"at the rock there?"

msgctxt "scene:39:2"
msgid ""
"Etwas Salpeter habe ich bereits\n"
"genommen, mehr brauche ich nicht."
msgstr ""
"I have already taken some saltpeter;\n"
"I do not need any more."

msgctxt "scene:39:4"
msgid ""
"Die Einstiegsluke, die unter\n"
"dem Misthaufen verborgen war."
msgstr ""
"The entry hatch that was hidden\n"
"under the dung heap."

msgctxt "scene:39:6"
msgid ""
"Da schimmert etwas an der\n"
"Wand..."
msgstr ""
"Something is shimmering there\n"
"on the wall..."

msgctxt "scene:39:8"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube, das ist\n"
"Salpeter!"
msgstr ""
"I believe that is\n"
"saltpeter!"

msgctxt "scene:39:10"
msgid ""
"Das Hanfseil, das ich zum\n"
"Runterklettern benutzt habe."
msgstr ""
"The hemp rope that I used for\n"
"climbing down."

msgctxt "scene:39:12"
msgid ""
"Da fliesst der Fluss ins\n"
"Freie, könnte für uns\n"
"eventuell ein Fluchtweg\n"
"werden."
msgstr ""
"There the river flows out into\n"
"the open; could eventually\n"
"become an escape route for\n"
"us."

msgctxt "scene:39:16"
msgid ""
"Massiver Felsen, der durch den\n"
"Fluss ganz feucht und vermoost\n"
"ist."
msgstr ""
"Solid rock, which is quite\n"
"damp and mossy from the\n"
"river."

msgctxt "scene:39:19"
msgid ""
"Da steckt ja eine alte\n"
"Hackenspitze im Boden."
msgstr ""
"Why, an old pickaxe tip\n"
"is stuck in the ground."

msgctxt "scene:39:21"
msgid ""
"Der Boden muss öfters\n"
"überschwemmt werden, er\n"
"ist total verschlammt."
msgstr ""
"The ground must often be\n"
"flooded; it is totally\n"
"muddy."

msgctxt "scene:39:24"
msgid ""
"Der kleine, unterirdische\n"
"Fluss hat eine sehr\n"
"starke Strömung."
msgstr ""
"The small underground river\n"
"has a very strong\n"
"current."

msgctxt "scene:39:27"
msgid ""
"Ohne Werkzeug kann ich\n"
"aus dem Felsen nichts\n"
"wegnehmen."
msgstr ""
"Without tools I cannot\n"
"take anything away from\n"
"the rock."

msgctxt "scene:39:30"
msgid ""
"Mit der blossen Hand kann\n"
"ich den Salpeter nicht von\n"
"der Wand kratzen."
msgstr ""
"With bare hands I cannot\n"
"scrape the saltpeter off\n"
"the wall."

msgctxt "scene:39:33"
msgid ""
"Jetzt brauche ich hier\n"
"noch nicht rauszugehen,\n"
"doch ich werde die Mög-\n"
"lichkeit offenlassen."
msgstr ""
"I do not need to go out\n"
"here just yet, yet I\n"
"shall keep the possibility\n"
"open."

msgctxt "scene:39:37"
msgid ""
"Aus dem massiven Felsen,\n"
"kann ich ohne Werkzeug\n"
"keine Stücke herausbrechen."
msgstr ""
"From the solid rock I cannot\n"
"break any pieces out without\n"
"tools."

msgctxt "scene:39:40"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Schlamm könnte\n"
"man Fangopackungen machen,\n"
"doch die werden erst im\n"
"20.Jahrhundert aktuell..."
msgstr ""
"With the mud one could make\n"
"fango packs, yet those will\n"
"only become topical in the\n"
"20th century..."

msgctxt "scene:39:44"
msgid "Ich bin nicht durstig."
msgstr "I am not thirsty."

msgctxt "scene:40:0"
msgid "Inzwischen..."
msgstr "Meanwhile..."

msgctxt "scene:40:1"
msgid ""
"Da ist die Farm, der\n"
"alte Butler scheint\n"
"uns noch nicht be-\n"
"merkt zu haben."
msgstr ""
"There is the farm; old\n"
"Butler seems not to have\n"
"noticed us yet.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:40:5"
msgid ""
"Das wird sich aber\n"
"schnell ändern, denn\n"
"jetzt erleichtern wir\n"
"ihn um sein Geld."
msgstr ""
"Yet that will change\n"
"quickly, for now we\n"
"shall relieve him of\n"
"his money."

msgctxt "scene:40:9"
msgid ""
"Richtig, Kameraden,\n"
"doch lasst uns erst\n"
"einmal eine Gute\n"
"Deckung suchen, be-\n"
"vor wir uns lautstark\n"
"ankündigen."
msgstr ""
"Right, comrades, yet\n"
"let us first seek good\n"
"cover before we announce\n"
"ourselves loudly.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:45:0"
msgid ""
"Wie ist das möglich?\n"
"Winnetou und Old\n"
"Firehand?"
msgstr ""
"How is that possible?\n"
"Winnetou and Old\n"
"Firehand?"

msgctxt "scene:45:3"
msgid ""
"Winnetou grüsst den\n"
"Grossen und Kleinen\n"
"Bär."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou greets the\n"
"Great and Little\n"
"Bear."

msgctxt "scene:45:6"
msgid ""
"Winnetou verfolgt mit\n"
"Old Firehand die Spur\n"
"zweier Banditen, die\n"
"Euren Schatz stehlen\n"
"wollen."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou, with Old Firehand,\n"
"is pursuing the trail of two\n"
"bandits who wish to steal\n"
"your treasure.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:45:11"
msgid ""
"Ihr kommt zu spät,\n"
"Freunde. Die Banditen\n"
"sind bereits auf der\n"
"Insel. Sie überrasch-\n"
"ten uns. Wir mussten\n"
"fliehen, wir werden\n"
"nun unsere Brüder zu\n"
"Hilfe holen."
msgstr ""
"You come too late, friends.\n"
"The bandits are already on the\n"
"island. They surprised us.\n"
"We were forced to flee; we\n"
"shall now fetch our brothers\n"
"to help us.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:45:19"
msgid ""
"Dann ist Euer Schatz\n"
"wohl verloren?"
msgstr ""
"Then your treasure is\n"
"likely lost?"

msgctxt "scene:45:21"
msgid ""
"Nein, die Rache des\n"
"Silbersees wird die\n"
"Bleichgesichter ins\n"
"Verderben stürzen.\n"
"Den Schatz sollen sie\n"
"nicht bekommen, und\n"
"nach ihnen auch nie-\n"
"mand mehr."
msgstr ""
"No, the vengeance of the\n"
"Silver Lake shall plunge\n"
"the pale-faces into\n"
"ruin.\n"
"The treasure they shall\n"
"not obtain, and after\n"
"them no one else\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:45:29"
msgid ""
"Es beruhigt mich, dass\n"
"Ihr hier seid, Freunde.\n"
"Kleiner Bär und ich,\n"
"wollen unsere Verbün-\n"
"deten aufsuchen, und\n"
"sie um Hilfe bitten.\n"
"Euch bitten wir auch\n"
"um Hilfe."
msgstr ""
"It reassures me that\n"
"you are here, friends.\n"
"Little Bear and I\n"
"wish to seek out our\n"
"allies, and ask them\n"
"for aid. We ask you\n"
"for help as well.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:45:37"
msgid ""
"Versucht die Frevler\n"
"aufzuhalten. Uns bleibt\n"
"nur wenig Zeit, lebt\n"
"wohl!"
msgstr ""
"Try to stop the miscreants.\n"
"We have but little\n"
"time left; farewell!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:45:41"
msgid ""
"Mögen meine Brüder\n"
"unsere Pferde nehmen!"
msgstr ""
"May my brothers take\n"
"our horses!"

msgctxt "scene:45:43"
msgid ""
"Danke mein Bruder, doch\n"
"wir haben unsere Pferde\n"
"im Wald zurückgelassen."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, my brother, yet\n"
"we left our horses\n"
"behind in the forest."

msgctxt "scene:45:46"
msgid ""
"Wir werden inzwischen\n"
"zusehen, dass wir dem\n"
"Cornel das Handwerk\n"
"legen."
msgstr ""
"Meanwhile we shall see\n"
"to it that we put a\n"
"stop to the Cornel's\n"
"game."

msgctxt "scene:45:50"
msgid ""
"Winnetou weiss, dass\n"
"ein geheimer Gang vom\n"
"Berg, unter den See\n"
"führt. Dieser Gang,\n"
"muss von den alten\n"
"Minen aus gehen."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou knows that a\n"
"secret passage leads from\n"
"the mountain under the lake.\n"
"This passage must start\n"
"from the old mines.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:0"
msgid ""
"Die unterste Sprosse ist\n"
"zu hoch, um sie zu erreichen."
msgstr ""
"The lowest rung is too\n"
"high to be reached."

msgctxt "scene:46:2"
msgid ""
"Ein Haufen Geröll hat den\n"
"Eingang eines anderen Stol-\n"
"lens verschüttet."
msgstr ""
"A pile of rubble has buried\n"
"the entrance to another\n"
"gallery."

msgctxt "scene:46:5"
msgid ""
"Oh, da liegt ja ein Seil\n"
"unter dem Geröll."
msgstr ""
"Oh, why there is a rope\n"
"lying under the rubble."

msgctxt "scene:46:7"
msgid ""
"Die Holzbalken weisen darauf\n"
"hin, dass der Stollen wohl\n"
"eingestürzt ist, zumindestens\n"
"der Eingang davon."
msgstr ""
"The wooden beams indicate\n"
"that the gallery has likely\n"
"collapsed, at least the\n"
"entrance to it."

msgctxt "scene:46:11"
msgid ""
"Es ist aber nicht ernst ge-\n"
"meint, dass ich den Schutt\n"
"von Hand wegräumen soll, das\n"
"würde ja Jahre dauern."
msgstr ""
"Surely it is not meant in\n"
"earnest that I am to clear\n"
"the rubble by hand; why, that\n"
"would take years."

msgctxt "scene:46:15"
msgid ""
"Die Wand ist steil, und\n"
"sehr hoch."
msgstr ""
"The wall is steep, and\n"
"very high."

msgctxt "scene:46:17"
msgid ""
"Eine Leiter aus Eisensprossen,\n"
"die in der Felswand eingelas-\n"
"sen wurden. Unten fehlen wohl\n"
"die beiden letzten Sprossen,\n"
"denn in der Felswand sind Löcher\n"
"zu sehen."
msgstr ""
"A ladder of iron rungs that\n"
"were set into the rock wall.\n"
"At the bottom the last two rungs\n"
"seem to be missing, for holes\n"
"are to be seen in the rock wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:23"
msgid ""
"Diese Balkenkonstruktion,\n"
"stützt wohl den Eingang\n"
"zur Mine."
msgstr ""
"This timber framework likely\n"
"supports the entrance to\n"
"the mine."

msgctxt "scene:46:26"
msgid ""
"Der Eingang zur Mine wirkt\n"
"etwas düster."
msgstr ""
"The entrance to the mine\n"
"appears somewhat gloomy."

msgctxt "scene:46:28"
msgid ""
"Das Dynamit, welches ich\n"
"im Geröllhaufen befestigt\n"
"habe. Es wartet nur noch\n"
"darauf, angezündet zu wer-\n"
"den."
msgstr ""
"The dynamite that I attached in\n"
"the pile of rubble. It only\n"
"awaits being lit now.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:33"
msgid ""
"Die Bohlen sind noch recht\n"
"gut erhalten."
msgstr ""
"The planks are still fairly\n"
"well preserved."

msgctxt "scene:46:35"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen sind so gut er-\n"
"halten, dass man sie noch\n"
"nutzen könnte."
msgstr ""
"The rails are so well preserved\n"
"that one could still use\n"
"them."

msgctxt "scene:46:38"
msgid ""
"Der Boden ist hier überall\n"
"festgetreten."
msgstr ""
"The ground here is firmly\n"
"trodden down everywhere."

msgctxt "scene:46:40"
msgid ""
"Eine Blume ziert hier etwas\n"
"die kahle Felslandschaft."
msgstr ""
"A flower somewhat adorns the\n"
"barren rock landscape here."

msgctxt "scene:46:42"
msgid ""
"Da die Mine schon seit gerau-\n"
"mer Zeit ausser Betrieb ist,\n"
"hat die Natur schon wieder\n"
"begonnen, die Wunden, die ihr\n"
"zugefügt wurden, zu heilen.\n"
"Das Gras, hat bereits den Anfang\n"
"gemacht."
msgstr ""
"Since the mine has been out of\n"
"operation for quite some time,\n"
"nature has already begun to heal\n"
"the wounds inflicted upon her.\n"
"The grass has already made a\n"
"start of it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:49"
msgid ""
"Einige Felsblöcke, die wohl vom\n"
"Berg heruntergefallen sind."
msgstr ""
"A few boulders that likely fell\n"
"down from the mountain."

msgctxt "scene:46:51"
msgid ""
"Einige Steine liegen hier\n"
"herum."
msgstr ""
"A few stones lie about\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:46:53"
msgid ""
"Die Wand ist zu steil, um\n"
"sie ohne die richtige Aus-\n"
"rüstung zu besteigen."
msgstr ""
"The wall is too steep to\n"
"climb without the proper\n"
"equipment."

msgctxt "scene:46:56"
msgid ""
"Diesen Balken lasse ich wohl\n"
"besser stehen, denn sonst\n"
"riskiere ich, dass der Minen-\n"
"eingang einstürzt."
msgstr ""
"I had better leave this beam\n"
"standing, or else I risk having\n"
"the mine entrance collapse.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:60"
msgid ""
"Jetzt habe ich eben erst\n"
"die Stange im Geröllhaufen\n"
"platziert, warum soll ich\n"
"sie herausnehmen - die war-\n"
"tet doch nur, angezündet zu\n"
"werden."
msgstr ""
"I have only just placed the stick\n"
"in the pile of rubble; why\n"
"should I take it out - why, it\n"
"only awaits being lit.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:66"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen sind zu schwer,\n"
"um die Bohlen unter ihnen\n"
"hervorzuholen."
msgstr ""
"The rails are too heavy to get\n"
"the planks out from under\n"
"them."

msgctxt "scene:46:69"
msgid ""
"Ohne das richtige Werkzeug,\n"
"habe ich keine Chance, die\n"
"Schienen von den Bohlen zu\n"
"lösen."
msgstr ""
"Without the proper tools I have\n"
"no chance of loosening the\n"
"rails from the planks.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:73"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keine Zeit, jetzt\n"
"Blumen zu pflücken."
msgstr ""
"I have no time to pick flowers\n"
"right now."

msgctxt "scene:46:75"
msgid ""
"Ich bin nicht auf einer bota-\n"
"nischen Exkursion."
msgstr ""
"I am not on a botanical\n"
"excursion."

msgctxt "scene:46:77"
msgid ""
"Die Steine, wären nur sinnloser\n"
"Ballast - ich habe auch nichts,\n"
"wo ich sie hineingeben könnte."
msgstr ""
"The stones would only be useless\n"
"ballast - nor do I have anything\n"
"to put them into."

msgctxt "scene:46:80"
msgid ""
"Ich möchte nicht auf die Felsen\n"
"klettern, das hilft mir sicher\n"
"nicht weiter."
msgstr ""
"I do not wish to climb onto the\n"
"rocks; that surely won't help me\n"
"any further."

msgctxt "scene:46:83"
msgid ""
"Die Leiter braucht nicht gestützt\n"
"werden."
msgstr ""
"The ladder does not need to\n"
"be supported."

msgctxt "scene:46:85"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen passt nicht in die\n"
"Löcher der Wand, und ausserdem\n"
"fehlen zwei Stufen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar does not fit into the\n"
"holes in the wall, and besides\n"
"two rungs are missing."

msgctxt "scene:46:88"
msgid ""
"Mit brachialer Gewalt vorzugehen,\n"
"hilft in meiner Situation nicht\n"
"weiter."
msgstr ""
"Proceeding with brute force does\n"
"not help further in my situation.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:91"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich auf die Figur steige,\n"
"könnte ich die unterste Stufe\n"
"erreichen, das ist mir bei dem\n"
"Boden aber etwas zu unsicher,\n"
"da muss es eine andere Lösung\n"
"geben..."
msgstr ""
"If I step onto the figure, I could\n"
"reach the lowest rung, yet with that\n"
"ground that seems a bit too unsafe to\n"
"me; there must be another solution...\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:97"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich auf die Figur steige,\n"
"könnte ich die unterste Stufe\n"
"erreichen, das ist mir bei dem\n"
"Boden aber etwas zu unsicher,\n"
"da muss es eine andere Lösung\n"
"geben..."
msgstr ""
"If I step onto the figure, I could\n"
"reach the lowest rung, yet with that\n"
"ground that seems a bit too unsafe to\n"
"me; there must be another solution...\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:103"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich auf die Figur steige,\n"
"könnte ich die unterste Stufe\n"
"erreichen, das ist mir bei dem\n"
"Boden aber etwas zu unsicher,\n"
"da muss es eine andere Lösung\n"
"geben..."
msgstr ""
"If I step onto the figure, I could\n"
"reach the lowest rung, yet with that\n"
"ground that seems a bit too unsafe to\n"
"me; there must be another solution...\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:109"
msgid ""
"Ich kann das Seil nicht be-\n"
"festigen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot fasten the\n"
"rope."

msgctxt "scene:46:111"
msgid ""
"Die passen nicht in die, für die\n"
"Sprossen vorgesehenen Löcher."
msgstr ""
"They do not fit into the holes\n"
"intended for the rungs."

msgctxt "scene:46:113"
msgid ""
"Das würde helfen, die verklemm-\n"
"ten Brocken zu lösen, doch\n"
"damit kann ich nicht den Haufen\n"
"wegschaffen."
msgstr ""
"That would help to loosen the jammed\n"
"chunks, yet I cannot clear the\n"
"pile away with that.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:117"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte den Haufen wegschaf-\n"
"fen, und nicht noch mehr d'rauf-\n"
"legen."
msgstr ""
"I should clear the pile away,\n"
"and not put even more upon\n"
"it."

msgctxt "scene:46:120"
msgid ""
"Ich werde mich hier nicht als\n"
"Eisenbahnarbeiter betätigen, dass\n"
"ist auch nicht notwendig."
msgstr ""
"I shall not act as a railroad\n"
"worker here; that is not necessary\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:46:123"
msgid ""
"Dieses Brecheisen ist ungeeignet\n"
"für Schienenarbeiten."
msgstr ""
"This crowbar is unsuitable for\n"
"railwork."

msgctxt "scene:46:125"
msgid ""
"Die sind viel zu schwach, um da-\n"
"mit an den Schienen zu arbeiten."
msgstr ""
"Those are far too weak to work on\n"
"the rails with them."

msgctxt "scene:46:127"
msgid ""
"Mit den Bohlen, kann ich die an-\n"
"deren Bohlen unter den Schienen\n"
"auch nicht hervorschlagen, ich\n"
"bin ja kein Muskelmann."
msgstr ""
"With the planks I cannot knock\n"
"the other planks out from under\n"
"the rails either; I am no\n"
"strongman."

msgctxt "scene:46:131"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen, ist viel zu\n"
"schwach für Arbeiten an den\n"
"Bohlen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is far too\n"
"weak for work on the\n"
"planks."

msgctxt "scene:46:134"
msgid ""
"Damit, bekomme ich die Bohlen\n"
"sicher unter den Schienen\n"
"hervor, doch ob die dann noch\n"
"viel mehr als ein Haufen Säge-\n"
"mehl sind, wage ich zu bezwei-\n"
"feln."
msgstr ""
"With that I would surely get the planks\n"
"out from under the rails, yet whether\n"
"they would then be much more than a\n"
"pile of sawdust, I dare to doubt.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:46:140"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for such\n"
"work..."

msgctxt "scene:46:142"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for such\n"
"work..."

msgctxt "scene:46:144"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for such\n"
"work..."

msgctxt "scene:47:0"
msgid ""
"Der Cornel hat die Ge-\n"
"rechte Strafe erhalten.\n"
"Der wird keine Unschul-\n"
"digen mehr überfallen\n"
"und ausrauben.\n"
"Der Silbersee hat ihn\n"
"samt dem Schatz ver-\n"
"schlungen."
msgstr ""
"The Cornel has received\n"
"his rightful punishment.\n"
"He will no longer attack\n"
"and rob innocent people.\n"
"The Silver Lake has swallowed\n"
"him up together with the\n"
"treasure.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:8"
msgid ""
"Dank Firehand, ist der\n"
"Schatz für immer sicher,\n"
"und kann nicht mehr\n"
"geraubt werden. Er\n"
"wird nun niemanden mehr\n"
"blenden..."
msgstr ""
"Thanks to Firehand, the\n"
"treasure is safe forever,\n"
"and can no longer be\n"
"stolen. It shall now\n"
"dazzle no one any\n"
"more..."

msgctxt "scene:47:14"
msgid ""
"Lass uns zu Butlers\n"
"Farm zurückreiten, und\n"
"unseren Freunden be-\n"
"richten, was geschehen\n"
"ist."
msgstr ""
"Let us ride back to Butler's\n"
"farm and report to our\n"
"friends what has happened.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:19"
msgid ""
"Sie werden auch froh\n"
"sein zu hören, dass\n"
"der Cornel niemandem\n"
"mehr Leid zufügen\n"
"kann. Winnetou wird\n"
"Dich begleiten."
msgstr ""
"They will also be glad to\n"
"hear that the Cornel can no\n"
"longer harm anyone. Winnetou\n"
"shall accompany you.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:25"
msgid ""
"Die Sprossen der Leiter sind zu\n"
"hoch, ich kann sie nicht errei-\n"
"chen."
msgstr ""
"The rungs of the ladder are too\n"
"high; I cannot reach them.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:28"
msgid ""
"An der Felswand ist eine Leiter\n"
"aus Eisensprossen, die in die\n"
"Wand eingelassen sind."
msgstr ""
"Upon the rock wall is a ladder\n"
"of iron rungs set into the\n"
"wall."

msgctxt "scene:47:31"
msgid ""
"Eine in der Felswand eingelassene\n"
"Leiter, doch die untersten Spros-\n"
"sen, scheinen herausgebrochen zu\n"
"sein."
msgstr ""
"A ladder set into the rock wall,\n"
"yet the lowest rungs seem to\n"
"have been broken out.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:35"
msgid ""
"Die Wand ist steil und\n"
"sehr hoch."
msgstr ""
"The wall is steep and\n"
"very high."

msgctxt "scene:47:37"
msgid ""
"Diese Balkenkonstruktion\n"
"stützt wohl den Eingang\n"
"zur Mine."
msgstr ""
"This timber framework likely\n"
"supports the entrance to\n"
"the mine."

msgctxt "scene:47:40"
msgid ""
"Der Eingang zur Mine wirkt\n"
"etwas düster."
msgstr ""
"The entrance to the mine\n"
"appears somewhat gloomy."

msgctxt "scene:47:42"
msgid ""
"Ein Eingang zu einem weiteren\n"
"Stollen, wurde durch die Spren-\n"
"gung frei geworden."
msgstr ""
"An entrance to another gallery\n"
"was cleared by the blast.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:45"
msgid ""
"Die Bohlen sind noch recht\n"
"gut erhalten."
msgstr ""
"The planks are still fairly\n"
"well preserved."

msgctxt "scene:47:47"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen sind so gut\n"
"erhalten, dass man sie noch\n"
"nutzen könnte."
msgstr ""
"The rails are so well preserved\n"
"that one could still use\n"
"them."

msgctxt "scene:47:50"
msgid ""
"Der Boden ist hier überall\n"
"festgetreten."
msgstr ""
"The ground here is firmly\n"
"trodden down everywhere."

msgctxt "scene:47:52"
msgid ""
"Eine Blume ziert hier etwas\n"
"die kahle Felslandschaft."
msgstr ""
"A flower somewhat adorns the\n"
"barren rock landscape here."

msgctxt "scene:47:54"
msgid ""
"Da die Mine schon seit gerau-\n"
"mer Zeit ausser Betrieb ist,\n"
"hat die Natur schon wieder\n"
"begonnen, die Wunden die ihr\n"
"zugefügt wurden, zu heilen.\n"
"Das Gras, hat bereits den Anfang\n"
"gemacht."
msgstr ""
"Since the mine has been out of\n"
"operation for quite some time,\n"
"nature has already begun to heal\n"
"the wounds inflicted upon her.\n"
"The grass has already made a\n"
"start of it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:61"
msgid ""
"Da liegen überall noch Reste des\n"
"weggesprengten Gerölls herum."
msgstr ""
"Remnants of the blasted rubble lie\n"
"about everywhere."

msgctxt "scene:47:63"
msgid ""
"Einige massive Felsblöcke, die\n"
"vermutlich vom Berg herunterge-\n"
"fallen sind."
msgstr ""
"A few massive boulders that presumably\n"
"fell down from the mountain.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:66"
msgid ""
"Ein Lederbeutel, der muss unter\n"
"dem Geröll gelegen, und bei der\n"
"Explosion herausgeschleudert\n"
"worden sein."
msgstr ""
"A leather pouch; it must have lain\n"
"under the rubble and been blown out\n"
"during the explosion.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:70"
msgid ""
"Die Wand ist zu steil, um\n"
"sie ohne die richtige Aus-\n"
"rüstung zu besteigen."
msgstr ""
"The wall is too steep to\n"
"climb without the proper\n"
"equipment."

msgctxt "scene:47:73"
msgid ""
"Diesen Balken lasse ich wohl\n"
"besser stehen, denn sonst\n"
"riskiere ich, dass der Minen-\n"
"eingang einstürzt."
msgstr ""
"I had better leave this beam\n"
"standing, or else I risk having\n"
"the mine entrance collapse.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:77"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen sind zu schwer,\n"
"um die Bohlen unter ihnen\n"
"hervorzuholen."
msgstr ""
"The rails are too heavy,\n"
"to get the planks out\n"
"from under them."

msgctxt "scene:47:80"
msgid ""
"Ohne das richtige Werkzeug,\n"
"habe ich keine Chance, die\n"
"Schienen von den Bohlen zu\n"
"lösen."
msgstr ""
"Without the proper tools,\n"
"I have no chance of\n"
"loosening the rails from\n"
"the planks."

msgctxt "scene:47:84"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keine Zeit, jetzt\n"
"Blumen zu pflücken."
msgstr ""
"I have no time to pick\n"
"flowers right now."

msgctxt "scene:47:86"
msgid ""
"Ich bin nicht auf einer bota-\n"
"nischen Exkursion."
msgstr ""
"I am not on a bota-\n"
"nical excursion."

msgctxt "scene:47:88"
msgid ""
"Die Steine sind nur unnötiger\n"
"Ballast, ich lasse sie liegen."
msgstr ""
"The stones are only unnecessary\n"
"ballast, I shall leave them lie."

msgctxt "scene:47:90"
msgid ""
"Auf die Felsen zu klettern,\n"
"hilft mir sicher auch nicht\n"
"weiter."
msgstr ""
"Climbing onto the rocks\n"
"surely won't help me\n"
"any further."

msgctxt "scene:47:93"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen passt nicht in die\n"
"Löcher der Wand, und ausserdem\n"
"fehlen zwei Stufen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar does not fit in the\n"
"holes of the wall, and besides\n"
"two rungs are missing."

msgctxt "scene:47:96"
msgid ""
"Mit brachialer Gewalt vorzugehen,\n"
"hilft in meiner Situation nicht\n"
"weiter."
msgstr ""
"Proceeding with brute force\n"
"does not help further in\n"
"my situation."

msgctxt "scene:47:99"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich auf die Figur steige,\n"
"könnte ich die unterste Stufe\n"
"erreichen, das ist mir bei dem\n"
"Boden aber etwas zu unsicher,\n"
"da muss es eine andere Lösung\n"
"geben..."
msgstr ""
"If I step onto the figure,\n"
"I could reach the lowest rung,\n"
"yet with that ground that\n"
"seems a bit too unsafe to me,\n"
"there must be another\n"
"solution..."

msgctxt "scene:47:105"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich auf die Figur steige,\n"
"könnte ich die unterste Stufe\n"
"erreichen, das ist mir bei dem\n"
"Boden aber etwas zu unsicher,\n"
"da muss es eine andere Lösung\n"
"geben..."
msgstr ""
"If I step onto the figure,\n"
"I could reach the lowest rung,\n"
"yet with that ground that\n"
"seems a bit too unsafe to me,\n"
"there must be another\n"
"solution..."

msgctxt "scene:47:111"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich auf die Figur steige,\n"
"könnte ich die unterste Stufe\n"
"erreichen, das ist nir bei dem\n"
"Boden aber etwas zu unsicher,\n"
"da muss es eine andere Lösung\n"
"geben..."
msgstr ""
"If I step onto the figure,\n"
"I could reach the lowest rung,\n"
"yet with that ground that\n"
"seems a bit too unsafe to me,\n"
"there must be another\n"
"solution..."

msgctxt "scene:47:117"
msgid ""
"Ich kann das Seil nicht be-\n"
"festigen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot fasten the\n"
"rope."

msgctxt "scene:47:119"
msgid ""
"Die passen nicht in die, für die\n"
"Sprossen vorgesehenen Löcher."
msgstr ""
"They do not fit into the\n"
"holes intended for the rungs."

msgctxt "scene:47:121"
msgid ""
"Das würde helfen, die verklemm-\n"
"ten Brocken zu lösen, doch\n"
"damit kann ich nicht die gan-\n"
"zen Steine wegschaffen."
msgstr ""
"That would help to loosen the\n"
"jammed chunks, yet with that\n"
"I cannot clear all the\n"
"stones away."

msgctxt "scene:47:125"
msgid ""
"Ich werde mich hier nicht als\n"
"Eisenbahnarbeiter betätigen,\n"
"das ist auch nicht notwendig."
msgstr ""
"I shall not act as a\n"
"railroad worker here,\n"
"that is not necessary."

msgctxt "scene:47:128"
msgid ""
"Dieses Brecheisen ist ungeeig-\n"
"net für Schienenarbeiten."
msgstr ""
"This crowbar is un-\n"
"suitable for railwork."

msgctxt "scene:47:130"
msgid ""
"Die sind viel zu schwach, um\n"
"damit an den Schienen zu ar-\n"
"beiten."
msgstr ""
"Those are far too weak\n"
"to work on the rails\n"
"with them."

msgctxt "scene:47:133"
msgid ""
"Mit den Bohlen, kann ich die\n"
"anderen Bohlen unter den\n"
"Schienen auch nicht hervor-\n"
"schlagen, ich bin ja kein\n"
"Muskelmann."
msgstr ""
"With the planks I cannot knock\n"
"the other planks out from\n"
"under the rails either, I\n"
"am no strongman.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:47:138"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen ist viel zu\n"
"schwach, für Arbeiten an den\n"
"Bohlen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is far too\n"
"weak for work on the\n"
"planks."

msgctxt "scene:47:141"
msgid ""
"Damit bekomme ich die Bohlen\n"
"sicher unter den Schienen her-\n"
"vor, doch ob die dann noch viel\n"
"mehr wie ein Haufen Sägemehl\n"
"sind, wage ich zu bezweifeln."
msgstr ""
"With that I would surely get\n"
"the planks out from under the\n"
"rails, yet whether they are\n"
"then much more than a pile of\n"
"sawdust, I dare to doubt."

msgctxt "scene:47:146"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:47:148"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:47:150"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:48:0"
msgid ""
"Pshaw, das war eine\n"
"ganz schön heftige\n"
"Explosion,da dürfte\n"
"der Geröllhaufen\n"
"schon weggeblasen\n"
"sein."
msgstr ""
"Pshaw, that was a\n"
"rather fierce\n"
"explosion, the\n"
"heap of rubble\n"
"should be blown\n"
"away by now."

msgctxt "scene:48:6"
msgid ""
"Ich möchte die Lore\n"
"auf die Schienen stel-\n"
"len, dazu brauche ich\n"
"aber die Hilfe meines\n"
"Bruders."
msgstr ""
"I would like to place\n"
"the cart onto the\n"
"rails, for that I need\n"
"the help of my\n"
"brother."

msgctxt "scene:48:11"
msgid ""
"Winnetou ist gerne\n"
"bereit seinem weis-\n"
"sen Bruder zu helfen."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou is glad to\n"
"help his pale\n"
"brother."

msgctxt "scene:48:14"
msgid "Etwas später..."
msgstr "A little later..."

msgctxt "scene:48:15"
msgid ""
"Die Balken sollen wohl\n"
"die Decke abstützen."
msgstr ""
"The beams are likely meant to\n"
"support the ceiling."

msgctxt "scene:48:17"
msgid ""
"Eine stabile Konstruktion,\n"
"die sogar ein höheres Gewicht\n"
"als das der Lore, ohne weiteres\n"
"aushalten kann."
msgstr ""
"A sturdy construction that\n"
"can easily withstand a\n"
"weight higher than that\n"
"of the mine cart."

msgctxt "scene:48:21"
msgid ""
"Da geht es weiter in die\n"
"Mine hinein."
msgstr ""
"It leads further into\n"
"the mine there."

msgctxt "scene:48:23"
msgid ""
"Man kann noch die Felswand\n"
"des Berges draussen erken-\n"
"nen."
msgstr ""
"One can still discern\n"
"the rock wall of the\n"
"mountain outside."

msgctxt "scene:48:26"
msgid ""
"Da liegen vom Berg herunter-\n"
"gestürzte Felsblöcke herum."
msgstr ""
"Boulders fallen from the mountain\n"
"lie about there."

msgctxt "scene:48:28"
msgid ""
"Eine umgekippte Lore, die\n"
"wurde sicher verwendet, um\n"
"das Erz aus der Mine zu\n"
"transportieren."
msgstr ""
"An overturned mine cart,\n"
"which was surely used to\n"
"transport the ore out\n"
"of the mine."

msgctxt "scene:48:32"
msgid ""
"Eichenbohlen liegen unter\n"
"den Schienen, um sie zu\n"
"stützen. Es scheint, als\n"
"hätten die Schienen für\n"
"die Ewigkeit gebaut sein\n"
"sollen."
msgstr ""
"Oak planks lie under the\n"
"rails to support them.\n"
"It seems as though the\n"
"rails were meant to be\n"
"built for eternity.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:48:38"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen sind noch gut\n"
"erhalten, sieht man von\n"
"dem bisschen Rost ab, und\n"
"davon, dass einige Bohlen\n"
"fehlen."
msgstr ""
"The rails are still well\n"
"preserved, setting aside\n"
"the bit of rust and the\n"
"fact that a few planks\n"
"are missing."

msgctxt "scene:48:43"
msgid ""
"Oh, die Stütze ist bereits\n"
"durchgebrochen. Ich glaube\n"
"nicht, dass sich der Stol-\n"
"len noch lange hält."
msgstr ""
"Oh, the support is already\n"
"broken through. I do not\n"
"believe that the gallery\n"
"will hold up much longer."

msgctxt "scene:48:47"
msgid ""
"Auf dem Boden liegt überall\n"
"eine Sandschicht. Das müs-\n"
"sen Staubablagerungen von\n"
"den Sprengungen sein."
msgstr ""
"A layer of sand lies\n"
"everywhere on the floor.\n"
"That must be dust deposits\n"
"from the blasting."

msgctxt "scene:48:51"
msgid ""
"Steine liegen in allen\n"
"Grössen herum."
msgstr ""
"Stones of all sizes lie\n"
"about."

msgctxt "scene:48:53"
msgid ""
"Da liegt ein Häufchen loser\n"
"Sand, der wird von der Decke\n"
"heruntergerieselt sein."
msgstr ""
"A small heap of loose sand lies\n"
"there; it must have trickled down\n"
"from the ceiling."

msgctxt "scene:48:56"
msgid ""
"Massiver Felsen, gestützt\n"
"von Balken - doch ich glau-\n"
"be, dass es am stabilen Fel-\n"
"sen liegt, dass hier noch\n"
"alles steht, denn die Stützen\n"
"sehen schon recht morsch aus."
msgstr ""
"Solid rock, supported by\n"
"beams - yet I believe it is\n"
"due to the sturdy rock that\n"
"everything is still standing\n"
"here, for the supports\n"
"already look quite rotten."

msgctxt "scene:48:62"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die Stütze entferne,\n"
"oder auch nur berühre, riskiere\n"
"ich, dass hier alles einstürzt."
msgstr ""
"If I remove the support or even\n"
"touch it, I risk having everything\n"
"collapse here."

msgctxt "scene:48:65"
msgid ""
"Die sind zu gross, um wegge-\n"
"tragen zu werden."
msgstr ""
"They are too large to be\n"
"carried away."

msgctxt "scene:48:67"
msgid ""
"Die müsste erst einmal auf die\n"
"Schienen gestellt werden,\n"
"bevor man mit ihr etwas an-\n"
"fangen kann."
msgstr ""
"It would first have to be\n"
"placed onto the rails\n"
"before one could accomplish\n"
"anything with it."

msgctxt "scene:48:71"
msgid ""
"Ich habe kein Werkzeug, um\n"
"die Bohlen unter den Schie-\n"
"nen hervorzuholen."
msgstr ""
"I have no tools to get the\n"
"planks out from under\n"
"the rails."

msgctxt "scene:48:74"
msgid ""
"Ohne das richtige Werkzeug,\n"
"kann man die Schienen nicht\n"
"von den Bohlen lösen."
msgstr ""
"Without the proper tools,\n"
"one cannot loosen the\n"
"rails from the planks."

msgctxt "scene:48:77"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die entferne,\n"
"stürzt sicher alles ein."
msgstr ""
"If I remove those, everything\n"
"will surely collapse."

msgctxt "scene:48:79"
msgid ""
"Die Steine sind nur un-\n"
"nötiger Ballast."
msgstr ""
"The stones are only\n"
"unnecessary ballast."

msgctxt "scene:48:81"
msgid ""
"Von Hand kann ich hier nichts\n"
"ausrichten, das ist massiver\n"
"Felsen."
msgstr ""
"By hand I can accomplish\n"
"nothing here, that is\n"
"solid rock."

msgctxt "scene:48:84"
msgid ""
"Den Flaschenzug lasse ich mal\n"
"stehen, jetzt brauche ich ihn\n"
"nicht, und sollte ich ihn spä-\n"
"ter brauchen, so kann ich ihn\n"
"noch immer holen."
msgstr ""
"I shall leave the tackle\n"
"block standing, right now I\n"
"do not need it, and should I\n"
"need it later, I can still\n"
"fetch it."

msgctxt "scene:48:89"
msgid ""
"An der Lore, kann ich damit\n"
"nichts ausrichten."
msgstr ""
"With that I can accomplish\n"
"nothing at the mine cart."

msgctxt "scene:48:91"
msgid ""
"Wozu den Sand in die Lore \n"
"schütten, das ist ja kein\n"
"Erz, und ich kein Bergwerks-\n"
"arbeiter."
msgstr ""
"Why pour the sand into\n"
"the cart; that is no\n"
"ore, and I am no miner.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:48:95"
msgid ""
"Die Lore ist aus Metall, und\n"
"brennt nicht."
msgstr ""
"The cart is made of metal\n"
"and does not burn."

msgctxt "scene:48:97"
msgid ""
"Ich werde mich hier nicht als\n"
"Eisenbahnarbeiter betätigen,\n"
"das ist auch nicht notwendig."
msgstr ""
"I shall not act as a\n"
"railroad worker here,\n"
"that is not necessary."

msgctxt "scene:48:100"
msgid ""
"Dieses Brecheisen ist ungeeignet\n"
"für Schienenarbeiten."
msgstr ""
"This crowbar is unsuitable\n"
"for railwork."

msgctxt "scene:48:102"
msgid ""
"Die sind viel zu schwach, um damit\n"
"an den Schienen zu arbeiten."
msgstr ""
"Those are far too weak\n"
"to work on the rails."

msgctxt "scene:48:104"
msgid ""
"Mit den Bohlen, kann ich die an-\n"
"deren Bohlen unter den Schienen\n"
"auch nicht hervorschlagen, ich\n"
"bin ja kein Muskelmann."
msgstr ""
"With the planks I cannot knock\n"
"the other planks out from under\n"
"the rails either; I am no\n"
"strongman."

msgctxt "scene:48:108"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen, ist viel zu\n"
"schwach für Arbeiten an den\n"
"Bohlen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is far too weak\n"
"for work on the planks.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:48:111"
msgid ""
"Damit bekomme ich die Bohlen\n"
"sicher unter den Schienen her-\n"
"vor, doch ob die dann noch viel\n"
"mehr wie ein Haufen Sägemehl\n"
"sind, wage ich zu bezweifeln."
msgstr ""
"With that I would surely get\n"
"the planks out from under the\n"
"rails, yet whether they are\n"
"then much more than a pile of\n"
"sawdust, I dare to doubt."

msgctxt "scene:48:116"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:48:118"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:48:120"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:48:122"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"For such work the crowbar is\n"
"too weak."

msgctxt "scene:48:124"
msgid ""
"Damit sprenge ich jede Felswand,\n"
"doch die Folgen, die eine solche\n"
"Explosion haben könnte, muss man\n"
"vorher bedenken."
msgstr ""
"With that I'll blast any rock\n"
"wall, yet the consequences of\n"
"such an explosion must be\n"
"considered beforehand."

msgctxt "scene:48:128"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten denk-\n"
"bar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely unsuitable\n"
"for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:48:130"
msgid ""
"Für Ackerbau haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"For agriculture we do not have\n"
"the necessary time right now."

msgctxt "scene:48:132"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow up the\n"
"ground here?"

msgctxt "scene:49:0"
msgid ""
"In der Hütte liegt ja noch ein\n"
"Haken eines alten Flaschenzuges."
msgstr ""
"In the hut there is still a hook\n"
"from an old tackle block."

msgctxt "scene:49:2"
msgid ""
"In der Hütte, ist ausser Spinnen-\n"
"netze und viel Staub, nichts zu\n"
"finden."
msgstr ""
"In the hut, apart from cobwebs\n"
"and much dust, nothing is to\n"
"be found."

msgctxt "scene:49:5"
msgid ""
"Massiver Felsen, und trotz-\n"
"dem haben die Bergleute\n"
"auch diesen Teil gross-\n"
"zügig ausgebaut. Es kann\n"
"natürlich sein, dass sie den\n"
"Verlauf der Silberader\n"
"verloren hatten, und suchen\n"
"mussten."
msgstr ""
"Solid rock, and yet the miners\n"
"expanded this part generously\n"
"as well. It may of course be\n"
"that they had lost the course\n"
"of the silver vein and had\n"
"to search for it.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:13"
msgid ""
"Die Stütze sieht nicht\n"
"sehr stabil aus."
msgstr ""
"The support does not look\n"
"very sturdy."

msgctxt "scene:49:15"
msgid ""
"Ein Brett wurde quer über\n"
"den Hütteneingang genagelt.\n"
"Das wird aber niemanden\n"
"aufhalten."
msgstr ""
"A board was nailed across the\n"
"entrance of the hut. Yet that\n"
"won't hold anyone back.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:19"
msgid ""
"Eine Holzhütte. Die wurde\n"
"wohl früher als Lager-\n"
"schuppen verwendet. Sieht\n"
"recht wackelig aus."
msgstr ""
"A wooden hut. It was likely\n"
"used as a storage shed in\n"
"earlier times. Looks quite\n"
"shaky."

msgctxt "scene:49:23"
msgid ""
"Absolut duster in der Hütte,\n"
"doch soweit ich das sehe, ist\n"
"hier nichts, ausser Staub und\n"
"Steinen zu holen."
msgstr ""
"Pitch dark in the hut, yet as\n"
"far as I can see, there is\n"
"nothing to be got here, except\n"
"dust and stones."

msgctxt "scene:49:27"
msgid ""
"Felsen und die Schienen,\n"
"führen genau bis hin..."
msgstr ""
"Rocks and the rails lead\n"
"right up to them..."

msgctxt "scene:49:29"
msgid ""
"Betrachtet man den Felsen\n"
"vor den Schienen etwas ge-\n"
"nauer, so erscheint er mir\n"
"schon etwas eigenartig zu\n"
"sein."
msgstr ""
"If one examines the rock in\n"
"front of the rails a bit more\n"
"closely, it appears quite\n"
"peculiar to me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:34"
msgid ""
"Es liegen überall Steine he-\n"
"rum, die sind sicherlich\n"
"von der Decke gefallen."
msgstr ""
"Stones lie about everywhere;\n"
"they surely fell down from the\n"
"ceiling."

msgctxt "scene:49:37"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen scheinen gerade-\n"
"wegs im Berg zu verschwinden."
msgstr ""
"The rails seem to disappear\n"
"straight into the mountain."

msgctxt "scene:49:39"
msgid ""
"Es wäre vielleicht ange-\n"
"bracht, die Sache näher\n"
"zu untersuchen..."
msgstr ""
"It might perhaps be appropriate\n"
"to investigate the matter\n"
"further..."

msgctxt "scene:49:42"
msgid ""
"Die Bohlen unter den Schie-\n"
"nen scheinen auch nicht mehr\n"
"die Besten zu sein, würden\n"
"aber sicher noch eine Weile\n"
"halten."
msgstr ""
"The planks under the rails do\n"
"not seem to be the best any\n"
"longer either, yet would surely\n"
"hold for a while yet.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:47"
msgid ""
"Die Bohlen waren wohl als\n"
"Stützen gedacht, sie sehen\n"
"noch recht gut erhalten aus."
msgstr ""
"The planks were likely meant as\n"
"supports; they still look fairly\n"
"well preserved."

msgctxt "scene:49:50"
msgid ""
"Der gesamte Boden ist von\n"
"Sprengstaub bedeckt."
msgstr ""
"The entire ground is covered\n"
"with blasting dust."

msgctxt "scene:49:52"
msgid ""
"Geborstene, morsche Stützen,\n"
"die zu nichts mehr gebraucht\n"
"werden können."
msgstr ""
"Burst, rotten supports that\n"
"can no longer be used for\n"
"anything."

msgctxt "scene:49:55"
msgid ""
"Keine Chance, ohne Werkzeuge\n"
"an diesem massiven Felsen\n"
"etwas auszurichten."
msgstr ""
"No chance of accomplishing\n"
"anything at this solid rock\n"
"without tools."

msgctxt "scene:49:58"
msgid ""
"Die Stütze zu entfernen,\n"
"wäre ein folgenschwerer\n"
"Fehler."
msgstr ""
"Removing the support would be\n"
"a mistake of grave\n"
"consequences."

msgctxt "scene:49:61"
msgid ""
"Das Brett zu entfernen,\n"
"wäre sicherlich leicht,\n"
"doch die Hütte würde bei\n"
"der kleinsten Berührung\n"
"zusammenfallen."
msgstr ""
"Removing the board would\n"
"surely be easy, yet the hut\n"
"would collapse at the\n"
"slightest touch.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:66"
msgid ""
"Ich will mich ja hier nicht\n"
"niederlassen..."
msgstr ""
"I have no intention of\n"
"settling down here..."

msgctxt "scene:49:68"
msgid ""
"So lebensmüde bin ich nicht,\n"
"dass ich die Hütte betreten\n"
"würde."
msgstr ""
"I am not so weary of life\n"
"that I would enter the\n"
"hut."

msgctxt "scene:49:71"
msgid ""
"Nein, ohne das richtige Werk-\n"
"zeug, lässt sich wirklich nicht\n"
"viel ausrichten."
msgstr ""
"No, without the proper tools\n"
"not much can really be\n"
"accomplished."

msgctxt "scene:49:74"
msgid ""
"Ach, die wären doch nur un-\n"
"nötiger Ballast."
msgstr ""
"Ah, those would only be\n"
"unnecessary ballast."

msgctxt "scene:49:76"
msgid ""
"Die wären für mich zu schwer,\n"
"zudem habe ich nicht das Werk-\n"
"zeug, um sie zu entfernen."
msgstr ""
"Those would be too heavy for me;\n"
"besides, I do not have the tools\n"
"to remove them."

msgctxt "scene:49:79"
msgid ""
"Die wurden mühsam unter die\n"
"Schienen gelegt und nun soll\n"
"ich die wieder hervorholen.\n"
"Ich würde das auch tun, wenn\n"
"ich das Werkzeug dazu hätte."
msgstr ""
"They were painstakingly laid under\n"
"the rails, and now I am to get\n"
"them out again. I would do so,\n"
"too, if I had the tools for\n"
"it."

msgctxt "scene:49:84"
msgid ""
"Die könnte man nur noch\n"
"als Brennholz verwerten,\n"
"und das brauche ich jetzt\n"
"nicht."
msgstr ""
"Those could only be used as\n"
"firewood now, and I do not\n"
"need that right now.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:88"
msgid ""
"Das Brett anzuzünden, wäre\n"
"keine gute Idee."
msgstr ""
"Lighting the board would\n"
"be no good idea."

msgctxt "scene:49:90"
msgid ""
"In die Hütte zu leuchten, ist\n"
"ja O.K., aber sie gleich nieder-\n"
"zubrennen, finde ich etwas dras-\n"
"tisch. Auch wäre die Rauchent-\n"
"wicklung für Winnetou und mich\n"
"sehr gefährlich."
msgstr ""
"Shining a light into the hut is fine,\n"
"yet burning it down outright I find\n"
"somewhat drastic. Also, the smoke\n"
"development would be very dangerous\n"
"for Winnetou and me.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:96"
msgid ""
"Da liegt ja eine unbenutzte\n"
"Fackel."
msgstr ""
"Why, an unused torch is\n"
"lying there."

msgctxt "scene:49:98"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja ein Brecheisen,\n"
"wie es oft benutzt wird,\n"
"um Transportkisten auf-\n"
"zustemmen."
msgstr ""
"Why, there is a crowbar, such\n"
"as is often used to pry open\n"
"transport crates.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:49:102"
msgid ""
"Ich werde mich hier nicht als\n"
"Eisenbahnarbeiter betätigen,\n"
"das ist auch nicht notwendig."
msgstr ""
"I shall not act as a railroad\n"
"worker here; that is not\n"
"necessary either."

msgctxt "scene:49:105"
msgid ""
"Dieses Brecheisen ist ungeeignet\n"
"für Schienenarbeiten."
msgstr ""
"This crowbar is unsuitable\n"
"for railwork."

msgctxt "scene:49:107"
msgid ""
"Die sind viel zu schwach, um damit\n"
"an den Schienen zu arbeiten."
msgstr ""
"Those are far too weak to work\n"
"on the rails with them."

msgctxt "scene:49:109"
msgid ""
"Mit den Bohlen, kann ich die an-\n"
"deren Bohlen unter den Schienen\n"
"auch nicht hervorschlagen, ich\n"
"bin ja kein Muskelmann."
msgstr ""
"With the planks I cannot knock\n"
"the other planks out from under\n"
"the rails either; I am no\n"
"strongman."

msgctxt "scene:49:113"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen ist viel zu\n"
"schwach, für Arbeiten an den\n"
"Bohlen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is far\n"
"too weak for work\n"
"on the planks."

msgctxt "scene:49:116"
msgid ""
"Damit bekomme ich die Bohlen\n"
"sicher unter den Schienen hervor,\n"
"doch ob die dann noch viel mehr\n"
"wie ein Haufen Sägemehl sind, wage\n"
"ich zu bezweifeln."
msgstr ""
"With that I would surely get\n"
"the planks out from under the\n"
"rails, yet whether they would\n"
"then be much more than a pile\n"
"of sawdust, I dare to doubt."

msgctxt "scene:49:121"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak\n"
"for such work..."

msgctxt "scene:49:123"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak\n"
"for such work..."

msgctxt "scene:49:125"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak\n"
"for such work..."

msgctxt "scene:49:127"
msgid ""
"Die Wände mit den Bohlen abzu-\n"
"stützen, wäre Wasser in den Fluss\n"
"tragen..."
msgstr ""
"Propping the walls with\n"
"planks would be carrying\n"
"water to the river..."

msgctxt "scene:49:130"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"For such work the\n"
"crowbar is too weak."

msgctxt "scene:49:132"
msgid ""
"Damit sprenge ich jeden Felsen,\n"
"doch die Folgen, die eine solche\n"
"Explosion haben könnte, muss man\n"
"vorher bedenken."
msgstr ""
"With that I'll blast any rock,\n"
"yet the consequences such an\n"
"explosion might have must be\n"
"considered beforehand."

msgctxt "scene:49:136"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten denk-\n"
"bar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely\n"
"unsuitable for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:49:138"
msgid ""
"Für Ackerbau, haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"For agriculture we do not have\n"
"the necessary time right now."

msgctxt "scene:49:140"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow\n"
"up the ground here?"

msgctxt "scene:49:142"
msgid ""
"Die Hütte stört dort niemanden,\n"
"also warum zerstören."
msgstr ""
"The hut bothers no one\n"
"there, so why destroy it."

msgctxt "scene:49:144"
msgid ""
"Ich habe nicht vor, hier einzu-\n"
"ziehen, und mir vorher das Bad\n"
"auszukacheln."
msgstr ""
"I do not intend to\n"
"move in here and tile\n"
"the bathroom first."

msgctxt "scene:49:147"
msgid ""
"Damit, könnte ich höchstens Ver-\n"
"zierungen in die Bretter schnitzen."
msgstr ""
"With that I could at best carve\n"
"ornaments into the boards."

msgctxt "scene:49:149"
msgid ""
"Die Wände mit den Bohlen abzu-\n"
"stützen, wäre Wasser in den Fluss\n"
"tragen..."
msgstr ""
"Propping the walls with\n"
"planks would be carrying\n"
"water to the river..."

msgctxt "scene:49:152"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das Brech-\n"
"eisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"For such work the\n"
"crowbar is too weak."

msgctxt "scene:49:154"
msgid ""
"Damit sprenge ich jeden Felsen,\n"
"doch die Folgen, die eine solche\n"
"Explosion haben könnte, muss man\n"
"vorher bedenken."
msgstr ""
"With that I'll blast any rock,\n"
"yet the consequences such an\n"
"explosion might have must be\n"
"considered beforehand."

msgctxt "scene:49:158"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten denk-\n"
"bar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely\n"
"unsuitable for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:50:0"
msgid ""
"Ist ausser Staub, und viel-\n"
"leicht noch verlorene Wunsch-\n"
"träume der Minenarbeiter,\n"
"nichts mehr zu finden?"
msgstr ""
"Is there nothing left to find\n"
"except dust and perhaps lost\n"
"daydreams of the miners\n"
"anymore?"

msgctxt "scene:50:4"
msgid ""
"Massiver Felsen, und trotz-\n"
"dem haben die Bergleute\n"
"auch diesen Teil gross-\n"
"zügig ausgebaut. Es kann\n"
"natürlich sein, dass sie den\n"
"Verlauf der Silberader\n"
"verloren hatten, und suchen\n"
"mussten."
msgstr ""
"Solid rock, and yet the miners\n"
"expanded this part generously\n"
"as well. It may of course be\n"
"that they had lost the course\n"
"of the silver vein and had\n"
"to search for it.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:12"
msgid ""
"Die Stütze sieht nicht\n"
"sehr stabil aus."
msgstr ""
"The support does not\n"
"look very sturdy."

msgctxt "scene:50:14"
msgid ""
"Ein Brett wurde quer über\n"
"den Hütteneingang genagelt.\n"
"Das wird aber niemanden\n"
"aufhalten."
msgstr ""
"A board was nailed across\n"
"the entrance of the hut.\n"
"Yet that won't hold\n"
"anyone back."

msgctxt "scene:50:18"
msgid ""
"Eine Holzhütte, die wurde\n"
"wohl früher als Lager-\n"
"schuppen verwendet. Sieht\n"
"recht wacklig aus."
msgstr ""
"A wooden hut, it was likely\n"
"used as a storage shed in\n"
"earlier times. Looks\n"
"quite shaky."

msgctxt "scene:50:22"
msgid ""
"Die Bohlen unter den Schie-\n"
"nen scheinen auch nicht mehr\n"
"die Besten zu sein, würden\n"
"aber sicher noch eine Weile\n"
"halten."
msgstr ""
"The planks under the rails do\n"
"not seem to be the best any\n"
"longer either, yet would surely\n"
"hold for a while yet.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:27"
msgid ""
"Der gesamte Boden ist von\n"
"Sprengstaub bedeckt."
msgstr ""
"The entire ground is\n"
"covered with blasting dust."

msgctxt "scene:50:29"
msgid ""
"Geborstene, morsche Stützen,\n"
"die zu nichts mehr gebraucht\n"
"werden können."
msgstr ""
"Burst, rotten supports that\n"
"can no longer be used for\n"
"anything."

msgctxt "scene:50:32"
msgid ""
"Die Schienen sind noch in\n"
"relativ gutem Zustand - was\n"
"wir jetzt bewiesen hätten."
msgstr ""
"The rails are still in fairly\n"
"good condition - as we have\n"
"just proven."

msgctxt "scene:50:35"
msgid ""
"Keine Chance, ohne Werkzeug\n"
"an diesem massiven Felsen\n"
"etwas auszurichten."
msgstr ""
"No chance of accomplishing\n"
"anything at this solid rock\n"
"without tools."

msgctxt "scene:50:38"
msgid ""
"Die Stütze zu entfernen,\n"
"wäre ein folgenschwerer\n"
"Fehler."
msgstr ""
"Removing the support would\n"
"be a mistake of grave\n"
"consequences."

msgctxt "scene:50:41"
msgid ""
"Das Brett zu entfernen,\n"
"wäre sicherlich leicht,\n"
"doch die Hütte würde bei\n"
"der kleinsten Berührung\n"
"zusammenfallen."
msgstr ""
"Removing the board would\n"
"surely be easy, yet the hut\n"
"would collapse at the\n"
"slightest touch.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:46"
msgid ""
"Ich will mich ja hier nicht\n"
"niederlassen..."
msgstr ""
"I have no intention of\n"
"settling down here..."

msgctxt "scene:50:48"
msgid ""
"So lebensmüde bin ich nicht,\n"
"dass ich die Hütte betreten\n"
"würde."
msgstr ""
"I am not so weary of life\n"
"that I would enter the\n"
"hut."

msgctxt "scene:50:51"
msgid ""
"Ach die wären doch nur un-\n"
"nötiger Ballast."
msgstr ""
"Ah, those would only be\n"
"unnecessary ballast."

msgctxt "scene:50:53"
msgid ""
"Die wären für mich zu schwer,\n"
"zudem habe ich nicht das Werk-\n"
"zeug, um sie zu entfernen."
msgstr ""
"Those would be too heavy for\n"
"me; besides, I do not have the\n"
"tools to remove them."

msgctxt "scene:50:56"
msgid ""
"Die wurden mühsam unter die\n"
"Schienen gelegt, und nun soll\n"
"ich die wieder hervorholen.\n"
"Ich würde das auch tun, wenn\n"
"ich das Werkzeug dazu hätte."
msgstr ""
"They were painstakingly laid\n"
"under the rails, and now I am to\n"
"get them out again. I would do\n"
"so, too, if I had the tools\n"
"for it."

msgctxt "scene:50:61"
msgid ""
"Die könnte man nur noch\n"
"als Brennholz verwerten,\n"
"und das brauche ich jetzt\n"
"nicht."
msgstr ""
"Those could only be used\n"
"as firewood now, and I do\n"
"not need that right now.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:65"
msgid ""
"Das Brett anzuzünden, wäre\n"
"keine gute Idee."
msgstr ""
"Lighting the board would\n"
"be no good idea."

msgctxt "scene:50:67"
msgid ""
"In die Hütte zu leuchten ist\n"
"ja O.K., aber sie gleich nieder-\n"
"zubrennen, finde ich etwas dras-\n"
"tisch. Auch wäre die Rauchent-\n"
"wicklung für Winnetou und mich\n"
"sehr gefährlich."
msgstr ""
"Shining a light into the hut is\n"
"fine, yet burning it down outright\n"
"I find somewhat drastic. Also,\n"
"the smoke development would be\n"
"very dangerous for Winnetou and\n"
"me."

msgctxt "scene:50:73"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja ein Brecheisen,\n"
"wie es oft benutzt wird,\n"
"um Transportkisten auf-\n"
"zustemmen."
msgstr ""
"Why, there is a crowbar, such\n"
"as is often used to pry open\n"
"transport crates.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:77"
msgid ""
"Da schaut noch ein Stück\n"
"von der Lore aus dem Geröll."
msgstr ""
"A piece of the cart still\n"
"sticks out from the rubble."

msgctxt "scene:50:79"
msgid ""
"Da ist hinter der einge-\n"
"stürzten Wand noch ein\n"
"weiterer Raum."
msgstr ""
"Behind the collapsed wall\n"
"there is another room.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:82"
msgid ""
"Da schaut noch ein Stück\n"
"eines abgebrochenen Bal-\n"
"kens aus dem Geröll."
msgstr ""
"A piece of a broken beam\n"
"still sticks out from the\n"
"rubble."

msgctxt "scene:50:85"
msgid ""
"Die eingestürzte Mauer, hat\n"
"einen ganz schönen Schutt-\n"
"haufen hinterlassen."
msgstr ""
"The collapsed wall left\n"
"quite a heap of rubble\n"
"behind."

msgctxt "scene:50:88"
msgid ""
"Das Holz lässt sich nur noch\n"
"als Brennholz verwenden, doch\n"
"dafür den Aufwand betreiben,\n"
"und es aus dem Schutt aus-\n"
"graben, lohnt sich nicht."
msgstr ""
"The wood can only be used as\n"
"firewood now, yet making the\n"
"effort to dig it out of the\n"
"rubble is not worth it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:50:93"
msgid ""
"Es kann nicht ernst gemeint\n"
"sein, die Lore da ausgraben\n"
"zu wollen, die wird ja völ-\n"
"lig kaputt sein."
msgstr ""
"It cannot be meant in earnest\n"
"to want to dig out the cart\n"
"there; why, it must be\n"
"completely broken."

msgctxt "scene:50:97"
msgid ""
"Das Geröll kann ich ohne Werk-\n"
"zeug nicht wegräumen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot clear the rubble\n"
"away without tools."

msgctxt "scene:50:99"
msgid ""
"Ich werde mich hier nicht als\n"
"Eisenbahnarbeiter betätigen,\n"
"das ist auch nicht notwendig."
msgstr ""
"I shall not act as a\n"
"railroad worker here; that\n"
"is not necessary either."

msgctxt "scene:50:102"
msgid ""
"Dieses Brecheisen ist ungeeignet\n"
"für Schienenarbeiten."
msgstr ""
"This crowbar is unsuitable\n"
"for railwork."

msgctxt "scene:50:104"
msgid ""
"Die sind viel zu schwach, um damit\n"
"an den Schienen zu arbeiten."
msgstr ""
"Those are far too weak to\n"
"work on the rails with them."

msgctxt "scene:50:106"
msgid ""
"Mit den Bohlen, kann ich die an-\n"
"deren Bohlen unter den Schienen\n"
"auch nicht hervorschlagen, ich\n"
"bin ja kein Muskelmann."
msgstr ""
"With the planks I cannot knock\n"
"the other planks out from\n"
"under the rails either; I\n"
"am no strongman."

msgctxt "scene:50:110"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen ist viel zu schwach\n"
"für Arbeiten an den Bohlen."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is far too weak\n"
"for work on the planks."

msgctxt "scene:50:112"
msgid ""
"Damit bekomme ich die Bohlen\n"
"sicher unter den Schienen her-\n"
"vor, doch ob die dann noch viel\n"
"mehr wie ein Haufen Sägemehl\n"
"sind, wage ich zu bezweifeln."
msgstr ""
"With that I would surely get\n"
"the planks out from under the\n"
"rails, yet whether they are\n"
"then much more than a pile of\n"
"sawdust, I dare to doubt."

msgctxt "scene:50:117"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:50:119"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:50:121"
msgid ""
"Das Werkzeug ist zu schwach für\n"
"solche Arbeiten..."
msgstr ""
"The tool is too weak for\n"
"such work..."

msgctxt "scene:50:123"
msgid ""
"Die Wände, mit den Bohlen abzu-\n"
"stützen, wäre Wasser in den Fluss\n"
"tragen..."
msgstr ""
"Propping the walls with\n"
"planks would be carrying\n"
"water to the river..."

msgctxt "scene:50:126"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"For such work the crowbar is\n"
"too weak."

msgctxt "scene:50:128"
msgid ""
"Damit sprenge ich jeden Felsen,\n"
"doch die Folgen, die eine solche\n"
"Explosion haben könnte, muss man\n"
"vorher bedenken."
msgstr ""
"With that I'll blast any rock,\n"
"yet the consequences of such an\n"
"explosion must be considered\n"
"beforehand."

msgctxt "scene:50:132"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten denk-\n"
"bar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely unsuitable\n"
"for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:50:134"
msgid ""
"Für Ackerbau, haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"For agriculture we do not have\n"
"the necessary time right now."

msgctxt "scene:50:136"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow up the\n"
"ground here?"

msgctxt "scene:50:138"
msgid ""
"Die Hütte stört dort niemanden,\n"
"also warum zerstören."
msgstr ""
"The hut bothers no one\n"
"there, so why destroy it."

msgctxt "scene:50:140"
msgid ""
"Ich habe nicht vor, hier einzu-\n"
"ziehen, und mir vorher das Bad\n"
"auszukacheln."
msgstr ""
"I do not intend to move in\n"
"here and tile the bathroom\n"
"first."

msgctxt "scene:50:143"
msgid ""
"Damit, könnte ich höchstens Ver-\n"
"zierungen in die Bretter schnitzen."
msgstr ""
"With that I could at best carve\n"
"ornaments into the boards."

msgctxt "scene:50:145"
msgid ""
"Das würde helfen, die verklemm-\n"
"ten Brocken zu lösen, doch\n"
"damit kann ich nicht den Haufen\n"
"wegschaffen."
msgstr ""
"That would help to loosen the\n"
"jammed chunks, yet with that\n"
"I cannot clear the pile\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:50:149"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tun würde, dann wäre\n"
"vom Berg und mir nichts mehr da,\n"
"denn da hinten lagert ja das\n"
"ganze Dynamit."
msgstr ""
"If I were to do that, nothing\n"
"would be left of the mountain\n"
"and me, for all the dynamite\n"
"is stored back there."

msgctxt "scene:51:0"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich denn mit dem\n"
"Brecheisen in den Dynamit-\n"
"stangen? Ich habe dabei nur\n"
"gute Chancen, dass das\n"
"ganze Zeug in die Luft\n"
"geht..."
msgstr ""
"What am I supposed to do with the\n"
"crowbar in the dynamite sticks?\n"
"I stand a good chance that the\n"
"whole business will blow up into\n"
"the air...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:6"
msgid ""
"Von Hand, kriege ich die Kiste\n"
"nicht auf, und zum Tragen ist\n"
"sie zu schwer. Zudem brauche\n"
"ich nur eine Stange Dynamit,\n"
"ich muss ja nicht den ganzen\n"
"Berg wegsprengen."
msgstr ""
"By hand I cannot pry open the crate,\n"
"and it is too heavy to carry. Besides,\n"
"I need but one stick of dynamite;\n"
"I need not blast away the whole\n"
"mountain.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:12"
msgid ""
"Die Kiste ist noch zu wenig\n"
"geöffnet, ich bekomme die\n"
"Dynamitstange nicht heraus."
msgstr ""
"The crate is not opened enough yet;\n"
"I cannot get the stick of dynamite\n"
"out."

msgctxt "scene:51:15"
msgid ""
"Ich brauche momentan nicht mehr\n"
"Dynamit, und ich möchte das Zeug\n"
"nicht einfach mit mir herum-\n"
"tragen und dabei riskieren,\n"
"dass plötzlich, nach einem\n"
"lauten Kracher, nur noch die\n"
"Stiefel von mir da stehen."
msgstr ""
"I do not need more dynamite at present,\n"
"and I do not wish to carry the stuff\n"
"about with me and risk that suddenly,\n"
"after a loud bang, only my boots remain\n"
"standing there.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:22"
msgid ""
"Ein richtiger Raum wurde hier\n"
"in den Felsen gehauen. Da es\n"
"trocken ist, ist das Gewölbe\n"
"ideal zum Einlagern von Spreng-\n"
"stoff."
msgstr ""
"A proper room was hewn into the rock\n"
"here. Since it is dry, the vault is\n"
"ideal for storing explosives.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:27"
msgid ""
"In der Mine ist wegen der\n"
"schummrigen Beleuchtung, alles\n"
"nur schemenhaft zu erkennen."
msgstr ""
"In the mine, due to the dim lighting,\n"
"everything can only be discerned\n"
"shadowy."

msgctxt "scene:51:30"
msgid ""
"Ein gebrochener Balken, muss\n"
"muss wohl beim Einsturz der\n"
"Wand gebrochen sein."
msgstr ""
"A broken beam; must have broken\n"
"when the wall collapsed.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:33"
msgid ""
"Heavens, da liegt ja genug\n"
"Dynamit um den gesamten Berg\n"
"nach Mexico zu blasen."
msgstr ""
"Heavens, there is enough dynamite\n"
"lying there to blow the whole mountain\n"
"to Mexico."

msgctxt "scene:51:36"
msgid "Eine einzelne Kiste Dynamit."
msgstr "A single crate of dynamite."

msgctxt "scene:51:37"
msgid ""
"Ein felsiger Boden, der\n"
"leicht mit Staub bedeckt\n"
"ist."
msgstr ""
"A rocky floor that is\n"
"lightly covered with\n"
"dust."

msgctxt "scene:51:40"
msgid ""
"Ein Haufen Geröll ist von der\n"
"eingestürzten Mauer übrig ge-\n"
"blieben."
msgstr ""
"A heap of rubble remains\n"
"from the collapsed wall.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:43"
msgid ""
"Von der Wand, kann ich nichts\n"
"nehmen, der Stein ist zu\n"
"hart."
msgstr ""
"From the wall I can take\n"
"nothing; the stone is too\n"
"hard."

msgctxt "scene:51:46"
msgid ""
"Den zerborstenen Balken, kann\n"
"man nur noch als Brennholz\n"
"verwenden."
msgstr ""
"The shattered beam can\n"
"only be used as firewood\n"
"anymore."

msgctxt "scene:51:49"
msgid ""
"Heavens, an denen sollte ich\n"
"nicht zu viel herumtun, ich\n"
"riskiere nur, dass alles ex-\n"
"plodiert. Gelagerte Dynamit-\n"
"stangen, können schwitzen und\n"
"Nitroglyzerin ausscheiden..."
msgstr ""
"Heavens, I should not meddle\n"
"too much with those, I only\n"
"risk having everything explode.\n"
"Stored dynamite sticks can\n"
"sweat and exude nitro-\n"
"glycerin..."

msgctxt "scene:51:55"
msgid ""
"Es gibt nichts, was man auf-\n"
"heben könnte..."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing that one\n"
"could pick up..."

msgctxt "scene:51:57"
msgid ""
"Den Haufen Geröll von Hand\n"
"wegzuschaffen, würde Jahre\n"
"dauern."
msgstr ""
"Clearing away the pile of\n"
"rubble by hand would take\n"
"years."

msgctxt "scene:51:60"
msgid ""
"Das würde helfen, die verklemm-\n"
"ten Brocken zu lösen, doch\n"
"damit kann ich nicht den Haufen\n"
"wegschaffen."
msgstr ""
"That would help to loosen the\n"
"jammed chunks, yet with that I\n"
"cannot clear the pile away.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:51:64"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tun würde, dann\n"
"wäre vom Berg und mir nichts\n"
"mehr da, denn hier lagert ja\n"
"das ganze Dynamit."
msgstr ""
"If I were to do that, nothing\n"
"would be left of the mountain\n"
"and me, for all the dynamite\n"
"is stored here."

msgctxt "scene:51:68"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"For such work the crowbar\n"
"is too weak."

msgctxt "scene:51:70"
msgid ""
"Damit sprenge ich jeden Felsen,\n"
"doch die Folgen, die eine solche\n"
"Explosion haben könnte, muss man\n"
"vorher bedenken."
msgstr ""
"With that I'll blast any rock,\n"
"yet the consequences such an\n"
"explosion might have must be\n"
"considered beforehand."

msgctxt "scene:51:74"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten\n"
"denkbar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely\n"
"unsuitable for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:51:76"
msgid ""
"Für Ackerbau, haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"For agriculture we do not have\n"
"the necessary time right now."

msgctxt "scene:51:78"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow up the\n"
"ground here?"

msgctxt "scene:51:80"
msgid ""
"So wie die Kisten stehen,\n"
"suche ich mir lieber eine,\n"
"die etwas günstiger steht,\n"
"denn wenn da eine beim Han-\n"
"tieren herunterfällt, kann ich\n"
"den irdischen Genüssen\n"
"entsagen."
msgstr ""
"The way the crates stand, I'd\n"
"rather look for one that is\n"
"placed a bit more favorably,\n"
"for if one falls while handling\n"
"it, I can renounce earthly\n"
"pleasures.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:0"
msgid ""
"Diesen Balken zu ver-\n"
"schieben, war ein schö-\n"
"nes Stück Arbeit."
msgstr ""
"Shifting this beam was\n"
"quite a fine piece of\n"
"work."

msgctxt "scene:52:3"
msgid ""
"Ja dieser Balken war\n"
"sehr schwer, doch wenn\n"
"zwei zusammenarbeiten,\n"
"können sie die Arbeit\n"
"von Vielen tun."
msgstr ""
"Yes, this beam was very\n"
"heavy, yet when two work\n"
"together, they can do\n"
"the work of many.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:8"
msgid ""
"Wir müssten zu Dritt sein,\n"
"um die Mechanik auszulösen."
msgstr ""
"There would need to be three\n"
"of us to trigger the mechanism."

msgctxt "scene:52:10"
msgid ""
"Kann mein Bruder\n"
"sich auf die dritte\n"
"Platte stellen?"
msgstr ""
"Can my brother stand\n"
"upon the third\n"
"plate?"

msgctxt "scene:52:13"
msgid ""
"Wenn mir mein Bruder\n"
"die Fackel gibt, kann\n"
"ich den Raum damit er-\n"
"hellen, und Firehand\n"
"hat beide Hände frei."
msgstr ""
"If my brother gives me the\n"
"torch, I can illuminate the\n"
"room with it, and Firehand\n"
"will have both hands free.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:18"
msgid ""
"Das Tor ist bereits\n"
"auf."
msgstr ""
"The gate is already\n"
"open."

msgctxt "scene:52:20"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht,\n"
"dass ich die Platten\n"
"nehmen kann!"
msgstr ""
"I do not believe\n"
"that I can take the\n"
"plates!"

msgctxt "scene:52:23"
msgid ""
"Die Deckenstützen sehen\n"
"nicht gerade vertrauens-\n"
"erweckend aus."
msgstr ""
"The ceiling supports do not\n"
"look particularly trust-\n"
"worthy."

msgctxt "scene:52:26"
msgid ""
"Dieser Stützbalken muss\n"
"bei unserem Eindringen\n"
"gebrochen sein."
msgstr ""
"This support beam must\n"
"have broken when we\n"
"entered."

msgctxt "scene:52:29"
msgid ""
"Der Stützbalken macht einen\n"
"stabilen und massiven Ein-\n"
"druck. Aus ihm könnte man\n"
"eine lebensgrosse Figur\n"
"schnitzen."
msgstr ""
"The support beam makes a\n"
"sturdy and solid impression.\n"
"From it one could carve a\n"
"life-sized figure.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:34"
msgid ""
"Dieser Balken ist ja kom-\n"
"plett morsch und nutzlos."
msgstr ""
"Why, this beam is completely\n"
"rotten and useless."

msgctxt "scene:52:36"
msgid ""
"Der Balken scheint den Ein-\n"
"gang zu stützen."
msgstr ""
"The beam seems to support the\n"
"entrance."

msgctxt "scene:52:38"
msgid ""
"Durch den Ausgang scheint\n"
"das Sonnenlicht herein."
msgstr ""
"Sunlight shines in through the\n"
"exit."

msgctxt "scene:52:40"
msgid ""
"Eine massive Steinplatte\n"
"versperrt den Eingang. Sie\n"
"ist mit einer Staubschicht\n"
"bedeckt."
msgstr ""
"A massive stone plate blocks the\n"
"entrance. It is covered with\n"
"a layer of dust.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:44"
msgid ""
"Das müssen Zeichen einer alten\n"
"indianischen Sprache sein, ich\n"
"kann sie nicht entziffern."
msgstr ""
"Those must be signs of an old\n"
"Indian language; I cannot\n"
"decipher them."

msgctxt "scene:52:47"
msgid ""
"Dieser Hinweis ist sehr offen-\n"
"sichtlich, ich glaube da kommen\n"
"noch einige Sachen auf uns zu,\n"
"das Sicherungssystem jetzt zu\n"
"unterschätzen, wäre sicherlich\n"
"fatal."
msgstr ""
"This hint is very obvious;\n"
"I believe a few more things are\n"
"in store for us. Underestimating\n"
"the security system now would\n"
"surely be fatal.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:53"
msgid ""
"Eine lockere Staubschicht\n"
"bedeckt den Boden. Vor\n"
"dem Eingang, scheint ein\n"
"felsiger Untergrund zu sein."
msgstr ""
"A loose layer of dust covers\n"
"the ground. In front of the\n"
"entrance, there seems to be\n"
"a rocky ground."

msgctxt "scene:52:57"
msgid ""
"Da sind ja drei Steinplatten\n"
"in den Boden eingelassen."
msgstr ""
"Why, three stone plates are\n"
"set into the ground."

msgctxt "scene:52:59"
msgid ""
"Die drei Platten sind vor dem\n"
"Steintor angeordnet. Sonst, ist\n"
"am Boden nichts zu erkennen."
msgstr ""
"The three plates are arranged in\n"
"front of the stone gate. Otherwise,\n"
"nothing is to be seen on the ground."

msgctxt "scene:52:62"
msgid ""
"Aaaaaarghhh... Der Balken ist\n"
"viel zu schwer."
msgstr ""
"Aaaaaarghhh... The beam is\n"
"far too heavy."

msgctxt "scene:52:64"
msgid ""
"Der Balken ist viel\n"
"zu schwer."
msgstr ""
"The beam is far\n"
"too heavy."

msgctxt "scene:52:66"
msgid ""
"Der Raum gleicht auf den\n"
"ersten Blick dem Eingang\n"
"einer Silbermine, doch die\n"
"Wände sind viel feiner aus\n"
"dem Felsen gehauen."
msgstr ""
"At first glance the room resembles\n"
"the entrance to a silver mine, yet\n"
"the walls are carved much more\n"
"finely from the rock.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:71"
msgid ""
"Ich werde die Stützen\n"
"nicht anrühren. Wenn\n"
"man die nur schief an-\n"
"sieht, riskiert man\n"
"einen Einsturz."
msgstr ""
"I shall not touch the supports.\n"
"If one but looks at them sideways,\n"
"one risks a collapse.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:76"
msgid ""
"Was könnte ich mit einem\n"
"durchgebrochenen Balken\n"
"anfangen."
msgstr ""
"What could I do with a\n"
"broken beam\n"
"anyway."

msgctxt "scene:52:79"
msgid ""
"Den Balken kann man nicht\n"
"einmal mehr als Brennholz\n"
"gebrauchen, so morsch wie\n"
"der ist."
msgstr ""
"One cannot even use the beam as\n"
"firewood anymore, as rotten as\n"
"it is.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:83"
msgid ""
"Ja,ja, wenn ich den weg-\n"
"nehme, dann hat das zur\n"
"Folge, dass der halbe\n"
"Berg herunterstürzt, und\n"
"dazu habe ich keine Lust."
msgstr ""
"Yes, yes, if I take that away, the\n"
"consequence will be that half the\n"
"mountain comes crashing down,\n"
"and I have no desire for that.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:88"
msgid ""
"Da hilft kein Drücken und\n"
"auch kein Schieben, wir\n"
"müssen uns da etwas einfal-\n"
"len lassen..."
msgstr ""
"No pushing and no shoving will\n"
"help here; we must think of\n"
"something...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:52:92"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Staub, der den\n"
"Boden bedeckt, kann ich\n"
"nichts anfangen."
msgstr ""
"I can do nothing with\n"
"the dust that covers the\n"
"ground."

msgctxt "scene:52:95"
msgid ""
"Der Felsen ist zu hart,\n"
"um sich in den Berg gra-\n"
"ben zu können."
msgstr ""
"The rock is too hard\n"
"to be able to dig into\n"
"the mountain."

msgctxt "scene:52:98"
msgid ""
"Die Wände, mit den Bohlen\n"
"abzustützen, wäre Wasser in\n"
"den Fluss tragen..."
msgstr ""
"Propping the walls with planks\n"
"would be carrying water to the\n"
"river..."

msgctxt "scene:52:101"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"For such work the crowbar\n"
"is too weak."

msgctxt "scene:52:103"
msgid ""
"Damit sprenge ich jede Felswand,\n"
"doch die Folgen die eine solche\n"
"Explosion haben könnte, muss man\n"
"vorher bedenken."
msgstr ""
"With that I'll blast any rock wall,\n"
"yet the consequences such an\n"
"explosion might have must be\n"
"considered beforehand."

msgctxt "scene:52:107"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten\n"
"denkbar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely\n"
"unsuitable for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:52:109"
msgid ""
"Für Ackerbau, haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"For agriculture we do not have\n"
"the necessary time right now."

msgctxt "scene:52:111"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow up the\n"
"ground here?"

msgctxt "scene:52:113"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brecheisen, kann ich\n"
"das schwere Tor sicher nicht\n"
"aufbekommen."
msgstr ""
"With the crowbar, I surely\n"
"cannot get the heavy gate\n"
"open."

msgctxt "scene:52:116"
msgid ""
"Das ist ein Steintor, und kann\n"
"nicht brennen."
msgstr ""
"That is a stone gate, and cannot\n"
"burn."

msgctxt "scene:53:0"
msgid ""
"Das Seil habe ich doch bereits\n"
"befestigt, warum also noch einmal\n"
"Kopf und Kragen riskieren, und da\n"
"hochklettern?"
msgstr ""
"I have already fastened the\n"
"rope, so why risk life and\n"
"limb again to climb up\n"
"there?"

msgctxt "scene:53:4"
msgid "Wozu soll ich da hochklettern?"
msgstr "Why should I climb up there?"

msgctxt "scene:53:5"
msgid "Etwas später..."
msgstr "A little later..."

msgctxt "scene:53:6"
msgid ""
"Ich habe die Befestigungs-\n"
"schrauben am Sockel des Pfahl's\n"
"bereits gelöst."
msgstr ""
"I have already loosened the\n"
"fastening screws at the base\n"
"of the pole."

msgctxt "scene:53:9"
msgid ""
"Der bewegt sich nicht - so\n"
"stark ich auch daran ziehe."
msgstr ""
"It does not move - no matter\n"
"how hard I pull on it."

msgctxt "scene:53:11"
msgid ""
"Das Loch in der Decke, ist\n"
"genau über dem Pfahl. Man\n"
"kann nicht erkennen, wo es\n"
"hinführt."
msgstr ""
"The hole in the ceiling is\n"
"right above the pole. One\n"
"cannot see where it\n"
"leads."

msgctxt "scene:53:15"
msgid ""
"Der Durchgang führt in einen\n"
"weiteren Raum."
msgstr ""
"The passage leads into\n"
"another room."

msgctxt "scene:53:17"
msgid ""
"Ein, aus Holz geschnitzter\n"
"Kopf, hängt an einer Kette\n"
"von der Decke."
msgstr ""
"A head carved out of wood\n"
"hangs from the ceiling by\n"
"a chain."

msgctxt "scene:53:20"
msgid ""
"Ein Totempfahl steht mitten\n"
"im Raum. Die verschiedenen\n"
"Gesichter, schauen auch nicht\n"
"gerade fröhlich d'rein."
msgstr ""
"A totem pole stands in the\n"
"middle of the room. The\n"
"various faces do not look\n"
"particularly cheerful either."

msgctxt "scene:53:24"
msgid ""
"Ein schlicht gehaltener Raum,\n"
"man könnte beinahe schon sagen,\n"
"dass er kahl wirkt."
msgstr ""
"A simply kept room, one\n"
"could almost say that it\n"
"appears bare."

msgctxt "scene:53:27"
msgid ""
"Der Durchgang führt zurück\n"
"zum Eingang."
msgstr ""
"The passage leads back\n"
"to the entrance."

msgctxt "scene:53:29"
msgid ""
"Eine brennende Fackel, die\n"
"hat wohl Winnetou angezündet."
msgstr ""
"A burning torch, Winnetou\n"
"must have lit it."

msgctxt "scene:53:31"
msgid ""
"Eine gemauerte Treppe, führt\n"
"zum Ausgang."
msgstr ""
"A brick staircase leads\n"
"to the exit."

msgctxt "scene:53:33"
msgid ""
"Die Kameraden, denen die \n"
"Schädel gehörten, haben\n"
"auch weiters keine Sorgen\n"
"mehr."
msgstr ""
"The comrades to whom those\n"
"skulls belonged do not have\n"
"any further worries\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:53:37"
msgid "An das Loch komme ich nicht."
msgstr "I cannot reach the hole."

msgctxt "scene:53:38"
msgid ""
"Winnetou hat bereits eine\n"
"Fackel, und mehr benötigen\n"
"wir nicht, also lasse ich\n"
"die in diesem Raum."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou already has a\n"
"torch, and we need no more,\n"
"so I will leave this one in\n"
"this room."

msgctxt "scene:53:42"
msgid ""
"Das sind keine Schrumpfköpfe,\n"
"und brauchen zuviel Platz. Ich\n"
"lasse sie hier, sollte ich die\n"
"noch brauchen, hole ich sie.\n"
"Die laufen sicher nicht mehr\n"
"davon."
msgstr ""
"Those are not shrunken heads,\n"
"and take up too much space. I\n"
"will leave them here; if I still\n"
"need them, I will get them.\n"
"They surely will not run\n"
"away anymore."

msgctxt "scene:53:48"
msgid ""
"Das Loch in der Decke, ist\n"
"genau über dem Pfahl. Man\n"
"kann nicht erkennen, wo es\n"
"hinführt."
msgstr ""
"The hole in the ceiling is\n"
"right above the pole. One\n"
"cannot see where it\n"
"leads."

msgctxt "scene:53:52"
msgid ""
"Der Durchgang führt in einen\n"
"weiteren Raum."
msgstr ""
"The passage leads into\n"
"another room."

msgctxt "scene:53:54"
msgid ""
"Ein, aus Holz geschnitzter\n"
"Kopf, hängt an einer Kette\n"
"von der Decke."
msgstr ""
"A head carved out of wood\n"
"hangs from the ceiling by\n"
"a chain."

msgctxt "scene:53:57"
msgid ""
"Ein Totenpfahl steht mitten\n"
"im Raum. Die verschiedenen\n"
"Gesichter schauen auch nicht\n"
"gerade fröhlich drein."
msgstr ""
"A totem pole stands in the\n"
"middle of the room. The\n"
"various faces do not look\n"
"particularly cheerful either."

msgctxt "scene:53:61"
msgid ""
"Ein schlicht gehaltener Raum,\n"
"man könnte beinahe schon sagen,\n"
"dass er kahl wirkt."
msgstr ""
"A simply kept room, one\n"
"could almost say that it\n"
"appears bare."

msgctxt "scene:53:64"
msgid ""
"Der Durchgang führt zurück\n"
"zum Eingang."
msgstr ""
"The passage leads back\n"
"to the entrance."

msgctxt "scene:53:66"
msgid ""
"Eine brennende Fackel, die\n"
"hat wohl Winnetou angezündet."
msgstr ""
"A burning torch, Winnetou\n"
"must have lit it."

msgctxt "scene:53:68"
msgid ""
"Eine gemauerte Treppe, führt\n"
"zum Ausgang."
msgstr ""
"A brick staircase leads\n"
"to the exit."

msgctxt "scene:53:70"
msgid ""
"Die Kameraden, denen die \n"
"Schädel gehörten, haben\n"
"auch weiters keine Sorgen\n"
"mehr."
msgstr ""
"The comrades to whom those\n"
"skulls belonged do not have\n"
"any further worries\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:53:74"
msgid ""
"Es würde mich wundern, wenn\n"
"die noch antworten."
msgstr ""
"I would be surprised if\n"
"they still answered."

msgctxt "scene:53:76"
msgid "Das ist ein stummer Wächter."
msgstr "That is a silent guardian."

msgctxt "scene:53:77"
msgid ""
"Ich bezweifle, dass der mit\n"
"mir reden wird."
msgstr ""
"I doubt that he will speak\n"
"to me."

msgctxt "scene:53:79"
msgid ""
"Der Kopf hängt zu hoch, da\n"
"komme ich so nicht heran."
msgstr ""
"The head hangs too high,\n"
"I cannot reach it like this."

msgctxt "scene:53:81"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich wenig ausrichten.\n"
"Auf alle Fälle passt es nicht, um\n"
"die Schrauben der Verankerung zu\n"
"lösen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot accomplish much with that.\n"
"In any case it does not fit to\n"
"loosen the screws of the\n"
"anchorage."

msgctxt "scene:53:85"
msgid ""
"Guter Versuch, aber leider passt\n"
"die nicht..."
msgstr ""
"Good try, but unfortunately\n"
"it does not fit..."

msgctxt "scene:53:87"
msgid ""
"Die Idee war gut, aber leider ohne\n"
"Wirkung."
msgstr ""
"The idea was good, but sadly\n"
"without effect."

msgctxt "scene:53:89"
msgid "Das geht leider nicht."
msgstr "Unfortunately that does not work."

msgctxt "scene:53:90"
msgid ""
"Die Figur ist etwas zu\n"
"wackelig."
msgstr ""
"The figure is a bit too\n"
"wobbly."

msgctxt "scene:53:92"
msgid ""
"Die Figur ist etwas zu\n"
"wackelig."
msgstr ""
"The figure is a bit too\n"
"wobbly."

msgctxt "scene:53:94"
msgid ""
"Der ist viel zu glatt, um\n"
"einfach so hochzuklettern!"
msgstr ""
"It is far too slippery to\n"
"just climb up like that!"

msgctxt "scene:54:0"
msgid ""
"Den Kopf kann ich nicht wegneh-\n"
"men. Ich sollte da auch nicht\n"
"zuviel daran machen, wer weiss\n"
"was da noch passiert."
msgstr ""
"I cannot take the head away.\n"
"I should not mess with it\n"
"too much either, who knows\n"
"what might happen then."

msgctxt "scene:54:4"
msgid ""
"Ich bin ja kein Fisch - das\n"
"Loch ist voll Wasser, da\n"
"kann ich nicht hinunter."
msgstr ""
"I am no fish after all -\n"
"the hole is full of water,\n"
"I cannot go down there."

msgctxt "scene:54:7"
msgid ""
"Das Loch im Boden, scheint\n"
"ein Durchgang zu sein."
msgstr ""
"The hole in the floor seems\n"
"to be a passage."

msgctxt "scene:54:9"
msgid ""
"Der Durchgang führt in einen\n"
"weiteren Raum."
msgstr ""
"The passage leads into\n"
"another room."

msgctxt "scene:54:11"
msgid ""
"Ein, aus Holz geschnitzter\n"
"Kopf, hängt an einer Kette\n"
"von der Decke."
msgstr ""
"A head carved out of wood\n"
"hangs from the ceiling by\n"
"a chain."

msgctxt "scene:54:14"
msgid ""
"Ein Totempfahl hängt mitten\n"
"im Raum. Die verschiedenen\n"
"Gesichter schauen auch nicht\n"
"gerade fröhlich d'rein."
msgstr ""
"A totem pole hangs in the\n"
"middle of the room. The\n"
"various faces do not look\n"
"particularly cheerful either."

msgctxt "scene:54:18"
msgid ""
"Ein schlicht gehaltener Raum,\n"
"man könnte beinahe schon sagen,\n"
"dass er kahl wirkt."
msgstr ""
"A simply kept room, one\n"
"could almost say that it\n"
"appears bare."

msgctxt "scene:54:21"
msgid ""
"Der Durchgang führt zurück\n"
"zum Eingang."
msgstr ""
"The passage leads back\n"
"to the entrance."

msgctxt "scene:54:23"
msgid ""
"Eine brennende Fackel, die\n"
"hat wohl Winnetou angezündet."
msgstr ""
"A burning torch, Winnetou\n"
"must have lit it."

msgctxt "scene:54:25"
msgid ""
"Eine gemauerte Treppe, führt\n"
"zum Ausgang."
msgstr ""
"A brick staircase leads\n"
"to the exit."

msgctxt "scene:54:27"
msgid ""
"Die Kameraden, denen die \n"
"Schädel gehörten, haben\n"
"auch weiters keine Sorgen\n"
"mehr."
msgstr ""
"The comrades to whom those\n"
"skulls belonged do not have\n"
"any further worries\n"
"either."

msgctxt "scene:54:31"
msgid ""
"Winnetou hat bereits eine\n"
"Fackel, und mehr benötigen\n"
"wir nicht, also lass ich\n"
"die in diesem Raum."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou already has a\n"
"torch, and we need no more,\n"
"so I will leave this one in\n"
"this room."

msgctxt "scene:54:35"
msgid ""
"Das sind keine Schrumpfköpfe,\n"
"und brauchen zuviel Platz. Ich\n"
"lasse sie hier, sollte ich die\n"
"noch brauchen, hole ich sie.\n"
"Die laufen sicher nicht mehr\n"
"davon."
msgstr ""
"Those are not shrunken heads,\n"
"and take up too much space. I\n"
"will leave them here; if I still\n"
"need them, I will get them.\n"
"They surely will not run\n"
"away anymore."

msgctxt "scene:54:41"
msgid ""
"Es würde mich wundern, wenn\n"
"die noch antworten."
msgstr ""
"I would be surprised if\n"
"they still answered."

msgctxt "scene:54:43"
msgid "Das ist ein stummer Wächter."
msgstr "That is a silent guardian."

msgctxt "scene:54:44"
msgid ""
"Ich bezweifle, dass der mit\n"
"mir reden wird."
msgstr ""
"I doubt that he will speak\n"
"to me."

msgctxt "scene:54:46"
msgid ""
"Der hängt zu hoch, da kann ich\n"
"nicht mehr hinaufklettern."
msgstr ""
"It hangs too high, I cannot\n"
"climb up there anymore."

msgctxt "scene:54:48"
msgid ""
"Guter Versuch, aber leider hängt\n"
"der Pfahl zu hoch."
msgstr ""
"Good try, but unfortunately the\n"
"pole hangs too high."

msgctxt "scene:54:50"
msgid ""
"Guter Versuch, aber leider hängt\n"
"der Pfahl zu hoch."
msgstr ""
"Good try, but unfortunately the\n"
"pole hangs too high."

msgctxt "scene:54:52"
msgid "Das geht leider nicht."
msgstr "That does not work."

msgctxt "scene:54:53"
msgid ""
"Den kann ich nicht von\n"
"der Kette wegnehmen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot take that one off\n"
"the chain."

msgctxt "scene:54:55"
msgid ""
"Der hängt zu hoch,\n"
"da komme ich ohne\n"
"Hilfsmittel nicht\n"
"heran."
msgstr ""
"It hangs too high,\n"
"I cannot reach it\n"
"without any tools\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:54:59"
msgid ""
"Die Figur ist etwas zu\n"
"wackelig."
msgstr ""
"The figure is a bit too\n"
"wobbly."

msgctxt "scene:54:61"
msgid ""
"Der Kopf ist doch\n"
"schon heruntergezogen!"
msgstr ""
"The head has already\n"
"been pulled down!"

msgctxt "scene:54:63"
msgid ""
"Die Figur ist etwas zu\n"
"wackelig."
msgstr ""
"The figure is a bit too\n"
"wobbly."

msgctxt "scene:54:65"
msgid ""
"Der Kopf ist doch\n"
"schon heruntergezogen!"
msgstr ""
"The head has already\n"
"been pulled down!"

msgctxt "scene:55:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Steinsäule, mit einem\n"
"eigenartigen Schalter, steht\n"
"da mitten im Raum."
msgstr ""
"A stone column with a\n"
"peculiar switch stands\n"
"there in the middle of the room."

msgctxt "scene:55:3"
msgid ""
"Es sieht hier wie in einem\n"
"Zeremonienraum aus. Am Ende\n"
"des Raumes, befindet sich\n"
"eine Steinpyramide mit ein-\n"
"gehauenen Treppen, und in\n"
"der Mitte des Raumes, ist im\n"
"Boden eine Vertiefung von\n"
"drei Zentimetern."
msgstr ""
"It looks like a ceremonial\n"
"room here. At the end of the\n"
"room, there is a stone\n"
"pyramid with carved steps,\n"
"and in the middle of the\n"
"room, there is a three-\n"
"centimeter depression in\n"
"the floor."

msgctxt "scene:55:11"
msgid ""
"Eine glatt geschliffene\n"
"Steinsäule. Sie ist etwas\n"
"breiter wie die, auf der\n"
"linken Seite. Eine gehei-\n"
"me Treppe ist ausgefahren."
msgstr ""
"A smoothly polished stone\n"
"column. It is slightly wider\n"
"than the one on the left\n"
"side. A secret staircase\n"
"has been extended."

msgctxt "scene:55:16"
msgid ""
"Eine glatt geschliffene\n"
"Steinsäule. Sie ist etwas\n"
"breiter wie die, auf der\n"
"linken Seite."
msgstr ""
"A smoothly polished stone\n"
"column. It is slightly wider\n"
"than the one on the left\n"
"side."

msgctxt "scene:55:20"
msgid ""
"Eine polierte Steinsäule,\n"
"etwas schmaler wie die, auf\n"
"der rechten Seite des Raumes.\n"
"Eine Treppe ist ausgefahren."
msgstr ""
"A polished stone column,\n"
"slightly narrower than the\n"
"one on the right side of the\n"
"room. A staircase is extended."

msgctxt "scene:55:24"
msgid ""
"Eine polierte Steinsäule,\n"
"etwas schmaler wie die, auf\n"
"der rechten Seite des Raumes."
msgstr ""
"A polished stone column,\n"
"slightly narrower than the one\n"
"on the right side of the room."

msgctxt "scene:55:27"
msgid ""
"Ein Gegenstand, den ich nicht\n"
"richtig erkennen kann, liegt\n"
"auf der Säule."
msgstr ""
"An object that I cannot make\n"
"out properly is lying on top\n"
"of the column."

msgctxt "scene:55:30"
msgid ""
"Ein Gegenstand, den ich nicht\n"
"richtig erkennen kann, liegt\n"
"auf der Säule."
msgstr ""
"An object that I cannot make\n"
"out properly is lying on top\n"
"of the column."

msgctxt "scene:55:33"
msgid ""
"Eine stehende Holzfigur.\n"
"Der Knabe blickt ganz\n"
"schön finster d'rein."
msgstr ""
"A standing wooden figure.\n"
"The fellow looks quite\n"
"gloomy indeed."

msgctxt "scene:55:36"
msgid ""
"Das ist ein Beutel, voll\n"
"mit Sand."
msgstr ""
"That is a pouch, filled\n"
"with sand."

msgctxt "scene:55:38"
msgid ""
"Diese Holzfigur sitzt auf\n"
"ihrem Sockel. Ein unfreund-\n"
"licher Geselle."
msgstr ""
"This wooden figure sits on\n"
"its pedestal. An un-\n"
"friendly fellow."

msgctxt "scene:55:41"
msgid ""
"Das ist ein Beutel, voll\n"
"mit Sand."
msgstr ""
"That is a pouch, filled\n"
"with sand."

msgctxt "scene:55:43"
msgid ""
"Eine Steintreppe die aus\n"
"Fels gehauen wurde, und\n"
"so genau zusammengefügt\n"
"ist, dass man den Ein-\n"
"druck gewinnt, die Treppe\n"
"sei aus einem Stück ge-\n"
"hauen."
msgstr ""
"A stone staircase carved out\n"
"of rock, and fitted together\n"
"so precisely that one gets\n"
"the impression that the\n"
"stairs were carved from a\n"
"single piece of stone,\n"
"indeed."

msgctxt "scene:55:50"
msgid ""
"Eine Steintreppe die aus\n"
"Fels gehauen wurde, und\n"
"so genau zusammengefügt\n"
"ist, dass man den Ein-\n"
"druck gewinnt, die Treppe\n"
"sei aus einem Stück ge-\n"
"hauen."
msgstr ""
"A stone staircase carved out\n"
"of rock, and fitted together\n"
"so precisely that one gets\n"
"the impression that the\n"
"stairs were carved from a\n"
"single piece of stone,\n"
"indeed."

msgctxt "scene:55:57"
msgid ""
"Eine Treppe, eingehauen in einen\n"
"pyramidenartigen Aufbau."
msgstr ""
"A staircase carved into a\n"
"pyramid-like structure."

msgctxt "scene:55:59"
msgid ""
"Gute Idee, doch ich glaube nicht,\n"
"dass die klappt, denn ich habe ja\n"
"keine 6 Figuren."
msgstr ""
"Good idea, but I do not think that\n"
"it will work, since I do not have\n"
"6 figures."

msgctxt "scene:55:62"
msgid ""
"Gute Idee, doch ich glaube nicht,\n"
"dass die klappt, denn ich habe ja\n"
"keine 6 Figuren."
msgstr ""
"Good idea, but I do not think that\n"
"it will work, since I do not have\n"
"6 figures."

msgctxt "scene:55:65"
msgid ""
"Gute Idee, doch ich glaube nicht,\n"
"dass die klappt, denn ich habe ja\n"
"keine 6 Figuren."
msgstr ""
"Good idea, but I do not think that\n"
"it will work, since I do not have\n"
"6 figures."

msgctxt "scene:55:68"
msgid ""
"Ich würde damit bestenfalls die\n"
"Platten beschädigen."
msgstr ""
"At best I would only damage the\n"
"slabs with that."

msgctxt "scene:55:70"
msgid ""
"Nicht überall ist pure Gewalt\n"
"gefragt."
msgstr ""
"Pure force is not required\n"
"everywhere."

msgctxt "scene:55:72"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte die Einrichtung\n"
"hier nicht beschädigen, denn\n"
"das kann negative Auswirkungen\n"
"auf mein Weiterkommen haben."
msgstr ""
"I should not damage the\n"
"fixtures here, as that could\n"
"have a negative impact on\n"
"my progress."

msgctxt "scene:55:76"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte die Einrichtung\n"
"hier nicht beschädigen, denn\n"
"das kann negative Auswirkungen\n"
"auf mein Weiterkommen haben."
msgstr ""
"I should not damage the\n"
"fixtures here, as that could\n"
"have a negative impact on\n"
"my progress."

msgctxt "scene:55:80"
msgid ""
"Was soll das bringen, wenn\n"
"ich Löcher in Boden und Wände\n"
"mache?"
msgstr ""
"What good would it do if I\n"
"make holes in the floor and\n"
"walls?"

msgctxt "scene:55:83"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brecheisen, kann ich an\n"
"der Säule nichts ausrichten."
msgstr ""
"With the crowbar I cannot accomplish\n"
"anything on the column."

msgctxt "scene:55:85"
msgid ""
"Mit den Sicheln kann ich an\n"
"den Säulen nichts machen, die\n"
"sind zu glattgeschliffen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot do anything to the columns\n"
"with the sickles; they are ground\n"
"too smooth."

msgctxt "scene:55:88"
msgid ""
"Mit den Sicheln kann ich an\n"
"den Säulen nichts machen, die\n"
"sind zu glattgeschliffen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot do anything to the columns\n"
"with the sickles; they are ground\n"
"too smooth."

msgctxt "scene:55:91"
msgid ""
"Eine dunkle Kachel, die etwas\n"
"aus der Wand ragt."
msgstr ""
"A dark tile protruding slightly\n"
"from the wall."

msgctxt "scene:55:93"
msgid ""
"In die Kachel ist eine In-\n"
"schrift graviert:"
msgstr ""
"An inscription is engraved\n"
"into the tile:"

msgctxt "scene:55:95"
msgid ""
"Take won to karke tor\n"
"sui harai tan."
msgstr ""
"Take won to karke tor\n"
"sui harai tan."

msgctxt "scene:55:97"
msgid ""
"Da sind ja zwei sichelartige\n"
"Geräte, die nehme ich mal."
msgstr ""
"There are two sickle-like implements\n"
"there; I will take those."

msgctxt "scene:55:99"
msgid ""
"Da befindet sich nichts mehr\n"
"in dem Geheimfach."
msgstr ""
"There is nothing left inside\n"
"the secret compartment."

msgctxt "scene:55:101"
msgid ""
"Ein Adler-Emblem, teils in die\n"
"Mauer graviert, und teils auf-\n"
"gelegt. An jedem der sechs Ecken,\n"
"befinden sich eine bestimmte\n"
"Anzahl Vertiefungen."
msgstr ""
"An eagle emblem, partly engraved\n"
"into the wall, and partly at-\n"
"tached. At each of the six corners\n"
"there is a certain number of\n"
"recesses."

msgctxt "scene:55:106"
msgid ""
"Da sind Steinplatten im Boden\n"
"eingelassen."
msgstr ""
"There are stone slabs embedded in\n"
"the floor."

msgctxt "scene:55:108"
msgid ""
"Das sieht aus, wie auf\n"
"die Wand aufgesetzt."
msgstr ""
"That looks as if it were placed\n"
"onto the wall."

msgctxt "scene:55:110"
msgid ""
"Das sieht aus, wie auf\n"
"die Wand aufgesetzt."
msgstr ""
"That looks as if it were placed\n"
"onto the wall."

msgctxt "scene:55:112"
msgid ""
"Ich habe es ja geahnt, es\n"
"ist nur eine Wandmalerei."
msgstr ""
"Just as I suspected, it is\n"
"only a mural."

msgctxt "scene:55:114"
msgid ""
"Das Ding ist zu weit weg,\n"
"da komme ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"That thing is too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach it."

msgctxt "scene:55:116"
msgid ""
"Meine Arme reichen nicht bis\n"
"dort hin, ich kann das nicht\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"My arms do not reach that\n"
"far, I cannot take that\n"
"thing."

msgctxt "scene:55:119"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:121"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:123"
msgid ""
"Meine Arme reichen nicht bis\n"
"dort hin, ich kann das nicht\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"My arms do not reach that\n"
"far, I cannot take that\n"
"thing."

msgctxt "scene:55:126"
msgid ""
"Das Ding ist zu weit weg,\n"
"da komme ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"That thing is too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach it."

msgctxt "scene:55:128"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:130"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:132"
msgid ""
"Ich bin ja froh, dass ich den\n"
"Beutel nicht mehr tragen muss."
msgstr ""
"I am glad that I do not have to\n"
"carry the pouch anymore."

msgctxt "scene:55:134"
msgid ""
"Da liegt ja bereits der\n"
"Beutel. Das wäre ein\n"
"schlechter Tausch."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already lying\n"
"there. That would be a\n"
"bad trade."

msgctxt "scene:55:137"
msgid ""
"Da habe ich ja bereits Sand\n"
"hineingefüllt."
msgstr ""
"I have already filled sand in\n"
"there."

msgctxt "scene:55:139"
msgid ""
"Ein Adler-Emblem, mit eigen-\n"
"artigen Zeichen an jedem\n"
"Eck' des Sechsecks."
msgstr ""
"An eagle emblem with peculiar\n"
"symbols at every corner of\n"
"the hexagon."

msgctxt "scene:55:142"
msgid ""
"Da sind Steinplatten im\n"
"Boden eingelassen."
msgstr ""
"There are stone slabs embedded\n"
"in the floor."

msgctxt "scene:55:144"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja oben eine Öffnung,\n"
"die in die Wand führt. Das muss\n"
"eine Art Trichter sein."
msgstr ""
"There is an opening at the top\n"
"leading into the wall. That must\n"
"be a kind of funnel."

msgctxt "scene:55:147"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass man\n"
"an der Wandmalerei etwas\n"
"machen kann..."
msgstr ""
"I do not think that anything\n"
"can be done with the mural\n"
"here..."

msgctxt "scene:55:150"
msgid ""
"Das Ding ist zu weit weg,\n"
"da komme ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"That thing is too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach it."

msgctxt "scene:55:152"
msgid ""
"Meine Arme reichen nicht bis\n"
"dort hin, ich kann das nicht\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"My arms do not reach that\n"
"far, I cannot take that\n"
"thing."

msgctxt "scene:55:155"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:157"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:159"
msgid ""
"Die Figur passt nicht auf diesen\n"
"Sockel."
msgstr ""
"The figure does not fit on this\n"
"pedestal."

msgctxt "scene:55:161"
msgid ""
"Ich bin ja froh, dass ich den\n"
"Beutel nicht mehr tragen muss."
msgstr ""
"I am glad that I do not have to\n"
"carry the pouch anymore."

msgctxt "scene:55:163"
msgid ""
"Das wäre ein schlechter Tausch!\n"
"Ich behalte die Figur."
msgstr ""
"That would be a bad trade!\n"
"I will keep the figure."

msgctxt "scene:55:165"
msgid ""
"Da habe ich ja bereits Sand\n"
"hineingefüllt."
msgstr ""
"I have already filled sand in\n"
"there."

msgctxt "scene:55:167"
msgid ""
"Ein Adler-Emblem, mit eigen-\n"
"artigen Zeichen an jedem der\n"
"sechs Ecken."
msgstr ""
"An eagle emblem with peculiar\n"
"symbols at each of the\n"
"six corners."

msgctxt "scene:55:170"
msgid ""
"Da sind Steinplatten im\n"
"Boden eingelassen."
msgstr ""
"There are stone slabs embedded\n"
"in the floor."

msgctxt "scene:55:172"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja oben eine Öffnung,\n"
"die in die Wand führt. Das muss\n"
"eine Art Trichter sein."
msgstr ""
"There is an opening at the top\n"
"leading into the wall. That must\n"
"be a kind of funnel."

msgctxt "scene:55:175"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass man\n"
"an der Wandmalerei etwas\n"
"machen kann..."
msgstr ""
"I do not think that anything\n"
"can be done with the mural\n"
"here..."

msgctxt "scene:55:178"
msgid ""
"Das Ding ist zu weit weg,\n"
"da komme ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"That thing is too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach it."

msgctxt "scene:55:180"
msgid ""
"Meine Arme reichen nicht bis\n"
"dort hin, ich kann das nicht\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"My arms do not reach that\n"
"far, I cannot take that\n"
"thing."

msgctxt "scene:55:183"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:185"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:187"
msgid ""
"Die Figur passt nicht auf diesen\n"
"Sockel."
msgstr ""
"The figure does not fit on this\n"
"pedestal."

msgctxt "scene:55:189"
msgid "Was war denn das?!?"
msgstr "What was that?!?"

msgctxt "scene:55:190"
msgid ""
"Autsch, die Treppe ist ganz\n"
"schön hart. Ich bin da plötz-\n"
"lich ausgerutscht..."
msgstr ""
"Ouch, the stairs are quite\n"
"hard. I suddenly slipped\n"
"there..."

msgctxt "scene:55:193"
msgid ""
"An der glatten Säule, komme\n"
"ich nicht hoch."
msgstr ""
"I cannot get up the\n"
"smooth column."

msgctxt "scene:55:195"
msgid ""
"Ich mache doch kein 'Trimm -\n"
"- Dich' Training, da oben\n"
"ist nichts zu holen."
msgstr ""
"I am not doing a fitness\n"
"workout, there is nothing\n"
"to get up there."

msgctxt "scene:55:198"
msgid ""
"Ich hab keine Saugnäpfe an\n"
"den Händen, an der glatten\n"
"Säule komme ich da nicht\n"
"hoch."
msgstr ""
"I have no suction cups on my\n"
"hands, I cannot climb up the\n"
"smooth column like\n"
"that."

msgctxt "scene:55:202"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich da raufklettere, kann\n"
"ich mir nur eine schweissgebade-\n"
"te Stirn holen, denn da oben ist\n"
"nichts mehr zu finden."
msgstr ""
"If I climb up there, I can only\n"
"get a sweat-drenched forehead,\n"
"because there is nothing left to\n"
"be found up there."

msgctxt "scene:55:206"
msgid ""
"Ich kann es nicht richtig er-\n"
"kennen, sieht aber wie eine\n"
"dunkle Kachel aus."
msgstr ""
"I cannot make it out properly,\n"
"but it looks like a dark\n"
"tile."

msgctxt "scene:55:209"
msgid ""
"Ein Adler-Emblem, mit eigen-\n"
"artigen Zeichen an jedem\n"
"Eck' des Sechsecks."
msgstr ""
"An eagle emblem with peculiar\n"
"symbols at every corner of\n"
"the hexagon."

msgctxt "scene:55:212"
msgid ""
"Da befinden sich ja Vertiefungen\n"
"in den Platten. Sieht aus wie\n"
"Zahlen... Auf jeden Fall, sind es\n"
"verschiedene Mengen von Punkten."
msgstr ""
"There are recesses in the slabs.\n"
"Looks like numbers... In any\n"
"case, they are different\n"
"quantities of dots."

msgctxt "scene:55:216"
msgid ""
"Das sieht aus, wie auf\n"
"die Wand aufgesetzt."
msgstr ""
"That looks as if it were placed\n"
"onto the wall."

msgctxt "scene:55:218"
msgid ""
"Das sieht aus, wie auf\n"
"die Wand aufgesetzt."
msgstr ""
"That looks as if it were placed\n"
"onto the wall."

msgctxt "scene:55:220"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass man\n"
"an der Wandmalerei etwas\n"
"machen kann..."
msgstr ""
"I do not think that anything\n"
"can be done with the mural\n"
"here..."

msgctxt "scene:55:223"
msgid ""
"Das Ding ist zu weit weg,\n"
"da komme ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"That thing is too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach it."

msgctxt "scene:55:225"
msgid ""
"Meine Arme reichen nicht bis\n"
"dort hin, ich kann das nicht\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"My arms do not reach that\n"
"far, I cannot take that\n"
"thing."

msgctxt "scene:55:228"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:230"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:232"
msgid ""
"Meine Arme reichen nicht bis\n"
"dort hin, ich kann das nicht\n"
"nehmen."
msgstr ""
"My arms do not reach that\n"
"far, I cannot take that\n"
"thing."

msgctxt "scene:55:235"
msgid ""
"Das Ding ist zu weit weg,\n"
"da komme ich nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"That thing is too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach it."

msgctxt "scene:55:237"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:55:239"
msgid ""
"Das geht nicht, ich bin zu weit\n"
"weg."
msgstr ""
"That does not work, I am too far\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:56:0"
msgid ""
"Hier gelange ich mit Benutzen\n"
"zurück in den Raum."
msgstr ""
"Using this brings me back\n"
"into the room."

msgctxt "scene:56:2"
msgid ""
"Das ist der Geheimschalter, der\n"
"aus dem Boden ausgefahren wurde."
msgstr ""
"That is the secret switch that\n"
"was extended from the floor."

msgctxt "scene:57:0"
msgid ""
"Die Kacheln sind zu weit\n"
"weg, von hier komme ich\n"
"nicht d'ran."
msgstr ""
"The tiles are too far away,\n"
"I cannot reach them from\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:57:3"
msgid ""
"Hier hat das Gewölbe\n"
"offenbar durch das\n"
"Wasser gelitten, doch\n"
"das gesamte Gangsystem,\n"
"ist recht imponierend\n"
"angelegt."
msgstr ""
"Here the vault has apparently\n"
"suffered from the water,\n"
"yet the entire system of\n"
"passages is constructed\n"
"in a quite impressive\n"
"manner."

msgctxt "scene:57:9"
msgid ""
"Ich frage mich, wie das\n"
"Spinnennetz hier hin-\n"
"kommt. Es könnte sein,\n"
"dass das Wasser nicht so\n"
"hoch gestiegen ist..."
msgstr ""
"I wonder how the spiderweb\n"
"got here. It could be that\n"
"the water did not rise\n"
"so very high after\n"
"all..."

msgctxt "scene:57:14"
msgid ""
"Die Säulen können nur\n"
"Zierde sein, denn das\n"
"gesamte Gewölbe besteht\n"
"aus massivem Felsen, und\n"
"braucht somit keine\n"
"Stütze."
msgstr ""
"The columns can only be\n"
"ornamental, because the\n"
"entire vault consists of\n"
"solid rock and thus needs\n"
"no support whatsoever\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:57:20"
msgid ""
"Da schauen Kacheln unter\n"
"dem abgesprungenen Verputz\n"
"hervor."
msgstr ""
"Tiles are peeking out from\n"
"under the flaked-off\n"
"plaster."

msgctxt "scene:57:23"
msgid ""
"Eine, in den Felsen gehauene\n"
"Treppe."
msgstr ""
"A staircase carved into\n"
"the rock."

msgctxt "scene:57:25"
msgid ""
"Wasserpfützen sind von dem\n"
"ganzen Wasser noch übrig\n"
"geblieben."
msgstr ""
"Water puddles are still left\n"
"over from all that\n"
"water."

msgctxt "scene:57:28"
msgid ""
"Eine einzelne Kachel liegt\n"
"hier am Boden."
msgstr ""
"A single tile is lying here\n"
"on the floor."

msgctxt "scene:57:30"
msgid ""
"Eine Plattform, die präzise\n"
"in den Felsen gehauen wurde."
msgstr ""
"A platform precisely carved\n"
"into the rock."

msgctxt "scene:57:32"
msgid ""
"Der Boden wurde genau gear-\n"
"beitet - welch ein Aufwand,\n"
"all die Gänge so fein aus-\n"
"gearbeitet in den Felsen zu\n"
"schlagen."
msgstr ""
"The floor was crafted with care -\n"
"what an effort to carve all\n"
"these passages so finely worked\n"
"out right into the solid\n"
"rock."

msgctxt "scene:57:37"
msgid ""
"Ein tiefer, und augenscheinlich\n"
"bodenloser Abgrund."
msgstr ""
"A deep and apparently\n"
"bottomless abyss."

msgctxt "scene:57:39"
msgid "Massiver Felsen..."
msgstr "Solid rock..."

msgctxt "scene:57:40"
msgid ""
"Das Spinnennetz hängt zu hoch,\n"
"und ich kann mir nicht vor-\n"
"stellen, wofür ich ein Spinnen-\n"
"netz benötigen könnte."
msgstr ""
"The spiderweb hangs too high,\n"
"and I cannot imagine what I\n"
"could possibly need a spiderweb\n"
"for."

msgctxt "scene:57:44"
msgid ""
"Die ist zu glatt, um daran hoch\n"
"zu klettern."
msgstr ""
"It is too smooth to climb\n"
"up on it."

msgctxt "scene:57:46"
msgid ""
"Ich habe keinen Durst. Das\n"
"bisschen Wasser, kann ich auch\n"
"nicht vom Boden aufnehmen."
msgstr ""
"I am not thirsty. I cannot\n"
"pick up that bit of water\n"
"from the floor either."

msgctxt "scene:57:49"
msgid ""
"Die kann ich nicht brauchen,\n"
"die ist bereits gesprungen\n"
"und brüchig."
msgstr ""
"I cannot use that one,\n"
"it is already cracked\n"
"and brittle."

msgctxt "scene:57:52"
msgid ""
"Nein, ich werde mich nicht\n"
"in den Abgrund stürzen..."
msgstr ""
"No, I am not going to\n"
"throw myself into the abyss..."

msgctxt "scene:57:54"
msgid ""
"Der ist so hart, da hat man\n"
"keine Chancen etwas ohne\n"
"Werkzeug herauszubrechen."
msgstr ""
"It is so hard that there is\n"
"no chance of breaking anything\n"
"off without tools."

msgctxt "scene:57:57"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten, ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is too weak\n"
"for such work."

msgctxt "scene:57:59"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten\n"
"denkbar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely\n"
"unsuitable for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:57:61"
msgid ""
"Für Ackerbau, haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"We do not have time for\n"
"agriculture right now."

msgctxt "scene:57:63"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow up\n"
"the floor here?"

msgctxt "scene:57:65"
msgid ""
"Für Acherbau, haben wir jetzt\n"
"nicht die nötige Zeit."
msgstr ""
"We do not have time for\n"
"agriculture right now."

msgctxt "scene:57:67"
msgid ""
"Wozu soll ich hier den Boden\n"
"umpflügen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I plow up\n"
"the floor here?"

msgctxt "scene:57:69"
msgid ""
"Dadurch werden nur die Sicheln\n"
"beschädigt."
msgstr ""
"That will only damage\n"
"the sickles."

msgctxt "scene:57:71"
msgid "Was hoffst Du dabei zu finden?"
msgstr "What do you hope to find?"

msgctxt "scene:57:72"
msgid ""
"Die beiden Figuren aus dem\n"
"Zeremoniensaal bilden zusam-\n"
"mengesetzt, eine Brücke über\n"
"den Abgrund."
msgstr ""
"The two figures from the\n"
"ceremonial hall put together\n"
"form a bridge across\n"
"the abyss."

msgctxt "scene:58:0"
msgid ""
"Puh, das wurde auch\n"
"Zeit!!!"
msgstr ""
"Phew, that was about\n"
"time!!!"

msgctxt "scene:58:2"
msgid ""
"Ich hab es mir gleich ge-\n"
"dacht, da ist es wieder\n"
"einmal nötig, sich etwas\n"
"einfallen zu lassen."
msgstr ""
"I thought as much,\n"
"once again it is necessary\n"
"to come up with\n"
"something."

msgctxt "scene:58:6"
msgid ""
"Auch hier wieder die\n"
"rundlichen Gewölbe, die\n"
"in den Berg gehauen,\n"
"und mit Mörtel verklei-\n"
"det wurden."
msgstr ""
"Here again the rounded\n"
"vaults carved into the\n"
"mountain and covered\n"
"with mortar for plaster-\n"
"ing."

msgctxt "scene:58:11"
msgid ""
"Eine massive Steintür\n"
"versperrt den Gang vor\n"
"uns."
msgstr ""
"A massive stone door\n"
"blocks the passage\n"
"ahead of us."

msgctxt "scene:58:14"
msgid ""
"Auch hier ist der Boden\n"
"noch ganz feucht. Der\n"
"gesamte Gang muss über-\n"
"flutet gewesen sein..."
msgstr ""
"Here too the floor is\n"
"still quite damp. The\n"
"entire passage must\n"
"have been flooded..."

msgctxt "scene:58:18"
msgid ""
"Der ganze Boden ist plan\n"
"geschliffen. Die Erbauer\n"
"dieser Anlage, haben sich\n"
"sehr viel Mühe gemacht."
msgstr ""
"The entire floor is polished\n"
"flat. The builders of this\n"
"facility took a great deal\n"
"of trouble indeed."

msgctxt "scene:58:22"
msgid "Massiver Granitfelsen!"
msgstr "Massive granite rock!"

msgctxt "scene:58:23"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"sich die Tür so einfach\n"
"öffnen lässt. Nicht ohne\n"
"guten Grund, wurde ein so\n"
"grosser Griff an der Tür\n"
"angebracht."
msgstr ""
"I do not think the door\n"
"opens that easily. Not\n"
"without good reason was\n"
"such a large handle\n"
"attached to the door\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:58:29"
msgid ""
"Das Wasser ist nicht geniess-\n"
"bar, zudem habe ich keinen\n"
"Durst."
msgstr ""
"The water is not drinkable,\n"
"besides I am not\n"
"thirsty."

msgctxt "scene:58:32"
msgid ""
"Der Boden ist aus massivem\n"
"Felsen, da kann ich nichts\n"
"machen."
msgstr ""
"The floor is made of solid\n"
"rock, there is nothing I\n"
"can do."

msgctxt "scene:58:35"
msgid ""
"Ich habe kein Werkzeug, um\n"
"von dem Felsen etwas abzu-\n"
"schlagen."
msgstr ""
"I have no tools to knock\n"
"anything off the\n"
"rock."

msgctxt "scene:58:38"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen ist zu schwach\n"
"dafür."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is too weak\n"
"for that."

msgctxt "scene:58:40"
msgid ""
"Für solche Arbeiten ist das\n"
"Brecheisen zu schwach."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is too weak\n"
"for such work."

msgctxt "scene:58:42"
msgid ""
"Die sind für Minenarbeiten\n"
"denkbar ungeeignet."
msgstr ""
"Those are completely\n"
"unsuitable for mining work."

msgctxt "scene:58:44"
msgid ""
"Dadurch werden nur die Sicheln\n"
"beschädigt."
msgstr ""
"That will only damage\n"
"the sickles."

msgctxt "scene:58:46"
msgid "Was erhoffst Du Dir dabei?"
msgstr "What do you hope to gain?"

msgctxt "scene:59:0"
msgid ""
"Ich lasse die Kiste wohl besser\n"
"stehen, bei der Konstruktion\n"
"kann man nicht wissen, was man\n"
"auslöst, wenn die Kiste weg-\n"
"genommen wird."
msgstr ""
"I had better leave the chest\n"
"standing here; with this design\n"
"there is no telling what one\n"
"might trigger if the chest is\n"
"removed."

msgctxt "scene:59:5"
msgid ""
"Ah, da komme ich gerade\n"
"noch rechtzeitig. Ich\n"
"muss Dir meine Achtung\n"
"aussprechen Firehand,\n"
"ich hätte Dich hier\n"
"nicht erwartet - und\n"
"dann noch in so be-\n"
"rühmter Begleitung."
msgstr ""
"Ah, I arrive just in the\n"
"nick of time. I must\n"
"express my respects to\n"
"you, Firehand. I would\n"
"not have expected you\n"
"here - and in such\n"
"famous company,\n"
"no less."

msgctxt "scene:59:13"
msgid ""
"Ah, da komme ich gerade\n"
"noch rechtzeitig. Ich\n"
"muss Dir meine Achtung\n"
"aussprechen Firehand,\n"
"ich hätte Dich hier\n"
"nicht erwartet - und\n"
"dann noch in so be-\n"
"rühmter Begleitung."
msgstr ""
"Ah, I arrive just in the\n"
"nick of time. I must\n"
"express my respects to\n"
"you, Firehand. I would\n"
"not have expected you\n"
"here - and in such\n"
"famous company,\n"
"no less."

msgctxt "scene:59:21"
msgid ""
"Auf Deine Achtung kann\n"
"ich verzichten Brinkley."
msgstr ""
"I can do without your respect,\n"
"Brinkley."

msgctxt "scene:59:23"
msgid ""
"Aber wieso denn so un-\n"
"freundlich, Firehand.\n"
"Ich habe Dir ja ge-\n"
"sagt, dass sich das\n"
"Blatt wenden wird, und\n"
"das hat es ja getan.\n"
"Und nun lasst uns\n"
"nicht noch mehr Zeit"
msgstr ""
"But why so unfriendly,\n"
"Firehand?\n"
"I told you that the\n"
"tables would turn, and\n"
"so they have.\n"
"And now let's not lose\n"
"any more time,\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:31"
msgid ""
"vertun, denn die zwei\n"
"Rothäute die wir ver-\n"
"trieben haben, werden\n"
"sicher schon bald mit\n"
"Verstärkung auftauchen."
msgstr ""
"for the two\n"
"Redskins we drove\n"
"off will surely soon\n"
"appear with back-\n"
"up."

msgctxt "scene:59:36"
msgid ""
"Glaubst Du wirklich, Du\n"
"kannst mit dem Schatz\n"
"entkommen, Brinkley?"
msgstr ""
"Do you really think you\n"
"can escape with the\n"
"treasure, Brinkley?"

msgctxt "scene:59:39"
msgid ""
"Ich habe es bis hierhin\n"
"geschafft, wer könnte\n"
"mich jetzt noch daran\n"
"hindern, den Schatz ab-\n"
"zutransportieren."
msgstr ""
"I made it this far,\n"
"who could possibly stop\n"
"me from hauling off\n"
"the treasure now.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:44"
msgid ""
"Ich denke, Ihr müsst\n"
"Euch vielmehr um\n"
"Eure Zukunft Gedan-\n"
"ken machen, oder auch\n"
"nicht, denn Ihr wer-\n"
"det Schwierigkeiten\n"
"haben, hier raus' zu\n"
"kommen."
msgstr ""
"I think you should\n"
"rather worry about\n"
"your future, or maybe\n"
"not, as you will have\n"
"a hard time getting\n"
"out of here.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:52"
msgid ""
"Du wirst Deiner ge-\n"
"rechten Strafe nicht\n"
"entgehen, Bleich-\n"
"gesicht."
msgstr ""
"You will not escape\n"
"your just punishment,\n"
"pale-face.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:56"
msgid ""
"Rede nur Rothaut,\n"
"ich werde in weni-\n"
"gen Augenblicken\n"
"verschwunden sein,\n"
"und mir mit dem\n"
"Schatz ein schö-\n"
"nes Leben machen."
msgstr ""
"Talk on, Redskin,\n"
"I will be gone in\n"
"just a few moments\n"
"and live a grand\n"
"life with the\n"
"treasure.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:63"
msgid ""
"Und nun pack den\n"
"Schatz in den\n"
"Beutel Firehand.\n"
"Ich möchte hier\n"
"nicht den ganzen"
msgstr ""
"And now pack the\n"
"treasure into the\n"
"bag, Firehand.\n"
"I don't want to spend\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:68"
msgid ""
"Tag vertrödeln,\n"
"auf mich wartet\n"
"ein Leben in\n"
"Reichtum..."
msgstr ""
"the whole day here,\n"
"a life of wealth\n"
"is waiting for\n"
"me..."

msgctxt "scene:59:72"
msgid ""
"Ich muss Dir meinen\n"
"innigsten Dank aus-\n"
"sprechen Firehand,\n"
"ich werde noch oft\n"
"an Dich denken."
msgstr ""
"I must express my\n"
"deepest thanks to you,\n"
"Firehand, I will think\n"
"of you often.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:77"
msgid ""
"So, und damit Euch\n"
"nicht einfällt mich\n"
"zu verfolgen, werdet\n"
"ihr schön die Plat-\n"
"ten, die in der Tür\n"
"stecken, entfernen.\n"
"Aber schnell..."
msgstr ""
"So, and so you don't\n"
"get the idea to follow\n"
"me, you will kindly\n"
"remove the slabs that\n"
"are stuck in the door.\n"
"Quickly, now...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:84"
msgid ""
"Nun möchte ich Euch\n"
"aber nicht weiter\n"
"stören, ich werde\n"
"mich verabschieden.\n"
"Viel Spass,Old\n"
"Firehand..."
msgstr ""
"Now I won't bother\n"
"you any further, I will\n"
"take my leave.\n"
"Have fun, Old\n"
"Firehand...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:90"
msgid ""
"Die Türe ist zu, und die\n"
"Mechanik verhindert, dass\n"
"man sie aufmachen, und\n"
"durchgehen kann."
msgstr ""
"The door is closed, and the\n"
"mechanism prevents anyone\n"
"from opening it and\n"
"passing through."

msgctxt "scene:59:94"
msgid ""
"Die Schatzkammer ist, wie\n"
"auch die anderen Räume,\n"
"aus dem Felsen gehauen."
msgstr ""
"The treasure chamber is, like\n"
"the other rooms, carved\n"
"out of the rock."

msgctxt "scene:59:97"
msgid ""
"Zwei Speere sind verkreuzt\n"
"an der Wand befestigt."
msgstr ""
"Two spears are attached\n"
"crossed to the wall."

msgctxt "scene:59:99"
msgid ""
"Ein Adler-Emblem ist in\n"
"die Wand graviert, es sieht\n"
"wie das im vorangegangenen\n"
"Saal aus, sicher hat es für\n"
"die Erbauer eine Bedeutung..."
msgstr ""
"An eagle emblem is carved\n"
"into the wall, it looks\n"
"like the one in the previous\n"
"hall, surely it had a meaning\n"
"for the builders..."

msgctxt "scene:59:104"
msgid ""
"Zwischen den Speerspitzen\n"
"hängt ein Tomahawk."
msgstr ""
"Between the spearheads\n"
"hangs a tomahawk."

msgctxt "scene:59:106"
msgid ""
"Ein bodenloser Abgrund, der\n"
"wohl natürlicher Herkunft sein\n"
"muss. So einen tiefen Graben,\n"
"kann man nicht in den Felsen\n"
"hauen."
msgstr ""
"A bottomless abyss, which\n"
"must be of natural origin.\n"
"One cannot carve such a\n"
"deep trench into the rock.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "scene:59:111"
msgid "Eine schwere Steintüre."
msgstr "A heavy stone door."

msgctxt "scene:59:112"
msgid ""
"Die Schatztruhe steht auf\n"
"einem Gestell, mit Sockel\n"
"und einer Aufhängung."
msgstr ""
"The treasure chest stands on\n"
"a frame with a pedestal\n"
"and a suspension."

msgctxt "scene:59:115"
msgid ""
"Noch so eine Figur. Die sollen\n"
"wohl als Wachen für den Schatz\n"
"da stehen."
msgstr ""
"Another figure like that. They\n"
"are probably supposed to stand\n"
"there as guards."

msgctxt "scene:59:118"
msgid ""
"Die Figur hat eine ausser-\n"
"gewöhnlich grosse Nase."
msgstr ""
"The figure has an excep-\n"
"tionally large nose."

msgctxt "scene:59:120"
msgid "Eine Holzkiste."
msgstr "A wooden box."

msgctxt "scene:59:121"
msgid ""
"Ein wertvoller Goldschatz\n"
"liegt da in der Kiste. Was\n"
"für Reichtümer."
msgstr ""
"A valuable gold treasure\n"
"lies there in the box. What\n"
"immense riches."

msgctxt "scene:59:124"
msgid "Eine Holzkiste."
msgstr "A wooden box."

msgctxt "scene:59:125"
msgid ""
"Die scheinen fest an der\n"
"Wand befestigt zu sein, ich\n"
"lasse die wohl besser hängen."
msgstr ""
"They seem to be firmly\n"
"attached to the wall; I had\n"
"better leave them hanging."

msgctxt "scene:59:128"
msgid ""
"Der Adler ist in den Felsen\n"
"graviert, den kann ich nicht\n"
"wegnehmen."
msgstr ""
"The eagle is engraved in\n"
"the rock, I cannot take it\n"
"away."

msgctxt "scene:59:131"
msgid ""
"Ich werde weder versuchen da\n"
"hinunter zu klettern, noch mich\n"
"in den Abgrund stürzen."
msgstr ""
"I will neither try to climb down\n"
"there, nor throw myself into the\n"
"abyss."

msgctxt "scene:59:134"
msgid ""
"Die Konstruktion ist mir nicht\n"
"sehr geheuer, wer weiss, was da\n"
"ausgelöst wird, wenn ich an dem\n"
"Gestell herumarbeite."
msgstr ""
"The construction seems a bit suspicious\n"
"to me, who knows what might be\n"
"triggered if I tamper with the\n"
"frame."

msgctxt "scene:59:138"
msgid ""
"In einem Garten, würde die Figur\n"
"sich sicherlich gut machen, doch\n"
"ich habe keinen Garten."
msgstr ""
"In a garden the figure would\n"
"certainly look good, but I do\n"
"not have a garden."

msgctxt "scene:59:141"
msgid ""
"Wie stellst Du dir das vor, von\n"
"Hand lässt sich die Nase sicher\n"
"nicht entfernen."
msgstr ""
"How do you imagine that, by hand\n"
"the nose surely cannot be removed\n"
"that easily."

msgctxt "scene:59:144"
msgid "Eine Holzkiste."
msgstr "A wooden box."

msgctxt "scene:59:145"
msgid ""
"Wir sind hier, um den Schatz\n"
"vor dem Cornel zu retten, und\n"
"nicht, damit wir ihn vorher\n"
"stehlen."
msgstr ""
"We are here to save the\n"
"treasure from the Cornel, and\n"
"not so that we steal it\n"
"first."

msgctxt "scene:59:149"
msgid "Die lasse ich besser stehen."
msgstr "I had better leave that standing."

msgctxt "scene:59:150"
msgid ""
"Der Freund wird uns kaum ant-\n"
"worten."
msgstr ""
"Our friend will hardly answer\n"
"us."

msgctxt "scene:59:152"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen ist dafür zu\n"
"schwach."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar is too weak for\n"
"that."

msgctxt "scene:59:154"
msgid ""
"Wieso soll ich das machen, die\n"
"Kiste ist ja offen."
msgstr ""
"Why should I do that, the box\n"
"is already open."

msgctxt "scene:59:156"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich hier nichts aus-\n"
"richten."
msgstr ""
"I cannot accomplish anything here\n"
"with that."

msgctxt "scene:59:158"
msgid ""
"Nasenbohren, sollte man nicht mit\n"
"solch harten Gegenständen."
msgstr ""
"Nose-picking should not be done\n"
"with such hard objects."

msgctxt "scene:59:160"
msgid ""
"Das Gestell sieht mir sehr dubios\n"
"aus, ich werde da nichts d'ran\n"
"herumbasteln."
msgstr ""
"The frame looks very suspicious to\n"
"me, I am not going to tamper with\n"
"it at all."

msgctxt "scene:59:163"
msgid "Soll ich ihn wie einen Baum fällen?"
msgstr "Should I chop it down like a tree?"

msgctxt "scene:59:164"
msgid ""
"Dabei ginge nur der Tomahawk in\n"
"Brüche."
msgstr ""
"Only the tomahawk would break\n"
"in the process."

msgctxt "scene:59:166"
msgid ""
"Das könnte ungeahnte, negative\n"
"Folgen haben."
msgstr ""
"That could have unforeseen,\n"
"negative consequences."

msgctxt "scene:59:168"
msgid ""
"Das Problem muss systematisch\n"
"angegangen werden, mit dem\n"
"Tomahawk nur in der Gegend\n"
"herumfuchteln, hilft uns nicht\n"
"weiter."
msgstr ""
"The problem must be approached\n"
"systematically; just waving the\n"
"tomahawk around in the area\n"
"does not help us any further\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:60:0"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja der Cornel,\n"
"er versucht gerade zu\n"
"fliehen..."
msgstr ""
"There is the Cornel,\n"
"he is trying to flee\n"
"right now..."

msgctxt "scene:60:3"
msgid ""
"Der Cornel ist mit den\n"
"Tramps in den Strudel\n"
"geraten. Nun hat ihn\n"
"die gerechte Strafe er-\n"
"eilt, und der Schatz\n"
"ist gerettet und uner-\n"
"reichbar."
msgstr ""
"The Cornel got caught in the\n"
"whirlpool with the tramps.\n"
"Now his just punishment has\n"
"overtaken him, and the\n"
"treasure is saved and\n"
"unreachable for anyone\n"
"now."

msgctxt "scene:60:10"
msgid "Aaaarrrrgh..."
msgstr "Aaaarrrrgh..."

msgctxt "scene:60:11"
msgid ""
"Die Winde klemmt, ich\n"
"kann die Kurbel kein\n"
"Stück bewegen."
msgstr ""
"The winch is jammed, I\n"
"cannot move the crank\n"
"one bit."

msgctxt "scene:60:14"
msgid ""
"Ein Dunstschleier ist am\n"
"Horizont zu sehen..."
msgstr ""
"A veil of haze can be seen\n"
"on the horizon..."

msgctxt "scene:60:16"
msgid ""
"Die Berge, sind nur schemen-\n"
"haft im Dunst zu erkennen."
msgstr ""
"The mountains can only be\n"
"faintly seen in the haze."

msgctxt "scene:60:18"
msgid ""
"Ein Damm reguliert den Wasser-\n"
"stand des Sees, und treibt wohl\n"
"auch die Mechanik der verschie-\n"
"denen Vorrichtungen im Geheim-\n"
"gang an."
msgstr ""
"A dam regulates the water level\n"
"of the lake, and probably also\n"
"drives the mechanics of the\n"
"various devices in the secret\n"
"passage."

msgctxt "scene:60:23"
msgid ""
"Auf der Insel in der Mitte des\n"
"Sees, ist der Haupteingang zur\n"
"Schatzkammer."
msgstr ""
"On the island in the middle of\n"
"the lake is the main entrance\n"
"to the treasure chamber."

msgctxt "scene:60:26"
msgid ""
"Eine kleine Holzhütte, befindet\n"
"sich auf der Insel."
msgstr ""
"A small wooden hut is located\n"
"on the island."

msgctxt "scene:60:28"
msgid ""
"Der See liegt richtig idyllisch,\n"
"inmitten von Wäldern."
msgstr ""
"The lake lies truly idyllically,\n"
"surrounded by woods."

msgctxt "scene:60:30"
msgid ""
"Ein schmales Ufer säumt den\n"
"ganzen See, und zur Mine am\n"
"Berg, führt eine Schneise\n"
"durch den Wald."
msgstr ""
"A narrow shore lines the entire\n"
"lake, and a swath leads through\n"
"the forest to the mine on the\n"
"mountain."

msgctxt "scene:60:34"
msgid ""
"Ein dichter Wald, der sich um\n"
"den See breitet. Bis hierher\n"
"sind die Holzfäller noch nicht\n"
"vorgedrungen..."
msgstr ""
"A dense forest that spreads\n"
"around the lake. The loggers\n"
"have not penetrated this far\n"
"yet..."

msgctxt "scene:60:38"
msgid ""
"Steine liegen hier auf dem\n"
"Plateau herum."
msgstr ""
"Stones are lying around here\n"
"on the plateau."

msgctxt "scene:60:40"
msgid ""
"Eine Holzwinde, sie ist mit\n"
"einer eigenartigen Flüssigkeit\n"
"überzogen, muss wohl ein Schutz\n"
"vor der Witterung sein."
msgstr ""
"A wooden winch, coated with a\n"
"peculiar liquid, must probably be\n"
"a protection against the elements\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:60:44"
msgid ""
"Es scheint, dass das Plateu in\n"
"dieser Form wohl aus dem Felsen\n"
"gehauen wurde. Auf drei Seiten,\n"
"erheben sich die steilen Fels-\n"
"wände des Berges."
msgstr ""
"It seems that the plateau in this\n"
"form was carved out of the rock.\n"
"On three sides rise the steep\n"
"rock walls of the mountain\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:60:49"
msgid ""
"Sobald eine Möglichkeit besteht,\n"
"setzen sich Grünpflanzen fest, und\n"
"gedeihen selbst hier, auf dem\n"
"Felsen."
msgstr ""
"As soon as an opportunity arises,\n"
"green plants take root, and thrive\n"
"even here on the rock\n"
"itself."

msgctxt "scene:60:53"
msgid "Dieser Busch trägt rote Früchte."
msgstr "This bush bears red berries."

msgctxt "scene:60:54"
msgid ""
"Die Steine sind nur unnötiger\n"
"Ballast."
msgstr ""
"The stones are only unnecessary\n"
"ballast."

msgctxt "scene:60:56"
msgid ""
"Da ist kein Hebel oder Kurbel an\n"
"der Winde, ich kann nichts machen."
msgstr ""
"There is no lever or crank on the\n"
"winch, I cannot do anything."

msgctxt "scene:60:58"
msgid ""
"Weiter auf den steilen Berg\n"
"möchte ich nicht klettern, da\n"
"sind keine Stufen und ohne\n"
"Sicherung ist das sehr ge-\n"
"fährlich, und meiner Meinung\n"
"nach, auch unnötig."
msgstr ""
"I do not want to climb further up\n"
"the steep mountain, there are no\n"
"steps and without safety gear it\n"
"is very dangerous, and in my\n"
"opinion unnecessary as well\n"
"here."

msgctxt "scene:60:64"
msgid "Mich stört der Busch nicht..."
msgstr "The bush does not bother me..."

msgctxt "scene:60:65"
msgid ""
"Man sollte Früchte, die man nicht\n"
"kennt, nicht einfach essen, dass\n"
"könnte fatale Folgen haben. Ich \n"
"werde diese Früchte nicht essen."
msgstr ""
"One should not simply eat fruits\n"
"that one does not know, that could\n"
"have fatal consequences. I will\n"
"not eat these fruits."

msgctxt "scene:60:69"
msgid "Ein Schweigen im Walde..."
msgstr "Silence in the forest..."

msgctxt "scene:60:70"
msgid ""
"Damit beschädige ich nur die\n"
"Winde, und dann geht gar nichts\n"
"mehr."
msgstr ""
"With that I will only damage the\n"
"winch, and then nothing works\n"
"at all anymore."

msgctxt "scene:60:73"
msgid ""
"Die brechen da nur ab, und\n"
"eigentlich wollte ich mir\n"
"die als Andenken an das\n"
"Abenteuer aufbehalten."
msgstr ""
"They will only break off, and\n"
"actually I wanted to keep\n"
"them as a souvenir of\n"
"the adventure."

msgctxt "scene:60:77"
msgid ""
"Nicht doch, damit mache ich\n"
"die Winde ja kaputt."
msgstr ""
"No, with that I will only\n"
"break the winch."

msgctxt "scene:60:79"
msgid "Gutes Zureden hilft da wenig."
msgstr "Persuasion won't help much here."

msgctxt "scene:61:0"
msgid "THE END"
msgstr "THE END"

msgctxt "scene:61:1"
msgid "MITGEWIRKT AN"
msgstr "CONTRIBUTED TO"

msgctxt "scene:61:2"
msgid "DER ENTWICKLUNG"
msgstr "THE DEVELOPMENT"

msgctxt "scene:61:3"
msgid "DES SPIELES"
msgstr "OF THE GAME"

msgctxt "scene:61:4"
msgid "HABEN"
msgstr "HAVE"

msgctxt "scene:61:5"
msgid "ARNDT HASCH"
msgstr "ARNDT HASCH"

msgctxt "scene:61:6"
msgid "GERLINDE GRIMMER"
msgstr "GERLINDE GRIMMER"

msgctxt "scene:61:7"
msgid "CHRISTIAN MICHEL"
msgstr "CHRISTIAN MICHEL"

msgctxt "scene:61:8"
msgid "MATTHIAS STEINWACHS"
msgstr "MATTHIAS STEINWACHS"

msgctxt "scene:61:9"
msgid "ROLF FEUSI"
msgstr "ROLF FEUSI"

msgctxt "scene:61:10"
msgid "MARKUS MUCKENSCHNABL"
msgstr "MARKUS MUCKENSCHNABL"

msgctxt "scene:61:11"
msgid "CHRISTIAN PREISSL"
msgstr "CHRISTIAN PREISSL"

msgctxt "scene:61:12"
msgid "MICHAEL TSCHOEGL"
msgstr "MICHAEL TSCHOEGL"

msgctxt "scene:61:13"
msgid "MARKUS GRIMMER"
msgstr "MARKUS GRIMMER"

msgctxt "scene:61:14"
msgid "CARSTEN KISSLAT"
msgstr "CARSTEN KISSLAT"

msgctxt "scene:61:15"
msgid "PETER KRAINER"
msgstr "PETER KRAINER"

msgctxt "scene:61:16"
msgid "JUDITH NUNN"
msgstr "JUDITH NUNN"

msgctxt "scene:61:17"
msgid "ELFRIEDE BOSONNET"
msgstr "ELFRIEDE BOSONNET"

msgctxt "scene:61:18"
msgid "SCHON BALD TREFFEN"
msgstr "SOON WE WILL MEET"

msgctxt "scene:61:19"
msgid "WIR UNS IM"
msgstr "AGAIN IN THE"

msgctxt "scene:61:20"
msgid "NAECHSTEN"
msgstr "NEXT"

msgctxt "scene:61:21"
msgid "KARLMAY ABENTEUER..."
msgstr "KARL MAY ADVENTURE..."

msgctxt "scene:61:22"
msgid "IM FRUEHJAHR BEI"
msgstr "IN SPRING AT"

msgctxt "scene:61:23"
msgid "EUREM HAENDLER"
msgstr "YOUR DEALER"

msgctxt "scene:61:24"
msgid "IN"
msgstr "IN"

msgctxt "scene:61:25"
msgid "DURCH DIE WÜSTE"
msgstr "THROUGH THE DESERT"

msgctxt "scene:61:26"
msgid "BIS BALD"
msgstr "SEE YOU SOON"

msgctxt "object:1:0"
msgid "Hallo, ich bin Old Firehand."
msgstr "Hello, I am Old Firehand."

msgctxt "object:1:1"
msgid ""
"Für Selbstgespräche habe\n"
"ich nicht sehr viel übrig."
msgstr ""
"I have little use for\n"
"talking to myself."

msgctxt "object:2:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Arkansaserfahrener\n"
"Captain, wie man ihn sich\n"
"nur wünschen kann. Den\n"
"kann so leicht nichts er-\n"
"schüttern."
msgstr ""
"An Arkansas-seasoned\n"
"captain as fine as one\n"
"could wish for. Nothing\n"
"shaketh him easily.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:4:0"
msgid ""
"Der schwarze Bootsjunge\n"
"des Captains."
msgstr ""
"The captain's black\n"
"cabin boy."

msgctxt "object:6:0"
msgid ""
"Dieser Tramp scheint\n"
"gelangweilt zu sein."
msgstr ""
"This tramp appears to\n"
"be bored."

msgctxt "object:6:2"
msgid "Hallo, Fremder..."
msgstr "Hello, stranger..."

msgctxt "object:6:3"
msgid ""
"Halt! Siehst Du\n"
"nicht, das Du\n"
"störst?"
msgstr ""
"Halt! Can you not\n"
"see that you are\n"
"bothering me?"

msgctxt "object:6:6"
msgid ""
"Der scheint mir für\n"
"Gespräche nicht auf-\n"
"gelegt zu sein."
msgstr ""
"He seems in no mood\n"
"for conversation.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:7:0"
msgid ""
"Das Mädchen ist in ernster\n"
"Gefahr. Wenn es noch lange\n"
"herumfuchtelt, dann wird\n"
"der Panther nur noch mehr\n"
"gereizt."
msgstr ""
"The girl is in grave\n"
"danger. If she flails\n"
"about much longer, the\n"
"panther shall be provoked\n"
"even further."

msgctxt "object:8:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Brett, das von der\n"
"Pantherkiste abgebrochen\n"
"ist."
msgstr ""
"A board broken off\n"
"from the panther's\n"
"crate."

msgctxt "object:8:3"
msgid ""
"Nimm bitte den Ausspruch:\n"
"EIN BRETT VOR DEN KOPF\n"
"NAGELN, nicht so wörtlich."
msgstr ""
"Please do not take the\n"
"saying TO NAIL A BOARD\n"
"TO ONE'S HEAD so literally."

msgctxt "object:8:6"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich an dem\n"
"Brett herumschnitzen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I carve\n"
"upon the board?"

msgctxt "object:8:8"
msgid ""
"Halt, nicht das Mädchen\n"
"bedroht den Panther!\n"
"Der Panther ist hier\n"
"der störende Faktor.\n"
"Also berücksichtigen\n"
"wir das, und gehen nicht\n"
"auch noch auf das Mädchen\n"
"los."
msgstr ""
"Hold! The girl is not\n"
"threatening the panther!\n"
"The panther is the nuisance\n"
"here. So let us consider\n"
"that and not attack\n"
"the girl as well.­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:9:0"
msgid ""
"Was für ein gewaltiges Tier.\n"
"Jetzt heisst es schnell han-\n"
"deln, bevor dem Mädchen etwas\n"
"geschieht."
msgstr ""
"What a mighty beast.\n"
"Now we must act swiftly\n"
"before harm befalleth\n"
"the maiden."

msgctxt "object:9:4"
msgid ""
"Was für eine alberne Idee,\n"
"einen wütenden Panther an-\n"
"sprechen zu wollen. Das\n"
"kann wohl nur einem Green-\n"
"horn einfallen."
msgstr ""
"What a foolish idea,\n"
"to speak to an angry\n"
"panther. Only a greenhorn\n"
"could think of that.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:12:0"
msgid ""
"Unsere Droll ist in\n"
"einer misslichen Lage.\n"
"Es muss Ihr umgehend\n"
"geholfen werden."
msgstr ""
"Our Droll is in a\n"
"precarious plight.\n"
"She must be aided at once.­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:12:4"
msgid ""
"Es wäre wohl nicht sehr\n"
"weise, die Aufmerksam-\n"
"keit der Tramps auf\n"
"sich zu lenken."
msgstr ""
"It would scarce be wise\n"
"to draw the attention of\n"
"the tramps unto ourselves.­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:12:8"
msgid ""
"Droll friert sicher nicht\n"
"am Kopf, ihre Probleme\n"
"sind eher anderer Natur."
msgstr ""
"Droll's head is surely\n"
"not cold; her troubles\n"
"are rather of another kind."

msgctxt "object:12:11"
msgid ""
"Droll mit Steinen zu\n"
"bewerfen, wäre nicht\n"
"gerade die feine Art."
msgstr ""
"Pelting Droll with\n"
"stones would scarce be\n"
"a polite gesture."

msgctxt "object:12:14"
msgid ""
"Hallo, ich glaube etwas\n"
"richtigstellen zu müssen -\n"
"Droll verliert nicht die\n"
"Hosen, sondern sollte be-\n"
"freit werden."
msgstr ""
"Hold, I must set something\n"
"straight-Droll is not losing\n"
"his trousers, but ought to\n"
"be set free.­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:12:19"
msgid ""
"In die Nähe von Droll\n"
"komme ich nicht, und wenn\n"
"ich den Schürhaken werfe,\n"
"treffe ich bestimmt Droll.\n"
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"ihm das gut bekommt."
msgstr ""
"I cannot get near Droll,\n"
"and if I throw the poker, I\n"
"shall surely hit Droll. I\n"
"deem that would not suit him.­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:12:25"
msgid ""
"Was soll Droll damit\n"
"anfangen, er hat ja\n"
"nicht einmal eine Hand\n"
"frei, um die Brotkrümel\n"
"herauszuklauben. Zudem\n"
"ist das Brot schimmelig."
msgstr ""
"What is Droll to do with\n"
"that? He hath not even a\n"
"hand free to pick out\n"
"the breadcrumbs.\n"
"Besides, the bread is\n"
"moldy."

msgctxt "object:12:31"
msgid ""
"Auf Ideen kommst Du,\n"
"was soll Droll mit\n"
"einem kaputten Käfig\n"
"anfangen?"
msgstr ""
"The ideas you have!\n"
"What should Droll do\n"
"with a broken cage\n"
"anyway?"

msgctxt "object:12:35"
msgid ""
"Sicher, Droll steht in so\n"
"einer Lage der Sinn nach\n"
"einem Vogelkäfig, und vie-\n"
"leicht noch ein Aquarium..?"
msgstr ""
"To be sure, in such a\n"
"plight Droll's mind\n"
"turns to a birdcage, and\n"
"perchance a fish tank..?"

msgctxt "object:12:39"
msgid ""
"Genau, eine Landkarte ist das,\n"
"was Droll jetzt braucht, um\n"
"den Fluchtweg zu studieren."
msgstr ""
"Indeed, a map is just\n"
"what Droll needs now to\n"
"study the escape route."

msgctxt "object:12:42"
msgid ""
"Jetz würde nur noch eine\n"
"Zahnbürste fehlen und Droll\n"
"wäre reisefertig..."
msgstr ""
"Now only a toothbrush is\n"
"missing and Droll would\n"
"be ready to travel..."

msgctxt "object:12:45"
msgid ""
"Bei einer solchen Fürsorge,\n"
"braucht sich Droll keine\n"
"Gedanken zu machen, eventuell\n"
"frieren zu müssen."
msgstr ""
"With such thoughtful\n"
"care, Droll need not\n"
"worry about perchance\n"
"freezing."

msgctxt "object:12:49"
msgid ""
"Super, darin kann Droll\n"
"die Murmelsammlung auf-\n"
"bewahren..."
msgstr ""
"Splendid, therein Droll\n"
"may keep his marble\n"
"collection..."

msgctxt "object:12:52"
msgid ""
"Wir haben nicht Karneval,\n"
"das ist der Wilde Westen.\n"
"Was soll Droll, verschnürt\n"
"wie ein Paket, mit einem\n"
"Beutel voller Knallfrösche?"
msgstr ""
"It is not carnival\n"
"time, this is the Wild\n"
"West. What is Droll to\n"
"do, bound like a parcel,\n"
"with bag of crackers?"

msgctxt "object:12:57"
msgid ""
"Mit welcher Hand soll er\n"
"den Knaller fangen, ver-\n"
"schnürt wie er ist.!?"
msgstr ""
"With which hand is he to\n"
"catch the cracker, bound\n"
"as he is!?"

msgctxt "object:12:60"
msgid ""
"Eine Reise, die ist lustig,\n"
"eine Reise, die... Nur mit\n"
"Fesseln geht alles viel\n"
"mühsamer..."
msgstr ""
"Oh, to boat upon the ocean,\n"
"Oh, to float... Only with\n"
"fetters everything is\n"
"far more arduous..."

msgctxt "object:12:64"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"der Cornel unserer Droll\n"
"Urlaub genehmigt."
msgstr ""
"I believe not that the\n"
"Cornel shall grant our\n"
"Droll a vacation."

msgctxt "object:12:67"
msgid ""
"Mit einem gezielten Wurf,\n"
"könnte ich Droll befreien,\n"
"doch treffe ich nicht\n"
"richtig, dann fühlt sich\n"
"Droll wohl wie ein Fakir..."
msgstr ""
"With an aimed throw\n"
"I could free Droll,\n"
"yet if I miss, Droll\n"
"shall feel like a\n"
"fakir..."

msgctxt "object:12:72"
msgid ""
"Die Gefahr einer akuten\n"
"Angina besteht wohl zur\n"
"Zeit nicht..."
msgstr ""
"The danger of acute sore\n"
"throat is scarce a\n"
"concern at present..."

msgctxt "object:12:75"
msgid ""
"Droll war einem kräftigen\n"
"Schluck noch nie abgeneigt,\n"
"doch in dieser Situation..."
msgstr ""
"Droll was never averse\n"
"to a hearty draught, yet\n"
"in this situation..."

msgctxt "object:13:0"
msgid ""
"Ing. Patterson, ein\n"
"rechtschaffener Mann."
msgstr ""
"Engineer Patterson, an\n"
"upright man."

msgctxt "object:13:2"
msgid ""
"So etwas tut man nicht,\n"
"denn eine solche Tat\n"
"macht keine Freunde."
msgstr ""
"One doth not do such a\n"
"thing, for such a deed\n"
"winseth no friends."

msgctxt "object:13:5"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube es nicht,\n"
"das kann wohl nicht\n"
"ernst gemeint sein.\n"
"Warum sollte ich\n"
"diesen ehrenwerten\n"
"Mann angreifen?"
msgstr ""
"I cannot believe it;\n"
"that can scarce be\n"
"meant in earnest.\n"
"Why should I attack\n"
"this honorable\n"
"man?"

msgctxt "object:15:0"
msgid ""
"Die Tramps führen\n"
"was im Schilde!\n"
"Was die wohl wieder\n"
"planen???"
msgstr ""
"The tramps are up to\n"
"something! What might\n"
"they be plotting\n"
"now???"

msgctxt "object:15:4"
msgid ""
"Bei dem dubiosen\n"
"Gespräch, sollte man\n"
"die beiden lieber\n"
"nicht stören."
msgstr ""
"During that dubious\n"
"conversation, one had\n"
"best not disturb the\n"
"two."

msgctxt "object:16:0"
msgid "Ein leeres Holzfass."
msgstr "An empty wooden barrel."

msgctxt "object:16:1"
msgid ""
"Wenn es etwas grösser wäre,\n"
"könnte ich mich wohl darin\n"
"verstecken, aber so..."
msgstr ""
"Were it somewhat larger,\n"
"I might hide inside, but\n"
"as it is..."

msgctxt "object:16:4"
msgid ""
"Soll ich jetzt Verzierungen\n"
"in das Fass schnitzen?"
msgstr ""
"Am I now to carve\n"
"ornaments into the barrel?"

msgctxt "object:17:0"
msgid ""
"Das Bowiemesser von\n"
"Patterson."
msgstr ""
"Patterson's Bowie\n"
"knife."

msgctxt "object:17:2"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte das Messer\n"
"von Patterson nicht\n"
"öffnen, das wäre ein\n"
"Vertrauensbruch."
msgstr ""
"I ought not to open\n"
"Patterson's knife; that\n"
"would be a breach of\n"
"trust."

msgctxt "object:17:6"
msgid ""
"Mir scheint, dass es\n"
"jetzt an der Zeit ist,\n"
"über eine Trennung in\n"
"Freundschaft zu sprechen.\n"
"Ich habe nicht vor\n"
"Selbstmord zu begehen!"
msgstr ""
"It seems to me that\n"
"the time has come to\n"
"speak of an amicable\n"
"parting. I have no\n"
"intention of\n"
"committing suicide!"

msgctxt "object:17:12"
msgid ""
"Mir ist rohe Gewalt ein\n"
"Greuel und ich werde sie zu\n"
"vermeiden wissen, wann\n"
"immer ich kann."
msgstr ""
"Brute force is an\n"
"abomination to me, and I\n"
"shall know how to avoid\n"
"it whenever I can."

msgctxt "object:17:16"
msgid ""
"Der Cornel ist zwar sicher-\n"
"lich ein schlechter Mann,\n"
"der den Tod schon mehr wie\n"
"einmal verdient, aber er muss\n"
"vor ein ordentliches Gericht."
msgstr ""
"The Cornel is surely an\n"
"evil man who hath\n"
"deserved death more than\n"
"once, but he must face a\n"
"proper court of justice."

msgctxt "object:17:21"
msgid ""
"Ich möchte Blutvergiessen\n"
"vermeiden, denn Gewalt ver-\n"
"ursacht nur Schaden..."
msgstr ""
"I wish to avoid\n"
"bloodshed, for violence\n"
"causeth only harm..."

msgctxt "object:19:0"
msgid ""
"Die scheinen ein\n"
"wichtiges Gespräch\n"
"zu führen."
msgstr ""
"They seem to be\n"
"having an important\n"
"conversation."

msgctxt "object:19:3"
msgid ""
"Es wäre schlecht,\n"
"die beiden zu\n"
"stören."
msgstr ""
"It would be unwise\n"
"to disturb the\n"
"two of them."

msgctxt "object:20:0"
msgid "Der Eimer ist voll Wasser."
msgstr "The bucket is full of water."

msgctxt "object:20:1"
msgid ""
"Das würde Dir so passen,\n"
"dass ich mir den vollen\n"
"Eimer aufsetze..."
msgstr ""
"That would suit you well,\n"
"putting a full bucket\n"
"upon my head..."

msgctxt "object:23:0"
msgid ""
"Eine offene und leere\n"
"Hutschachtel."
msgstr ""
"An open and empty\n"
"hatbox."

msgctxt "object:23:2"
msgid ""
"Ha, jetzt wird es aber\n"
"etwas absurd. Nun soll\n"
"ich mir schon eine Hut-\n"
"schachtel aufsetzen..."
msgstr ""
"Ha, now it groweth a bit\n"
"absurd. Am I now to put\n"
"a hatbox upon my\n"
"head..."

msgctxt "object:23:6"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich die\n"
"Schachtel zerschnip-\n"
"peln?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I shred\n"
"the box into\n"
"pieces?"

msgctxt "object:23:9"
msgid ""
"Die Schachtel wird ja\n"
"nass..."
msgstr ""
"The box will get\n"
"wet..."

msgctxt "object:23:11"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tue,\n"
"wird die Schachtel\n"
"beschädigt, und die\n"
"Dame aus der Kabine\n"
"wird mir ganz schön\n"
"einheizen..."
msgstr ""
"If I do that, the\n"
"hatbox shall be damaged,\n"
"and the lady from the\n"
"cabin shall make it\n"
"quite hot for me...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:23:17"
msgid ""
"Nein, die Kakerlake\n"
"pack ich nicht in\n"
"die Schachtel, denn\n"
"wenn ich sie vergesse,\n"
"wird die Dame nicht\n"
"viel Freude mit mir\n"
"haben..."
msgstr ""
"No, I shall not put\n"
"the cockroach into the\n"
"box, for if I forget it,\n"
"the lady shall not have\n"
"much pleasure with me...\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:24:0"
msgid "Ein Damenhut mit Schleier."
msgstr "A lady's hat with a veil."

msgctxt "object:24:1"
msgid ""
"Nein, nein, ich habe ja\n"
"bereits einen Hut."
msgstr ""
"No, no, I already have\n"
"a hat."

msgctxt "object:25:0"
msgid ""
"Wie soll ich denn\n"
"den Hut in die ge-\n"
"schlossene Schachtel\n"
"hineinlegen?"
msgstr ""
"How am I to put the\n"
"hat into the closed\n"
"hatbox?\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:25:4"
msgid "Eine geschlossene Hutschachtel."
msgstr "A closed hatbox."

msgctxt "object:25:5"
msgid ""
"Ich sollte die Schachtel\n"
"erst einmal aufmachen."
msgstr ""
"I ought to open the\n"
"box first."

msgctxt "object:25:7"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich die\n"
"Schachtel zerschnip-\n"
"peln?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I shred\n"
"the box into\n"
"pieces?"

msgctxt "object:25:10"
msgid ""
"Die Schachtel wird ja\n"
"nass..."
msgstr ""
"The box will get\n"
"wet..."

msgctxt "object:25:12"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tue,\n"
"wird die Schachtel\n"
"beschädigt, und die\n"
"Dame aus der Kabine\n"
"wird mir ganz schön\n"
"einheizen..."
msgstr ""
"If I do that, the\n"
"hatbox shall be damaged,\n"
"and the lady from the\n"
"cabin shall make it\n"
"quite hot for me...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:25:18"
msgid ""
"In eine geschlossene\n"
"Hutschachtel kann ich\n"
"nichts hineinpacken,\n"
"und als Kakerlaken-\n"
"futter taugt sie nicht."
msgstr ""
"Into a closed hatbox\n"
"I cannot pack a thing,\n"
"and it is no good as\n"
"cockroach food.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:26:0"
msgid "Ein leerer Metalleimer."
msgstr "An empty metal bucket."

msgctxt "object:26:1"
msgid ""
"Well, mir scheint, dass\n"
"Dir mein Freund, nicht\n"
"klar ist, dass ein echter\n"
"Westmann sich keine Eimer\n"
"über den Kopf stülpt..."
msgstr ""
"Well, it seemeth to me\n"
"you realize not that a\n"
"true Westman doth not put\n"
"buckets over his head...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:27:0"
msgid "Ein Feuerhaken."
msgstr "A poker."

msgctxt "object:28:0"
msgid ""
"Ein etwas schmuddeliger\n"
"Lappen."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat dingy\n"
"rag."

msgctxt "object:28:2"
msgid ""
"Ich brauche kein\n"
"Kopftuch."
msgstr ""
"I need no\n"
"headscarf."

msgctxt "object:28:4"
msgid ""
"Der Lappen ist so klein,\n"
"dass es sich nicht lohnt,\n"
"ihn in Stücke zu schnei-\n"
"den."
msgstr ""
"The rag is so small that\n"
"it is not worth cutting\n"
"it into pieces.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:29:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Brett in einen Lappen\n"
"eingewickelt."
msgstr ""
"A board wrapped in\n"
"a rag."

msgctxt "object:29:2"
msgid ""
"Jetzt habe ich mühsam\n"
"den Lappen um das Brett\n"
"befestigt, und nun soll\n"
"ich ihn wiederum weg-\n"
"schneiden?! Das wäre\n"
"sinnlos..."
msgstr ""
"Now I painstakingly\n"
"wrapped the rag around\n"
"the board, and now I am\n"
"to cut it off again?!\n"
"That would be senseless...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:30:0"
msgid "Eine Kohlenschaufel."
msgstr "A coal shovel."

msgctxt "object:32:0"
msgid "Eine Kakerlake."
msgstr "A cockroach."

msgctxt "object:32:1"
msgid ""
"Was?! Das kann wohl nur\n"
"ein dummer Scherz sein.\n"
"Ich werde niemals einen\n"
"Kakerlaken essen!!!"
msgstr ""
"What?! That can only be\n"
"a foolish jest.\n"
"I shall never eat a\n"
"cockroach!!!"

msgctxt "object:32:5"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube kaum, dass der\n"
"Tramp sich vor einem\n"
"Kakerlaken schrecken wird."
msgstr ""
"I scarce believe the\n"
"tramp shall be frightened\n"
"by a cockroach."

msgctxt "object:34:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Tasse voll\n"
"Tinte."
msgstr ""
"A cup full of\n"
"ink."

msgctxt "object:35:0"
msgid "Eine Tasse."
msgstr "A cup."

msgctxt "object:36:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Axt, die wie\n"
"neu aussieht."
msgstr ""
"An axe that looks\n"
"as good as new."

msgctxt "object:37:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Axtklinge,\n"
"leicht ange-\n"
"schwärzt vom\n"
"Feuer."
msgstr ""
"An axe blade,\n"
"slightly blackened\n"
"by the fire.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:38:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Reservestiel für\n"
"eine Axt, offenbar\n"
"noch nie gebraucht."
msgstr ""
"A spare handle for\n"
"an axe, seemingly\n"
"never used."

msgctxt "object:39:0"
msgid ""
"Das ist Branshky, ein\n"
"gerissener Geschäfts-\n"
"mann..."
msgstr ""
"That is Branshky, a\n"
"cunning businessman...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:39:3"
msgid ""
"Da ist ja mein Messer,\n"
"das haben Sie sicher\n"
"hinten am Weg gefunden.\n"
"Behalten Sie es, Sie\n"
"haben es ja gefunden."
msgstr ""
"There is my knife;\n"
"you surely found it back\n"
"along the path. Keep it,\n"
"for you have found it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:39:8"
msgid ""
"Kitzeln Sie mich nicht\n"
"mit diesem Zeug, ich bin\n"
"allergisch darauf."
msgstr ""
"Do not tickle me with\n"
"that stuff; I am\n"
"allergic to it."

msgctxt "object:39:11"
msgid ""
"Ohne die Klinge nützt\n"
"mir dieser Axtstiel\n"
"nichts."
msgstr ""
"Without the blade,\n"
"this axe handle is of\n"
"no use to me."

msgctxt "object:40:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Brief an einen\n"
"Daniel...\n"
"Lieber Neffe Daniel,\n"
"ich habe mich über\n"
"Deinen Besuch im\n"
"Winter vor zwei Jah-\n"
"ren sehr gefreut."
msgstr ""
"A letter to one\n"
"Daniel...\n"
"Dear nephew Daniel,\n"
"I was very pleased with\n"
"your visit two years\n"
"ago in the winter.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:40:7"
msgid ""
"Ich mache mir Sorgen,\n"
"dass Du Dich erkäl-\n"
"ten könntest. Wie Du\n"
"mir ja erzählt hast,\n"
"herrscht ein kaltes\n"
"und rauhes Klima bei\n"
"Euch im Wald. Aus\n"
"diesem Grunde habe"
msgstr ""
"I am worried that you\n"
"might catch a cold.\n"
"As you told me, a cold\n"
"and harsh climate\n"
"reigneth in your forest.\n"
"For that reason I have\n"
"knitted for you\n"
"the enclosed scarf."

msgctxt "object:40:15"
msgid ""
"ich Dir den beiliegen-\n"
"den Schal gestrickt.\n"
"Onkel Joseph meinte\n"
"zwar, Du würdest so\n"
"etwas nicht anziehen,\n"
"doch ich weiss, dass\n"
"mein Junge sich über"
msgstr ""
"Uncle Joseph thought\n"
"you would not wear\n"
"such a thing, but I\n"
"know that my boy shall\n"
"be very pleased with\n"
"the scarf.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:40:22"
msgid ""
"den Schal sehr freuen\n"
"wird.\n"
"Bitte lass nicht\n"
"wieder 10 Jahre ver-\n"
"streichen bevor Du\n"
"uns besuchst.\n"
"Deine liebe Tante\n"
"Amalie."
msgstr ""
"Please do not let 10\n"
"years pass again before\n"
"you visit us.\n"
"Your dear Aunt Amalie.\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:40:30"
msgid ""
"Der hat sich so sehr\n"
"gefreut, dass er das\n"
"Paket gleich hier im\n"
"Dachboden verstaut\n"
"hat..."
msgstr ""
"He was so delighted\n"
"that he stowed the\n"
"parcel right here in\n"
"the attic...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:41:0"
msgid "Verschimmeltes Brot!"
msgstr "Moldy bread!"

msgctxt "object:41:1"
msgid ""
"Was!? Ich soll\n"
"verschimmeltes\n"
"Brot essen? Das\n"
"ist ungesund."
msgstr ""
"What!? Am I to eat\n"
"moldy bread?\n"
"That is unhealthy.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:41:5"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit dem\n"
"verschimmelten Brot\n"
"anfangen? Wenn ich\n"
"Sie nun nicht kennen\n"
"würde, müsste ich das\n"
"als Beleidigung auf-\n"
"fassen."
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with\n"
"the moldy bread? Were\n"
"I not acquainted with\n"
"you, I should take that\n"
"as an insult.\n"
"­\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:42:0"
msgid ""
"Etwas älter schon,\n"
"aber noch gutes Brot."
msgstr ""
"A bit stale, but\n"
"still good bread."

msgctxt "object:42:2"
msgid "Das Brot war sehr gut."
msgstr "The bread was very good."

msgctxt "object:42:3"
msgid ""
"Hmmm, gut das Brot,\n"
"doch soll ich es\n"
"wirklich essen?"
msgstr ""
"Hmmm, good bread,\n"
"yet am I truly to\n"
"eat it?"

msgctxt "object:43:0"
msgid "Ein offenes Kuvert."
msgstr "An open envelope."

msgctxt "object:44:0"
msgid ""
"Ein verschlossenes\n"
"Kuvert."
msgstr ""
"A sealed\n"
"envelope."

msgctxt "object:45:0"
msgid ""
"Das ist eine Waschbär-\n"
"mütze erster Güte."
msgstr ""
"That is a coonskin\n"
"cap of finest quality."

msgctxt "object:45:2"
msgid ""
"Ich habe schon eine solche\n"
"Mütze, und von der trenne ich\n"
"mich nicht mehr."
msgstr ""
"I already possess such a\n"
"cap, and from it I shall\n"
"part no more."

msgctxt "object:45:5"
msgid ""
"Ich könnte versuchen, dem\n"
"die Mütze über die Augen\n"
"zu ziehen und hoffen, er\n"
"sieht mich dann nicht\n"
"mehr, aber nur wenn ich\n"
"verrückt wäre..."
msgstr ""
"I could try to pull the\n"
"cap over his eyes and\n"
"hope he sees me no\n"
"more, but only if I were\n"
"mad...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:45:11"
msgid ""
"Der hat ja einen Hut und\n"
"braucht keine Mütze."
msgstr ""
"He already has a hat\n"
"and needs no cap."

msgctxt "object:45:13"
msgid ""
"Sie gehört ihm, aber ich\n"
"bezweifle, dass er sich\n"
"erkenntlich zeigen wird,\n"
"wenn ich die Mütze zurück-\n"
"gebe."
msgstr ""
"It belongs to him, yet I\n"
"doubt he shall show himself\n"
"grateful if I return\n"
"the cap.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:45:18"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich die Mütze\n"
"in Stücke schneiden..?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I cut the\n"
"cap into pieces..?"

msgctxt "object:45:20"
msgid ""
"Danke, ich bin kein\n"
"Mützentyp. Ich trage\n"
"lieber eine Melone."
msgstr ""
"Thank you, I am no\n"
"cap person. I prefer\n"
"to wear a bowler."

msgctxt "object:46:0"
msgid "Ein Whiskyglas..."
msgstr "A whisky glass..."

msgctxt "object:47:0"
msgid "Ein alter Ledergürtel."
msgstr "An old leather belt."

msgctxt "object:48:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Schürhaken, der\n"
"wie ein Brecheisen\n"
"gebogen ist."
msgstr ""
"A poker that is\n"
"bent like a\n"
"crowbar."

msgctxt "object:49:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Wachhund...\n"
"Der wird mich\n"
"kaum vorbei\n"
"lassen."
msgstr ""
"A watchdog...\n"
"He will scarce\n"
"let me pass\n"
"by."

msgctxt "object:49:4"
msgid ""
"Ich glaube nicht, dass\n"
"mich dies weiterbrin-\n"
"gen wird.\n"
"Aber ich kann es ja\n"
"versuchen..."
msgstr ""
"I believe not that\n"
"this shall get me\n"
"any further.\n"
"Yet I can surely\n"
"try..."

msgctxt "object:49:9"
msgid ""
"Braver' Hund,\n"
"guter Hund!'..."
msgstr ""
"Good dog,\n"
"fine dog!'..."

msgctxt "object:49:11"
msgid "Groarrr, Wau, GRRRRRR"
msgstr "Groarrr, Woof, GRRRRRR"

msgctxt "object:49:12"
msgid "Ich hab's ja gesagt."
msgstr "I told you so."

msgctxt "object:49:13"
msgid ""
"Die frisch gewaschenen\n"
"Kleider kann ich nicht\n"
"dem Hund hinwerfen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot throw the\n"
"freshly washed clothes\n"
"to the dog."

msgctxt "object:49:16"
msgid ""
"Man sollte nicht mit\n"
"Steinen nach dem Hund\n"
"werfen, er tut ja nur\n"
"seine Pflicht, und es\n"
"wäre beinahe Tierqäle-\n"
"rei."
msgstr ""
"One ought not to throw\n"
"stones at the dog, he\n"
"is only doing his duty,\n"
"and it would be well-\n"
"nigh cruelty to\n"
"animals."

msgctxt "object:49:22"
msgid ""
"Nicht doch, ich habe kei-\n"
"nen Grund den Hund umzu-\n"
"bringen, da muss es eine\n"
"andere Lösung geben."
msgstr ""
"Nay, I have no cause\n"
"to kill the dog; there\n"
"must be another\n"
"solution."

msgctxt "object:52:0"
msgid "Ein massives Brett."
msgstr "A solid board."

msgctxt "object:54:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Vogelkäfig mit\n"
"Brotkrumen am Käfig-\n"
"boden."
msgstr ""
"A birdcage with\n"
"breadcrumbs on the\n"
"bottom."

msgctxt "object:55:0"
msgid ""
"Ein kaputter\n"
"Vogelkäfig."
msgstr ""
"A broken\n"
"birdcage."

msgctxt "object:56:0"
msgid "Ein leerer Vogelkäfig."
msgstr "An empty birdcage."

msgctxt "object:57:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Vogelkäfig mit\n"
"einer zahmen Dole."
msgstr ""
"A birdcage with\n"
"a tame jackdaw."

msgctxt "object:58:0"
msgid ""
"Eine sehr genaue Land-\n"
"karte von diesem Gebiet."
msgstr ""
"A very accurate map\n"
"of this region."

msgctxt "object:60:0"
msgid "Ein paar Kieselsteine."
msgstr "A few pebbles."

msgctxt "object:60:1"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich das tue, werde\n"
"ich sicher von den Tramps\n"
"ebenfalls geschnappt, und\n"
"ich kann Droll nicht mehr\n"
"helfen."
msgstr ""
"If I do that, I shall\n"
"surely be nabbed by the\n"
"tramps as well, and\n"
"can help Droll no\n"
"more."

msgctxt "object:60:6"
msgid ""
"Den würde ich sicher von\n"
"hier aus treffen, doch es\n"
"hilft mir nicht Droll zu\n"
"befreien."
msgstr ""
"Him I could surely hit\n"
"from here, yet it doth\n"
"not help me free\n"
"Droll."

msgctxt "object:60:10"
msgid ""
"Den Tramp wütend zu machen,\n"
"hilft mir nicht, Droll zu\n"
"befreien."
msgstr ""
"Making the tramp angry\n"
"doth not help me free\n"
"Droll."

msgctxt "object:60:13"
msgid ""
"Mein lieber Firehand,\n"
"was soll ich mit ein\n"
"paar Steinen anfangen,\n"
"wenn ich welche brau-\n"
"che, dann gehe ich\n"
"runter zum Fluss."
msgstr ""
"My dear Firehand, what\n"
"am I to do with a few\n"
"stones; if I need any,\n"
"I shall go down\n"
"to the river.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:61:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Koffer voller\n"
"Wäsche. Wegen des\n"
"kaputten Schlosses,\n"
"kann man ihn nicht\n"
"zumachen."
msgstr ""
"A suitcase full of\n"
"linen. Because of\n"
"the broken lock,\n"
"one cannot close\n"
"it."

msgctxt "object:62:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Stapel frisch\n"
"gewaschener Kleider."
msgstr ""
"A stack of freshly\n"
"washed clothes."

msgctxt "object:62:2"
msgid ""
"Die Kleider haben nicht\n"
"meine Grösse"
msgstr ""
"The clothes are not\n"
"my size"

msgctxt "object:62:4"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich die\n"
"frisch gewaschenen Klei-\n"
"der zu einem Bündel zu-\n"
"sammenschnüren?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I tie\n"
"the freshly washed\n"
"clothes into a\n"
"bundle?"

msgctxt "object:63:0"
msgid "Ein leerer Lederbeutel."
msgstr "An empty leather pouch."

msgctxt "object:64:0"
msgid ""
"Von hier den Vogel mit\n"
"den Knallfröschen loszu-\n"
"schicken, bringt sicher\n"
"nicht den gewünschten\n"
"Erfolg."
msgstr ""
"Dispatching the bird\n"
"from here with the\n"
"firecrackers will\n"
"scarce bring desired\n"
"success."

msgctxt "object:64:5"
msgid ""
"Ein Lederbeutel voller\n"
"Knallfrösche."
msgstr ""
"A leather pouch full of\n"
"firecrackers."

msgctxt "object:65:0"
msgid ""
"Knallfrösche erster\n"
"Güte!"
msgstr ""
"Firecrackers of top\n"
"quality!"

msgctxt "object:66:0"
msgid ""
"Ein offener Koffer\n"
"mit defektem Schloss."
msgstr ""
"An open suitcase\n"
"with a broken lock."

msgctxt "object:66:2"
msgid ""
"Warum einen leeren\n"
"Koffer zubinden?"
msgstr ""
"Why tie up an\n"
"empty suitcase?"

msgctxt "object:67:0"
msgid ""
"Ein geschlossener Koffer,\n"
"voller Kleider."
msgstr ""
"A closed suitcase,\n"
"full of clothes."

msgctxt "object:68:0"
msgid ""
"Ein zerknülltes Stück\n"
"Papier...Sieht etwas\n"
"eigenartig aus."
msgstr ""
"A crumpled piece of\n"
"paper... Looks somewhat\n"
"peculiar."

msgctxt "object:71:0"
msgid "Ein rostiges Messer."
msgstr "A rusty knife."

msgctxt "object:71:1"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich die\n"
"frisch gewaschenen\n"
"Kleider zerschneiden?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I cut up\n"
"the freshly washed\n"
"clothes?"

msgctxt "object:71:4"
msgid ""
"Warum den Koffer zer-\n"
"säbeln? Dann hätte ich\n"
"ihn gleich stehen las-\n"
"sen können."
msgstr ""
"Why hack up the\n"
"suitcase? I might as\n"
"well have left it\n"
"behind."

msgctxt "object:71:8"
msgid ""
"Jetzt habe ich mir so\n"
"Mühe gegeben um die\n"
"Kleider in den Koffer\n"
"zu schlichten, und nun\n"
"soll ich sie zerschnei-\n"
"den. Kommt mir nicht\n"
"in den Sinn."
msgstr ""
"Now I took such pains\n"
"to pack the clothes into\n"
"the suitcase, and now I\n"
"am to cut them up.\n"
"I shall not think\n"
"of it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:71:15"
msgid ""
"Warum den mühsam ver-\n"
"schlossenen Koffer\n"
"wieder aufschneiden?"
msgstr ""
"Why cut open again\n"
"the painstakingly\n"
"closed suitcase?"

msgctxt "object:71:18"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich das\n"
"schimmelige Brot in\n"
"Scheiben schneiden?\n"
"Ich werde es sicher\n"
"nicht essen!"
msgstr ""
"Why should I slice\n"
"the moldy bread?\n"
"I shall certainly\n"
"not eat it!\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:72:0"
msgid ""
"Eine offene,leere\n"
"Kartonschachtel."
msgstr ""
"An open, empty\n"
"cardboard box."

msgctxt "object:73:0"
msgid "Eine Kartonschachtel."
msgstr "A cardboard box."

msgctxt "object:74:0"
msgid ""
"Ein roter, handge-\n"
"strickter Wollschal."
msgstr ""
"A red, hand-knitted\n"
"woolen scarf."

msgctxt "object:75:0"
msgid ""
"Ein paar trockene Schilf-\n"
"stauden."
msgstr ""
"A few dry reed\n"
"stalks."

msgctxt "object:75:2"
msgid ""
"Den Hund muss ich loswerden,\n"
"mit dem Schilf kann ich ihn\n"
"nur kitzeln..."
msgstr ""
"I must get rid of the dog;\n"
"with the reed I can only\n"
"tickle him..."

msgctxt "object:76:0"
msgid ""
"Einige schöne, gerade\n"
"Stäbe aus Schilfgras.\n"
"Die sind auch noch\n"
"recht stabil."
msgstr ""
"A few fine, straight\n"
"sticks of reed grass.\n"
"They are also quite\n"
"sturdy."

msgctxt "object:79:0"
msgid ""
"Well, so ein Schluck\n"
"tut gut!"
msgstr ""
"Well, such a draught\n"
"doth good!"

msgctxt "object:79:2"
msgid ""
"Auch ein 2. Schluck\n"
"ist nicht zu verach-\n"
"ten. Hick..."
msgstr ""
"A second draught is\n"
"not to be despised\n"
"either. Hic..."

msgctxt "object:79:5"
msgid ""
"Well...hick...noch..\n"
"hick,hick..."
msgstr ""
"Well...hic...more..\n"
"hic,hic..."

msgctxt "object:79:7"
msgid ""
"Eine Flasche, und da ist\n"
"sogar noch ein Tröpfchen\n"
"übrig geblieben."
msgstr ""
"A bottle, and there is\n"
"even a tiny drop left\n"
"inside."

msgctxt "object:81:0"
msgid "Ein leerer Stoffbeutel."
msgstr "An empty cloth bag."

msgctxt "object:81:1"
msgid ""
"Das Messer würde den\n"
"Beutel zerschneiden."
msgstr ""
"The knife would cut\n"
"the bag to pieces."

msgctxt "object:81:3"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist zu klein\n"
"für den Beutel."
msgstr ""
"The bag is too small\n"
"for the bag."

msgctxt "object:81:5"
msgid ""
"Die Bücher passen nicht in\n"
"den Beutel, und als Lesezeichen\n"
"ist der Beutel wiederum nicht\n"
"geeignet."
msgstr ""
"The books fit not into\n"
"the bag, and as a bookmark\n"
"the bag is not suitable\n"
"either."

msgctxt "object:81:9"
msgid ""
"Warum soll ich die Dose in\n"
"den Beutel stecken?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I put the tin\n"
"into the bag?"

msgctxt "object:81:11"
msgid ""
"Das ist eine gute Idee, doch leider\n"
"ist der Beutel etwas zu klein."
msgstr ""
"That is a good idea, yet alas\n"
"the bag is a bit too small."

msgctxt "object:81:13"
msgid ""
"Die Kerzen brauch ich nicht\n"
"einzupacken."
msgstr ""
"I need not pack up\n"
"the candles."

msgctxt "object:81:15"
msgid ""
"Da wird der Beutel ja ganz\n"
"schmutzig."
msgstr ""
"That would make the bag\n"
"quite dirty."

msgctxt "object:81:17"
msgid ""
"Die Spitze des Korkenziehers würde\n"
"durch den Beutel stossen."
msgstr ""
"The point of the corkscrew would\n"
"pierce right through the bag."

msgctxt "object:81:19"
msgid ""
"Jetzt habe ich sie doch gerade\n"
"ausgepackt, lassen wir das."
msgstr ""
"I just unpacked them,\n"
"so let us leave it be."

msgctxt "object:81:21"
msgid ""
"Den Beutel würde ich nie mehr\n"
"richtig sauber bekommen."
msgstr ""
"I should never get the bag\n"
"truly clean again."

msgctxt "object:81:23"
msgid ""
"Den Schluessel brauche ich nicht\n"
"in den Beutel zu packen."
msgstr ""
"I need not pack the key\n"
"into the bag."

msgctxt "object:81:25"
msgid ""
"So könnte man eventuell eine\n"
"Granate bauen, doch das Pulver\n"
"wird so zu wenig gepresst."
msgstr ""
"One might thus build a\n"
"grenade, yet the powder is\n"
"too little compressed."

msgctxt "object:81:28"
msgid ""
"Da wird der Beutel nur ganz gelb\n"
"von dem Schwefel."
msgstr ""
"The bag would only turn yellow\n"
"from the sulfur."

msgctxt "object:81:30"
msgid ""
"Die Socken brauche ich nicht in\n"
"den Beutel zu stecken, die sind\n"
"frisch gewaschen."
msgstr ""
"I need not put the socks\n"
"into the bag; they are\n"
"freshly washed."

msgctxt "object:81:33"
msgid ""
"Der Spachtel, mit seinen schar-\n"
"fen Kanten, würde den Beutel\n"
"nur beschädigen, darum steck\n"
"ich ihn nicht hinein."
msgstr ""
"The spatula, with its sharp\n"
"edges, would only damage\n"
"the bag, so I shall not\n"
"put it in."

msgctxt "object:81:37"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist zu klein, um\n"
"das reinzupacken."
msgstr ""
"The bag is too small to\n"
"pack that inside."

msgctxt "object:81:39"
msgid ""
"Nein, das würde nur den ganzen\n"
"Beutel verkleben."
msgstr ""
"No, that would only glue up\n"
"the whole bag."

msgctxt "object:81:41"
msgid ""
"Es ist nicht nötig, den Topf-\n"
"lappen in den Beutel zu stecken."
msgstr ""
"There is no need to put the\n"
"potholder into the bag."

msgctxt "object:81:43"
msgid ""
"Die Wolle muss nicht speziell\n"
"geschützt werden, also warum\n"
"soll ich sie in den Beutel\n"
"packen."
msgstr ""
"The wool needs no special\n"
"protection, so why should\n"
"I pack it into the\n"
"bag."

msgctxt "object:81:47"
msgid ""
"Die Wolle muss nicht speziell\n"
"geschützt werden, also warum\n"
"soll ich sie in den Beutel\n"
"packen."
msgstr ""
"The wool needs no special\n"
"protection, so why should\n"
"I pack it into the\n"
"bag."

msgctxt "object:81:51"
msgid ""
"Die Holzwürfel passen nicht\n"
"in den Beutel."
msgstr ""
"The wooden cubes fit not\n"
"into the bag."

msgctxt "object:81:53"
msgid ""
"Den Zettel kann ich gut so ein-\n"
"gesteckt haben..."
msgstr ""
"I can well keep the note\n"
"in my pocket..."

msgctxt "object:82:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Stoffbeutel, voll\n"
"mit Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"A cloth bag, full\n"
"of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:2"
msgid ""
"Den Beutel brauch ich nicht\n"
"aufzuschneiden, der lässt\n"
"sich leicht öffnen."
msgstr ""
"I need not cut open the\n"
"bag; it can easily be\n"
"opened."

msgctxt "object:82:5"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist schon\n"
"voller Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"The bag is already\n"
"full of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:7"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist schon\n"
"voller Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"The bag is already\n"
"full of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:9"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist schon\n"
"voller Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"The bag is already\n"
"full of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:11"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist schon\n"
"voller Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"The bag is already\n"
"full of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:13"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist schon\n"
"voller Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"The bag is already\n"
"full of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:15"
msgid ""
"Nebst den Murmeln, hat das\n"
"nicht auch noch Platz."
msgstr ""
"Besides the marbles, that\n"
"hath no space as well."

msgctxt "object:82:17"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist schon\n"
"voller Murmeln."
msgstr ""
"The bag is already\n"
"full of marbles."

msgctxt "object:82:19"
msgid ""
