"the tin."

msgctxt "object:92:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Papierdrachen, mit einem\n"
"langen Stück Hanfschnur als\n"
"Schwanz."
msgstr ""
"A paper kite with a\n"
"long piece of hemp twine as\n"
"a tail."

msgctxt "object:93:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Papierdrachen, an\n"
"dem der Schwanz fehlt.\n"
"Ohne den, wird er nicht\n"
"fliegen."
msgstr ""
"A paper kite missing\n"
"its tail. Without it,\n"
"it shall not fly\n"
"at all."

msgctxt "object:94:0"
msgid "Ein alter Blecheimer."
msgstr "An old tin bucket."

msgctxt "object:94:1"
msgid ""
"Warum den Schnaps in den\n"
"Eimer schütten, da ver-\n"
"dunstet ja der ganze Al-\n"
"kohol."
msgstr ""
"Why pour the liquor into the\n"
"bucket? All the alcohol\n"
"shall evaporate\n"
"then."

msgctxt "object:94:5"
msgid ""
"Warum den Schnaps in den\n"
"Eimer schütten, da ver-\n"
"dunstet ja der ganze Al-\n"
"kohol."
msgstr ""
"Why pour the liquor into the\n"
"bucket? All the alcohol\n"
"shall evaporate\n"
"then."

msgctxt "object:94:9"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die Kartoffeln in\n"
"den Eimer packe, dann kann\n"
"ich ihn nicht weiter ver-\n"
"wenden, und ich brauche den\n"
"Eimer sicher noch."
msgstr ""
"If I pack the potatoes into\n"
"the bucket, I cannot use\n"
"it any further, and I surely\n"
"shall need the bucket\n"
"yet."

msgctxt "object:94:14"
msgid ""
"Warum die Kerzen in den\n"
"Eimer legen, damit ist er\n"
"nur belegt, und ich kann die\n"
"Kerzen ja auch so tragen."
msgstr ""
"Why place the candles in the\n"
"bucket? It only occupieth it,\n"
"and I can carry the candles\n"
"as I am."

msgctxt "object:94:18"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die in den Eimer\n"
"schütte, wird sie ganz feucht."
msgstr ""
"If I pour it into the bucket,\n"
"it shall get quite damp."

msgctxt "object:94:20"
msgid ""
"Die machen nur unnötigen Lärm\n"
"in dem Eimer."
msgstr ""
"They only make needless noise\n"
"in the bucket."

msgctxt "object:94:22"
msgid ""
"Der Salpeter wird nur feucht,\n"
"wenn ich ihn in den Eimer schütte."
msgstr ""
"The saltpeter only groweth damp\n"
"if I pour it into the bucket."

msgctxt "object:94:24"
msgid ""
"Der Schwefel wird feucht, wenn\n"
"ich ihn in den Eimer schütte."
msgstr ""
"The sulfur groweth damp if\n"
"I pour it into the bucket."

msgctxt "object:94:26"
msgid ""
"Der Eimer ist noch feucht, und\n"
"wenn ich das Schwarzpulver in\n"
"den Eimer schütte, wird es\n"
"unbrauchbar."
msgstr ""
"The bucket is still damp, and if\n"
"I pour the gunpowder into\n"
"the bucket, it shall become\n"
"useless."

msgctxt "object:94:30"
msgid ""
"Ohne Wasser kann man die Socken\n"
"nicht waschen."
msgstr ""
"Without water one cannot wash\n"
"the socks."

msgctxt "object:94:32"
msgid ""
"Das Öl ist in der Tasse gut\n"
"aufgehoben, wenn ich es in den\n"
"Eimer schütte, werde ich den\n"
"nie wieder sauber bekommen."
msgstr ""
"The oil is well kept in the\n"
"cup; if I pour it into the\n"
"bucket, I shall never get\n"
"it clean again."

msgctxt "object:94:36"
msgid ""
"Warum den Teig in den\n"
"schmutzigen Eimer geben,\n"
"den kann man hinterher\n"
"nicht mehr zum Backen\n"
"brauchen."
msgstr ""
"Why put the dough into\n"
"the dirty bucket? One\n"
"cannot use it for baking\n"
"afterward.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:95:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Blecheimer voller\n"
"Wasser."
msgstr ""
"A tin bucket full of\n"
"water."

msgctxt "object:95:2"
msgid ""
"Warum den Schnaps ins Wasser\n"
"schütten?"
msgstr ""
"Why pour the liquor into\n"
"the water?"

msgctxt "object:95:4"
msgid ""
"Warum den Schnaps ins Wasser\n"
"schütten, er wird so nicht\n"
"besser."
msgstr ""
"Why pour the liquor into\n"
"the water, it won't get\n"
"any better that way."

msgctxt "object:95:7"
msgid ""
"Wo liegt der Sinn darin, die\n"
"Kerzen ins Wasser zu schmeissen?"
msgstr ""
"What is the point in throwing\n"
"the candles into the water?"

msgctxt "object:95:9"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die Kohle in den Eimer\n"
"schütte, wird sie aufgelöst."
msgstr ""
"If I pour the coal into the bucket,\n"
"it will dissolve."

msgctxt "object:95:11"
msgid ""
"Der Salpeter wird sich im Wasser\n"
"auflösen."
msgstr ""
"The saltpeter will dissolve in\n"
"the water."

msgctxt "object:95:13"
msgid ""
"Der Schwefel wird sich im Wasser\n"
"auflösen."
msgstr ""
"The sulfur will dissolve in\n"
"the water."

msgctxt "object:95:15"
msgid ""
"Das Wasser wird dem Schwarzpulver\n"
"nicht gut tun."
msgstr ""
"The water won't do the gunpowder\n"
"any good."

msgctxt "object:95:17"
msgid ""
"Heute ist nicht mein Waschtag,\n"
"und ausserdem sind die Socken\n"
"frisch gewaschen, aus dem Schrank."
msgstr ""
"Today is not my washday,\n"
"and besides the socks are\n"
"freshly washed, out of the closet."

msgctxt "object:95:20"
msgid ""
"Der Eimer ist voll Wasser, da\n"
"kann ich das Öl nicht dazuleeren."
msgstr ""
"The bucket is full of water, so\n"
"I cannot pour the oil in there."

msgctxt "object:95:22"
msgid ""
"Der Eimer ist voll Wasser, da\n"
"kann ich die Kartoffeln nicht\n"
"dazugeben, oder hast Du gemeint\n"
"ich werde die jetzt waschen?"
msgstr ""
"The bucket is full of water, I\n"
"cannot add the potatoes there,\n"
"or did you mean I am going to\n"
"wash them right now?"

msgctxt "object:95:26"
msgid ""
"Der Teig würde ja ganz wässrig und\n"
"unbrauchbar."
msgstr ""
"The dough would turn all watery\n"
"and useless."

msgctxt "object:96:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Schnapsflasche mit\n"
"einem Hanfseil umwickelt."
msgstr ""
"A liquor bottle wrapped in\n"
"a hemp rope."

msgctxt "object:96:2"
msgid ""
"Ja, sobald die Flasche leer\n"
"ist, kann ich daraus einen\n"
"Kerzenständer machen."
msgstr ""
"Yes, as soon as the bottle is\n"
"empty, I can make a candle-\n"
"stick out of it."

msgctxt "object:96:5"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich machen? Die Socken\n"
"mit dem Alkohol desinfizieren?"
msgstr ""
"What am I to do? Disinfect\n"
"the socks with the alcohol?"

msgctxt "object:97:0"
msgid "Eine Schnapsflasche."
msgstr "A liquor bottle."

msgctxt "object:97:1"
msgid ""
"Ja, sobald die Flasche leer\n"
"ist, kann ich damit einen\n"
"Kerzenständer machen."
msgstr ""
"Yes, as soon as the bottle is\n"
"empty, I can make a candle-\n"
"stick with it."

msgctxt "object:97:4"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich machen? Die Socken\n"
"mit dem Alkohol desinfizieren?"
msgstr ""
"What am I to do? Disinfect\n"
"the socks with the alcohol?"

msgctxt "object:98:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Spitzhacke, die aus\n"
"dem Stiel der Schaufel\n"
"gemacht wurde."
msgstr ""
"A pickaxe made out of\n"
"the handle of the shovel\n"
"here."

msgctxt "object:99:0"
msgid ""
"Eine angerostete\n"
"Hackenspitze."
msgstr ""
"A rusty pickaxe\n"
"tip."

msgctxt "object:100:0"
msgid ""
"Ein paar Lagerkartoffeln.\n"
"Bei der Menge, werden die\n"
"Butler's so schnell kei-\n"
"nen Mangel verspüren."
msgstr ""
"A few storage potatoes.\n"
"With that amount, the\n"
"Butlers will not feel any\n"
"shortage anytime soon."

msgctxt "object:100:4"
msgid ""
"Für einen Kartoffelsalat müssten\n"
"die Kartoffeln aber gekocht sein."
msgstr ""
"For a potato salad, however, the\n"
"potatoes would have to be cooked."

msgctxt "object:100:6"
msgid ""
"Soll ich die Kartoffeln über\n"
"einem einzigen Streichholz\n"
"rösten?"
msgstr ""
"Am I supposed to roast the\n"
"potatoes over a single match\n"
"here?"

msgctxt "object:100:9"
msgid ""
"Wenn das Oel heiss wäre, dann\n"
"könnte man die Kartoffeln bra-\n"
"ten."
msgstr ""
"If the oil were hot, then\n"
"one could fry the potatoes\n"
"here."

msgctxt "object:101:0"
msgid ""
"Sobald ich die Kerze dem\n"
"Wind aussetze, wird Sie\n"
"erlöschen."
msgstr ""
"As soon as I expose the\n"
"candle to the wind, it\n"
"will go out."

msgctxt "object:102:0"
msgid ""
"Die Kerze habe ich aus\n"
"der abmontierten Lampe."
msgstr ""
"I got the candle from\n"
"the dismantled lamp."

msgctxt "object:103:0"
msgid ""
"Vier Kerzen aus dem\n"
"Leuchter, den wir\n"
"abmontiert haben."
msgstr ""
"Four candles from\n"
"the chandelier we\n"
"dismantled earlier."

msgctxt "object:103:3"
msgid ""
"Wenn die Kerze brennen würde, so\n"
"könnte man das Schwarzpulver gut\n"
"damit anzünden."
msgstr ""
"If the candle were burning, one\n"
"could easily ignite the black\n"
"powder with it."

msgctxt "object:103:6"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die so anzünde, dann sind\n"
"die Kerzen beim kleinsten Windstoss\n"
"erloschen."
msgstr ""
"If I light them like that, the\n"
"candles will go out at the very\n"
"slightest gust of wind."

msgctxt "object:106:0"
msgid "Etwas Holzkohle."
msgstr "Some charcoal."

msgctxt "object:107:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Korkenzieher, richtig\n"
"schade, dass keine Wein-\n"
"flasche zur Hand ist."
msgstr ""
"A corkscrew, a real pity\n"
"that there is no wine\n"
"bottle at hand."

msgctxt "object:108:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Lampe, die aus\n"
"einem alten Wagenrad\n"
"hergestellt wurde."
msgstr ""
"A lamp made out of\n"
"an old wagon wheel\n"
"previously."

msgctxt "object:108:3"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich doch das Ding\n"
"nicht zerkleinern."
msgstr ""
"I cannot chop up that thing\n"
"with this after all."

msgctxt "object:108:5"
msgid ""
"Oh, jetzt soll ich wohl mit\n"
"roher Gewalt dahinter. Ich\n"
"bezweifle, dass dies eine gute\n"
"Idee ist. Lass uns etwas an-\n"
"deres zum Einheizen suchen."
msgstr ""
"Oh, now I am supposed to\n"
"use brute force. I doubt\n"
"that this is a good idea\n"
"here. Let us look for\n"
"something else to heat up."

msgctxt "object:108:10"
msgid "Damit habe ich zu wenig Wucht."
msgstr "I have too little momentum with that."

msgctxt "object:108:11"
msgid ""
"Tja, damit könnte man mit viel\n"
"Gewalt das Ding zerkleinern, doch\n"
"ich bin mir nicht sicher, ob das\n"
"gut wäre. Wir sollten etwas ande-\n"
"res zum Einheizen suchen..."
msgstr ""
"Well, with a lot of force one could\n"
"chop that thing up, but I am not\n"
"sure if that would be a good idea.\n"
"We should look for something else\n"
"to heat up the stove..."

msgctxt "object:108:16"
msgid ""
"Mit der Schaufelspitze alleine,\n"
"habe ich zu wenig Wucht..."
msgstr ""
"With the shovel tip alone, I\n"
"have too little momentum..."

msgctxt "object:109:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Lampe, die aus\n"
"einem alten Wagenrad\n"
"hergestellt wurde."
msgstr ""
"A lamp made out of\n"
"an old wagon wheel\n"
"previously."

msgctxt "object:109:3"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich doch das Ding\n"
"nicht zerkleinern."
msgstr ""
"I cannot chop up that thing\n"
"with this after all."

msgctxt "object:109:5"
msgid ""
"Oh, jetzt soll ich wohl mit\n"
"roher Gewalt dahinter. Ich\n"
"bezweifle, dass dies eine gute\n"
"Idee ist. Lass uns etwas an-\n"
"deres zum Einheizen suchen."
msgstr ""
"Oh, now I am supposed to\n"
"use brute force. I doubt\n"
"that this is a good idea\n"
"here. Let us look for\n"
"something else to heat up."

msgctxt "object:109:10"
msgid "Damit habe ich zu wenig Wucht."
msgstr "I have too little momentum with that."

msgctxt "object:109:11"
msgid ""
"Tja, damit könnte man mit viel\n"
"Gewalt das Ding zerkleinern, doch\n"
"ich bin mir nicht sicher, ob das\n"
"gut wäre. Wir sollten etwas ande-\n"
"res zum Einheizen suchen..."
msgstr ""
"Well, with a lot of force one could\n"
"chop that thing up, but I am not\n"
"sure if that would be a good idea.\n"
"We should look for something else\n"
"to heat up the stove..."

msgctxt "object:109:16"
msgid ""
"Mit der Schaufelspitze alleine,\n"
"habe ich zu wenig Wucht..."
msgstr ""
"With the shovel tip alone, I\n"
"have too little momentum..."

msgctxt "object:110:0"
msgid "Das ist Mrs. Butler."
msgstr "That is Mrs. Butler."

msgctxt "object:111:0"
msgid "Eine Handvoll Murmeln."
msgstr "A handful of marbles."

msgctxt "object:112:0"
msgid ""
"Alte Musketen, zwar sind\n"
"das nur Vorderlader, aber\n"
"die krachen genauso, wenn\n"
"es darauf ankommt."
msgstr ""
"Old muskets, although they\n"
"are only muzzle-loaders,\n"
"they bang just as loud when\n"
"it comes down to it."

msgctxt "object:113:0"
msgid ""
"Ein stabiler Holz-\n"
"pfahl, der an einem\n"
"Ende angespitzt ist."
msgstr ""
"A sturdy wooden\n"
"stake sharpened at\n"
"one end."

msgctxt "object:113:3"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich doch das Ding\n"
"nicht zerkleinern."
msgstr ""
"I cannot chop up that thing\n"
"with this after all."

msgctxt "object:113:5"
msgid ""
"Oh, jetzt soll ich wohl mit\n"
"roher Gewalt dahinter. Ich\n"
"bezweifle, dass dies eine gute\n"
"Idee ist. Lass uns etwas an-\n"
"deres zum Einheizen suchen."
msgstr ""
"Oh, now I am supposed to\n"
"use brute force. I doubt\n"
"that this is a good idea\n"
"here. Let us look for\n"
"something else to heat up."

msgctxt "object:113:10"
msgid "Damit habe ich zu wenig Wucht."
msgstr "I have too little momentum with that."

msgctxt "object:113:11"
msgid ""
"Tja, damit könnte man mit viel\n"
"Gewalt das Ding zerkleinern, doch\n"
"ich bin mir nicht sicher, ob das\n"
"gut wäre. Wir sollten etwas ande-\n"
"res zum Einheizen suchen..."
msgstr ""
"Well, with much force one might\n"
"break the thing to pieces, yet I\n"
"am not sure if that were good.\n"
"We should search for something\n"
"else to kindle..."

msgctxt "object:113:16"
msgid ""
"Mit der Schaufelspitze alleine,\n"
"habe ich zu wenig Wucht..."
msgstr ""
"With the shovel tip alone,\n"
"I have too little momentum..."

msgctxt "object:114:0"
msgid ""
"Oh, ein altes Wagenrad.\n"
"So wird ein Leuchter\n"
"zweckentfremdet."
msgstr ""
"Oh, an old wagon wheel.\n"
"Thus a chandelier is\n"
"misappropriated."

msgctxt "object:114:3"
msgid ""
"Damit kann ich doch das Ding\n"
"nicht zerkleinern."
msgstr ""
"I cannot break the thing to\n"
"pieces with that."

msgctxt "object:114:5"
msgid ""
"Oh, jetzt soll ich wohl mit\n"
"roher Gewalt dahinter. Ich\n"
"bezweifle, dass dies eine gute\n"
"Idee ist. Lass uns etwas an-\n"
"deres zum Einheizen suchen."
msgstr ""
"Oh, now I am to go at it with\n"
"brute force. I doubt that this\n"
"is a good idea. Let us look for\n"
"something else to heat the place.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:114:10"
msgid "Damit habe ich zu wenig Wucht."
msgstr "I have too little momentum with that."

msgctxt "object:114:11"
msgid ""
"Tja, damit könnte man mit viel\n"
"Gewalt das Ding zerkleinern, doch\n"
"ich bin mir nicht sicher, ob das\n"
"gut wäre. Wir sollten etwas ande-\n"
"res zum Einheizen suchen..."
msgstr ""
"Well, with much force one might\n"
"break the thing to pieces, yet I\n"
"am not sure if that were good.\n"
"We should search for something\n"
"else to kindle..."

msgctxt "object:114:16"
msgid ""
"Mit der Schaufelspitze alleine,\n"
"habe ich zu wenig Wucht..."
msgstr ""
"With the shovel tip alone,\n"
"I have too little momentum..."

msgctxt "object:115:0"
msgid "Etwas Salpeterpulver."
msgstr "Some saltpeter powder."

msgctxt "object:116:0"
msgid ""
"Eine alte und stumpfe\n"
"Schaufel, mit einem neuen\n"
"Stiel."
msgstr ""
"An old and dull\n"
"shovel with a new\n"
"handle."

msgctxt "object:117:0"
msgid "Eine stumpfe Schaufelspitze."
msgstr "A dull shovel tip."

msgctxt "object:118:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Lampenschirm, der\n"
"wohl die dazugehörige\n"
"Kerze vor dem Wind\n"
"schützen sollte."
msgstr ""
"A lampshade that\n"
"likely ought to protect\n"
"the matching candle\n"
"from the wind."

msgctxt "object:119:0"
msgid ""
"Die Lampenschirme waren\n"
"vorher auf der Lampe."
msgstr ""
"The lampshades were\n"
"previously on the lamp."

msgctxt "object:120:0"
msgid ""
"Ein schwerer Messing-\n"
"schlüssel."
msgstr ""
"A heavy brass\n"
"key."

msgctxt "object:124:0"
msgid "Es fehlt noch Kohlepulver!"
msgstr "Coal powder is still missing!"

msgctxt "object:124:1"
msgid "Es fehlt noch Salpeter!"
msgstr "Saltpeter is still missing!"

msgctxt "object:124:2"
msgid "Der Schwefel fehlt noch!"
msgstr "The sulfur is still missing!"

msgctxt "object:124:3"
msgid ""
"So, jetzt haben wir das\n"
"notwendige Schwarzpulver."
msgstr ""
"There, now we have the\n"
"necessary gunpowder."

msgctxt "object:124:5"
msgid "Eine Porzellanschüssel."
msgstr "A porcelain bowl."

msgctxt "object:124:6"
msgid ""
"Eine Porzellanschüssel.\n"
"Sie enthält:"
msgstr ""
"A porcelain bowl.\n"
"It contains:"

msgctxt "object:124:8"
msgid "Schwefel."
msgstr "Sulfur."

msgctxt "object:124:9"
msgid "Kohle."
msgstr "Coal."

msgctxt "object:124:10"
msgid "Salpeter."
msgstr "Saltpeter."

msgctxt "object:125:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Porzellanschüssel\n"
"mit Teig."
msgstr ""
"A porcelain bowl\n"
"with dough."

msgctxt "object:126:0"
msgid "Schwarzpulver"
msgstr "Gunpowder"

msgctxt "object:127:0"
msgid "Das ist Schwefel."
msgstr "That is sulfur."

msgctxt "object:128:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Hanfseil, leider etwas\n"
"zu kurz..."
msgstr ""
"A hemp rope, alas somewhat\n"
"too short..."

msgctxt "object:129:0"
msgid ""
"Ein schönes Stück\n"
"Hanfschnur, dass wir\n"
"vom Drachen wegge-\n"
"nommen haben."
msgstr ""
"A fine piece of\n"
"hemp twine that we\n"
"have taken from the\n"
"kite."

msgctxt "object:130:0"
msgid ""
"Die beiden Hanfseile\n"
"zusammen verwendet,\n"
"ergibt ein schönes\n"
"und starkes Seil,\n"
"dass mir nützen wird."
msgstr ""
"The two hemp ropes\n"
"used together make a\n"
"fine and strong\n"
"rope that shall serve\n"
"me well."

msgctxt "object:131:0"
msgid "Ein Paar rote Socken."
msgstr "A pair of red socks."

msgctxt "object:132:0"
msgid "Ein Spachtel."
msgstr "A spatula."

msgctxt "object:133:0"
msgid ""
"Eine rote Holzente\n"
"auf Rädern. Da würde\n"
"sich manches Kind\n"
"darüber freuen."
msgstr ""
"A red wooden duck\n"
"on wheels. Many a\n"
"child would be\n"
"delighted with it."

msgctxt "object:134:0"
msgid "Ein Streichholz."
msgstr "A match."

msgctxt "object:135:0"
msgid "Eine leere Tasse."
msgstr "An empty cup."

msgctxt "object:136:0"
msgid "Eine Tasse voll Oel."
msgstr "A cup full of oil."

msgctxt "object:137:0"
msgid "Eine Portion Teig."
msgstr "A portion of dough."

msgctxt "object:138:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Topflappen in\n"
"Form einer Hand,\n"
"wie praktisch."
msgstr ""
"A potholder in the\n"
"shape of a hand;\n"
"how practical."

msgctxt "object:139:0"
msgid ""
"In diesem Windlicht ist\n"
"die Kerzenflamme bestens\n"
"geschützt."
msgstr ""
"In this lantern the\n"
"candle flame is well\n"
"protected."

msgctxt "object:140:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Knäuel rote\n"
"Wolle."
msgstr ""
"A ball of red\n"
"wool."

msgctxt "object:141:0"
msgid ""
"Die Wolle ist mit\n"
"Alkohol getränkt."
msgstr ""
"The wool is soaked\n"
"with alcohol."

msgctxt "object:142:0"
msgid "Bunte Holzwürfel."
msgstr "Colorful wooden blocks."

msgctxt "object:143:0"
msgid ""
"Oh ein Brief...\n"
"Sehr verehrte Mrs. Butler,\n"
"ich möchte Sie im Namen\n"
"der Schule....\n"
"... Hochachtungsvoll\n"
"Die Schrift ist ja kaum\n"
"zu entziffern, doch das\n"
"ist ja sowieso unwichtig."
msgstr ""
"Oh, a letter...\n"
"Dear Mrs. Butler,\n"
"I should like on behalf\n"
"of the school....\n"
"... Yours respectfully\n"
"The handwriting is scarce\n"
"legible, yet that is\n"
"unimportant anyway."

msgctxt "object:143:8"
msgid ""
"Ein Stück Papier, das\n"
"beschrieben ist."
msgstr ""
"A piece of paper\n"
"that is written upon."

msgctxt "object:148:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Lore, die zum Transpor-\n"
"tieren des Erzes verwendet\n"
"wurde. Sie ist schon wieder\n"
"fahrbereit."
msgstr ""
"A mine cart used for\n"
"transporting ore. It is\n"
"ready to roll once\n"
"more."

msgctxt "object:148:4"
msgid ""
"An der Lore, kann ich nichts\n"
"herumarbeiten."
msgstr ""
"On the mine cart I can\n"
"work on nothing."

msgctxt "object:148:6"
msgid ""
"Wozu den Sand in die Lore \n"
"schütten, das ist ja kein\n"
"Erz, und ich kein Bergwerks-\n"
"arbeiter."
msgstr ""
"Why pour sand into the cart?\n"
"That is no ore, and I am\n"
"no miner.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:148:10"
msgid ""
"Die Lore ist aus Metall, und\n"
"brennt nicht."
msgstr ""
"The mine cart is of metal\n"
"and burneth not."

msgctxt "object:150:0"
msgid "Ein leicht vergilbter Lederbeutel."
msgstr "A slightly yellowed leather pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:1"
msgid ""
"Dein Augenmass täuscht Dich\n"
"sehr, das Brecheisen passt da\n"
"nie hinein."
msgstr ""
"Your eye deceiveth you greatly;\n"
"the crowbar shall never fit\n"
"in there."

msgctxt "object:150:4"
msgid ""
"Nicht doch, warum soll ich den\n"
"Beutel verbrennen?"
msgstr ""
"Nay, why should I burn the\n"
"pouch?"

msgctxt "object:150:6"
msgid ""
"Von der Figur, hat knapp der Kopf\n"
"im Beutel Platz."
msgstr ""
"Of the figure, scarce the head\n"
"hath space in the pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:8"
msgid ""
"Von der Figur, hat knapp der Kopf\n"
"im Beutel Platz."
msgstr ""
"Of the figure, scarce the head\n"
"hath space in the pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:10"
msgid ""
"Den Sand, möchte ich nicht in\n"
"den Beutel schütten, da wird\n"
"er nur von den Rückständen im\n"
"Beutel verunreinigt."
msgstr ""
"I wish not to pour the sand into\n"
"the pouch, for it would only be\n"
"soiled by the residues in\n"
"the pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:14"
msgid ""
"Den Sand, möchte ich nicht in\n"
"den Beutel schütten, da wird\n"
"er nur von den Rückständen im\n"
"Beutel verunreinigt."
msgstr ""
"I wish not to pour the sand into\n"
"the pouch, for it would only be\n"
"soiled by the residues in\n"
"the pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:18"
msgid ""
"Wenn ich die Sicheln in den\n"
"Beutel packe, dann wird er\n"
"zerschnitten."
msgstr ""
"If I pack the sickles into the\n"
"pouch, it shall be cut to\n"
"pieces."

msgctxt "object:150:21"
msgid ""
"Die Stange hat in dem Beutel\n"
"keinen Platz."
msgstr ""
"The rod hath no space in\n"
"the pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:23"
msgid ""
"Mit Deinem Augenmass hapert es\n"
"etwas, die Stange hat im Beutel\n"
"nie Platz."
msgstr ""
"Your eye for measure is somewhat\n"
"flawed; the rod shall never fit in\n"
"the pouch."

msgctxt "object:150:26"
msgid ""
"Was sollte mein Freund Winnetou\n"
"mit dem Beutel anfangen?!"
msgstr ""
"What should my friend Winnetou\n"
"do with the pouch?!"

msgctxt "object:151:0"
msgid "Ein Lederbeutel voll Sand."
msgstr "A leather pouch full of sand."

msgctxt "object:151:1"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:3"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:5"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:7"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:9"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:11"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:13"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:15"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:17"
msgid ""
"Der Beutel ist bereits voll\n"
"Sand, da hat nichts mehr Platz."
msgstr ""
"The pouch is already full of\n"
"sand; naught else hath space."

msgctxt "object:151:19"
msgid ""
"Winnetou kann mit dem Beutel voll\n"
"Sand sicher nichts anfangen."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou can surely do naught\n"
"with the pouch full of sand."

msgctxt "object:151:21"
msgid ""
"Ich bin froh, dass ich den Sand\n"
"in den Beutel packen konnte, ich\n"
"lasse ihn lieber da d'rin, das er-\n"
"spart mir, dass alles schmutzig\n"
"wird. "
msgstr ""
"I am glad I could pack the sand\n"
"into the pouch; I prefer to leave\n"
"it inside, for that saveth me from\n"
"everything growing dirty.\n"
"­ "

msgctxt "object:152:0"
msgid ""
"Zwei gut erhaltene Bohlen,die\n"
"halten schon einem rechten\n"
"Gewicht stand."
msgstr ""
"Two well-preserved planks that\n"
"can withstand quite a fair\n"
"weight."

msgctxt "object:152:3"
msgid ""
"Die Bohlen mit dem Brecheisen zu\n"
"bearbeiten, bringt mich überhaupt\n"
"nicht weiter."
msgstr ""
"Working the planks with the\n"
"crowbar getteth me nowhere\n"
"at all."

msgctxt "object:152:6"
msgid ""
"Den Sand auf die Bohlen zu\n"
"schütten, ist eigentlich wenig\n"
"sinnvoll."
msgstr ""
"Pouring the sand upon the planks\n"
"is in truth of little\n"
"sense."

msgctxt "object:152:9"
msgid ""
"Eine etwas eigentümliche Art,\n"
"Kleinholz zu machen."
msgstr ""
"A somewhat peculiar way\n"
"to make kindling."

msgctxt "object:152:11"
msgid ""
"Wozu die Bohlen anzünden, ich\n"
"habe keinen Bedarf an einem\n"
"Lagerfeuer."
msgstr ""
"Why set fire to the planks; I\n"
"have no need for a\n"
"campfire."

msgctxt "object:152:14"
msgid ""
"Wie soll ich den Haken an den\n"
"Bohlen befestigen?"
msgstr ""
"How am I to fasten the hook\n"
"unto the planks?"

msgctxt "object:152:16"
msgid ""
"Ein Floss will ich nicht bauen,\n"
"also warum sollte ich die Bohlen\n"
"mit dem Seil zusammenbinden."
msgstr ""
"I wish not to build a raft, so\n"
"why should I tie the planks\n"
"together with the rope."

msgctxt "object:152:19"
msgid ""
"Der wird sich bedanken, wenn ich\n"
"ihm meinen Kram aufhalse."
msgstr ""
"He shall scarce thank me if I\n"
"burden him with my gear."

msgctxt "object:153:0"
msgid ""
"Ein Brecheisen, wie es verwen-\n"
"det wird, um Verpackungskisten\n"
"zu öffnen."
msgstr ""
"A crowbar such as is used\n"
"to open packing\n"
"crates."

msgctxt "object:153:3"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Sand, könnte ich das\n"
"Eisen eventuell polieren, doch\n"
"das ist überflüssig..."
msgstr ""
"With the sand I might perchance\n"
"polish the iron, yet that\n"
"is superfluous..."

msgctxt "object:153:6"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Eisen, möchte ich nicht\n"
"in der Dynamitstange herumsto-\n"
"chern, da könnte es plötzlich\n"
"einen bösen Knall geben."
msgstr ""
"With the iron I wish not to poke\n"
"around in the stick of dynamite,\n"
"for there might suddenly be a\n"
"grievous bang."

msgctxt "object:153:10"
msgid ""
"So wird das Eisen zwar heiss,\n"
"doch ich brauche weder ein\n"
"Brandeisen, noch kann ich das\n"
"Eisen ohne Hammer und Amboss\n"
"schmieden."
msgstr ""
"Thus the iron groweth hot, yet I\n"
"need no branding iron, nor can I\n"
"forge the iron without a hammer\n"
"and anvil.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:153:15"
msgid ""
"Rohe Gewalt bringt überhaupt\n"
"nichts."
msgstr ""
"Brute force accomplisheth\n"
"naught at all."

msgctxt "object:153:17"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brecheisen, kann ich\n"
"an der Figur überhaupt nichts\n"
"ausrichten."
msgstr ""
"With the crowbar I can achieve\n"
"naught at all upon\n"
"the figure."

msgctxt "object:153:20"
msgid ""
"Brachiale Gewalt, hat noch nie\n"
"etwas zum Vorteil verändert."
msgstr ""
"Brutal force hath never altered\n"
"anything unto advantage."

msgctxt "object:153:22"
msgid ""
"Die Kombination, kombiniert über-\n"
"haupt nicht."
msgstr ""
"The combination combineth not at\n"
"all."

msgctxt "object:153:24"
msgid ""
"Ich kann mir nicht vorstellen,\n"
"wie ich das Brecheisen zusammen\n"
"mit dem Seil und Haken verwen-\n"
"den kann."
msgstr ""
"I cannot imagine how I might use\n"
"the crowbar together with\n"
"the rope and hook.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:153:28"
msgid ""
"Mit dem Brecheisen, kann ich\n"
"zwar die Kacheln zerkleinern,\n"
"doch was würde das nützen?"
msgstr ""
"With the crowbar I could break\n"
"the tiles to pieces, yet what\n"
"would that avail?"

msgctxt "object:153:31"
msgid ""
"Ja das würde einen Holzhammer\n"
"ergeben, doch so einen brauche\n"
"ich nicht."
msgstr ""
"Aye, that would make a wooden\n"
"mallet, yet I have no need for\n"
"such a thing."

msgctxt "object:153:34"
msgid ""
"Das Ding scheint schon komplett\n"
"zu sein, ein Brecheisen braucht\n"
"es dazu sicher nicht."
msgstr ""
"The thing seemeth complete\n"
"already; it surely needeth no\n"
"crowbar for that."

msgctxt "object:153:37"
msgid ""
"Eine gute Idee, wenn ich\n"
"das Seil jemanden über\n"
"einen Abgrund zuwerfen\n"
"müsste, aber das ist\n"
"nicht der Fall."
msgstr ""
"A good idea were I in need to\n"
"throw the rope to someone across\n"
"an abyss, yet that is\n"
"not the case.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:153:42"
msgid ""
"Den Tomahawk, brauche ich damit\n"
"nicht zu schleifen, der ist\n"
"scharf genug."
msgstr ""
"I need not sharpen the tomahawk\n"
"with that; it is sharp\n"
"enough."

msgctxt "object:153:45"
msgid ""
"Winnetou braucht so ein\n"
"Brecheisen bestimmt nicht."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou surely hath no need\n"
"for such a crowbar."

msgctxt "object:154:0"
msgid "Ein Haufen grober Sand."
msgstr "A heap of coarse sand."

msgctxt "object:154:1"
msgid "Der Sand brennt nicht."
msgstr "The sand burneth not."

msgctxt "object:154:2"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit dem groben\n"
"Sand und der Figur?"
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with the coarse\n"
"sand and the figure?"

msgctxt "object:154:4"
msgid ""
"Was soll ich mit dem groben\n"
"Sand und der Figur?"
msgstr ""
"What am I to do with the coarse\n"
"sand and the figure?"

msgctxt "object:154:6"
msgid ""
"Den Groben und den feinen\n"
"Quarzsand, sollte ich nicht\n"
"mischen."
msgstr ""
"The coarse and the fine quartz\n"
"sand I ought not to\n"
"mix."

msgctxt "object:154:9"
msgid ""
"Den Groben und den feinen\n"
"Quarzsand, sollte ich besser\n"
"nicht mischen."
msgstr ""
"The coarse and the fine quartz\n"
"sand I had best not\n"
"mix."

msgctxt "object:154:12"
msgid ""
"Das ist Winnetou und kein\n"
"Gärtner. Ich bin nicht über-\n"
"zeugt, dass er über mein\n"
"Geschenk erfreut wäre."
msgstr ""
"That is Winnetou, not a gardener.\n"
"I am not convinced that he would\n"
"be pleased with my\n"
"gift."

msgctxt "object:155:0"
msgid "Eine Stange Dynamit."
msgstr "A stick of dynamite."

msgctxt "object:155:1"
msgid ""
"Ich glaub nicht, dass ich das\n"
"mache während ich das Dynamit\n"
"in der Hand halte. Das gibt\n"
"nähmlich einen bösen Knall\n"
"und von mir stehen nur noch\n"
"die Stiefel da."
msgstr ""
"I do not think I will do\n"
"that while holding dynamite\n"
"in my hand. That would make\n"
"a nasty bang, and only my\n"
"boots would be left\n"
"standing here."

msgctxt "object:155:7"
msgid ""
"Winnetou wird sicher nicht\n"
"an einer Stange Dynamit\n"
"interessiert sein."
msgstr ""
"Winnetou will surely not\n"
"be interested in a stick\n"
"of dynamite."

msgctxt "object:156:0"
msgid "Eine brennende Fackel."
msgstr "A burning torch."

msgctxt "object:156:1"
msgid "Warum sollte ich den anzünden?"
msgstr "Why should I ignite that?"

msgctxt "object:156:2"
msgid ""
"Ich habe das mühsam zusammen-\n"
"gesucht, und nun soll ich es\n"
"anzünden? Nicht doch!"
msgstr ""
"I painstakingly gathered this\n"
"together, and now I should\n"
"light it? Surely not!"

msgctxt "object:156:5"
msgid ""
"Das Seil würde zwar brennen,\n"
"doch wäre das sinnlose Zer-\n"
"störung."
msgstr ""
"The rope would burn, but\n"
"that would be senseless\n"
"destruction."

msgctxt "object:157:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Fackel, die noch recht\n"
"ungebraucht aussieht."
msgstr ""
"A torch that looks fairly\n"
"unused still."

msgctxt "object:158:0"
msgid "Da ist nichts mehr in der Figur."
msgstr "There is nothing left in the figure."

msgctxt "object:158:1"
msgid ""
"Eine stehende Holzfigur. Ein\n"
"finster dreinschauender Knabe."
msgstr ""
"A standing wooden figure. A\n"
"gloomy-looking fellow."

msgctxt "object:158:3"
msgid ""
"Die Öffnung ist so klein, dass\n"
"man ohne Trichter, den Sand gar\n"
"nicht einfüllen könnte. Doch ich\n"
"wüsste nicht, wozu das gut sein\n"
"soll."
msgstr ""
"The opening is so small that\n"
"without a funnel one could not\n"
"pour the sand in at all. But I\n"
"would not know what that would\n"
"be good for."

msgctxt "object:158:8"
msgid ""
"Die Öffnung ist so klein, dass\n"
"man ohne Trichter, den Sand gar\n"
"nicht einfüllen könnte. Doch ich\n"
"wüsste nicht, wozu das gut sein\n"
"soll."
msgstr ""
"The opening is so small that\n"
"without a funnel one could not\n"
"pour the sand in at all. But I\n"
"would not know what that would\n"
"be good for."

msgctxt "object:159:0"
msgid ""
"Eine neue Figur, zusammengesetzt\n"
"aus den zwei Figuren aus dem\n"
"Zeremoniensaal. Mir scheint, dafür\n"
"waren sie auch vorgesehen."
msgstr ""
"A new figure, assembled out of\n"
"the two figures from the\n"
"ceremonial hall. It seems to me\n"
"they were intended for that."

msgctxt "object:160:0"
msgid "Da ist nichts mehr in der Figur."
msgstr "There is nothing left in the figure."

msgctxt "object:160:1"
msgid ""
"Eine sitzende Holzfigur. Ein\n"
"finster dreinschauender Knabe."
msgstr ""
"A sitting wooden figure. A\n"
"gloomy-looking fellow."

msgctxt "object:160:3"
msgid ""
"Die Öffnung ist so klein, dass\n"
"man ohne Trichter, den Sand gar\n"
"nicht einfüllen könnte. Doch ich\n"
"wüsste nicht, wozu das gut sein\n"
"soll."
msgstr ""
"The opening is so small that\n"
"without a funnel one could not\n"
"pour the sand in at all. But I\n"
"would not know what that would\n"
"be good for."

msgctxt "object:160:8"
msgid ""
"Die Öffnung ist so klein, dass\n"
"man ohne Trichter, den Sand gar\n"
"nicht einfüllen könnte. Doch ich\n"
"wüsste nicht, wozu das gut sein\n"
"soll."
msgstr ""
"The opening is so small that\n"
"without a funnel one could not\n"
"pour the sand in at all. But I\n"
"would not know what that would\n"
"be good for."

msgctxt "object:161:0"
msgid "Ein stabiler Flaschenzug."
msgstr "A sturdy block and tackle."

msgctxt "object:162:0"
msgid "Ein Haken, um Lasten zu heben."
msgstr "A hook to lift heavy loads."

msgctxt "object:163:0"
msgid "Haken und Seil kombiniert."
msgstr "Hook and rope combined."

msgctxt "object:164:0"
msgid "Einige Tonkacheln."
msgstr "Some clay tiles."

msgctxt "object:164:1"
msgid ""
"Ich bezweifle, dass Winnetou\n"
"mit den Kacheln etwas anzu-\n"
"fangen weiss. In seinem Tipi\n"
"hat er kaum gekachelte Wände."
msgstr ""
"I doubt that Winnetou\n"
"knows what to do with\n"
"the tiles. In his tepee\n"
"he hardly has tiled walls."

msgctxt "object:166:0"
msgid ""
"Das ist die Nase, die ich von der\n"
"Figur abgeschlagen habe."
msgstr ""
"That's the nose I knocked off\n"
"the figure."

msgctxt "object:166:2"
msgid ""
"Warum sollte ich an der Holznase\n"
"herumschnitzen?"
msgstr ""
"Why should I carve around on the\n"
"wooden nose?"

msgctxt "object:166:4"
msgid ""
"Nicht doch, die Nase ist doch\n"
"gerade richtig in der Grösse."
msgstr ""
"Not at all, the nose is actually\n"
"just the right size."

msgctxt "object:166:6"
msgid "Winnetou braucht keine Nase..."
msgstr "Winnetou doesn't need a nose..."

msgctxt "object:171:0"
msgid "Quarzsand."
msgstr "Quartz sand."

msgctxt "object:172:0"
msgid "Quarzsand."
msgstr "Quartz sand."

msgctxt "object:173:0"
msgid ""
"Das sieht aus, wie ein Griff\n"
"oder Schlüssel..."
msgstr ""
"That looks like a handle\n"
"or key..."

msgctxt "object:174:0"
msgid "Ein starkes Hanfseil."
msgstr "A strong hemp rope."

msgctxt "object:175:0"
msgid ""
"Zwei fein gearbeitete, sichelartige\n"
"Geräte."
msgstr ""
"Two finely crafted, sickle-like\n"
"tools."

msgctxt "object:176:0"
msgid "Zwei abgewinkelte Eisen."
msgstr "Two angled irons."

msgctxt "object:177:0"
msgid ""
"Ein ca. 40cm langes, abgerundetes\n"
"Eisen."
msgstr ""
"An approximately 40cm long,\n"
"rounded iron bar."

msgctxt "object:178:0"
msgid ""
"Ein überdimensionaler Schrauben-\n"
"zieher..."
msgstr ""
"An oversized screwdriver...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:178:2"
msgid ""
"Die Stangen sind so fest inei-\n"
"nander eingerastet, dass ich sie\n"
"nicht mehr auseinander bekomme."
msgstr ""
"The rods are locked together\n"
"so tightly that I can't get them\n"
"apart anymore."

msgctxt "object:179:0"
msgid ""
"Eine Eisenstange, an der einen\n"
"Seite abgeflacht, und an der an-\n"
"deren Seite, mit einer grossen\n"
"Öse versehen."
msgstr ""
"An iron rod, flattened on one\n"
"side and provided with a large\n"
"eyelet on the other.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:179:4"
msgid ""
"Das Brecheisen, passt nicht durch\n"
"die Öse durch."
msgstr ""
"The crowbar doesn't fit\n"
"through the eyelet."

msgctxt "object:180:0"
msgid "Ein reich verzierter Tomahawk."
msgstr "An decorated tomahawk."

msgctxt "object:180:1"
msgid ""
"Ich kann den Tomahawk Winnetou\n"
"schenken, wenn alles überstanden\n"
"ist - jetzt brauche ich ihn\n"
"eventuell noch."
msgstr ""
"I can give the tomahawk to Winnetou\n"
"as a present when everything is over -\n"
"right now I might still need it.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:0"
msgid ""
"Hat mein roter Bruder\n"
"etwas, um diese Fackel\n"
"anzuzünden?"
msgstr ""
"Does my red brother\n"
"have something to light\n"
"this torch?"

msgctxt "object:181:3"
msgid ""
"Ich habe Feuersteine\n"
"bei mir, damit kann\n"
"ich die Fackel anzün-\n"
"den."
msgstr ""
"I have flints with me,\n"
"I can use them to light\n"
"the torch.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:7"
msgid ""
"Wohin will Firehand\n"
"den Balken tragen?"
msgstr ""
"Where does Firehand want\n"
"to carry the beam?"

msgctxt "object:181:9"
msgid ""
"Sobald Firehand meine\n"
"Hilfe braucht, wird\n"
"Ihm Winnetou zur Seite\n"
"stehen."
msgstr ""
"As soon as Firehand\n"
"needs my help, Winnetou\n"
"will stand by his\n"
"side."

msgctxt "object:181:13"
msgid ""
"Kann Winnetou diese\n"
"Zeichen deuten?"
msgstr ""
"Can Winnetou interpret\n"
"these signs?"

msgctxt "object:181:15"
msgid ""
"Ich werde sie mir\n"
"einmal anschauen,\n"
"ich glaube, es ist\n"
"die alte Sprache der\n"
"Schatzhüter..."
msgstr ""
"I will take a look at them,\n"
"I believe it is\n"
"the old language of the\n"
"treasure keepers...\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:20"
msgid ""
"Ja, es ist die Spra-\n"
"che der Schatzwächter,\n"
"die nur den Häuptlin-\n"
"gen,von Generation zu\n"
"Generation weitergege-\n"
"ben wird. Ich habe sie\n"
"von meinem Vater erhal-\n"
"ten."
msgstr ""
"Yes, it is the langua-\n"
"ge of the treasure guards,\n"
"which is only passed down\n"
"from chief to chief, from\n"
"generation to generation.\n"
"I received it from my\n"
"father.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:28"
msgid ""
"Übersetzt man die Zei-\n"
"chen in Deine Sprache,\n"
"Firehand, so sagen sie:"
msgstr ""
"If you translate the sig-\n"
"ns into your language,\n"
"Firehand, they say:"

msgctxt "object:181:31"
msgid ""
"Das Tor wird sich nur\n"
"drei Geistern, die\n"
"sich zusammentun und\n"
"einig, das gleiche\n"
"Ziel anstreben, auf-\n"
"schliessen."
msgstr ""
"The gate will only open\n"
"to three spirits who\n"
"join together and, united,\n"
"strive for the same\n"
"goal.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:37"
msgid ""
"Wir müssen in diesem\n"
"Raum etwas übersehen\n"
"haben."
msgstr ""
"We must have overlooked\n"
"something in this room.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:40"
msgid "Wie kann ich Dir helfen?"
msgstr "How can I help you?"

msgctxt "object:181:41"
msgid ""
"Ich helfe Firehand den\n"
"Balken auf das Feld zu\n"
"stellen."
msgstr ""
"I'm helping Firehand set\n"
"the beam onto the square.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:44"
msgid "Gut, und nun gemeinsam!"
msgstr "Good, and now together!"

msgctxt "object:181:45"
msgid ""
"Wie kann ich meinem\n"
"Freund helfen?"
msgstr ""
"How can I help my\n"
"friend?"

msgctxt "object:181:47"
msgid ""
"Bis hier ging ja\n"
"alles gut."
msgstr ""
"So far everything\n"
"went well."

msgctxt "object:181:49"
msgid "Winnetou!"
msgstr "Winnetou!"

msgctxt "object:181:50"
msgid ""
"Ich kann Firehand nicht\n"
"helfen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot help\n"
"Firehand."

msgctxt "object:181:52"
msgid "Winnetou!"
msgstr "Winnetou!"

msgctxt "object:181:53"
msgid ""
"Ich kann Firehand nicht\n"
"helfen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot help\n"
"Firehand."

msgctxt "object:181:55"
msgid "Winnetou!"
msgstr "Winnetou!"

msgctxt "object:181:56"
msgid ""
"Ich kann Firehand nicht\n"
"helfen."
msgstr ""
"I cannot help\n"
"Firehand."

msgctxt "object:181:58"
msgid "Winnetou!"
msgstr "Winnetou!"

msgctxt "object:181:59"
msgid ""
"Wie kann ich Firehand\n"
"helfen?"
msgstr ""
"I cannot help\n"
"Firehand."

msgctxt "object:181:61"
msgid ""
"Kann mir Winnetou die\n"
"Bedeutung der Inschrift\n"
"sagen?"
msgstr ""
"Can Winnetou tell me\n"
"the meaning of the\n"
"inscription?"

msgctxt "object:181:64"
msgid ""
"Die Zeichen  bedeuten\n"
"in Deiner Sprache:\n"
"Der Geist der in den\n"
"rechten Lüften schwebt,\n"
"wird wachen über den\n"
"Schlüssel, der zum\n"
"Tore führt."
msgstr ""
"In your language, the\n"
"signs mean:\n"
"The spirit that floats in\n"
"the right breezes will\n"
"watch over the\n"
"key that leads to the\n"
"gate."

msgctxt "object:181:71"
msgid ""
"Kann Winnetou mir\n"
"diesen Satz über-\n"
"setzen?"
msgstr ""
"Can Winnetou\n"
"translate this\n"
"sentence for me?"

msgctxt "object:181:74"
msgid ""
"Wenn Firehand ihn mir\n"
"noch einmal wiederholt."
msgstr ""
"If Firehand repeats\n"
"it for me once more."

msgctxt "object:181:76"
msgid ""
"Oh,ich habe ihn\n"
"vergessen..."
msgstr ""
"Oh, I have forgotten\n"
"it..."

msgctxt "object:181:78"
msgid ""
"Kann mir Winnetou die\n"
"Bedeutung der Inschrift\n"
"noch einmal sagen?"
msgstr ""
"Can Winnetou tell me\n"
"the meaning of the\n"
"inscription once more?"

msgctxt "object:181:81"
msgid ""
"Die Zeichen  bedeuten\n"
"in Deiner Sprache:\n"
"Der Geist der in den\n"
"rechten Lüften schwebt,\n"
"wird wachen über den\n"
"Schlüssel, der zum\n"
"Tore führt."
msgstr ""
"The signs mean in\n"
"your language:\n"
"The spirit that floats\n"
"in the right breezes\n"
"will watch over the key\n"
"that leads to the gate.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:88"
msgid ""
"Kann mir Winnetou die\n"
"Bedeutung der Inschrift\n"
"noch einmal sagen?"
msgstr ""
"Can Winnetou tell me\n"
"the meaning of the\n"
"inscription once more?"

msgctxt "object:181:91"
msgid ""
"Die Zeichen  bedeuten\n"
"in Deiner Sprache:\n"
"Der Geist der in den\n"
"rechten Lüften schwebt,\n"
"wird wachen über den\n"
"Schlüssel, der zum\n"
"Tore führt."
msgstr ""
"The signs mean in\n"
"your language:\n"
"The spirit that floats\n"
"in the right breezes\n"
"will watch over the key\n"
"that leads to the gate.\n"
"­"

msgctxt "object:181:98"
msgid ""
"Das war ein beschwer-\n"
"licher Weg bis hier."
msgstr ""
"That was an arduous\n"
"way to get here."

msgctxt "object:181:100"
msgid ""
"Firehand hat die Hin-\n"
"dernisse zum Schatz\n"
"bisher gut überwunden."
msgstr ""
"Firehand has overcome the\n"
"obstacles to the treasure\n"
"well so far."

msgctxt "object:181:103"
msgid ""
"Kann mein Freund\n"
"Winnetou die Tür\n"
"aufmachen?"
msgstr ""
"Can my friend\n"
"Winnetou open\n"
"the door?"

msgctxt "object:181:106"
msgid ""
"Ja, Winnetou wird\n"
"für Firehand die\n"
"Türe halten."
msgstr ""
"Yes, Winnetou will\n"
"hold the door for\n"
"Firehand."

msgctxt "object:181:109"
msgid ""
"Den stör' ich jetzt\n"
"besser nicht"
msgstr ""
"I'd better not disturb\n"
"him now"

msgctxt "object:181:111"
msgid "Winnetou."
msgstr "Winnetou."

msgctxt "object:181:112"
msgid ""
"Wie kann ich meinem\n"
"Freund Firehand helfen?"
msgstr ""
"How can I help my\n"
"friend Firehand?"

msgctxt "object:181:114"
msgid "Winnetou."
msgstr "Winnetou."

msgctxt "object:181:115"
msgid ""
"Wie kann ich meinem\n"
"Freund Firehand helfen?"
msgstr ""
"How can I help my\n"
"friend Firehand?"

msgctxt "object:181:117"
msgid ""
"Das ist Winnetou der Häuptling\n"
"der Apachen, und Freund der\n"
"rechtschaffenen Weissen."
msgstr ""
"That is Winnetou, the chief\n"
"of the Apaches, and friend of\n"
"the righteous white men."

